window.FWN_HERO_SUMMONING_PEACE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_HERO_SUMMONING_PEACE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2401,"title":"Chapter 2401: Spreading Aftermath 2","paragraphs":["As expected of a seasoned merchant with countless battles behind her, Akane-san exuded a pressure that seemed impossible for her small frame to produce, but after a moment, her expression softened slightly.","[...Well, it’s not like I came here to scold you this time, Kaito.]","[Arehh? You didn’t?]","[Yeah. I mean, if you trace the cause of this mess, and a few other ones, it often leads back to you...... But if you ask me whether that makes it your fault, well... I’d have to tilt my head and think on that one.]","It didn’t look like she was transitioning into a lecture after all. Akane-san’s face relaxed, and with a somewhat exasperated expression, she continued speaking.","[Remember how we ran into War King-sama during Archlesia Empire’s Founding Festival? That whole thing gave both me and Kaori stomachaches...... But then again, could that have been avoided if you’d been more careful, Kaito? Not really.]","[Well, yeah. That was really just a matter of ridiculous timing. It’s not like Kaito-kun invited us to your shop or called out to War King-sama. I mean, sure, you could say that Kaito-kun’s the type to attract that kind of crazy coincidence, but still...... it was me and Akane-san who decided to go to the Founding Festival in the first place. It’d be unfair to blame you for that.]","[Exactly. It’s not like Kaito’s aiming for trouble, nor is there any malice behind it. If we’re talking about right or wrong, Kaito hasn’t done anything wrong. This time’s probably something like that too, I figure.]","The conversation shifted to one that seemed to defend me, and I felt a small sense of relief, until Akane-san suddenly cut her words short, pointed sharply at me, and declared:","[But still, when you think about all the people, myself included, who’ve had to deal with stomachaches because of this guy’s antics, I figure someone’s gotta scold him every once in a while. So I figured I’d do it, just for form’s sake.]","[I see.................... yeah, Akane-san, I think you could stand to scold him a bit more firmly.]","[Kaori-san!?]","Ah, cr*p, this was one of those no-allies situations...... It had become a perfect two-against-one setup, and I couldn’t help but feel miserably cornered.","Also, I had more than a few things come to mind that made it hard to argue back.","As I was thinking that, Kaori-san gave a wry smile and spoke.","[......Just kidding. But really, Kaito-kun, you’re unbelievable sometimes. I still get nervous thinking that someday, out of nowhere, you’ll show up at my restaurant bringing along some incredibly important person again.]","[...................]","[......Hmmm, Kaito-kun? Why did you just avert your eyes so awkwardly? That’s rude, you know. Come on, look at me. Let’s talk properly, depending on what you’re hiding, I might end up being the one to scold you instead of Akane-san...... So tell me, why did you react like someone with a guilty conscience just now?]","She had every reason to ask that. I did, in fact, have something in mind. Or rather, someone, Magnawell-san. To be fair, it had only happened yesterday, and I simply hadn’t had the chance to tell her yet. I was going to explain it properly.","[......Well, I was planning to tell you soon, but...... Magnawell-san heard some things from Megiddo-san and, umm, seems to have taken an interest in your restaurant...... So, I promised to show her around next time.......]","[..............]","Upon hearing that, Kaori-san covered her face with both hands and looked up at the ceiling.","[You’re trying to bring another of the Six Kings here. Even setting aside Phantasmal King-sama, if Dragon King-sama shows up, that’s already half of them! Wait, are you seriously trying to completely gather all the Six Kings or something!? Kaito-kun, I think you’re misunderstanding something here, my place is a diner! A diner! It’s not supposed to be the gathering spot for the rulers of the Demon Realm, you knoooow!?]","[Um, errr, how should I say this...... Ah, here, this tea helps with stomachaches.]","[You gave up, didn’t you? You just totally gave up! From experience, you’ve already accepted that somehow, in the end, all six of them are gonna show up anyway, haven’t you!? So you’ve decided to stop resisting and start treating my stomach instead, haven’t you!? ......Thanks for the tea though!!!]","I handed her a can of MK Blend HS I’d bought from Canalis-san. Kaori-san, half in tears, perfectly read my state of mind while yelling her complaints.","Considering what happened with Lilia-san, I really do get the feeling that, somehow, I’ll end up bringing all of them sooner or later. I honestly have no idea how I’d even manage to bring someone like Lillywood-san, who doesn’t even eat or drink, to her restaurant...... but somehow, I can still see it happening.","And even as she shouted, Kaori-san still remembered to thank me for the tea in the end, that’s just so like her.","As I was thinking that, Akane-san patted me on the shoulder with a sigh.","[......Kaito, next time I’ll buy you a dictionary. Seems like the one you’ve got is defective, missing words like “restraint” and “moderation”. I’ll make sure to write them in big red letters right on the cover.]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [So far, the ones who’ve already visited her restaurant are Kuro and Megiddo, and if we count that guy who’s constantly by Kaito’s side, we can probably include Alice too. Now he’s planning to bring Magnawell, and since he got a control accessory from Canalis for Isis, if he ever decides to take her to some restaurant, Kaori’s place would obviously be the top candidate...... meaning the flag for Isis showing up is already raised as well. Honestly, if Lillywood ever ends up with even the slightest reason to visit, we might actually see a full Six Kings complete set...... Come to think of it, Kaori’s the only one in this world who owns trees that grow yuzu and sudachi, isn’t she......]"]},{"number":2402,"title":"Chapter 2402: Spreading Aftermath 3","paragraphs":["Kaori-san had always been like that, quick to switch gears, so at first she wore an inscrutable expression when she heard that Magnawell-san’s visit was coming up, but after a moment she pulled herself together and spoke.","[......Sigh. My stomach and my head hurt, but I’ll think about that later. Sorry, Akane-san, I cut in on your story, you can go on.]","[You also had it rough huh, Kaori...... Well, anyway, we got off track; let’s get back to the point......]","Come to think of it, if scolding me wasn’t the point, then Akane-san must have summoned me for some other business, and I hadn’t yet heard what that was.","Since she’d started by bringing up merchants from Archlesia Empire, maybe it was related to that?","[But listen, the matter’s simple. My merchant instincts say there’s a big money-making sign in the movements of those merchants from Archlesia Empire. Word is the Lord Trading Company is even arranging the funds, so this looks like a major score. The thing with this sort of opportunity is that the initial speed matters above all, right now the information’s all jumbled, so we can’t tell where a spark might flare up. Conversely, if we can get the core information ahead of the other trading companies, there’s a real chance to rake in solid profits.]","After saying that, Akane-san smiled in a way that made me feel a little suspicious and suddenly looped her arm around me, pressing close.","[......Hey, Kaito, since we’re close, let’s drop stupid secrets and be straight with each other. Also, I’ve got a favor to ask...... You’re almost certainly involved in whatever spark is about to ignite, so spill everything you did in Archlesia Empire recently.]","[Ah, yes.]","So it seemed the reason I’d been called here was simple: Akane-san’s merchant senses had sniffed out a profit, and she’d come to question me, the suspected...... or rather, the confirmed culprit for details.","A- As expected of an efficient merchant, she's quick to act...... well, fine. As for what I’d done in Archlesia Empire related to merchants, the Victor Trading Company matter from yesterday came to mind, but that felt too recent to be the source.","So maybe it was something else...... I couldn’t think of much, so I decided to start with the tea party Eris-san had hosted.","I explained, as thoroughly as I could, that I’d met noble ladies at the tea party Eris-san organized, that Marie-san had given me ripples and it was a large amount, so I’d distributed it to acquaintances while introducing them, about what happened with Cornelia-san from yesterday, and so on in as much detail as possible.","[......So that’s it for Archlesia Empire-related matters, I guess.]","[......I see. I think what I caught wind of is something to do with the Ritch Barony. If it were news about the Victor Trading Company, it’d be too soon to have reached me, and besides, that one involves Sharon County, so it wouldn’t be this vague. After hearing what you said, I’ve got a good idea of what the Lord Trading Company is aiming for...... Really, thanks for the info. But sorry, I’ve got to retort to you a bit...... You’re spreading bombs around more extravagantly than I imagined! Are you trying to give the Ritch Barony and Sharon County stomachaches and topple them?!]","[I’ve never met them, but I sincerely pity Lady Marie and Lady Cornelia......]","While Akane-san kept making sharp remarks even as she thanked me for the information I’d given, Kaori-san quietly nodded in agreement, as if acknowledging the truth of it.","However, Akane-san quickly switched to her merchant persona, her expression turning serious as she seemed to be contemplating something.","[......The part our trading house can get involved in is the one with Ritch Barony. The Victor Trading Company is effectively under the Sharon Trading Company, so Sharon Trading Company will definitely be steering that. They’re a pretty big trading company, and if we poke our noses in carelessly, we’d just get on their bad side, so we’ll ignore that part.]","[Arehh? But isn’t the Lord Trading Company operating in Ritch Barony? Wouldn’t it be worse to get on their bad side?]","[No, if our reading is correct, we won’t collide there. They’re one of the Five Great Trading Houses, they’ve arranged the funds, so there’s no way they’re fussing over buying ripples now. I mean, the fact that we even hear about them preparing funds shows that the ripple transactions aren’t that huge. This is just a prediction, but I think what the Lord Trading Company is trying to get their hands on was the Barony, and by extension, the logistics of Western Archlesia Empire itself.]","[What do you mean by that......]","[Ah, don’t worry, I’ve heard the details, and since people you know are involved, I’ll explain my reading in detail. This will be a long story...... Kaori, could I trouble you for a refill of tea?]","It seemed Akane-san was making predictions about something that was about to happen in Western Archlesia Empire, and she was going to explain them to me and Kaori-san.","I hadn’t really done anything related to the Lord Trading Company...... to Nia-san’s side, so why was the conversation leading towards them...... Perhaps listening to Akane-san’s predictions would clarify that point.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see...... so this is how it ties into the story of Marie’s stomach being destroyed...... Don't you have a heart......?]"]},{"number":2403,"title":"Chapter 2403: Spreading Aftermath 4","paragraphs":["Kaori-san prepared a refill of tea and herself sat down, adopting a posture to listen to Akane-san’s story.","[First, the area around the Ritch Barony's lands in the Western Archlesia Empire, our trading company has sourced from there a few times in the past, and the land itself has high potential. The soil is good, and the climate is stable compared to the rest of the Archlesia Empire, so high-quality crops can be harvested. In terms of quality, you could even say it’s top-class within the empire.]","[Hehh, but the Ritch Barony is poor, right? Well, I guess \"poor\" is relative among nobles; compared to commoners, they’re still wealthy.]","[Just having good quality doesn’t automatically mean you can sell a lot. In the end, things like publicity, image, demand and supply balance, and sales strategy all have to be solid, otherwise nothing will sell spectacularly. Even if the quality is high, it’s not like it’s the best in the world. Compared to places like Symphonia Kingdom, which also has high-quality crops, some of them are cheaper or even surpass in quality.]","Actually, even Raz-san gave high praise to Ritch Barony’s ripples, so there’s no doubt the quality and taste are genuinely good. But selling it based on that alone is difficult; publicity and recognition are also crucial. And naturally, proper advertising requires money, which the Ritch Barony likely doesn’t have.","Furthermore, logistics are poor, so even if they tried to sell on a larger scale, there would be many hurdles to overcome.","[The logistics aren’t good either, right?]","[That’s right, that’s a big issue too. First, there’s no teleportation gate in Ritch Barony, and that area is home to wyverns, so Flying Dragon Services won’t fly there. On top of that, because there are many mountains, the roads aren’t wide or well-built, and there are lots of areas with elevation differences, so it’s simply not suitable for transporting large amounts of cargo.]","Unless someone like Akane-san can use Teleportation Magic to transport goods, even teleportation magic tools are expensive and impractical for crop transport.","[I don’t really understand that kind of business, but don’t they try to develop infrastructure to improve logistics?]","[Well, if it’s profitable, that kind of idea would come up, but maintaining roads through monster-inhabited areas or building teleportation gates costs an enormous amount. If the expected return isn’t worth it, no one invests. Even the country has plenty of other places to prioritize. They wouldn’t allocate a large budget to remote lands that only produce moderately good crops. So in the end, Ritch Barony was seen as a place with decent potential...... but too remote for the investment required to improve logistics......]","I understood the intent behind Akane-san pausing there. The use of past tense suggests the situation has changed now.","As I thought this, Akane-san pointed at me with a slightly exasperated look.","[But then, this bombshell came along and injected both publicity and demand. From Kaito’s perspective, it was probably just sharing gifts with acquaintances, but your acquaintances are famous on a global scale. Even in our world, when a famous person uses or favors something, it’s a huge talking point and can ignite a trend, right?]","[Like using celebrities in TV commercials or advertisements.]","[Exactly. And that costs a lot of money, and usually you can’t get someone with global fame without special connections. But this idiot went and spread it to Death King-sama and various Count-ranks. Death King-sama even intended to buy it, and she casually asked Raz-sama, whose farm is world-famous for crops, to recommend it to acquaintances. She probably had no idea how extensive her connections are...... and that’s why it’s like this now.]","[So, Raz-sama really is an amazing person? I always thought her as just kind and cute......]","[With matters related to crops, she’s at the top globally, and her network is enormous. Just Raz-sama showing interest is enough to generate buzz. Add Death King-sama, Kaito, and the others Raz-sama recommended those apples to, it’s guaranteed that a trend will catch fire before long.]","Honestly, just as Akane-san said, I knew Raz-sama had a wide network, but I hadn’t realized she was such a famous figure in the industry.","I had just recommended it to a few people, thinking it might slightly boost sales at Marie-san’s place, but it seems like it’s become far more outrageous than I imagined.","[I’ve said it many times, but the potential in that area is high. So if publicity and demand catch fire, there’s more than enough capacity for it to take off. And once demand grows and things heat up, the region itself will naturally start to develop...... that’s probably what the Lord Trading Company is aiming for. I think they intend to build a teleportation gate in the Ritch Barony lands. By controlling the logistics of land with high development potential, they can make a huge profit. Of course, only a company like the Lord Trading Company, capable of moving such massive funds to build a teleportation gate quickly, could pull that off.]","[Ah, I see...... I think I’m starting to understand. If demand rises due to publicity, attention increases, and other trading companies start opening shops or establishing sales bases in the area, the region will develop. Then, if Lord Trading Company fixes the previously flawed logistics, the area can develop rapidly all at once.]","[Exactly. Normally, creating that much of a boom or publicity would cost a ridiculously huge amount of money...... but this monster managed to generate it just by casually sharing some ripples with acquaintances.]","[......Seriously, Kaito-kun is just...... Kaito-kun huh.]","Feeling a mix of embarrassment and awkwardness, I averted my gaze from Kaori-san and Akane-san, who were looking at me with that indescribable exasperated expression on their faces.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [It was skipped over in the story, but if that much attention is focused there, Archlesia Empire will naturally move to develop the land, so the development of the Ritch Barony is basically a done deal...... On top of that, there’s even God of Fertility trying to do something......]"]},{"number":2404,"title":"Chapter 2404: Spreading Aftermath 5","paragraphs":["Akane-san explained her predictions for the future of the Ritch Barony and its surroundings, while also pointing out how she and her company could profit from it.","[So, our target is to make our move before that predicted teleportation gate is completed. No matter how enormous the Lord Trading Company’s funds are, that doesn’t mean a teleportation gate will just pop up overnight. There are negotiations over the land, and if a teleportation gate is being established, Archlesia Empire's government needs to be notified. If it’s the influential Lord Trading Company, construction could happen fairly quickly, but even at the fastest, it would take over half a year. All sorts of procedures are involved, so there’s no mistake...... Well, unless someone like Kaito, who can ignore laws and rights, tries to make one, or some omnipotent god snaps their fingers and creates the gate, that’s a different story, but that’s something only Kaito could do; others can’t replicate it.]","[TKK...... \"Though it's only for Kaito-kun\", right!?]","[Kaori-san, don’t make weird acronyms.]","I couldn’t help throwing a tsukkomi back at Kaori-san, who was casually making a snappy acronym as if saying \"only works for ikemen\", just for fun.","[......Well, does that mean, Akane-san, that your plan is to earn while the teleportation gate is being built?]","[Exactly. The idea is that there’s demand and buzz, but logistics haven’t been optimized yet. For a mobile trading company like ours, this is the perfect time to make a profit. Once the teleportation gate is completed, bigger companies will have the advantage in many aspects, so we aim to earn as much as possible before then and retreat at the right timing.]","[I see, yeah, that really does sound profitable.]","As Kaori-san said, it really does seem like a lucrative opportunity. For Mikumo Trading Company, which specializes in Teleportation Magic and has the agility of a small-to-medium-sized operation, this plan seems perfectly suited.","After finishing her explanation, Akane-san started muttering while holding her chin in thought, wearing a serious expression.","[......That said, there are plenty of trading companies that might think the same thing. Especially this time, there’s no need to use Teleportation Magic repeatedly over a short period, and any company with a Teleportation magic tool could do the same. Thanks to hearing from Kaito, we currently have an informational advantage, but that will be leveled out in a few days. I don’t think the Ritch Barony has the capacity to negotiate with multiple companies at once...... so it seems like whoever piques their interest first will win...... Hey, Kaito, I need to consult with you about something, is that okay?]","[What is it?]","Akane-san, who seemed to have organized her thoughts, spoke in a serious tone. I tilted my head slightly and asked back, and she took a piece of paper from her magic box and placed it in front of me.","The paper was filled with small writing, with a spot at the bottom for a signature.","[It's written in a roundabout way, but to summarize, it says \"The merchant who brings this is trustworthy, so whether or not you trade, please at least hear them out\". In other words, it’s a letter of introduction.]","[Errr, you’re asking me to write a letter of introduction for you?]","[Exactly...... but first, hear me out. We consider you a close friend. You have your flaws, but you’re a good person. That’s why I want to be honest with you, no secrets. This opportunity will definitely bring us a big profit. But there are likely other trading companies thinking the same thing, so it’s a speed race...... the one who secures the contract with the Ritch Barony first will win. And if the letter comes from you, the Ritch Barony will undoubtedly prioritize listening to our company’s proposal.]","Akane-san’s expression was completely serious, openly conveying her analysis and intentions to me without holding anything back.","[I’ll be blunt. I want to use our connections with you so our company can make a profit. But don’t get me wrong, I also have pride as a merchant. If you just introduced us out of kindness because we’re acquaintances, it would only be embarrassing. So, if you think a deal between us and Mikumo Trading Company is beneficial for Lady Marie and the Ritch Barony, and you’re okay with it, then please sign. If you don’t think so, or simply don’t feel like it, just say no. I won’t complain, and it won’t affect our relationship going forward. In fact, I’d rather you honestly say no if it’s a no...... How about it?]","In truth, Akane-san is extremely sincere and earnest when it comes to business. Even when we first met, I offered her a Fruit of the World Tree as a gift, and though it would have been easier for her to accept it outright, she refused it because its value didn’t match the gesture. From that moment, I already thought she was an honest and trustworthy person.","[That’s fine. Akane-san, you’re someone I can trust, and honestly, I think if the Ritch Barony is going to do business, your Mikumo Trading Company would be the best choice.]","[Really? If that’s how you feel, I’d be grateful.]","Even ignoring the fact that she’s a friend, Akane-san and Mikumo Trading Company seem well-suited for the Ritch Barony. The Ritch Barony is poor among the nobility, and Lady Marie even joked that she’s practically like a peasant. They also likely have little to no experience dealing with large trading companies.","So, if approached by a huge company, they’d probably be intimidated. A company of Mikumo Trading Company’s size would be easier for them to deal with. On top of that, since Mikumo Trading Company excels at Teleportation Magic and is highly mobile, they can compensate for the current shortcomings of the Ritch Barony. It truly seems like the ideal fit.","[Should I sign here?]","[Yeah, but before that, let’s talk about remunerations. You might say money doesn’t matter to you, but that’s not acceptable for me as a merchant. As a token of thanks for the introduction, I plan to return a portion of the profits to you, but we should discuss what percentage, and finalize that contract too.]","Her sincerity in matters like this once again made me realize how trustworthy she is as a merchant.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [In reality, she perfectly fits the conditions for the Ritch Barony, and since she’s not someone who’s easily intimidated, plus with other major trading companies seeing this as \"a recommendation from Kaito\", they probably won’t interfere awkwardly. So she does seem like the optimal choice.]"]},{"number":2405,"title":"Chapter 2405: Spreading Aftermath 6","paragraphs":["In the end, regarding my contract with Akane-san, we settled on me receiving 10% of the profits. Akane-san seemed a little dissatisfied, or rather, it felt like she wanted me to take a larger share, but she also seemed to understand that I wasn’t particularly interested in money to begin with, and that I already had more funds than I knew what to do with. In the end, she accepted it.","[Sign here...... Should I also stamp it?]","[If you’ve got a seal, I’d appreciate it if you used it. Do you have the same kind of seal that Anima-san used for business deals, Kaito?]","[Yes, Anima made one for me and gave it to me.]","Since Anima handles financial management and investments, our household does have an official seal. The one Anima uses is the seal of the proxy of the house, while mine is a slightly more ornate version meant to be used by the actual head...... at least, that’s the official reasoning behind it.","It seems this sort of thing is standard among nobles. Lilia-san, for instance, also has a personal seal that only she is permitted to use, apart from the one belonging to Albert Duchy.","Anyway, I pressed my seal next to my signature, completing the letter of introduction.","[Thanks a bunch. With this, I reckon I’ll make a solid profit, so look forward to your share, Kaito.]","[Do your best...... By the way, Akane-san.]","[Hmm?]","[You said you didn’t really plan on getting involved with the Sharon County, but I’d like to hear what you think might happen over there......]","[Ah, I’d like to hear that too. So far, the only thing I can think of is that maybe their place will become trending among the Dragon King’s subordinates, with them having Kaito-kun's recommendation.]","Akane-san’s predictions regarding matters related to the Ritch Barony were sharp enough to make me think, as expected of a first-class merchant. I hadn’t imagined things would develop like that, so it was extremely informative.","That said, I feel like someone like Marie-san might have a hard time with it, so depending on how things go, I might need to lend a hand somehow...... But when it comes to land development or trade, an amateur like me interfering could just make things worse. It’s a tough call......","Well, for now, setting the Ritch Barony matters aside, I wanted to know what Akane-san thought would happen concerning the Sharon County.","[Hmmm, at this point, there are still too many unknowns. Like Kaori said, it’s all about whether it becomes a trend, but that depends on Kaito liking the finished brush first. Once people like Nidzveld-sama hear Kaito’s review and decide to try it themselves, that’s when it might take off. If you actually use it and find it lacking though, then it’ll end right there...... Anyway, let’s talk about what might happen if Kaito does like the custom brush and tells Nidzveld-sama it’s a fine product, okay?]","[Please do.]","[The first thing that comes to mind is an increase in demand. There are a ton of dragons under the Dragon King’s command, and even if only about 10% of them get interested, that’d still make for a pretty big boom. But, I dunno...... Honestly, I can’t imagine how many dragons would want a custom-made brush. Some probably use magic to keep themselves clean, and I’m not sure how many would care enough to get one made just for them. I mean, I don’t really understand what dragons think about their scales, you know......]","[So basically, it’s like asking whether we’d want a custom comb or something like that, right? Hmm, I think store-bought ones are fine for me. I can’t even tell the difference between them, really......]","Indeed, as both Akane-san and Kaori-san pointed out, there were still many uncertainties about how many dragons would actually want custom brushes. If you compare it to humans, it’s like beauty products, I suppose? If someone asked me whether I’d want my own personalized version...... I’d probably say no. So maybe, it wouldn’t be as widespread or popular as we first imagined.","[If dragons end up being really particular about how well the brush fits or feels, then yeah, it could become a massive hit. But if that happens, the Victor Trading Company wouldn’t be able to handle all the orders on its own. In that case, I reckon the Sharon Trading Company would step in. Either they’d buy out Victor’s rights entirely, or they’d create a new department within the Sharon Trading Company focused on monsters and handle orders there...... Something like that, I think. Either way, I don’t see much room for any other competitors to get involved.]","[But the Sharon Trading Company deals in magic tools, right?]","[Yeah, that’s true...... So maybe the Sharon County might establish a new trading company altogether. They could bring Victor Trading Company fully under their wing, allocate funds to them, and eventually turn it into a monster-related business...... But like I said before, a lot depends on Kaito’s opinion. I’m not sure if they’d make any major moves at this stage......]","It seemed that Cornelia-san would have her hands full as well, and while I wanted to help somehow, according to Akane-san, there were still too many uncertain factors at the moment.","[......By the way, if I do end up liking the brush, should I actively recommend it to others?]","[Hmm, if it stays under the Victor Trading Company, I think they’d get overwhelmed with orders. But if the Sharon County gets involved and sets up a proper trading company for it, they’d probably be expecting large-scale demand anyway, so in that case, I’d say go ahead and promote it. Unlike ripples, this is a niche product with limited buyers, so even if Kaito spreads the word all over, it’s unlikely to cause any unexpected problems.]","[I see, thank you. I’ll keep that in mind.]","Fumu, for now, I’ll remember Akane-san’s advice...... but in any case, it looks like everything depends on how the custom brush actually feels in use.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see. So even though there are a lot of the Dragon King’s subordinates, since the target audience is limited, it’ll probably just become a big trend within certain circles...... But somehow, I can’t shake the feeling that there’s some kind of pitfall waiting in there.]"]},{"number":2406,"title":"Chapter 2406: Spreading Aftermath 7","paragraphs":["After my conversation with Akane-san had reached a certain conclusion and things had settled down, Kaori-san stood up from her chair with a smile.","[Is the talk over? Then, how about it, since it’s a rare opportunity, why don’t both of you have a little something to eat? There’s a dish I was thinking of putting on the limited-time menu, and I’d like to hear your thoughts on it.]","[Huh? If it’s okay with you, Kaori, I’m a bit hungry, so I’d like to eat...... but I feel kind of bad about it. You’re letting us use your place and even treating us, if it’s too much trouble, I can pay for the meal.]","[Kaori-san’s cooking is delicious, and it’s a kind offer but...... just like Akane-san said, we’ll pay, okay?]","While I appreciated Kaori-san offering to serve us her cooking, I felt a bit guilty. She had let us use her shop as a place for our discussion, served us tea, and now was even treating us to a meal, even though it had little to do with the conversation between Akane-san and me.","Still, Kaori-san smiled as if to say \"Don’t worry about it\".","[I haven’t even set a price for it as a menu item yet, and since this is a tasting...... I can’t accept money for it as a professional.]","[Ahaha, now that you put it that way, I can’t argue. Then, I’ll gratefully accept your treat. Kaito, that’s fine with you too, right?]","[Yes. I’ll find another opportunity to properly thank Kaori-san......]","[......Just within normal courtesy, please...... w- well, anyway, I’ll get it ready right away. Oh, it’s stew. You can choose between beef stew and white stew, both are already prepared and in the magic box, so it doesn’t take extra effort to get either one ready.]","With a wry smile, Kaori-san wrapped a triangular headscarf around her head, put on an apron, and headed into the kitchen, asking Akane-san and me which stew we preferred.","[Kaito, which one do you want? I like both, so why don’t we order different ones for the occasion? You can choose first.]","[I like both as well...... then, I’ll go with the white stew.]","[Then I’ll take the beef stew.]","[Alright. I’ll have it ready right away, so just wait a moment~~]","After hearing our responses, Kaori-san pulled two large pots from her magic box into the back of the kitchen and began preparing the tableware and other items.","[But as a set meal, it’s a bit of an unusual menu, isn’t it?]","[Yeah. I usually make set meals to go with rice, but in this world, rice isn’t that common. So I thought it would be nice to have some bread-based options too, so customers have a choice. I’m still figuring out the exact menu, though it’ll start with limited-time dishes and adjust based on customer reactions.]","[Houu~~ you’ve put a lot of thought into it. Kaori’s shop must be popular, hasn’t it been featured in magazines and such?]","[It was introduced in travel magazines as a place where you can eat authentic Otherworld Cuisine. Whether my set meals are truly authentic is another matter, but with Olivia-sama being a regular, it’s become quite prosperous. It’s often fully booked at night.]","I remembered seeing an article about Kaori-san’s shop too. It was about two pages long and seemed like a fairly thorough feature. Olivia-san being a regular probably contributed a lot, but the novelty of rice-centered otherworldly cuisine must also be a factor.","In the Friendship City Hikari, a place with lots of tourists, that novelty brought in plenty of customers.","[But that must make it hard for just Kaori-san to run the shop alone, right?]","[No, not really. I actually have a lot more leeway than before. Having that leeway is why I can make these limited-time dishes and experiment from time to time.]","[Even though the shop is doing well, you have more leeway than before?]","I shared the same puzzled look as Akane-san. Logically, a busier shop should mean less free time, yet Kaori-san said she had more leeway than before, and she didn’t seem to be lying.","[My shop was originally set up with just enough seats for me to manage alone, so running out of hands isn’t really an issue. That reason’s part of it, but more than anything...... for a restaurant, having a large-capacity magic box really makes you realize it’s a godsend.]","[Ah, I see. You just make it and put it in there, huh.]","[Unn. Cooking, like stew and such, is more efficient if you make a certain amount all at once. But if you make too much, then if it doesn’t sell, you have to throw it away. You have to consider how many orders each dish will get and make accordingly. Even if you prep some things in advance, there are lots of dishes you still have to cook after receiving an order, so I couldn’t really increase the number of menu items. The more you try to increase it, the harder it is to predict sales, and leftovers pile up.]","Indeed, when I first came to Kaori-san’s shop, the menu had about half as many items and no limited-time offerings. The fact that the menu had grown meant she had gained enough leeway to expand it, and the magic box seemed to be a key factor in that.","[But with a large-capacity magic box, I can make a batch, put it in, and just plate it when needed, it’s super easy. And since it’s stored in a freshly cooked state, there’s no need to reheat it. Any limited-time items that don’t sell, I can just eat for dinner, so food waste is almost nonexistent. It’s easier, more profitable, and really convenient. Thanks to that, I can come up with all sorts of new menu ideas, which is fun. That's why I’m grateful to Raz-sama for giving me the magic box and to Kaito-kun for introducing her to me.]","Kaori-san said this with a beaming smile, clearly enjoying herself, and it was clear that she simply loved cooking itself. Seeing that smile, I couldn't help smiling as well.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [That’s true, if you can prevent food from spoiling, keep dishes in a freshly cooked state, and have a capacity equivalent to an entire mansion, then for a restaurant handling ingredients, it really is a godsend...... But according to Shigenobu, a black magic box easily costs over a hundred million, so for an ordinary restaurant, installing a large-capacity magic box would be far too expensive......]"]},{"number":2407,"title":"Chapter 2407: Spreading Aftermath 8","paragraphs":["While Kaito was spending enjoyable moments with the two from his hometown, those involved with the Ritch Barony at the center of the storm were steadily starting to move as well.","Deep within the headquarters of the Lord Trading Company in Archlesia Empire, in the private chamber of its head, Satania Darklord, sat Gluttony, one of the same Ten Demons, across from her.","[......So, I want you to cooperate as well.]","[If it benefits Miyama Kaito-sama, there is no reason for me to refuse cooperation. I can act immediately, if needed.]","[No, it’s not that simple. First, we need to present the plan to construct a teleportation gate in the Ritch Barony, get approval, apply through the Archlesia Empire, and purchase the necessary land. Requests for teleportation permission fall under the jurisdiction of us Phantasmal King's subordinates, so that part will go smoothly, but considering applications for constructing a large structure and notifying the surrounding area, preparations alone will take at least a month. Actual construction can only begin after that.]","[......I’ll leave the rights and permissions to you. As for construction, using my Dimension Beasts, it can be completed without issue in two days.]","Gluttony was a master of space-time magic, but that wasn’t all, she commanded her own unique forces, Dimension Beasts created from her own flesh and blood. Among them, Natasha, her masterpiece, possessed the ability of a Peak Count-rank, and she had many other powerful Dimension Beasts under her command. By mobilizing them, even a massive teleportation gate could be completed from scratch, including all adjustments to the ritual, within two days.","However, Satania shook her head at Gluttony’s words.","[No, that won’t do. If the goal were simply to establish the teleportation gate, that would be fine, but this time, we also need to adjust logistics and the flow of money in the Western Archlesia Empire...... the Ritch Barony. By employing and dispatching workers and increasing local consumption, we can raise the total volume of money circulating within Ritch Barony's domains.]","[......Fumu.]","[Furthermore, we don’t want a situation where the Lord Trading Company wins everything alone, that could create unnecessary enemies. We need to give other trading companies some leeway to operate, including competing in commercial battles. Considering the time it would take for other trading companies to establish sales points or stores within the Ritch Barony, I initially thought three months would be ideal...... but just now, Shalltear-sama instructed that the teleportation gate should be completed \"six months from now\".]","[Shalltear-sama did?]","According to Satania’s calculations, if they wanted to complete the teleportation gate while giving other trading companies a chance to earn, improving logistics, employment, and consumption without letting the Lord Trading Company dominate too much, three months would have been ideal, but then a timing directive arrived from Alice.","[Yeah, apparently it’s because \"she was pleased with how they handled things and intends to let them profit as planned\". Shalltear-sama wants to give the merchants she’s taken interest in an opportunity to earn.]","[I see. In any case, if it’s Shalltear-sama’s order, it’s absolute. The teleportation gate will be completed six months from now.]","[Yes. I’ll contact you again when the time comes.]","[Understood.]","Gluttony confirmed her cooperation, and Satania nodded in satisfaction, ending the discussion about the teleportation gate. Both were devoted to Alice without question or dissent, and the completion of the teleportation gate was set firmly for six months later.","At the same time, in the imperial office of the Archlesia Empire, Emperor Chris was staring into the distance while reviewing a stack of documents, making a strange motion of pressing her eyes and shaking her head.","A close aide, wearing an expression somewhere between pity and unease, spoke up.","[Your Majesty, lamenting it won’t change the results of these reports.]","[......I almost want to hit my past self for saying it would be better if Miyama-sama were more involved with the Empire. So much...... in just a few days...... things have moved this much...... and now the west...... the budget proposal will need to be reconsidered, and the nation can’t just sit idle...... but having the Lord Trading Company involved makes things difficult.]","[It’s impressive, I must say. I didn’t expect they would gather information faster than us. Ideally, we would have wanted the teleportation gate to be state-led...... but already, we’ve received a preemptive letter of inquiry for the construction permit, clearly an attempt to keep us in check.]","[At this point, we have no choice but to give up. Their initial moves were far faster than ours; if we intervene clumsily, it will only lead to conflict with the Lord Trading Company.]","Chris, of course, was aware of the movements of merchants within her own country, and she had even paid close attention to the participants of the tea party hosted by Eris.","She had learned that Marie of the Ritch Barony had given ripple to Kaito...... but she could never have predicted that Kaito, while distributing it among acquaintances and promoting it, would draw so much attention in just a few days that merchants caught wind of it and began moving, ultimately affecting the entire Western Archlesia Empire.","Among all this, the Lord Trading Company moved at an astonishing speed. The state had wanted to be involved in the construction of the teleportation gate, which promised immense profit, but that now seemed almost impossible.","[For now, improving the surrounding infrastructure of the Ritch Barony is essential. We need to allocate a larger budget to ensure at least that large horse-drawn carriages can pass through without issue.]","[Yes. I’ve already given instructions to the Minister of Finance and the key financial officers, so a meeting can be held immediately...... Another point of concern is the movements of Goddess of Fertility-sama.]","[......Inviting the Ritch Baron and Lady Marie to the temple...... I don’t expect the Gods to get involved in a commercial battle...... but for what purpose......]","Based on the information Chris had, the Goddess of Fertility wished to speak as soon as possible, which led to the Ritch Baron and Marie visiting her temple today. Imagining what kind of discussion would unfold there...... Chris unconsciously moved her hand as if stroking her stomach.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well, it’s only natural, after all, this is happening within the empire, so even this Stomachache Warrior is bound to be affected.]"]},{"number":2408,"title":"Chapter 2408: Spreading Aftermath 9","paragraphs":["Within the Archlesia Empire, the Temple of Fertility is a place that many people are deeply familiar with. Due to the land’s nature, the Archlesia Empire has always been less suitable for agriculture compared to Symphonia Kingdom or Hydra Kingdom, and until the temple was built, its food self-sufficiency rate had remained low.","However, after Shallow Vernal dispatched the Goddess of Fertility, Elune, to the Archlesia Empire to establish her temple there, things changed. Thanks to the Divine Protection of Fertility she bestows every year across the entire empire, crops began to grow steadily even in Archlesia’s harsh lands. For the Archlesia Empire, Elune became an exceptionally vital figure, and faith towards her quickly grew widespread.","Even before the White God Festival, Elune herself had always been one of the more Human-friendly Gods among the Gods, occasionally attending national ceremonies as a guest of honor. However, while she did attend such events, she would never participate in parties or private gatherings, maintaining a respectful distance. Her conduct, neither too distant nor overly familiar, was often praised by Life as exemplary, a perfect model for low-ranking Gods dispatched to the Human Realm.","After the White God Festival, it seemed that she began appearing more often in public ceremonies in line with the collective stance of the Gods...... Even so, receiving a personal summons from her was unheard of, an utterly extraordinary event.","And now, trembling as they made their way towards the Temple of Fertility after receiving this unprecedented summons from a God, were Baron Ritch and Marie Ritch.","[......T- This is actually my first time going to Goddess of Fertility-sama’s main sanctuary......]","[You didn’t even receive the New Year’s blessing this year. Considering the distance between our territory and the capital, that’s only natural.]","Naturally, not every member of a noble family receives a Temporary Blessing directly from a low-ranking God. After all, while Blessings given directly by such Gods are undeniably effective, they also come at a steep price, one gold coin per blessing.","For the Ritch Barony, known to all as a poor noble household, they could not possibly afford to give even their fourth daughter, Marie, an annual Blessing.","And beyond the Blessing fee itself, traveling from the Ritch Barony to the Temple of Fertility where Elune resides requires a long carriage journey, paying for the use of a teleportation gate, then renting another carriage in the capital to continue the trip...... The travel expenses alone are considerable.","Although the family does travel to the Imperial Capital’s Temple of Fertility once a year for the ceremony, rather than visiting the smaller temple near their domain, Marie and the other younger siblings merely receive a Blessing from a priest at the front shrine. Only Baron Ritch, his wife, their heir and eldest son, and their eldest daughter who manages the family’s farmland are permitted into the main sanctuary to receive Elune’s direct blessing.","Thus, this was the first time Marie would be meeting Elune in person, and she was understandably nervous.","[......I borrowed another dress from Elder Sister. Well, I don’t own any clothes that would be suitable for meeting Goddess of Fertility-sama, so I had no choice, but I can’t help worrying I might stain it somehow.]","[It seems we’ll need to buy you a proper, high-quality dress of your own soon. We couldn’t make it in time for this visit, but you’ll also need formal attire for our future negotiations with the Lord Trading Company and the Death King's subordinate. Since we’re in the Imperial Capital, we might as well buy one before we return.]","[A- Ahaha...... Normally I’d be thrilled to go shopping for clothes in the capital, but right now my stomach just hurts.]","[I understand the feeling. Honestly, I have no idea what’s going on or what we’re supposed to do. I’d have liked to take the words about \"seeking counsel anytime\" literally and rush to consult with Marquis Hamilton, but...... we couldn’t possibly keep Goddess of Fertility-sama waiting.]","To be frank, Baron Ritch’s capabilities could hardly be called impressive, and above all, he lacked any real experience. Having grown up in a remote frontier far removed from political schemes and noble intrigue, Baron Ritch had no idea how to deal with this unprecedented situation. It was only natural that he wanted to seek advice from someone far more intelligent, like Marquis Hamilton.","[......The capital is so dazzling. If we were here just for sightseeing or shopping, I might actually be enjoying this......]","[If we register this location into your teleportation magic tool, it’ll be easier to come to the Imperial Capital next time, won’t we?]","[Even if we do come, it’s not like we’ll have the money to go shopping around the capital. Still, yes, I suppose we should register it, if only because it might become necessary later.]","As she gazed at the Temple of Fertility coming into view beyond the window, Marie gave a faint, helpless smile, as though trying to escape reality. Deep down, she wished for only one thing...... that this ordeal would end peacefully, without incident.","......A wish that, unfortunately, would not be granted......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [What a merciless narration......]"]},{"number":2409,"title":"Chapter 2409: Spreading Aftermath 10","paragraphs":["Baron Ritch and Marie, having arrived at the Temple of Fertility, were guided by the priest toward the main hall where Elune awaited. Baron Ritch, having visited several times before, remained composed, but Marie, visiting the main hall for the first time, seemed somewhat unsettled, her gaze moving around nervously under the solemn atmosphere.","After walking for a while, they reached a grand door, where the priest bowed toward them and then spoke.","[......I have brought them here.]","[Please allow them to enter.]","[Understood. You two, please step inside.]","Hearing Elune’s voice, the priest bowed and opened the doors, gesturing for Baron Ritch and Marie to enter. Once he confirmed that they had stepped inside, the priest closed the doors without entering himself.","At the far end of the spacious room, dotted with numerous trees, stood the God of Fertility, Elune. Baron Ritch and Marie approached to a suitable distance and assumed a posture of prayer.","[You may make yourselves comfortable. Please, take a seat here...... I apologize for calling you here on such short notice today.]","[N- No, it’s an honor to meet the Goddess of Fertility.]","[Y- Yes.]","Though both Baron Ritch and Marie were extremely tense, Elune was fundamentally gentle and calm, smiling warmly as she invited them to sit and placed tea in front of each of them.","[Baron Ritch, we have met a few times during the New Year’s Blessing, but this would be our first meeting, right, Marie Ritch-san?]","[Y- Y- Y- Yes! I am Marie Ritch.]","[Pleased to meet you. Generally, Gods do not reveal their names except in special circumstances...... but you are a friend of Miyama-san, correct? In that case, it would be rude not to introduce myself...... I am Elune, God of Fertility. May today’s meeting lead to a positive relationship going forward.]","[Y- Yesh!?]","For the Gods, a name is an extremely important thing, granted to them by Shallow Vernal along with their Authority. It is normally only revealed to those who have received their True Blessing or are of great importance to the God Realm.","For Elune to reveal her name here was essentially a declaration that Marie’s existence was recognized as significant to the God Realm.","(We only met once and spoke though!? N- No, we were called friends, and we exchanged letters but...... b- being a friend of Kaito-sama could really lead to something like this......?)","Marie could not hide her genuine shock, yet Elune smiled calmly, paying it no particular mind, and sat down at the seat opposite them.","[Now that the brief introductions are over, let us move to the main topic, which I’m sure you are curious about. That is, the reason I called you both here. I believe you can somewhat guess, but it concerns Miyama-san. To confirm, Marie-san, you did indeed give Ritch Barony's ripples to Miyama-san, correct?]","[Y- Yes. I gave them...... Ah, u- um, did I perhaps make some mistake......?]","[No, we are not reproaching you. On the contrary, Miyama-san held your ripples in high regard, and my superior, God of Life-sama, also received some of them from Miyama-san.]","[Hiieek......]","This was truly a bolt from the blue. Marie felt as if her breath had momentarily stopped. She had indeed sent extra ripples, and it was expected that Kaito might share them with his acquaintances.","But she could never have imagined that...... they would be shared with a Supreme God, and the thought left her mind in turmoil.","[God of Life-sama was pleased that Miyama-san liked the Archlesia Empire's ripples, but also had some concerns. Namely, that Miyama-san’s influence might cause the demand for the Ritch Barony’s ripples to rise excessively...... You both have likely noticed similar signs, haven’t you?]","[Y- Yes, we did receive letters from unexpected people...... but we didn't really think it would be that bad......]","Listening to Elune, Baron Ritch finally began to connect the letters from the Lord Trading Company and the Death King's subordinate into a single line in his mind. Indeed, the letters Marie received mentioned that the Death King’s subordinate intended to purchase ripples, but the movements of the Lord Trading Company had been a mystery.","However, from Elune’s explanation...... he concluded that the increase in demand for the Ritch family’s ripples had prompted the great Lord Trading Company, to act as well.","Yes, unfortunately, Baron Ritch had little connection with merchants and was not aware of their movements, so he simply assumed that the Lord Trading Company was also aiming to buy ripples. He could never have imagined it was about creating a transfer gate, and he would have been completely flabbergasted if he had actually heard it, but at this moment, he had no room to realize that mistake.","[Anticipating this increase in demand, and taking Miyama-san’s friend into consideration...... the conclusion reached by the Gods, including God of Life-sama, is to strengthen the Divine Protection over the Ritch Barony’s territory.]","[ [ ................... ] ]","[This time, we have called you here to discuss the finer details of that scope and the timing.]","Elune is kind and gentle, but she also possesses the Godly traits typical of a subordinate of Life. The reason she called Baron Ritch and Marie was not to make a \"proposal\", but to \"inform them of the decision\". Once Life made the decision, the strengthening of the Divine Protection was already set in stone, and they were summoned only to coordinate the details.","Of course, Baron Ritch and Marie, who had not even imagined such a thing, were left gaping in stunned astonishment......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [But looking at it this way, the differences in experience among the noble families are striking. Eris and Marquis Hamilton, despite getting stomachaches, still manage to swiftly handle countermeasures and meetings each time. Cornelia and Count Sharon can keep up with Eris and the others to a certain extent, but beyond a certain point, they're having it rough. Baron Ritch and Marie, on the other hand, are completely unable to cope and just get swept away by the torrent.]","? ? ? : [Well, in any pattern, it all ends up as a stomachache anyway, so it doesn’t really change much, I guess.]","Serious-senpai : [That’s just too cruel.]"]},{"number":2410,"title":"Chapter 2410: Spreading Aftermath 11","paragraphs":["After enjoying Kaori-san’s delicious stew, we relaxed with Akane-san and Kaori-san over tea and casual conversation before parting ways.","[Are you heading straight back to Symphonia, Kaito?]","[Ah, no, I was thinking of stopping by Archlesia Empire's Imperial Capital for a bit.]","[Archlesia Empire's Imperial Capital? Is something happening there today?]","When I answered Akane-san’s question, Kaori-san tilted her head curiously and asked back.","[No, nothing like that. Isis-san once told me there’s a really big bookstore in Archlesia Empire, and I’ve been wanting to go. Since I’m already out, I thought I might as well stop by. I can get to the Imperial Capital quickly using a teleportation magic tool anyway.]","[Ahh, you talking about that ridiculously huge shop on Central Avenue. I’ve never been there myself, but I’ve heard they’ve got everything, from magazines to old books.]","[Yeah. I’ve got plenty of time today, so I figured I’d take it easy and enjoy myself......]","There might be books I can’t find at my usual stores, and since I’ve got time to spare, it’s perfect. After briefly saying goodbye to the nodding Akane-san and Kaori-san, I activated the teleportation magic tool and headed for Archlesia Empire's Imperial Capital.","The bookstore I was heading to was, just as Akane-san had said, ridiculously huge. I could tell where it was the moment I got close. It was several times larger than any bookstore I usually went to, and the inside was spacious, lined wall to wall with books. It almost looked like an enormous library, but since it was a bookstore, there were clearly divided sections, with popular books stacked flat on tables, it had a distinctly different atmosphere.","For now, I headed to the magazine section, but even that was enormous, filled with a ton of magazines I’d never seen before.","As I was browsing for something interesting, I came across an area lined with magazines featuring photographs on their covers.","......I see, fashion magazines huh...... Well, photographs go hand-in-hand with fashion after all. Even if recording magic tools were still in the process of spreading, the impact they had brought to the publishing world was tremendous.","Still, even fashion magazines here were quite different from those in my old world......","< Monthly Undead >","......Huh. I ended up finding a magazine with Sechs-san on the cover, wearing what looked like a very stylish formal outfit. Well, Sechs-san is supposedly an extremely popular and dashing gentleman among the Undead, so it’s not exactly strange for him to be treated like this...... b- but still, what a sight.","From what I could gather from the cover, it looked like Sechs-san had a 14-page feature inside. The cover even had a tagline saying something like \"Because we’re bones, we must have backbone\".","D- D*mn it...... I really want to see it. I’m insanely curious about the inside...... but no. That’s not good. Because right now, I don’t want to look inside it for its purpose as a fashion magazine, but because I want to see it for its comedic value. That’s no good.","It’s disrespectful to treat something from a field you don’t understand as a joke. I’m curious. I'm extremely curious, but...... I’ve got to restrain myself here......","[Ah, by the way, there’s a tagline in the photo section that says \"Youngsters just don’t have our bone density!\". Maybe bone density is considered a mark of handsomeness among skeletons?]","[Pff! Stop that, idiot, don’t tell me weird stuff like that......]","[And apparently, there’s even a sexy shot showing off his ribs.]","[A sexy shot showing ribs!? So ribs are sexy in the undead world...... Wait, just stop, seriously, don’t feed me any more information.]","Alice started saying all sorts of unnecessary things, and I couldn’t help but burst out laughing. Stop, d*mn it, you’re making me want to buy it!!!","No, Miyama Kaito, stop. Don’t do something that would make it impossible to look Sechs-san in the eye again as a friend. Stay strong. Move on to another magazine......","< This Year’s Must-See Buff Yet Cute Minotaur Outfits >","......What is this section? Some kind of fashion hell? Right next to the Undead fashion magazine was one featuring three muscular, scantily clad...... presumably female Minotaurs, posing confidently, each with the face of a bull.","Also, \"buff yet cute\"? Seriously, buff yet cute? From my perspective, they just looked strong and ripped. Without the text, I’d think it was a bodybuilding poster, but maybe in Minotaur culture, it’s different...... I’m really feeling the species gap here.","Well, I can kind of get the Undead thing since their culture is broad, but are there even enough Minotaurs for them to have a dedicated magazine?","......Ah, wait, looking closer at the cover, it also mentions Cyclops and Orcs, so it seems to be a fashion magazine that covers multiple species.","Come to think of it, I remember hearing once that Mina-san, Minagard-san, one of Nia-san’s Minotaur aides, is considered a peerless beauty among Minotaurs.","This too, I don’t really understand, about as much as I don’t understand how it was like with the Undead...... but well, when it comes to Mina-san, I can somewhat see the reasoning.","Her voice is incredibly high and beautiful, and every one of her gestures is so refined that, now that it’s been pointed out, she does have that air of elegance and nobility. I can see how that would make her a beauty in the Minotaur community.","As for Sechs-san’s bone density or bone structure, yeah, that’s still completely beyond me......","A- Anyway, as expected of such a massive bookstore, there really is an unbelievable variety of magazines.","< Monthly Maid Fashion >","......Yeah, this section would be a den of madness, isn’t it?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [A magazine called Maid Fashion...... That naturally implies there are probably all sorts of maid-related magazines out there. And it’s also safe to assume that Ein is somehow involved in this.]","? ? ? : [Well, that’s true, but...... Marie-san and the others are in the Imperial Capital right now, aren’t they?]","Serious-senpai : [......Ah.]"]},{"number":2411,"title":"Chapter 2411: Spreading Aftermath 12","paragraphs":["As expected of a massive bookstore, there were all sorts of sections besides the magazine area, and countless books that caught my eye; before I knew it, I’d ended up buying quite a lot.","I guess the thought that I didn’t know when I’d next come here made me want to pick up the rarer ones while I could.","That said, I couldn’t help but notice an absurd amount of maid-related books. For example, in the Cooking Recipe section, there was a book titled <The Culinary Arts of a First-Class Maid>, and in the section about tea, there was one called <The Refinement of a Maid – Tea Edition>. I even spotted titles like <Cleaning Techniques As Taught by Maids>.","Well, that much is still fine...... no, it’s not fine, but at least it’s within the realm of understanding. However, when I saw that there was <The History of Maids> sitting in the history section, or a massive exam prep book for something called Maidology, supposedly covering the test to become a maid, or combat-related books like <Maid-Style Fluid Movements> and <Combat Techniques Suited for Maid Uniforms>, I couldn’t help having a very complicated expression on my face.","I mean seriously, why does every single genre have its own independent maid category? That’s terrifying. The Maid World is an outright abyss.","When it comes to maid-related matters, I can almost feel my sense of normality being eroded away...... Wait, hold on. I’ve already moved to this world, haven’t I? Which means that, in practice, this world’s version of \"maids\" will eventually become my new normal huh...... that’s a really unpleasant thought.","A- Anyway, for now, I’ll just deal with this by pretending not to see anything about maid culture. If Lilia-san herself is uninformed about maid-related stuff, or chooses not to be, it should be a world I don’t need to get involved with.","Well, the problem is that in my case, it’s the Maid World that keeps approaching me...... mainly because of Ein-san, but still......","Thinking about all that, I left the store and stored the books I’d bought into my magic box. This wasn’t unique to this store, but generally, taking out your magic box inside was forbidden to prevent shoplifting.","There were exceptions though, if you’d bought a lot, you could tell the cashier, \"I’ll be taking these home in my magic box\", and pack them then. Basically, it was fine at checkout, but not anywhere else inside.","[......Three o’clock huh......]","I murmured, glancing at the time. Still plenty of time left. Since I was already out in the Imperial Capital of the Archlesia Empire...... maybe I should stop by a monster pet goods store too?","Archlesia Empire was famous for its monster races, so there were far more people who kept monsters as pets compared to other countries, and the specialty shops were well stocked.","Of course, I like to think I’ve gathered only the best gear for Bell and Lynn, but just like Victor Trading Company’s special brush, there are still plenty of items I don’t know about.","Visiting pet goods shops is actually pretty fun; you sometimes find clever little gadgets or interesting new products.","Recently, I even bought a moisturizing cream for the paw pads of beast-type pets. Bell has paw pads too, and she loves that cream, often begging for it herself.","Though honestly, in Bell’s case...... I think she sees the whole \"applying cream to her paws\" part less as skincare and more as playtime with me. For her, the moisturizing cream seems to be like a ball or frisbee is for a dog. Basically, a toy.","So, even though she’s the one asking for it, she tends to wriggle around a lot while I’m applying it, playing the entire time, making it pretty hard to spread evenly...... but well, she’s so cute that I can’t possibly complain......","I’d been to the monster pet supply store several times before, so I knew exactly where it was and walked there without hesitation.","After a while, I entered a street lined with luxury shops, meaning my destination was close. As expected, keeping a monster as a pet wasn’t something just anyone could afford, so the monster pet supply store was located in a high-end shopping district. This area seemed to cater mostly to the nobility, with upscale stores everywhere.","Particularly in Archlesia Empire, the influence of the nobility was apparently very strong. Even in districts like this, the level of refinement and extravagance seemed to exceed that of the Symphonia Kingdom...... Unn?","As I casually looked around at the shops along the way, I suddenly spotted a familiar figure. Standing in front of a luxury clothing boutique, pacing back and forth with a somewhat hesitant look, was Marie-san.","I had no idea why Marie-san was in the Imperial Capital, but from the look of it...... she’d probably come to buy clothes, only to be overwhelmed by the intimidating aura of a high-end store, unable to bring herself to go inside...... Well, since I happened to see her, I might as well go over and say hello.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [So, if Baron Ritch isn’t around and it’s just Marie, that probably means something happened after the exchange at the temple, Baron Ritch went somewhere else, and Marie came here alone to buy clothes with the money she got huh? I guess the details about that will be revealed next time? Anyway...... looks like we’ve got some follow-up on that after all......]"]},{"number":2412,"title":"Chapter 2412: Spreading Aftermath 13","paragraphs":["The story turns back a little in time, Marie had been at the temple with her father, Baron Ritch, listening to Elune speak, both of them somewhat dazed and overwhelmed. To be honest, even as she listened, Marie found the whole thing so unreal that she could hardly keep up with what was being said.","Of course, she wasn’t the only one confused. Strengthening their Divine Protection would bring tremendous benefits, yes, but it would also essentially announce to the world that the Ritch Barony had an unusually close relationship with the Gods, which made Baron Ritch want to hold his head in his hands when he thought about the future.","However, this wasn’t a proposal, it was a settled matter...... It was, in a sense, a gesture of goodwill from the God Realm itself from the Supreme God, Life. Refusal wasn’t an option. Not only was it unthinkable to reject a God, but even if refusal were possible, doing so would surely lead to other nobles accusing them of disrespecting the Gods, followed by a storm of criticism. Either way, the outcome would have been the same.","[The range extends to here on the map, is that acceptable? Strengthening my Divine Protection over this area should greatly increase the harvests and yields.]","[Y- Y- Y- Yes. That’s perfectly fine.]","At the very least, setting aside matters of social balance and relations with other noble houses, there was no doubt this was nothing but gain for the Ritch Barony.","Ripples were already in surplus as it were, but given the recent trends, both Baron Ritch and Marie could easily predict that sales would likely rise. Increased crop yields were a welcome boon for the future...... even if they didn’t particularly want to think about that future right now......","[Oh, and this isn’t part of the Divine Protection itself...... but God of Earth-sama has also agreed to assist in this matter. She will make a few adjustments to the soil within that area within my Divine Protection. However, since this isn’t part of my Divine Protection, the effect won’t remain permanently, the condition of the soil could change later depending on environmental factors, so please keep that in mind.]","[Y- Yesh......]","For Marie, the one true mercy in all of this was that her father, Baron Ritch, was here with her. As head of the house, all direct dealings with Elune fell to him, meaning Marie herself wasn’t responsible for handling any of it, something for which she was profoundly grateful.","Watching her father bow and scrape with such humility, she even found herself thinking how lucky she was not to be the heir.","After discussing a few remaining details...... like the timing of the Divine Protection’s enhancement, the meeting concluded. Thereupon, Elune turned toward Marie and spoke to her directly.","[......Changing the subject a bit, Marie-san, I notice you haven’t received a Blessing yet, have you?]","[Ah, y- yes, I- I’m terribly sorry, w- we haven’t had the financial means......]","[Oh no, I’m not reprimanding you. Blessings aren’t something anyone is forced to receive...... However, since you’re a friend of Miyama-san’s, it would be unfortunate if you were to fall ill unexpectedly. Even the Blessing of a low-ranking God has the power to ward off sickness. Allow me to bestow upon you a Provisional Blessing.]","[Eh?]","[I- If that’s the case, then please, allow us to pay the proper fee......]","Marie stared blankly in disbelief as Elune offered to give her a Provisional Blessing. Baron Ritch began to say he would pay the standard amount, but Elune shook her head.","[No, to take money after I was the one to suggest it would be beneath my honor. Payment is unnecessary...... Marie-san, I grant you the Blessing of Fertility......]","[ ! ? T- Thank you very much. I- I- I- I am honored beyond words.]","[There will also be no need for you to pay for Provisional Blessings in the future. When the New Year comes, please come to the temple along with the others receiving Provisional Blessings.]","Once again struck by the sheer influence of being Kaito’s friend, Marie found herself swept along in the current of events like a leaf in a raging river. Her and Baron Ritch’s visit to the temple thus came to an end, and the two of them emerged outside, utterly exhausted.","Originally, as they had discussed on the way there, they were supposed to go buy some formal clothes for Marie afterward...... but as soon as they stepped out of the temple, they noticed a luxurious carriage waiting nearby.","[......That crest...... could it be the Hamilton Marquisdom’s?]","As Baron Ritch tilted his head at the sight of the crest engraved on the carriage, the maid waiting in front of it approached him and Marie, offering a polite bow before speaking.","[Master wishes to speak with you regarding this matter and the future, if you would be so kind as to accompany us.]","[A- Ahh, I see...... That’s a relief, actually. I had been hoping to consult Marquis Hamilton as soon as possible.]","It seemed Marquis Hamilton had already learned that Baron Ritch and Marie had been summoned to the Temple of Fertility, and had sent for them to discuss the matter. For Baron Ritch, this was a welcome turn of events...... he knew well that such matters were far beyond his experience, and he would be unable to properly plan for what lay ahead on his own. Having the chance to seek the Marquis’s counsel was a godsend.","But then, Baron Ritch glanced at the daughter beside him. From the look of her, the conversation with Elune had taken quite a toll on her nerves, she looked mentally exhausted. The father in him couldn’t help but show concern.","[......However, I must apologize. My daughter is tired, so I’ll attend the meeting alone. Marie, I’ll go speak with Marquis Hamilton. You should go buy your dress on the noble street. I’ll give you the money.]","[U- Understood. Thank you very much, Father.]","[In that case, allow me to have the carriage take you to the shopping district. Shall I also arrange for an escort?]","[Ah, no, that won’t be necessary. I don’t usually have escorts with me anyway.]","The Ritch Barony was too poor a noble house to afford personal guards, and except for the eldest son and daughter, the younger children all had at least basic self-defense training. Marie, too, could at least run away swiftly if something happened.","Besides, she was only going to a street lined with high-end shops, a safe and well-patrolled area, so there was no real need for guards.","[Very well then, Marie. Once I’m finished, I’ll contact you via hummingbird. If you have time after buying your clothes, go to a café and treat yourself to something sweet. I’ll give you more than enough money, so don’t hesitate to use it all and relax a little.]","[Father...... thank you.]","And so, Marie set off on her own, heading toward the avenue of luxury shops to buy her new clothes.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see, a father’s compassion, trying to spare his daughter from any further stomachache...... truly beautiful, deeply moving...... And yet, as a result, he ended up throwing his daughter alone into the Imperial Capital, a place haunted by that stomachache monster known to have \"100% chance of running into acquaintances\"...... What a cruel irony.]"]},{"number":2413,"title":"Chapter 2413 - Spreading Aftermath 14","paragraphs":["It was an accidental encounter, but when I saw Marie-san, looking just a little bit uneasy...... or rather, visibly intimidated by the aura of the high-class store, I decided to call out to her and approached.","I hadn’t come to the pet shop with any particular item in mind to buy; it was more like I had some free time and figured, why not stop by? So, changing plans wasn’t a problem at all.","[......Hello, Marie-san.]","[ ! ? Eh? Ah, K- Kaito-sama!? Why are you in a place like this......? Ah, pardon me. Good day to you, Kaito-sama.]","[Sorry for surprising you. I came to the bookstore on the main street, but after finishing my shopping, I had some extra time and decided to wander around a bit. That’s when I happened to see you...... Marie-san, are you here to buy clothes?]","While greeting Marie-san, I turned my gaze toward the shop in front of us...... it was a store that dealt in clothing for nobles. So, assuming she was here for that, I asked, and after taking a deep breath to steady herself, Marie-san replied.","[Yes. I was originally supposed to come with my father, but he had another task in hand, so I came alone...... However, it’s rather embarrassing to admit, but up until now, all my clothes have been hand-me-downs from my sisters, and I’ve hardly ever bought anything myself. We don’t have such high-end noble shops in our territory either...... so, well, I came here, but I haven’t quite worked up the nerve to step inside yet......]","[Ah, I understand completely. Before I came to this world, I was basically what you’d call a commoner here, so I had no connection to fancy stores...... Walking into one that just radiates luxury definitely takes courage. Well, these days I’ve gotten pretty used to it, one way or another......]","[Kaito-sama as well...... Yes, it really does bring up all sorts of anxieties, like whether I’ll be able to properly respond when the staff approaches me inside.]","I completely understand how she felt. There’s just something about luxury shops, a unique atmosphere that makes you tense up when you walk in for the first time.","Thankfully, I’ve been rather well-off in this world, and I’ve had several opportunities to visit high-end stores. By now, I’ve gotten used to it, but in the beginning, I really wanted someone to come along with me. In fact, Lilia-san often accompanied me when I went shopping back then.","[......By the way, since you came all the way to the Imperial Capital to shop, you must be buying something quite expensive, right? Are you attending a party or something?]","[Ah, no, nothing like that...... It’s true that I came to buy some fine clothes, but not for a party. I just wanted attire that wouldn’t seem disrespectful when meeting people of high status.]","[......I see......]","......Wait, hold on. Could this actually be my fault? A while back, I talked with Akane-san and found out that the whole situation around the Ritch Barony had become far more impressive than I’d ever imagined......","For example, there’s the case with Rasal-san, but if there were others introduced by Raz-san who took an interest in the Ritch Barony’s ripples, then the person they’d contact...... would likely be Marie-san.","And Raz-san would probably mention that Marie-san is a friend of mine, too......","[......Um, Marie-san. Could it be, this is because I recommended it to so many people......?]","[......Ah, no, well, it’s true that it’s related to that, but it’s not a bad thing! The Ritch Barony is happy that ripple sales have increased, and I did send extra ripples to Kaito-sama, hoping you might recommend it to others...... It’s just that, well, I was a little thoughtless, or maybe too naive...... Since our connections have expanded in that direction, there are now times when I need to attend meetings together with my father, so I thought I should have proper attire for such occasions......]","......Yeah, this is totally my fault! Marie-san was kind enough to phrase it gently so I wouldn’t feel guilty, but it’s clear that she now needs expensive clothes because of me.","For that talk about the Lord Trading Company and such, it doesn’t feel like she’d be there discussing things like teleportation gates with them. More likely, it’s that when she accompanies her father to meet notable people connected to Rasal-san or Raz-san, she needs to dress appropriately for the occasion.","[Ah, um, how should I say this...... I’m really sorry.]","[P- Please don’t apologize! You’ve done nothing wrong, Kaito-sama. On the contrary, for me, it’s actually a fortunate coincidence. I get the chance to buy some fine clothes for myself, which I rarely can, so in a way, I’m the one gaining from this. I’ve always admired how other noble ladies dress elegantly, but with my family’s finances, my older brother and sister had to be prioritized, so this is an unexpected happiness that’s fallen into my lap.]","[I- I see. Well, if that’s how you feel, I’m glad......]","Even so, I couldn’t shake off the feeling of guilt toward Marie-san, nor the urge to make it up to her somehow...... And right now, we were standing in front of a clothing store, I had plenty of free time, and she was clearly nervous about entering a high-end shop for the first time...... hmm.","[......Marie-san, if you don’t mind, as a small token of apology...... would you let me buy you a dress? I know you said not to worry about it, but I still feel bad. And since we happened to run into each other like this, maybe it’s fate or something......]","[T- That’s far too generous, but...... u- um, still, I’m very grateful for the thought. And if it’ll put your mind at ease, Kaito-sama...... well, the truth is, I was nervous about going into this store alone...... In that case, may I accept your offer?]","[Yes, of course.]","When I told her I wanted to buy her a dress as an apology, Marie-san thought of it for a moment, but in the end, she agreed. For her, having someone accompany her into a store she had been hesitant to enter alone must have sounded quite appealing, and I had to admit, for an idea I came up with on the spot, it turned out to be a pretty good one.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Alright, let’s think this through. Setting aside the rank or price of the clothing, walking into a noble-exclusive boutique together with a noble lady and saying “I’d like to buy her a dress as a gift”...... That’s a situation where anyone watching would assume you’re lovers or something. And there’s a fair chance other nobles could be in the store too...... At this rate, Marie’s name will spread across the social circles in no time.]","? ? ? : [Yeah, Marie-san really gives off that air of inexperience. Unlike Eris-san or Cornelia-san, she hasn’t spent much time in social settings, so she doesn’t think about how other nobles might perceive her or what kind of rumors might spread. Though, maybe she’s just too mentally drained to think that far right now......]"]},{"number":2414,"title":"Chapter 2414: Spreading Aftermath 15","paragraphs":["When I entered the shop together with Marie-san, I was immediately struck by how spacious it was, truly fitting for a high-class establishment. Unlike the clothing stores I’d been to several times before in the Symphonia Kingdom, this one seemed to specialize exclusively in women’s attire. There wasn’t a single piece of men’s clothing in sight; the staff and other customers were almost entirely women as well. The few men I did spot were clearly there accompanying women, just like me.","At a glance, it looked like each group of customers was personally attended by a staff member who guided them around the store, giving off an unmistakable air of a boutique for nobles. Soon, a neatly dressed female clerk, looking sharp in what resembled a tailored suit, approached us and bowed politely.","[Thank you for visiting.]","[I’d like to buy some clothes for her......]","[Certainly. May I ask about your budget?]","[......Let’s see...... errr......]","Ah, I see, so that’s how it usually works...... You tell them how much you’re willing to spend, and then they guide you to the section with clothes in that price range, assisting you with your selection......","Now then, how much should I say? After all that confident talk earlier about being familiar with such things and insisting on buying Marie-san a gift, it’s hard to turn around now and ask \"How much should we spend on your clothes?\". Besides, if I did ask, she’d probably get all modest and suggest something way cheaper than what would actually be appropriate.","And just a glance to the side showed Marie-san looking completely intimidated by the luxurious atmosphere of the store, so much so that even if I asked her, she probably wouldn’t be able to respond properly. Clearly, this was something I needed to decide on myself.","As for how much noble clothing usually costs, thankfully, I had some reference from past experience.","Before the Six Kings Festival, I went shopping for clothes with Lilia-san, and the outfit she bought then wasn’t as flashy as formal wear or a party gown, but still carried a definite sense of elegance and refinement. I figured it would be similar to what Marie-san would want this time.","Back then, I’d given Lilia-san a set of clothes as a gift, so I remembered how much it cost.","......But I’m not stupid. Lilia-san is the head of a Duchy, while Marie-san is a Baron’s daughter. If I used Lilia-san’s outfit as a reference, I’d likely end up with something far more expensive than Marie-san would ever expect.","Fortunately, by coincidence, Sieg-san was also at that same store back then...... and I’d bought her an outfit as well, so I knew how much that one cost too.","Sieg-san, while making a decent living, was still a commoner, whereas Marie-san is a noble. Therefore, clothes for her should naturally be of a higher price range than the ones Sieg-san bought back then.","In other words, the price range suitable for Marie-san would be one higher than the clothes bought for Sieg-san, yet lower than those bought for Lilia-san.","......Well, the only issue is that the price gap between those two is huge. Lilia-san’s outfit was 90,000R...... about nine million yen, while Sieg-san’s was 15,000R...... around one and a half million yen. With such a big range, figuring out the right balance was tricky.","At first glance, you’d think splitting the difference at around 50,000R would work nicely...... but from experience, that kind of middle-ground choice usually backfires. So instead, I figured it’d be better to err on the lower side, closer to Sieg-san’s price range.","I’d watch both the clerk’s and Marie-san’s reactions, and use my Sympathy Magic too...... and if it seemed off, I could always adjust the number.","[......Not including accessories, about three gold coins for just the clothes, please.]","[ ! ? ! ? ]","[Certainly. Right this way please.]","When I told them my estimated price, five gold coins, or 50,000 R......then reduced it by nearly half to three gold coins, or 30,000 R...... the clerk didn’t show any particular reaction and simply bowed. Marie-san looked momentarily surprised, but her expression quickly returned to normal, and the emotions conveyed through Sympathy Magic also seemed to have calmed down, so it's probably fine, right?","Judging from her reaction, maybe two gold coins would’ve been just right...... but oh well. At least, I didn’t sense any feelings of \"that’s wrong but I can’t correct him\" or that kind of reserved hesitation from her, so while it might have been a bit higher than what she’d expected, it was likely still within a range she could accept.","[......Must've misheard...... that three silver coins...... I must've misheard......]","Completely convinced I’d named a reasonable amount, I failed to catch Marie-san's faint mutterings quietly trying to convince herself otherwise.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Oh ho, this time, for once, it seems Kaito actually made a well-thought-out, reasonable decision instead of his usual impulsive ones, he carefully calculated the amount based on solid reasoning but...... something about this feels off. What went wrong here, Commentator ???-san?]","? ? ? : [He picked the wrong examples to reference. What Kaito-san should have used as a reference here was the price from when he went with his two kouhais to buy clothes for Seigi-san’s wedding. If he’d gone with that, things would’ve been fine...... After all, the time he went shopping with Lilia-san was during the first ever Six Kings Festival, when Lilia, as a Duchess, had been personally invited by all five of the Six Kings to attend the final day’s grand banquet. She was buying clothes befitting that level of attention, so those were even more expensive than your standard party dresses to begin with.]","Serious-senpai : [Hohouu......]","? ? ? : [And while using Sieg-san’s clothes as a reference wasn’t a bad idea, Kaito-san completely forgot one crucial detail: the outfit he bought for Sieg-san back then was the one Sieg-san herself saw the price of and said \"That’s way too expensive, I can’t accept that\". In other words, it far exceeded what Sieg-san had actually expected to spend.]","Serious-senpai : [......So, it’s bad huh?]","? ? ? : [For reference, the amount Baron Ritch gave Marie, telling her \"It’s okay to use all of this\", was five silver coins.]","Serious-senpai : [Oh......]"]},{"number":2415,"title":"Chapter 2415: Spreading Aftermath 16","paragraphs":["Marie is the fourth daughter of the Barony, and since she is neither an heir nor in line for succession, she rarely appears in social gatherings. Although Baron Ritch does differentiate among his heirs, he loves all his children equally, so occasionally she is allowed to attend less formal parties. Still, her position is such that she could never dream of interacting with influential people, and her experience is overwhelmingly lacking.","......Yes, to put it bluntly, Marie’s mental capacity had already been thoroughly exceeded the moment she faced Elune, and even though it concerned her own affairs, it all felt like an unreal, dreamlike state.","Even now, to escape the pressure of such intense mental strain, she unconsciously avoided thinking about difficult matters, keeping her thoughts somewhat optimistic.","(......As expected of a high-end store favored by the nobility. Was that a Countess over there? I’m not very familiar with the nobles' faces, so I can’t say for sure, but being able to come to a clothing store I’d always thought I’d never have access to is, after all, a little thrilling. Though perhaps I’m a bit too nervous, I thought I heard Kaito-sama say the budget was \"three gold coins\". Fufufu, it’s embarrassing that I was so surprised when I should have realized it was ridiculous with just a little thought. After all, that kind of amount is for dresses that high-ranking noble daughters wear for special parties on commemorative occasions, not for someone like me, the fourth daughter of a Barony.)","Her sense of money is closer to that of a commoner than a noble, and since she usually wears her sisters’ hand-me-downs, anything costing gold coins is far beyond her expectations.","Thus, she had convinced herself that the budget Kaito mentioned was three silver coins...... or rather, it could be said she was desperately averting her eyes from reality.","If she thought about it rationally...... a gift of clothing from someone who had previously sent her a teleportation magic tool in return for ripples...... could it really be contained within such a modest budget?","But no matter how much she avoided reality, the time would come when she had to face it...... and so, when the shop assistant presented the candidate dresses, she had no choice but to confront reality.","[This dress, while having a generally calm design, features decorations made with a special thread called Stardrop, which sparkles as it catches the light.]","[Hehh, it’s beautiful.]","[I- I- I- Indeed. It's certainly dazzling.]","Kaito remarked on the dress’s sparkling effect under the light, and Marie, flustered, nodded while her eyes darted around.","(......Stardrop? W- Wait a minute. I heard about it from Elder Sister...... Isn’t it a super-high-end thread that easily exceeds the cost of an ordinary dress, even for just a few meters? And they’ve used so much of it...... N- No, that means, no matter how I think about it, this can’t possibly be measured in silver coins...... E- Ehhh?)","Yes, that’s the issue. The dress brought by the shop assistant was, quite literally, on a completely different scale from what Marie had imagined.","To Marie, it was the kind of clothing that could only be seen in magazines or admired on display in stores, a class of dress that should not exist within her reach.","[It's just, if it’s too flashy, I suppose it might not suit Marie-san's purpose, wouldn't it?]","[T- T- T- That's right. Something of calmer colors would be better......]","[In that case, how about this one? We focused on the texture, with a calm color palette and design.]","[Ah, t- this is nice. The colors are subdued, and......]","The next dress the shop assistant presented was a set of top and long skirt with a balanced, subdued tone, giving off elegance without being flashy or overly dress-like, matching Marie’s taste.","Feeling that it had a good atmosphere, Marie accepted the outfit, but inside, she was once again deeply flustered.","(......No, umm, the texture is unbelievable...... Isn't the material used for this thing clearly not ordinary? It’s so soft and pleasant that I want to keep touching it, and it’s incredibly light...... And looking closely, the quality of the material is obviously......)","Unlike the previous dress, which was visibly dazzling, she could understand by touch that this one was still clearly far above ordinary clothing.","[Would you like to try it on?]","[......Ehh? Ah, y- yes.]","Once again, Marie’s capacity had long since been exceeded. In her confusion, she couldn’t properly think through her answer, so she simply went along with it and began to try the outfit on.","Fortunately, the size seemed to fit, so changing was smooth...... but once she wore it, she realized even more clearly just how incredibly high-end it was.","(Amazing. The texture is incredible...... Eh? How much is this? I can tell it’s an unbelievably good dress, but with my knowledge, I have no idea about the price...... But then again, in this situation where Kaito-sama is purchasing it, would it be rude for me to ask the price? Ah no, and it’s not like it’s even decided that I’m buying it......)","Having finished trying it on, she stepped out of the fitting room, and Kaito smiled as he spoke.","[It suits you very well. The subdued color palette seems to match you, Marie-san.]","[Yes, indeed. A gentle and refined young lady like you looks best in calm, elegant clothing.]","Following Kaito’s praise, the female shop assistant also complimented her with a smile, but Marie forced a somewhat strained smile in response, unable to fully express her feelings.","(Praise like this, I’ve never heard in my life...... I’m not particularly beautiful, so I feel like the dress is completely outshining me...... N-no, more importantly, I want to know the price of this dress. Kaito-sama! Please! Just one sentence, one simple question!!! Ask the shop assistant \"How much is this dress?\". I can’t calm my mind if I’m wearing something so obviously high-end without knowing the price......)","Of course, her wish went unfulfilled. Kaito didn’t ask about the price and simply listened attentively to the shop assistant’s explanation of the dress.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I think Marie’s sense of money is probably about the same level as Kaori’s, but Kaito seems to be estimating her level much higher just because \"she’s a noble\", right? Her lack of experience with nobility is backfiring...... Wait, this guy, the nobles he interacts with most were high-ranking ones like the Head of her Duchy, the heir of Marquisdom, and even a Prince, right!?]","? ? ? : [It’s the same with titled ranks, but somehow, Kaito-san tends to become close with people starting from the highest ranks first. The Hamilton Marquisdom is one of the largest noble families in the Archlesia Empire, and the Sharon County is among the top domestically in terms of wealth...... On the other hand, the Ritch Barony might be considered a rare exception.]"]},{"number":2416,"title":"Chapter 2416: Spreading Aftermath 17","paragraphs":["Marie tried on several outfits, but the one that felt the best to her was the one with a soft texture and a calm design. Or rather, it would be more accurate to say that it seemed like the safest choice.","On the other hand, the fact that the design didn’t have any features that clearly looked expensive might mean that the material itself was of high quality, something only those with an eye for it would recognize.","(......Kaito-sama doesn’t seem interested in asking about the price at all...... Is this how shopping at luxury stores usually goes? Well, he did mention the budget amount at the start, so I suppose he already knows it’s within that range. Maybe it’s just my lack of experience that makes me unsure about these things.)","For Marie, this was her first time shopping in a luxury store, and she was completely feeling her way through it. Seeing Kaito talking with the clerk in a fairly relaxed manner, she convinced herself that this must be normal.","For the moment, she decided to try on once more the clothing with the calm design she liked best so far. Just as the discussion began to move toward purchasing that outfit, the clerk opened her mouth to speak.","[Of course, even as it is, I believe this outfit already highlights the young lady’s beauty perfectly. However, since the overall design is on the modest side, adding a decorative piece as a focal point would enhance the balance even more. I would recommend a brooch, for example, what do you think?]","[Ah, right, accessories would definitely be nice too. Could you prepare a few options that might go well with this?]","Regarding that exchange as well, Marie assumed that was simply how things went...... buying clothes together with accessories as a set. Now that the outfit had been chosen, moving on to accessories seemed like a natural next step.","[Certainly. May I ask if there is an upper limit to your budget for the accessories?]","[Ah, errr...... not really.]","In this case, it was just Kaito lacking in experience. Unlike with the clothes, he didn’t have any past example to reference, so he decided to simply leave it up to the clerk’s judgment.","Besides, since accessories were separate from clothing, he reasoned that noble-grade accessories would naturally be expensive, and that it would be appropriate for them to be so. Thus, he didn’t set any upper limit.","(No limit!? N- No, Kaito-sama!? I- If you say that, won’t they bring out something ridiculously expensive...... A- Although, maybe they’ll pick something that suits the outfit’s style and stay in the same price range?)","Although she was surprised when Kaito declared there was no upper limit, Marie, inexperienced as she was, convinced herself \"that must simply be how things worked\", and waited, somewhat optimistically.","......At least, until the clerk returned carrying something that, even to Marie’s untrained eyes, was clearly going to be outrageously priced.","[......As expected, since the overall design of the outfit is calm, a brighter, more brilliant accessory would make for a nice contrast. This here is a brooch set with a large Crimson Ruby. When worn at the chest, it tightens the overall impression beautifully......]","Seeing the ruby brooch resting on an obviously luxurious display stand, Marie felt the blood drain from her face.","(......That gem is far too big!? It’s nearly half the size of my palm!? A- And did she say Crimson Ruby!? If I remember correctly, Elder Sister has a Crimson Ruby necklace...... It’s her most expensive piece of jewelry. But the ruby on my sister’s necklace was small! The ruby on this brooch looks like a completely different species altogether......!)","When it came to the clothes, Marie had managed to stay somewhat optimistic. Her lack of knowledge meant she couldn’t properly gauge their value, so she’d forced herself to believe it was within her imagined price range.","But when it came to an accessory featuring a clearly enormous gemstone, it was a different story. Even to Marie’s eyes, this was obviously expensive...... far more so than the dress itself.","[If you’re going to wear it, it should go around here.]","[......That looks nice. Indeed, with that touch of red there, her overall image feels much sharper and more balanced.]","While Marie stood frozen in disbelief, the clerk had already attached the brooch. Seeing it, Kaito smiled in approval, clearly pleased with the result.","Noticing that expression and sensing that he was leaning toward buying it, Marie panicked internally, unable to figure out what she should do.","(Kaito-sama! Please ask the price!!! The words \"How much is this?\" are very important!!! When shopping, confirming the price is...... it’s...... ehhhh...... he’s not asking at all...... I- Is this normal!? Do true members of the upper class, unlike poor nobles like us, simply not bother asking about prices when they shop!?)","Marie wanted him to ask the price, or rather, she hoped that once he heard it, Kaito might decide not to buy it. But, as mentioned before, this was her first time shopping in a high-end store...... and seeing how smoothly the deal seemed to be proceeding, she didn’t have the courage to interrupt.","She began to wonder if, for truly wealthy people, this level of jewelry wasn’t even worth checking the price of.","In reality, Kaito was in a position where he had more wealth than he could possibly use. But more than that...... a brooch with a Crimson Ruby was genuinely a trivial expense to him.","In fact, he was familiar with gemstones far more valuable than that, and had even used an Astral Ruby, a gem rarer than the Crimson Ruby itself, as material for a custom-made accessory he’d gifted to Sieglinde. At this point, checking the price of such an item was truly unnecessary for him.","For Marie though, this was an entirely unknown world, and she could only watch silently as the discussion smoothly moved towards a conclusion she could no longer stop.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......The reason Kaito probably isn’t reacting to the large gem is that, for him, the standard for an \"expensive gemstone\" is something like Sela’s Midnight Diamond (the kind that costs dozens of white gold coins even uncut).]","? ? ? : [And next chapter, we’ll see the beginnings of Marie’s transformation into a Charge-Type Stomachache Warrior......]","Serious-senpai : [You’re still sending out pursuing attacks?]"]},{"number":2417,"title":"Chapter 2417: Spreading Aftermath 18","paragraphs":["While Marie was still bewildered, the conversation moved along, and in the end, it was decided that they would purchase both the dress and the brooch. Since Kaito never asked about the price, Marie watched the payment process with a tense expression.","Kaito took out a single platinum coin and placed it on the tray the clerk had prepared. Seeing that, a cold sweat ran down Marie’s back.","(W- White gold coin......! N No, calm down. It’s possible he just doesn’t have smaller change......)","Watching him pay with a white gold coin, Marie realized that the amount Kaito had initially offered was almost certainly not the three silver coins she had desperately hoped for, but rather three gold coins.","But that also meant she could more or less estimate the price of the enormous Crimson Ruby brooch based on the change he received.","Soon enough, the clerk returned with the tray and handed Kaito...... two gold coins.","(......Two gold coins as change...... meaning this brooch costs f- f- five gold coins...... I- I- I- I see...... A- Ahh, thank goodness. Since I’m the fourth daughter of a Barony with no connection to high-society parties, this won’t turn into one of those \"How dare a lower noble wear something so pretentious!\" situations...... really, what a relief...... A-Ah, wait, this wasn’t even a party dress. The dress was just...... clothes...... and the clothes cost gold coins...... Arehh?)","When faced with immense psychological stress...... stomach-churning levels of it, people’s reactions differ greatly. For example, though she’s now grown accustomed enough to endure it, Lilia used to faint outright in such situations.","Eris, on the other hand, relied on her noble pride and strong willpower, screaming inwardly while maintaining a perfect smile on the outside.","Cornelia, meanwhile, would try to postpone the issue, or bear with it like Eris, using various coping methods to reduce the strain, but if it became unbearable, she would briefly lose consciousness.","And in comparison to those three, Marie, lacking both experience and mental fortitude, responded to the crushing stomachache that assailed her by......","(......Ah, I see...... \"This is a dream\" huh!)","......escaping from reality.","(Of course it is, there’s no doubt about that...... There’s no way a poor Baron’s fourth daughter like me would ever receive such luxurious clothes and accessories as gifts. Well, I have always admired the elegant, glittering look of high-born ladies in fine dresses, so I suppose that longing has just made me dream something silly like this. Yes, that’s it. This is a dream. Definitely a dream......)","And unlike Cornelia, who would temporarily avert her eyes, Marie’s version was a full-force sprint away from reality itself, a wholehearted, desperate flight.","Of course, it was merely escapism; running away wouldn’t stop reality from catching up eventually. Sooner or later, it would overtake her, and all that accumulated pressure would come crashing down as overwhelming stomachache.","But until that happened, she would run with everything she had...... That was the unconscious decision of Marie Ritch.","(Since it’s a dream anyway...... and one that fulfills a secret wish I’ve held deep inside, I’d be wasting it if I didn’t enjoy it, right?)","And at that moment, a subtle change stirred within her heart.","[Kaito-sama, once again, thank you so very much. For someone like me, the fourth daughter of a Barony, to receive such fine attire is something that could never happen under normal circumstances...... But to be honest, I’ve always longed to wear beautiful dresses and elegant accessories. So even though I’m shamelessly indulging in your kindness, I’m truly happy that my little dream has become reality.]","First of all, it’s important to make clear that Marie hadn’t broken down under mental strain or anything like that. Rather, as a result of turning her eyes completely away from a reality that would otherwise cause her stress, she had entered what could be described as a kind of ultra-optimistic mindset.","At this moment, she was unconsciously protecting herself...... automatically shutting out any thoughts that might lead to stomach-churning anxiety...... In other words, she had entered what could only be called a temporary invincible mode, immune to psychological stress.","Because she had thoroughly purged all potentially stressful factors from her mind, what surfaced instead were only the pure joys, the happiness of receiving the luxurious clothes she had long admired, and the delight of being given such gifts of clothing and accessories by Kaito. With nothing but genuine feeling, she could express her gratitude from the heart.","............And that, in a sense...... created the worst possible combination.","For example, when Cornelia once went out with Kaito, there came a point where she could no longer keep up her composure. Kaito, sensing that through his Sympathy Magic, had been able to notice her distress and offer gentle consideration and support.","But Marie, in her current state, had automatically shut out all negative emotions. Thanks to her ultra-optimistic thinking, only joy and excitement were visible on the surface.","Kaito’s Sympathy Magic allowed him to read emotions carried through another’s magic power, but not their deeper thoughts.","In other words, there was no way for him to notice that Marie was escaping from reality. So when he saw her apparent delight, it was only natural for him to conclude that \"she’s really happy\".","And when someone expresses such pure happiness and gratitude, it’s only human to feel happy in return.","[......Marie-san, if you’d like, how about another dress? It might be good to have a spare or two.]","[That’s a very tempting offer for me, but wouldn’t that be a burden for you, Kaito-sama?]","[Not at all. Honestly, I’ve got more money than I know what to do with......]","[I feel awful for constantly relying on your kindness, but...... if Kaito-sama insists...... actually, among the ones I tried on, there was another outfit that caught my eye......]","Even at this sudden suggestion, Marie, utterly convinced this was a dream and thinking that since it was a dream, she might as well enjoy it to the fullest, accepted Kaito’s generosity after a light exchange between them.","......But one mustn’t forget. She was merely running from reality. Sooner or later, the time would come when she would regain her calm...... when reality would catch up, and she would awaken from the dream.","And when that happened, all the emotional debts she had unconsciously deferred would come crashing down upon her in the form of stomach-wrenching agony...... But for now, unaware of any of that, Marie simply smiled brightly, overjoyed by Kaito’s kindness.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Oi, you idiot! Wait, Marie! Stop!!! You’re running full speed into danger as a result of escaping from reality!? So that’s what a Charge-type means...... Once the stress exceeds a certain threshold, you enter that so-called invincible mode, a \"Fully Automatic Postponement State\", and then all the accumulated stomachache hits you all at once later on......]"]},{"number":2418,"title":"Chapter 2418: Spreading Aftermath 19","paragraphs":["The guilt of knowing I was the cause of all this still lingered, but when I offered to buy Marie-san some clothes, an idea that came to me on a whim, she was genuinely delighted, and that, in turn, put me at ease.","The accessories turned out to be more expensive than I’d expected, and I worried the high price might make her feel uncomfortable. But thankfully, that didn’t seem to be the case, she accepted them with pure joy.","For Marie-san, the fourth daughter of a Barony, shopping in stores like this or owning fine clothing was something she rarely experienced. When she spoke of how much she had longed for it, her expression overflowed with happiness, and I couldn’t help but suggest buying her another outfit as well. She was delighted by that too, of which I was truly glad to oblige.","[Ahh, excuse me. I’d like to have the clothes sent to my home, if possible......]","[Arehh? Marie-san, aren’t you going to put them in your Magic Box?]","This time, since the outfit didn’t need to be tailored precisely to her body like a party dress would, and since they already had her size in stock, there was no need for alterations. She could have just taken it home directly, but it seemed Marie-san preferred to have it sent to her Barony instead.","[I’m embarrassed to admit it, but the Magic Box I own only has the capacity of a small wardrobe. Considering what I already keep inside, there isn’t much room left. I thought I’d store only the accessories in it and have the clothes sent separately......]","[I see...... Ah, in that case, I actually have something that might help. Would you like to use this?]","Hearing Marie-san’s concern about her limited Magic Box capacity, I took out a deep green, square-shaped magic crystal, a Magic Box, from my own.","[A Magic Box...... and quite a fine one at that. Forgive me, but I’m a little surprised to see you with one that color, Kaito-sama. I had assumed all of yours would be made from black magic crystals.]","[Ahh, that’s because this one actually wasn’t something I bought...... Errr, are you familiar with the Hydra Kingdom’s Founding Festival’s Water Dragon Parade and its prize lottery?]","[Yes, if I remember right, the ticket numbers themselves are the lottery numbers, and the winners are announced later, correct?]","[Exactly. And this Magic Box was actually one of the prizes I won in that lottery.]","Yes, the Magic Box I’d won in the Sea Dragon Parade’s ticket lottery had a decent capacity, about the size of a small one-room apartment. If you were to buy one, it would probably cost around a white gold coin, making it a remarkably luxurious prize for what was essentially a bonus raffle attached to the tickets. Well, it was the grand prize, after all......","That said, to be honest, it was kind of an awkward item for me, a little difficult to make use of.","[As Marie-san said, I already own Magic Boxes with larger capacity. And if I were ever to buy another, I’d definitely choose a black one again. Besides, all my acquaintances already have ones even larger than this. So I never really found a use for it, it’s just been sitting untouched inside one of my other Magic Boxes ever since.]","A Magic Box’s capacity isn’t determined by the purity of its magic crystal, but by the magic formula inscribed within it. Of course, creating a complex formula that grants a large capacity requires a considerable amount of magic power, so in practice, a high-purity crystal is needed. Still, even with crystals of identical purity, the final size of the box can differ depending on the formula used.","That part depends on the skill of the craftsman. For example, even if two Magic Boxes are made from black crystals, the one crafted by Sechs-san and the one made by Kuro would differ greatly in capacity.","And that’s also where the problem lies. Even if I asked Tre-san to replace this deep green crystal with a black one, the inscribed formula wouldn’t change, meaning its capacity would stay the same.","On top of that, erasing and rewriting a magic formula once it’s been engraved into a crystal takes a lot of effort and time. At that point, it’s far easier to just buy a new crystal and make a new Magic Box from scratch.","What’s more, all of my acquaintances already own Magic Boxes larger than this one, so I couldn’t really give it away to anyone...... And as for me, if I ever needed more capacity, I’d just add another black one to my collection. So this one honestly had no purpose, and I’d been wondering what to do with it.","[......Anyway, since it’s just been gathering dust, I’d be happy if you used it instead, Marie-san. It’s better for someone to put it to good use than for it to sit forgotten in storage.]","[I’m truly happy to accept it...... but I feel bad, receiving so much from you. I’m very grateful for your kindness, Kaito-sama, but please, allow me to offer something in return......]","Though she looked a bit apologetic, Marie-san accepted the Magic Box without hesitation. Honestly, I preferred it that way, it really was something I didn’t know what to do with, so there was no need for her to feel guilty. But after thinking for a moment, she seemed to come up with an idea.","[......Ah, that’s right. Actually, my father gave me a little extra allowance today, saying that after buying clothes, I should treat myself to some sweets at a café. If it’s convenient for Kaito-sama, would you care to join me afterward? I didn’t end up spending the money I’d set aside for clothing, so please let me treat you, as a small token of thanks. I know it doesn’t come close to matching what you’ve given me, but......]","[That’s not true at all. In that case, I’ll gladly take you up on the offer.]","Indeed, after receiving two outfits, accessories, and even a Magic Box, it was only natural that Marie-san would want to repay me in some small way, and since I had no reason to refuse, I decided to graciously accept her kindness.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......She’s actively stacking additional stomachache charges on herself...... Baron Ritch, your daughter’s speeding headfirst into a death zone, if you don’t realize it soon, things are going to get really bad for you too! And from Kaito’s side, it just looks like a calm, ordinary exchange, so there’s no way for him to notice...... When reality finally catches up later, her stomach is probably going to cease to exist......]"]},{"number":2419,"title":"Chapter 2419: Spreading Aftermath 20","paragraphs":["In the end, to thank Kaito for buying her so many things, Marie invited him to a café. Kaito readily agreed, and the two of them walked a short distance from the clothing store to one nearby.","Of course, being located in the upscale shopping district, the café was also a high-class establishment. However, even there, the cost of tea for two would never exceed the amount of money Marie currently carried.","After entering the café, they sat facing each other and placed their orders. Once that was done, Kaito suddenly spoke as if something had just occurred to him.","[......Come to think of it, Marie-san, did you come to the Imperial Capital with your father to buy clothes? Or were you here for something else and just shopping on the side?]","[Yes, our original purpose was to visit the temple of the Goddess of Fertility. Once that was done, we decided to shop as well.]","[The temple? So, it wasn’t for prayer or anything like that, was it?]","Kaito tilted his head curiously at her words. During their previous tea party, he had learned that Marie rarely visited the Imperial Capital. It seemed unlikely she would come all this way just to offer prayers, and it wasn’t even the New Year season when blessings were usually granted.","Well, not that blessings were strictly limited to certain times of the year, but something about her explanation felt faintly odd to him.","[Errr, it was more like I was summoned by Goddess of Fertility-sama herself.]","[By Erune-san?]","[Yes. It was truly an honor, apparently, she wishes to strengthen the Divine Protection over Baron Ritchy, so both my father and I were summoned.]","[............Errr...... that’s probably because of me, right? I mean, if you were summoned too, that must be related.]","If it weren’t somehow connected to Kaito, there would be no reason for the fourth daughter, Marie, to be personally summoned, so he quickly realized he was indeed the cause.","[Ahh, please don’t worry about it. It’s nothing but good news for our household, on the contrary, we’re deeply honored and grateful.]","[R- Really? Well, I’m glad to hear that......]","[Yes. Besides the strengthening of the Divine Protection, God of Earth-sama will apparently make some adjustments to the soil as well, so the quality of the ripples we harvest should improve. I can hardly wait to see the results.]","Once again, though this had been stated already, Marie was currently in an extremely optimistic mental state. Any feelings that might cause her emotional distress were automatically shut off, so she could only view this blessing as something joyous and honorable. Seeing this, Kaito’s expression softened with relief.","[Who knows, maybe you’ll even be able to harvest golden ripples.]","[Golden ripples? Are those amazing?]","[Ahh, no, not really amazing...... nor are they literally golden-colored. It’s just a made-up story about ripples said to be the most delicious in the world, worth their weight in gold...... A sort of marketing legend.]","[A story, huh?]","[Yes. The current territory of the Ritch Barony used to be governed by another noble household. When that noble family fell into ruin, the land temporarily became royal territory, and later, when my great-grandmother was granted the baronial title, it was bestowed upon her. As for the so-called \"Golden Ripples\", it was actually a kind of promotional tale spread by the previous ruling noble, who had worked hard to establish a brand image in order to sell the Ripple from their domain at a higher price.]","[Ahh, so kind of like a sales strategy.]","Hearing her explanation, Kaito nodded in understanding. It was common for merchants to exaggerate the qualities of their products for marketing purposes, and it all sounded perfectly reasonable to him.","[They used to say it was the most delicious ripple in the world, worth as much as gold. And the pie made from those golden ripples was a special dish to be shared with one’s dearest person...... if the two shared it together, they would live happily ever after. They even mixed in stories about the Spirits' golden fruits to make it sound more romantic.]","[Hehh. Well, if they went that far, they must’ve been pretty confident in the taste, right?]","[No, the quality was said to be only so-so. If it had really been that popular, the territory would have prospered far more. In fact, you never hear about it anywhere else. Still, in the Ritch Barony, it remains as a kind of old rumor, something the farmers occasionally bring up, like a legendary ideal ripple to aspire to.]","[I see. So the promotion outpaced the product’s actual quality. But even so, stories like that carry a bit of history, they’re kind of fun to hear.]","It was truly just lighthearted small talk. A failed business venture that had turned into a sort of local legend, that was all. And so, Kaito and Marie continued chatting pleasantly, enjoying their harmless conversation.","It was nothing more than idle small talk...... there had never actually been such a thing as a golden ripple in the past, nor was the current Ritch Barony aiming to cultivate one.","It was simply the kind of light conversation one might have in a café, the sort where you might say \"It’d be nice if the Divine Protection improved the quality\", and leave it at that...... or at least, that’s how it should have been.","[......Houu...... Golden ripples, you say...... A special dish to share with one’s beloved...... With one’s beloved, hm......]","However, somewhere in the \"Sanctuary\"...... there was a certain being who muttered those words with great interest, clearly intrigued by this so-called golden ripple......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Oi, idiot, stop that! That’s not something you joke about, and she’s the kind of being who doesn’t get jokes! If you keep this up, a real golden ripple is actually going to come into existence...... Someone, please stop Marie...... She’s seriously not just digging her own grave, she’s sprinting headlong into certain doom!]","? ? ? : [Off to a stomachache-filled future, let’s gooo!]","Serious-senpai : [Could you help her instead!?]","? ? ? : [No, even Alice-chan wouldn’t know what that airheaded goddess is muttering up in the Sanctuary right now. Until the Gods themselves start moving, there’s no way for her to realize what’s happening.]"]},{"number":2420,"title":"Chapter 2420: Spreading Aftermath 21","paragraphs":["At the mansion of the Hamilton Marquisdom in the Archlesia Empire, the summoned Baron Ritch sat facing Marquis Hamilton and Eris.","Since the Marchioness was out, the three of them were currently discussing the situation concerning Kaito.","[......I see, so it’s the strengthening of the Divine Protection...... We’d already noticed that the merchants were becoming restless, but movements from the God Realm are certainly unexpected.]","[Y- Yes, honestly, I have no idea what I’m supposed to do about it......]","At Marquis Hamilton’s words, Baron Ritch nodded with a complicated expression on his face. There had been precedents for the strengthening of a Divine Protection before, but those cases occurred only temporarily, such as when natural disasters threatened to drastically reduce harvests. This situation, however, was different.","Since Elune had not specified any duration, it was assumed that the strengthened Divine Protection would continue semi-permanently, making this an unprecedented case.","[With Divine Protections involved, we’ll need to inform Her Majesty Chris as well. Whether we should announce it publicly or keep it quiet until asked should be decided after consulting Her Majesty. We’ll also need to consider Marie-sama’s mental care. She’ll likely have more occasions to visit unfamiliar places......]","[That’s right. That’s also why I didn’t have Marie accompany me here and sent her out shopping instead. I hope shopping in the high-end district helps her relax......]","Because Divine Protections affected a wide range by their nature, they needed to involve Chris, the nation’s ruler, in any decision. It couldn’t be settled here on the spot.","Eris, recalling her own past experiences, couldn’t help worrying for Marie, who would likely face many new challenges ahead.","The conversation then shifted to the growing interest merchants were showing toward the lands near the Ritch Barony...... when, at that very moment, a flustered maid rushed into the room.","[Pardon the intrusion! Urgent report...... Miyama Kaito-sama has been sighted at a bookstore on the main avenue......]","[ [ [ ! ? ] ] ]","At the maid’s words, the room was instantly filled with tension. It was a report about none other than Kaito, the very topic of their discussion, and to have him sighted not in the Symphonia Kingdom, but within the Archlesia Empire, suggested that something significant might be about to happen.","However, upon hearing the maid’s report, Eris’ expression turned to one of disbelief.","[......A sighting report of Kaito-sama?]","[Yes.]","[...............]","After confirming it, Eris fell deep into thought, her expression grave. As one of the great noble houses, the Hamilton Marquisdom possessed a wide intelligence network, and the Archlesia Imperial Capital was well within their reach.","Even so, information about Kaito’s whereabouts reaching them was something that, under normal circumstances, should have been impossible.","(......Normally, obtaining information about Kaito-sama casually visiting another city or shopping somewhere would be extremely difficult. If Kaito-sama were truly in the Capital, there would surely be many who’d wish to meet him, even just to greet him. Those who know him would undoubtedly pay attention...... but such attention would surely be troublesome for Kaito-sama, and there’s no way Phantasmal King-sama would allow it.)","Yes, under normal circumstances, reports of Kaito’s whereabouts would never reach them. Before such information could spread, it would be swiftly concealed by subordinates of the Phantasmal King. In fact, even when Kaito had previously visited pet shops or other stores, despite those being located in the high-end shopping district well within the Hamilton Marquisdom’s surveillance range, they had never received any such information.","But for that information to reach them so quickly this time could only mean one thing......","[......Phantasmal King-sama must have deemed this information something we should know. But why......!? D- Don’t tell me......]","[Eris? What’s wrong...... wait, no, could it be!?]","[Eh? Ehhh?]","Eris, who had been deep in thought, suddenly turned pale and looked toward Baron Ritch. Seeing her reaction, Marquis Hamilton also appeared to realize something a beat later, turning to look at the Baron as well.","Caught off guard by their sudden stares, Baron Ritch looked bewildered, unable to follow the situation, but before any explanation could be given, there was something Eris needed to confirm first. She turned toward the maid.","[......You probably stopped midway through your report when you saw our reaction, didn’t you? There’s more, isn’t there? Most likely...... the sighting of Kaito-sama at the bookstore was followed by reports that he finished shopping and headed toward the high-end shopping district...... is that correct?]","[Y- Yes, that’s right.]","[I thought so...... then that means...... Marie-sama had......]","Hearing the exchange between Eris and the maid, Baron Ritch finally grasped the situation and his face drained of color.","[......N- No, even so....... the high-end shopping district is quite large, you know!? A- And Marie went to a women’s clothing boutique, so the odds of them meeting by chance are......]","[......They will, with it being him...... I mean, in this vast Capital, Kaito-sama just happened to head for the high-end district exactly where Marie-sama would be at that timing...... Besides, the fact that this sighting information even reached us must mean Phantasmal King-sama expects Marie-sama and Kaito-sama to encounter each other......]","[For now, gather all related information immediately! Check for any sightings or signs of major figures within the Capital, such as the Six Kings or their Executives! Also, look into any events scheduled to take place today!]","From their past experiences, both Eris and Marquis Hamilton were almost certain that Kaito would end up meeting Marie, and they immediately ordered their subordinates to collect other relevant intelligence.","If any major figures happened to be visiting the capital, then an encounter between them would be inevitable.","And realizing that his daughter might soon find herself in a truly extraordinary situation, Baron Ritch closed his eyes and clutched his head, praying for her peace of mind.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [So they’ve entered emergency alert status for the Subject K...... Well, it’s already too late for that, if we’re being honest......]","? ? ? : [\"The incident isn’t happening in the Capital! It’s happening in the God Realm!\" or something like that, yeah?]","Serious-senpai : [Then tell them already.]","? ? ? : [That’s the thing, at this point, even Alice-chan doesn’t know about it yet.]"]},{"number":2421,"title":"Chapter 2421: Spreading Aftermath 22","paragraphs":["There was a high possibility that something would happen when Kaito encountered Marie...... though in truth, something had already happened. One of the rooms in the Hamilton Marquisdom’s estate had now entered a state of near-lockdown.","After issuing a series of orders to the servants, Eris turned toward the Marquis Hamilton and spoke.","[......Father. Though we’ve taken what countermeasures we could think of, we are far too inexperienced when it comes to handling such matters. As things stand, we’re like raw recruits charging at a behemoth. Therefore, I have a proposal. It may make us look as though we’re bowing our heads, but...... what do you think about seeking advice from Duchess Lilia?]","[......I agree. Even putting aside the matter concerning Miyama Kaito-sama, it would be wise to strengthen our ties with the Albert Duchy for the future. In terms of influence, they already surpass us. Even if our actions make us seem like the ones requesting aid, it likely won’t cause much backlash.]","Eris’ suggestion, to ask Lilia for advice, who almost certainly had far more experience with situations involving Kaito, was met with the Marquis’ approval.","The Hamilton faction was one of the leading noble blocs in the kingdom, so appearing subservient to nobles of another nation could easily send ripples through their own ranks.","There was concern that the Hamilton faction might be perceived as weaker than the Albert faction, but even with that risk considered, they decided it was wiser to seek counsel.","When Eris contacted Lilia via hummingbird and explained the situation, a reply came back astonishingly fast.","\"Lady Eris, Marquis Hamilton, I can truly and painfully understand your struggle. However, in my experience, attempting to locate major figures within the Capital tends to end in futility. For some reason, when one takes precautions or moves to act in advance, Kaito-san has an uncanny ability to slip past them, almost as if intentional...... However, if you neglect to investigate or prepare, that’s exactly when a major figure suddenly appears in the capital, so I do recommend maintaining a degree of vigilance.\"","From Lilia’s experience, the conclusion was that even if the Hamilton Marquisdom desperately searched for important visitors in the capital, they were unlikely to find anyone fitting.","\"I may sound terribly harsh, but speaking from experience...... taking precautions or devising countermeasures against Kaito-san is almost meaningless. He has a tendency to strike from completely unexpected directions, to the point you might suspect him of doing it on purpose, so prevention is impossible. The only viable approach is to respond as swiftly as possible once an incident occurs.\"","Most likely, within Trinia, the one who has suffered the most and the worst stomachaches because of Kaito, and can rightfully be called an expert in stomachache-related matters caused by him, is Lilia. And based on her past experiences, the conclusion she has reached is this...... any countermeasures against Kaito are meaningless. One should simply go with the flow and respond to whatever situation arises, as if surrendering oneself to a raging current.","[......According to Duchess Lilia’s conclusion...... there are no countermeasures.]","[......I see...... If the Duchess Albert says so...... then there truly must be none.]","After reading the hummingbird’s reply, Eris murmured distantly, and Marquis Hamilton, wearing a similarly distant look, nodded in agreement. Then, another hummingbird message arrived from Lilia.","\"As for predicting Kaito-san’s movements or influence, only someone on the level of Alice-sama...... Phantasmal King-sama could hope to do so. For the rest of us, there’s little point in wracking our brains over it. What you should pay attention to, however, is not so much Phantasmal King-sama’s actions..... Her state of affairs, I mean. Phantasmal King-sama never offers advice unless something would adversely affect Kaito-san...... but on the rare occasion she provides assistance even when Kaito-san remains unharmed, that’s an extremely dangerous sign. It means that the situation has become so bad \"you become so pitiful in her eyes\" and feels compelled to intervene, which suggests that something quite big is about to occur.]","Reading that message, Eris and Marquis Hamilton began to consider their current situation. There had been a reported sighting of Kaito, most likely information obtained through the Phantasmal King. But that was all, it was merely intelligence gathered by Hamilton agents and passed along without being suppressed. There had been no follow-up or intervention.","If that were the case, perhaps this incident would not escalate into anything too serious. Eris and the Marquis were just beginning to feel some relief when another Hummingbird arrived from Lilia.","\"From the information you’ve provided, I believe this situation will be rather difficult for Lady Marie, but it shouldn’t become anything too severe...... That said...... well, I have no evidence for this, it’s simply a gut feeling, so please take it as half in jest, but I can’t shake the sense that...... this time, the matter will seem manageable at first, only for an unavoidable blow to strike a few days later, when everyone has let their guard down. ......No, perhaps I’m overthinking it. In any case, I sincerely pray that this incident ends favorably for Lady Eris, Marquis Hamilton, and everyone of the Ritch Barony.\"","Even though Lilia clearly stated it was nothing more than her intuition, the contents, a premonition of unease, made both Eris and Marquis Hamilton turn pale.","[......I don’t know why, but this hummingbird message is more terrifying than any horror story I’ve ever seen.]","[......An unavoidable blow...... If it’s unavoidable, then there’s nothing we could do even if it happens...... No, it’s not as though it’s certain to happen, but still......]","Though an inexplicable anxiety lingered, Lilia herself had admitted there was no concrete basis for her warning. Unable to draw any firm conclusions, Eris and the others continued their discussions on how to deal with the ongoing situation in the Imperial Capital, all while that uneasy atmosphere quietly hung over the room.","<Afterword>","[Regarding Kaito's Sightings]","Generally speaking, reports of Kaito’s sightings...... especially real-time ones, rarely ever show up within the information networks of nobles or governments. The reason, of course, is the Phantasmal King, Alice. It is thanks to her information control that Kaito’s face remains largely unknown to the general public, while his name alone is famous among the nobility.","That influence extends even when Kaito walks through the streets. Alice blocks, conceals, or scrambles information about him. For large public events such as the Six Kings Festival or the Maid Olympia, where he inevitably attracts attention, she intentionally spreads conflicting reports of his appearance and even his name, throwing any gathered data into total confusion.","When necessary, she even casts Recognition Inhibition Magic or Information Concealment Magic directly on Kaito, supporting him in countless unseen ways behind the scenes. Thanks to that devotion, Kaito has never become widely recognized among the public.","That said, in cases like the one in Rigforeshia, she sometimes can’t resist teasing him, provoking him into retaliating with his trusty piko piko hammer, a bit of mischievous fun that also demonstrates the usefulness of those “Super Recognition Inhibition Glasses”.","But even considering those pranks, the benefits she provides far outweigh them. Her support is nothing short of selfless, and the fact that she never boasts of it, always working quietly in the background, is just like Alice.","Kaito is aware of it as well. Though exasperated by her pranks, he is deeply grateful for all her efforts regarding information management."]},{"number":2422,"title":"Chapter 2422: Spreading Aftermath 23","paragraphs":["God Realm, Sanctuary, Life had been urgently summoned by Shallow Vernal. Upon appearing before her, Life knelt down and bowed her head.","After confirming her posture with a light nod, Shallow Vernal spoke in her usual calm tone.","[......You recently gave instructions concerning Baron Ritch of the Archlesia Empire, did you not? Regarding that matter, please ensure that golden ripples can also be harvested.]","[......Shallow Vernal-sama, forgive my ignorance, but what exactly are these golden ripples?]","[It’s a special kind of ripple, meant to be eaten with one’s most beloved. I want to eat it with Kaito-san...... I could create it myself, but I’d prefer to preserve the authenticity of it being a local specialty, so make it possible for them to be harvested in Baron Ritch’s territory. Rather than a detailed explanation, I’ll show you directly.]","As she said this, Shallow Vernal raised her finger, and an image appeared in Life’s mind, the conversation Shallow Vernal had just overheard between Kaito and Marie.","Through this, Life came to understand that the so-called golden ripple was an imaginary fruit created by nobles of the past for promotional purposes, and that Shallow Vernal wished to make that fictional fruit a reality.","[......I see. Understood. I shall make the necessary adjustments so that golden ripples can be harvested within Baron Ritch’s domain.]","[I’ll leave it to you.]","There was no issue with that request itself. In essence, the golden ripple was simply an exceptionally delicious variety of ripple, and making it possible to harvest such a fruit was an easy task for Life, the God of Life.","[By the way, Shallow Vernal-sama, may I ask one question?]","[You may.]","[......What is that island over there?]","After accepting Shallow Vernal’s request, Life took the opportunity to ask something that had piqued her curiosity since arriving in the Sanctuary. Near the Sanctuary floated an island in the sky, with several buildings of unfamiliar design, unlike anything commonly seen in Trinia.","[That is an onsen town.]","[......Onsen town?]","[Yes. I promised Kaito-san a lovely-dovey onsen trip. However, since we’ve already gone to onsens together several times in the past, I wanted to add some variety, so I decided to create an entire onsen town. The one you see now is a direct copy of an onsen town from Earth God's world. It would work fine as is, but since it’s a special lovey-dovey trip with Kaito-san, leaving it as a mere replica feels lacking, so I’m currently making adjustments to better suit this world.]","[I see...... Adjustments huh......]","Nodding as if in understanding, Life seemed to ponder something deeply. After a short silence, she bowed her head respectfully before speaking again.","[......Shallow Vernal-sama, if I may be so bold...... I wish to offer a personal opinion regarding the golden ripples.]","[You may. Speak.]","[Yes! Regarding the golden ripples...... what if we were to actually create ripples with a golden hue?]","[Fumu......]","[I am still inexperienced, but through the White God Festival and the events related to Miyama-san, I have broadened my knowledge somewhat. I have learned that the sense of uniqueness and rarity in an item’s appearance can enhance its value and set it apart from ordinary goods. Strictly speaking, golden ripples do not yet exist in this world, and from what I understand, they don’t necessarily have to look the same as normal ripples. Therefore, since this is a fruit meant for Shallow Vernal-sama to share with Miyama-san, I humbly propose making it a special fruit with an appearance worthy of that occasion.]","[I see...... A sense of visual uniqueness is indeed appealing. Very well, do it that way.]","[Yes!]","After hearing the word \"adjustment\" from Shallow Vernal and approving Life’s suggestion that the golden ripples should be made into a truly golden fruit in every sense of the word, Shallow Vernal fell silent for a moment before speaking again.","[......Not only its appearance, but also every other aspect of the golden ripple’s creation, I shall leave it entirely in your hands. You seem to have gained much knowledge and broadened your perspective, and the fact that you thought for yourself and offered your opinion to me shows growth. With the way you are now, I am certain you will create something that will satisfy me...... I’m counting on you, \"Life\".]","[ ! ? ! ? ! ? ]","At that instant, Life felt a tremendous shock within her heart. Such overwhelming joy flooded her chest that she wondered if anything in existence could ever be more blissful; tears began streaming uncontrollably down her cheeks.","Struggling to suppress the joy that made her want to shout aloud, Life bowed deeply.","[Yes! I will, without fail, create something worthy of Shallow Vernal-sama’s expectations!!!]","When Shallow Vernal called her name, spoke to her with expectation, and entrusted her with a task, the impact was immense. In Life’s eyes burned a blazing determination.","......It was the very moment that God of Life, Life’s motivation towards creating the golden ripples surpassed its limits.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [No, you can't do that...... If you say something like that, Life’s gonna get seriously fired up! The entire Ritch Barony’s gonna be in trouble!]"]},{"number":2423,"title":"Chapter 2423: Spreading Aftermath 24","paragraphs":["Life returned from the Sanctuary to the upper layer and immediately set things in motion. Because the Gods can communicate through telepathy simply by picturing the person they want to contact, thanks to the Authority of the God of Thoughts, Omoikane, getting in touch with the other Gods is easy.","Well, the receiving side can refuse the connection, so back when Fate had been slacking off, she simply ignored her......","(God of Thoughts, can you hear me? Connect a telepathic link to all Gods immediately.)","(As you command.)","However, this method only works within the range of Omoikane’s Authority. Normally, this means it can only be used in the God Realm, where Omoikane constantly keeps her power deployed. If one wants to contact lower-ranking Gods in the Human Realm, or hold a telepathic conversation with multiple people at once, one must first contact Omoikane to expand the reach of her authority.","(A message to all Gods. Fifteen minutes from now, an emergency meeting will be held at my temple. Anyone whose Authority even slightly influences the creation of plants or fruits, as well as anyone with knowledge or experience in agriculture or related tasks, is to gather at my temple. This concerns a request from Shallow Vernal-sama and takes priority over all other duties. Also, this meeting is only to determine the broad direction we’ll take. After a basic policy is decided, we will send another announcement to gather opinions from all Gods, as we will need perspectives of every kind, so even those who do not meet the earlier conditions should be mentally prepared.)","Entrusted by Shallow Vernal and told they had expectations for her, Life had no intention of allowing even the slightest compromise in the creation of the golden ripples.","She understood that relying solely on her own knowledge would leave gaps or cause oversights, so she planned to gather ideas widely from other Gods as well.","After sending the telepathic message, Life returned to her own temple...... only to find that Fate and Chronois were already there.","[As expected, fast as always, God of Fate, God of Time and Space.]","[When you say it’s something Shallow Vernal-sama wants, of course we’ll hurry...... but more importantly, God of Life, aren’t you overflowing with motivation right now? It’s practically radiating off you.]","[Just looking at you, I can feel your resolve......]","As Fate pointed out, Life was absolutely brimming with enthusiasm. Her eyes, usually half-closed, were now wide open, and her crimson gaze burned with such intensity that it looked as though flames might be flickering within them. Anyone could see how fired up she was.","[Yes, let me explain the general situation to you two first. I was summoned by Shallow Vernal-sama earlier......]","Since Fate and Chronois were also Supreme Gods, she decided to give them the details beforehand and explained what had happened in the God Realm.","[Ahh, I see. Yeah, that’d definitely get you fired up.]","[To be expected. If Shallow Vernal-sama not only entrusted you with this task but even called you by name, it’s only natural your spirit would burn. I admit I feel a little envious, but more than that, I understand how you feel. I will assist you with all my strength.]","[Of course, same here...... and judging from what you’re aiming for, instead of trying to mess with Divine Protections and such, it seems better to grow a golden ripple tree on our side and hand it over to Baron Ritch. That way the rarity stays intact, and it suits your specialty as well.]","The feelings driving Life were something any god could genuinely empathize with, and both Fate and Chronois immediately pledged their cooperation. Fate then offered a suggestion with a speed completely unimaginable from her usual lazy behavior, and Life nodded lightly at her words.","[Yes, that was the direction I was considering as well. Plants are life, creating a new plant life will allow my Authority to shine. However, I want to avoid narrowing my perspective. Even if I believe something is the best approach, there may be flaws when viewed from another angle. So I want to gather opinions as broadly as possible.]","[Good thinking. We should also run prototypes. With my Authority over time, repeating trial and error is trivial. Let us create something truly worthy of satisfying Shallow Vernal-sama.]","[Then those like God of Agriculture and God of Vegetations should show up thanks to your earlier call, so that’s fine...... but when we think about turning it into ripple pie, we should also hear from God of Cooking and God of Food, right?]","While the Gods of the God Realm were beginning to move in response to Life’s summons...... Down in the underground bar belonging to Iris beneath Kaito’s home, Alice, who had been about to sip wine at the counter, suddenly froze mid-motion.","[......Eh? Seriously......? They’re moving...... Wow......]","[Unn? What’s wrong?]","[Ah, no, it’s just......]","[Why are you putting the wine away?]","[......Well, even I feel more pity than amusement this time...... guess I should go give them a bit of support...... actually, let’s start by making sure stupid Makina doesn’t make a move first.]","After putting away the wine she had planned to drink, Alice muttered with a hint of exasperation. Her extraordinary mind rapidly ran through the developments to come, and she began arranging support for Marie and Baron Ritch.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Even Alice ended up feeling more of pity!?]"]},{"number":2424,"title":"Chapter 2424: Spreading Aftermath 25","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I don't have much time today, so today's chapter is a bit short.","After enjoying tea and cake with Kaito at the café, and since the time for her pickup was drawing near, Marie parted ways with Kaito there, each going their separate ways at the café, and Marie moved to the place where her pickup was scheduled to arrive, as previously arranged.","Up until now, Marie had been floating in a dreamlike haze. It was a feeling brought about entirely because of an unreasonable situation and an unreasonable existence like Kaito. But once she separated from him and had a moment to breathe, reality sped up and crept right up behind her all at once.","[......Marie!]","[Ah, F- Father......]","Originally, someone from the Hamilton Marquisdom was supposed to pick her up, and she was supposed to meet her father afterward at Marquis Hamilton’s residence. However, when he heard there was a possibility that Marie might unexpectedly encounter Kaito again at the Hamilton estate, Baron Ritch became worried and came to pick her up himself.","And perhaps because she relaxed a little upon seeing her father’s face...... a bit of calm surfaced in her heart...... and the reality she had been avoiding bared its fangs.","[......M- Marie? What’s the matter? Your face is pale...... no, beyond pale...... And you’re sweating so much......]","[F- F- Father...... t- this is strange...... I can’t...... wake up...... from the dream......]","[A dream? What are you talking about?]","[B- Because...... everything until now must have been a dream...... If it wasn’t......]","Marie’s face grew so drained of color it seemed as though all the blood had left it, and she began trembling violently, sweat pouring down her in large drops.","Seeing her in such an abnormal state, Baron Ritch was confused, but he somehow managed to get Marie into the carriage. Even after she sat down in the seat, Marie’s trembling didn’t calm, in fact, it grew worse and worse. It was immediately clear that something was very wrong.","[......F- F- Father...... I- I might already be done for. I’ve committed...... unforgivable disrespect toward Kaito-sama......]","[Disrespect? J- Just calm down. Take slow, deep breaths and calmly tell me what happened.]","[Because something like that could never happen! So I thought it was a dream...... but if it was real...... t- then I shamefully extorted Kaito-sama for expensive clothes and accessories...... and even received a large-capacity magic box...... ababa...... T- That alone adds up to over three white gold coins’ worth...... N- No matter if Kaito-sama was the one who suggested it, it’s still far too rude...... I- It’s over. That terrifying God will surely punish me. Father, please forgive your daughter for passing before you......]","[C- Calm down. I still don’t understand the situation. Start from the beginning, slowly......]","[Ah, no, I can’t...... I can’t...... aah......]","[Marie!? Get a hold of yourself, Marie!!]","With her invincibility mode gone, everything she had been avoiding came crashing into her mind all at once. Unable to withstand the torrent of information and emotion flooding her head, Marie lost consciousness.","This, of course, left Baron Ritch troubled. He understood that something serious had happened, and Marie had said something terrifying about having committed disrespect towards Kaito, but he had no idea what the details were.","And without knowing those details, there was nothing he could do...... Holding the unconscious Marie in his arms, Baron Ritch could only stare blankly, his own face turning pale.","Incidentally, Kaito didn’t think Marie had disrespected him at all, if anything, he had simply enjoyed himself, and his evaluation of Marie had risen considerably.","As for the value of over three white gold coins, that amount would normally be astonishing, but to Kaito, it \"costs less than Alice’s binge eating\", and thus not even remotely worth worrying about.","And as for the terrifying God, Makina, whom Marie worried would punish her, since Kaito was happy, there was no reason for her to punish anyone. Marie’s fear was completely unnecessary...... though neither she nor Baron Ritch had any way of knowing that at this point.","That said, what would trouble Baron Ritch going forward would be that the nobles would soon begin regarding Marie as either Kaito’s lover or mistress...... but of course, he also had no way of knowing that yet.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Terrifying God, she said......]","Makina : [How rude! What part of me is supposed to be terrifying? I don’t go around punishing my beloved child’s friends without reason, nor do I nitpick and accuse them of extortion when my beloved child himself doesn’t mind. Well, having awe and reverence towards a God is natural, so I’m not going to call it disrespect.]","Serious-senpai : [No, isn’t it because you threatened every noble......? And you literally made some of them experience the future as a form of punishment, showing them hell......]","Makina : [Serious-senpai? Right now, we're talking about lumps of flesh who at least have enough substance to understand the bare minimum. I’m not talking about garbage, so that example doesn’t apply.]","Serious-senpai : [......Ah, yes.]"]},{"number":2425,"title":"Chapter 2425: Spreading Aftermath 25","paragraphs":["When I returned home from Archlesia Empire, it was already around the time the sun was about to set. Shopping and going to the café with Marie-san had been so much fun that quite a bit of time had passed.","Since Marie-san is younger than me and about the same age as Aoi-chan and Hina-chan, I can’t help wanting to buy her things or look after her.","Even though she’s a noble lady, she isn’t noble-like in a bad way; she feels surprisingly down-to-earth, so personally, she’s very easy to get along with.","Well, in any case, I had fun, and she seemed happy, so that was good. According to Akane-san, various troubles were drawn to her because of the Ritch Barony’s territory matters, even though that wasn't my intention, so it seems this outing was a good distraction for her, which really was a relief.","She mentioned admiring pretty clothes and such too, so maybe Marie-san actually likes shopping a lot. She doesn’t have the financial leeway to visit the high-class shopping district often, but since her situation must be difficult, maybe next time I can take her there again as a little break.","[Welcome home, Kaito-san.]","[Sieg-san? Good evening. Just finished work?]","[Yes, today I was on duty until evening, so I just got off. And I happened to see you coming home......]","[I see...... I was thinking of taking Bell for a short walk before dinner, would you like to come with us?]","It seemed Sieg-san had finished work at just the right time, so since we’d crossed paths, I invited him to come along on Bell’s walk.","Bell is quite prideful, but she’s fond of Sieg-san, who takes good care of her, and doesn’t mind letting Sieg-san ride on her back, so going for a walk together wouldn’t be a problem.","Well, I got home later than expected today, so it won’t be a long walk, just something light......","[That sounds nice. But in that case, how about we go after dinner?]","[After dinner?]","[Yes. Apparently, today’s a night when you can see a meteor shower. If we head a little farther out to the hill southwest of the capital, we should get a beautiful view. If you’re willing, would you like to go see it together?]","[That sounds great. It seems fun, and Bell would enjoy a long trip too.]","According to Shiro-san, there is no such thing as \"outer space\" in this world, and the stars and moon in the night sky exist as part of a kind of world system.","Still, it’s not the exact same sky every night, there are periodic meteor showers, solar eclipses, and lunar eclipses, so the night sky doesn’t feel any different from the one in the world I came from.","[Since it’s a special occasion, shall we bring some alcohol? Drinking a little while watching the stars sounds nice.]","[Indeed. In that case, I still have some ripple wine, the same one we drank together when Kaito-san visited my family home in Rigforeshia, so let’s bring that.]","[I’m looking forward to it. I’ll go explain things to Bell real quick. Time-wise, right after dinner should be fine?]","[Yes. If we head out about 30 minutes after dinner, it should be just the right timing when we reach the hill.]","An unexpectedly fun plan had suddenly been added to my evening. After having a quick chat with Sieg-san, I explained things to Bell and then returned to my room.","Since I’d be heading out again soon, I didn’t bother changing into loungewear, staying as I was should be fine. There wasn’t anything extra I needed to bring either; most things were already inside the Magic Box.","As I was thinking that, a section of my room’s wall suddenly slid open...... revealing a staircase of some sort, and Alice climbed up from it.","[Kaito-san, if you’re going to see the meteor shower, I’ve got something good for you.]","[......Before that, I want to know where those stairs I’ve never seen before lead.]","[......Well, somewhere. Anyway, more importantly, here!]","[I really should ask Canalis-san to do a thorough sweep someday...... So, what is...... hm? Wine?]","I accepted what Alice handed me despite my exasperation. It was a bottle of wine that looked rather expensive. Is she telling me to take it with me and drink it with Sieg-san while we watch the meteor shower? But why wine, all of a sudden?","[Well, I was planning to drink it myself...... but the situation isn't really one I can just sit back and enjoy, so please drink it with Sieg-san.]","[U- Unn? Well, I mean, I appreciate the wine, but...... did something happen?]","[Hmm, rather than something happened, it's more like something's about to happen...... well, don’t worry about it. If you start getting involved in weird ways, there’s a chance even more things will pop up, so just don’t worry about it.]","[Wait, that sounds almost like you’re saying it’s basically my fault......]","[Well, it’s fine. This Subject K is an easy one for me, just some light information control. So don’t think about it and enjoy your date with Sieg-san~~]","Saying that, Alice vanished. H- Hmmm...... I’m curious, obviously, but if Alice says it’s fine, then I guess I’m better off not worrying about it.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Carelessness, a lack of caution...... tell me, is that really something that applies only to the Stomachache Warriors?]","Serious-senpai : [W- What are you......?]","●gar Devil : [You, Serious-senpai. Are you acting like some detached observer, thinking you can just relax and have a good time? Aren’t you...... letting your guard down a bit too much?]","Serious-senpai : [Eh? M- Me?]","●● Devil : [Your turn has come...... that’s what this means. The sweet dream is over...... no, perhaps the sweet dream is only just beginning......]","Serious-senpai : [Y- Your name...... is changing......!]","Su● Devil : [Can’t understand? Or is it that you don’t want to understand? Or perhaps......]","Serious-senpai : [A- Ahh...... n- no way......]","Sugar Devil: [Don’t tell me...... you’re still holding onto the fantasy sweeter than honeyed toast———— \"It’s a stomachache chapter so I’ll be fine\"? ]","Serious-senpai : [Gyaaaa!? It appeared!?]"]},{"number":2426,"title":"Chapter 2426: Stargazing Wine 1","paragraphs":["If Bell were to run through the streets, it would cause a commotion, but walking all the way outside the city from a house located near the center of the royal capital would be far too far.","And so, for when we go on walks, I have the area outside the capital registered in the teleportation magic tool. It is just outside the west gate, so there is a bit of distance to the southern hill, but with Bell’s speed that is no problem.","After making some quick preparations, I teleport together with Bell and Sieg-san to the registered location. The sun has already set, and it is dark all around, so I activate two floating illumination magic tools and adjust their direction so they shine forward like car headlights.","[Bell, it’s dark, but are you okay?]","[Gau!]","Well, Bell can see in the dark anyway, so there’s no problem, but if it’s pitch black, neither I nor Sieg-san can see ahead...... actually, if Sieg-san uses her special magic, she can see at night about as well as in the daytime, so this is mostly for me. Since I can’t see ahead, it’s a bit worrying, so I decided to light the path.","At my signal, Bell dashes forward at considerable speed, but with the anti-fall and motion-dampening magic tools active, it’s completely safe and very comfortable.","[She really is fast. At this rate, we should reach the southern hill soon.]","[Yeah. Still, it’s a fair distance, and it’s longer than our usual walking route, so going straight there should be fine.]","I give a light reply to Sieg-san, who is riding behind me. Bell’s body is very large despite her being young, and even with both me and Sieg-san riding, there’s plenty of room. Thanks to the magic tools, it’s stable on her back, so we don’t need to press close together the way you would when two people ride a horse.","It feels like a bit of a waste, but realistically, if there were any shaking, I’d definitely be the first one to lose balance, and then I’d probably end up being the one clinging to Sieg-san.","[......Hmm, it’s not that it’s necessary, but it does feel a bit of a shame.]","[Hm? What does?]","[Well, in romance novels, when people ride together, the man and woman end up pressed close and become aware of each other, right? Being in a similar situation but without that feels like a bit of a waste.]","[Ah, I kind of thought that too.]","As a side note, Sieg-san reads a lot of novels. She’s the one who first showed me the bookstore, and she seems to have always read quite a bit. She prefers stories with narrative elements, like novels.","Before, she mostly read adventure tales and the like, and hardly any romance, but after we became lovers, she started reading romance novels now and then.","After that conversation, Sieg-san quietly slips her arms around my stomach from behind and presses close.","[Like this, perhaps?]","[I don’t know what the perfect answer is supposed to be, but this feels pretty nice.]","[Hehe, I like things like this too. Then, until we reach our destination, let’s stay like this......]","It is not a tight embrace. She isn’t clinging to me, but with her arms gently around me, the warmth of her hands, the heat of her body against my back, and her soft voice right near my ear......","It isn’t just soothing, this gentle closeness that makes me think \"I’m really happy\" feels unbelievably pleasant.","It did not take long before we arrived at the hill. There were no trees or anything else blocking the view, making it an excellent place to see the stars.","Since it was a fair distance from the royal capital, it seemed no one else had come all the way out here to watch the meteor shower. It appeared that, although rare, monsters sometimes showed up in this area as well, so it would likely be difficult for ordinary people to come.","As for us, there was no problem at all, monsters are very sensitive to those stronger than they are, and they almost never pick fights with stronger creatures. So among the monsters that inhabit the Human Realm, there are almost none that would attack when Bell is present. A few dangerous types, like wyverns, which are low in intelligence and aggressive, might attack regardless, but such monsters do not live near the capital, so we could watch the stars in peace.","Once we got off Bell and found a good spot to lay down the sheet after discussing it with Sieg-san, Bell immediately laid down like she had been waiting for this, wagging her tail and staring at me with eyes full of expectation.","[......You just had dinner, so only one, okay?]","[Gau!]","To summarize the look Bell was giving me: \"See? I laid down nicely and became a backrest. I’m a good girl, right? Reward, please.\"","Smiling wryly at that, I took from the magic box what Bell was certainly hoping for, a hunk of meat larger than my arm, and placed it before her.","What it was, essentially, was something like beef jerky. It was made from the meat of an Agisauro...... a monster that lives in the Demon Realm. I’ve never seen one personally, but based on the illustrations, it looks like a Tyrannosaurus-like creature. It’s processed into a treat for large pets, and it’s one of Bell’s absolute favorites.","Humans, by the way, can’t eat it. Not because it’s poisonous, but because...... it’s absurdly hard. So hard that even steel literally cannot dent it. So hard that if someone strong were to swing this jerky like a club, they could smash iron armor with it.","[Gau~~]","Lynn and Sela also refuse to eat this jerky because it’s too tough, but for Bell, it seems to have the perfect chewiness and flavor, making it the best treat ever. Whenever she gets some, she cherishes it and eats it slowly, savoring every bit.","Watching Bell happily gnaw at her jerky, I smiled, then leaned back against her body with Sieg-san as we gazed up at the sky.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Calm down, Kaito! Keep it gentle, keep it heartwarming! You’re already flirting a little, but you can still turn back! Sure, drinking together under the stars with your lover...... it’s a perfect situation for flirting! But there are noble ladies out there suffering stomachaches because of you, you know!!! In a situation like that, don’t you feel the least bit guilty about flirting with your girlfriend?! Alice also said something concerning, so let’s focus on that instead!!]","? ? ? : [Ah, that part’s fine. Last chapter, I...... err, Alice-chan hinted to Kaito-san that \"when Kaito-san gets involved, the trouble multiplies, so please behave and just enjoy your date with your girlfriend\". Kaito-san is also someone who switches gears quickly, so he took the hint properly. He’s letting me handle things while he enjoys his date.]","Serious-senpai : [W- Why did you have to add that unnecessary clarification......]"]},{"number":2427,"title":"Chapter 2427: Chapter 2428: Stargazing Wine 3","paragraphs":["For a while, my eyes were captured by the breathtaking sight of the meteor shower, but since the whole point had been to enjoy a drink while watching it, it would’ve been a waste not to, so we decided to get things ready.","[Oh, right. Alice gave me a bottle of wine and told me to drink it with Sieg-san, so let’s have this.]","[This is quite a fine wine. Why would Alice-sama give this to us? No, not that I’m ungrateful......]","[Hmm, she said she’d planned to drink it herself but there's apparently a change in her schedule, so I think she just happened to have it on her.]","In reality, I’m pretty sure it also served as a subtle warning, which was why she brought it out at that moment. It’s probably related to Archlesia Empire stuff she talked about with Akane-san. As for Marie-san’s side, there shouldn’t be much activity happening yet, so I suspect it’s something connected to Cornelia-san.","Tetra-san was clearly interested in the Sharon Trading Company, and if things have started to move there, it wouldn’t surprise me if Alice judged that she’d need to handle the information processing soon.","I do feel guilty, since I’m the cause of it, but Alice indirectly told me \"Right now, everything can still be handled with simple information processing, so don’t do anything that complicates things, just behave\", so I’ve decided to leave all that to her and simply enjoy stargazing with Sieg-san.","[I prepared some light snacks as well.]","[Eh? Sieg-san, you made all this? How did you find the time......?]","[Oh, I’d already finished dinner when I called out to Kaito-san, so I prepared these while you were eating. Though really, they’re all simple dishes I threw together in a short time.]","When I set out the wine, Sieg-san pulled out something like a multi-tiered food box and laid it out on the sheet. Inside were various bite-sized snacks, all looking delicious.","There were things like cream cheese wrapped in prosciutto, skewers with cherry-tomato-like vegetables, and bite-sized sandwiches, everything looked like it would pair well with wine or ripple-based liquor.","Sieg-san said they were simple to make, and while each dish probably didn’t take much effort, there were so many varieties that it must have required a fair bit of work.","[I see...... but still, with this many varieties, that’s impressive.]","[Fufu, I reused a few things I’d prepared earlier, so there are some shortcuts...... But I think the taste should be fine.]","[Sieg-san’s cooking is not only delicious, there’s also this gentle, warm flavor to it. I really like it.]","[That’s because it’s filled with love for you, Kaito-san. You’ll eat it in a moment, but could you try this one first?]","After smiling gently, Sieg-san picked up a bite-sized sandwich, supported it with one hand, and held it out to me.","That probably meant she intended to feed me. Sieg-san had the air of a calm and gentle older sister, and seeing her offer food with a soft smile like this gave me a sense of...... well, warmth and comfort. ráɴо฿ЕS","When I opened my mouth and let her feed me the sandwich, it was probably a ham sandwich. There was a slight tang to it, so she might have used mustard as well. The slightly stronger flavor felt like it would pair perfectly with alcohol.","[It’s delicious. I think it’ll go well with the wine too.]","[I brought snacks that pair with ripple-based liquor, so if they also match the wine, all the better.]","[However, with snacks and drinks all prepared by you, and the wine conveniently coming from Alice, I feel like I should take something out of my magic box...... though that might make the amount too much.]","[That’s true. Neither of us drinks or eats a lot, so I think it’s better not to add more.]","There’s food and alcohol stored inside the magic box, so if I wanted to bring out more, I could. But just as Sieg-san said, neither of us are heavy drinkers; if anything, the atmosphere suggested we would be enjoying our drinks slowly, focusing on conversation. Adding more would only be excessive.","[So then, Kaito-san, how about you put that desire to do something...... toward spoiling me instead?]","[Ahaha, I see...... But Sieg-san, you know a statement like that comes with responsibility, right?]","[Oh my, is that so...... fufu, now I’m looking forward to it.]","She said she wanted me to use that desire, to do something, to flirt with her like a proper couple, which was an adorably sweet request. I mimicked the way she had phrased things earlier and replied in kind.","Thereupon, Sieg-san smiled happily and leaned gently against me.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [S- Stop flirting already...... guh, d- d*mmit!? The rate of encroachment is too fast, half my body is already turning into konpeito!?]","Makina : [......munch munch...... all the tiny konpeito are clustering together to form the shape of your body, and the colors match your original appearance too...... crunch crunch...... even your clothes have turned into konpeito, which feels weird...... munch munch...... I wonder if they count as part of your body?]","Serious-senpai : [Why are you eating me like it’s your natural right, you deranged god!?]","Makina : [Hmm...... it tastes good, but since it’s based on the original Serious-senpai, the colors are...... konpeito is a candy you enjoy visually too, you know? It’d be better if it were more colorful......]","Serious-senpai : [You eat someone’s body without permission and then complain about it? That’s beyond tyrannical......]","Makina : [.........................Alright then...... \"Serious-senpai Colorful Beam\".]","Serious-senpai : [Huh? Gyaaaa!? The remaining parts of my body are turning rainbow-colored!? What the heck are you doing!?]","Makina : [Now I can eat bright, colorful konpeito!]","Serious-senpai : [Don’t screw with me...... no, seriously, if you’re going that far, just create colorful konpeito yourself!!! That’d obviously be easier and faster!!!]","Makina : [......haahh...... Serious-senpai. The shortest route, the path of highest efficiency, isn’t always the optimal solution.]","Serious-senpai : [I can tell you for certain that painting my body rainbow is not the optimal solution......]"]},{"number":2428,"title":"Chapter 2428: Chapter 2429: Stargazing Wine 4","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I’m going on a business trip tomorrow, so the next update will be posted on the day after tomorrow.","I held up the wine Alice had given me, poured into a wine glass, toward the night sky where a dazzling meteor shower streamed overhead. The meteors reflected in the wine, and somehow, it looked incredibly fantastical and beautiful.","[It’s sparkling so much that it feels like I’m indulging in something unbelievably luxurious.]","[That’s true. Alice-sama’s wine is very fine wine, and we’re watching a meteor shower from a place most people would never be able to visit, so in reality, this is certainly luxury.]","[And we’ve also got the delicious snacks you made, Sieg-san. It really is luxury.]","[N- No, if you compare my cooking to high-class wine and a meteor shower, it’ll look shabby in comparison, so it’s a bit embarrassing......]","[If anything, for me, between the wine, the meteor shower, and Sieg-san’s cooking, Sieg-san’s cooking makes me the happiest.]","[Y- You’re exaggerating...... though I’m happy to hear it.]","To be honest, out of those three, Sieg-san’s homemade cooking was the one I appreciated the most. Sieg-san was good at cooking, but opportunities to actually eat her cooking were surprisingly rare.","Since I usually ate meals in Lilia-san’s mansion’s dining hall, the head chef and the other cooks she employed prepared the food. And because Sieg-san’s work with the security force often caused her mealtimes to shift, she tended to cook and eat on her own as needed......","Well, Sieg-san is kind, so if I said I wanted to eat her cooking, she’d probably make it for me whenever I asked. But even so, it’s hard to say it’s something I could casually request.","When we had tea together, she often served handmade sweets, so I had plenty of chances to eat those. But when it came to actual meals, the opportunities were truly few and therefore precious.","[Like I said earlier, Sieg-san’s cooking has this gentle, comforting taste...... I personally like it a lot, so being able to eat it like this really makes me happy.]","[......If you’re going to say that much, then I’ll make you another packed lunch next time. How about we take a little trip somewhere?]","[Oh, that sounds great. A picnic is nice, but going sightseeing in some town and eating in a park sounds good too. Lately, I’ve been getting more chances to visit places outside the capital, and each town has its own character...... it’s really fun.]","[I’d like to hear more about that. I haven’t traveled much outside Symphonia Kingdom myself, so I’m curious what the towns in Archlesia Empire or Hydra Kingdom are like.]","[For example, if you’re looking for something peaceful...... when I participated in that flying board tournament......]","I snacked on the delicious appetizers, sipping wine while chatting idly with Sieg-san. She listened to my stories, nodding along with a gentle smile, and now and then she offered a bit of her own experiences too. ȐÅNꝊBЁŜ","As we talked, our conversation naturally shifted into ideas about going somewhere together again next time, and my list of things to look forward to grew longer. I had said earlier that this felt incredibly luxurious, but at the same time, it also felt like I was spending an impossibly happy moment with her, my heart felt warm in a way that was hard to describe.","[......Come to think of it, Sieg-san......]","[Yes?]","I was about to ask her something, but the moment I looked at her face, my mind went completely blank. Sieg-san had always been a stunning beauty, an elegant, kind-looking elf onee-san, her features refined and serene. Her visual charm alone was overwhelming from the start.","And now, probably because I was her lover, she leaned against me with an expression that felt just a little unguarded. The starlight cast a soft glow over her face, faintly flushed with alcohol...... and, well, it hit me again just how unbelievably cute she was. It was a shock that somehow brought a sudden reaffirmation.","[Ah, sorry. I completely forgot what I was about to ask.]","[Fufu, that happens sometimes. If you remember, tell me, okay?]","[Yes.]","Chuckling softly, Sieg-san rubbed her cheek against my chest. It was too cute. Tonight, she seemed even more relaxed and affectionate than usual, she felt more open, more willing to show her softness. Because of that contrast with her usual demeanor, every gesture she made felt extra adorable.","[Hm?]","[Ah, errr......]","Apparently I had been staring at her too intently, lost in admiration, and Sieg-san tilted her head with a slightly puzzled look.","While I hesitated over how to answer, Sieg-san smiled gently and spoke.","[......How about...... a kiss?]","[Eh? Ah, yes. Then, excuse me......]","That actually wasn’t what I’d meant at all, but because I had been staring at her face, Sieg-san seemed to think I wanted to kiss her, and that I had been waiting for the right moment since she had been drinking.","And well...... when the person you adore, someone so beautiful that you can’t help but stare, asks you something like that, of course you get in the mood. I nodded to her suggestion, leaned in, and pressed my lips to hers.","[Nn......]","Maybe it was because we were both drinking, or because she was feeling a little shy...... but compared to the kiss from before, Sieg-san’s lips felt warmer tonight. That warmth was impossibly pleasant, and before I knew it, I was completely absorbed in the moment.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai (full body konpeito) : [.............]","Makina : [munch munch...... fumu... hmm...... mun!]","Serious-senpai : [Hah!? M- My body is back to normal...... Makina, did you turn me back? I appreciate it, but with this sugar level, I’ll probably turn into konpeito again any moment......]","Makina : [It’s fine. I adjusted it so you won’t turn into konpeito anymore before restoring you.]","Serious-senpai : [Oh right... you are a god huh. Huh. I thought you were just a totally insane, unhinged weirdo, but I guess you actually have some—————]","Makina : [I’m getting tired of konpeito, so I adjusted you so that next time, you’ll turn into a star-shaped milky cookie.]","Serious-senpai : [.........You were the same insane, unhinged weirdo as always......... I was a fool to think better of you even for a second.]"]},{"number":2429,"title":"Chapter 2429: Chapter 2430: Stargazing Wine 5","paragraphs":["Watching the meteor shower while quietly sharing a drink with Sieg-san was deeply comforting, giving me the sense that time itself was drifting along more slowly.","No, in fact, more time had likely passed than I felt, but perhaps the calm atmosphere was what made it seem to flow so gently.","[......Come to think of it, when I went back to Rigforeshia, it was nighttime as well, and I feel like most of the times I drink with Kaito-san are at night.]","[True...... well, neither you nor I drink during the day anyway. If we drank together in the daytime, it would probably be tea.]","[I see, then it’s only natural that we’d drink at night more often. Though honestly, I almost never drink in the first place......]","[Ah, right, aside from times like this when we drink together, I don’t think I’ve ever really seen you drinking. Even at the ship party you were holding juice, weren’t you?]","Now that I thought about it, I could hardly remember ever seeing Sieg-san drink alcohol at all. Really, it was only times like this, sharing a quiet drink together. At the ship party and even at my birthday party, she hadn’t touched any alcoholic drinks.","[Given my position as Lili’s guard, you know. I can sober up instantly if I want to, but there’s still the matter of public perception. Even if I’m attending an event as an individual, I generally don’t drink alcohol where many eyes are on me.]","[I see.]","Indeed, just like during the ship party or at my birthday party, even when Sieg-san is attending purely as an individual, she is usually serving as Lilia-san’s guard, so there must be many situations where people still perceive her as Lilia-san’s escort.","At events she attends on her own, it is not as if drinking alcohol is forbidden, and in reality, those around us probably do not pay that much attention to it. Even so, there are undoubtedly aspects she has to be mindful of, and it might be difficult for her to enjoy drinking freely.","[And on a simpler note, I have far more chances to drink tea. I love tea, so I’m more likely to think of drinking tea before I think of drinking alcohol. Which naturally means I end up drinking alcohol less often.]","[Yeah, the image of you drinking tea is much stronger than that of you drinking alcohol.]","[I do like alcohol just fine though...... except for beer.]","[Oh, right, you said you weren’t good with it.]","[Wine or fruit liquor, I mostly stick to those.]","I remembered her once saying that she disliked both ales and lagers. Wine too, but Sieg-san preferred fruit-based alcohols, and didn’t seem to care much for anything else.","While those thoughts drifted through my mind, Sieg-san let out a soft, amused sigh.","[But if I’m drinking at night like this with you, Kaito-san, then alcohol is better. Tea just doesn’t have enough romantic atmosphere for this kind of mood......]","[If it’s at night, then yeah, something like wine definitely feels more like...... well, a nice moment shared between lovers.]","[Yes. So for me, alcohol is something I only drink with someone I feel I can truly relax around...... let’s put it that way.]","Sieg-san smiled with a hint of mischief, and it was incredibly adorable. Or rather, today her mood seemed a little more upbeat than usual. She still had her usual calm, gentle air, of course, but on top of that, she was showing so many cute expressions that I couldn’t help feeling happy.","[......Ah, right. Another reason I don’t drink very often is that I don’t feel like drinking when I have work the next day. I mean, I can instantly erase any intoxication, but still......]","[Ah, I get that. Thanks to Shiro-san’s blessing, I can sober up immediately if I want to, and my breath doesn’t end up smelling like alcohol either...... but if I have something scheduled early the next morning, I don’t feel like drinking. Arehh? So that means...... Sieg-san, do you have the day off tomorrow?]","[Yes. My next shift is the night watch the day after tomorrow, so from now until then I have about two full days off.]","[Ohh, then it sounds like you’ll be able to relax quite a bit.]","Sieg-san worked as a guard at Lilia-san’s mansion. She herself said \"Nothing really happens, so it’s basically patrols and training or giving instruction, it’s a very easy job\", but her shifts alternated between day and night, and she also accompanied Lilia-san whenever she went out, so all things considered, it seemed like a demanding position.","[That’s right, relax and......]","[Unn?]","[Ah, no, I’ll say it a little later, so please don’t mind it.]","Sieg-san had been laughing cheerfully, but midway, she stopped and stared straight at my face. When I tilted my head in confusion, she just smiled wryly and said she’d tell me later.","As she raised her glass, she seemed to murmur something quietly under her breath, but I couldn’t catch what it was. It did make me curious, but since she said she’d talk about it later, I decided to just wait.","[......Since staying up late wouldn’t be a problem...... and staying in a different room would also be...... That said, I should probably confirm Kaito-san’s plans for tomorrow first......]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [G- Ghaaagh, a shared-bed flag......? M- My body is really turning into a star-shaped cookie......]","Makina : [munch munch]","Serious-senpai : [Kuh, because I’ve become a milky, crumbly cookie, this deranged god is eating me again......]","Makina : [Mm, no, you’re a little moist, so you don’t really have that crispiness...... but the flavor’s good. 85 points.]","Serious-senpai : [You’re eating my body, criticizing it, and giving it a score!?]"]},{"number":2430,"title":"Chapter 2430: Chapter 2431: Stargazing Wine 6","paragraphs":["After I came to the hill with Sieg-san and we started watching the meteor shower, about an hour had passed when the number of shooting stars in the night sky began to dwindle.","It seemed that the time we arrived had been the peak of the meteor shower, and from this point on, while there were still shooting stars, their numbers were no longer as high.","Even so, the amount was about the same as the meteor showers in the world I used to live in...... well, if that blindingly bright cascade of countless meteors we saw earlier continued all night long, that would be exhausting, so perhaps this level was just right.","[......Come to think of it, are the ones managing the stars in the night sky subordinates of Life-san?]","[Yes. I’ve heard that the Goddess of Stars...... God of Star-sama, governs the laws of the stars. And since it is night, God of Night Sky-sama is also involved. Both are high-ranking Gods...... and they should be under Sky-sama’s authority. I do not know the details myself though......]","I see, a God who governs the night sky, and a God who governs the stars...... that being the case, there is probably a God who governs the daytime sky as well. And Sky-san, the God of Sky, oversees those sky-related Gods, while Life-san oversees most natural phenomena, from sky to earth, all together.","If the God of Star grants a blessing, would it be called the Blessing of the Stars then? The phrase has a cool ring to it, and I feel like Amel-san would get extremely excited about it.","Arehh? Unn? A phrase suddenly popped into my head......","\"The Blessing of the Polar Star God.\"","......Arehh? Why did that phrase come to mind? Where did \"Polar\" come from?","[......Sieg-san, is \"God of Star\" the correct title for the Goddess of Stars? Not something like \"Polar Star God\"?]","[Polar Star? No, the Goddess of Stars is rather well-known among the high-ranking Gods, but I have never heard her referred to as Polar Star.]","[......I see...... Well, I just suddenly had the words Polar Star God pop into my head......]","[Perhaps that is how she is known among the Gods, and you may have heard that title somewhere before, Kaito-san.]","[Ah, that makes sense. It’s possible I happened to hear it in passing during a conversation with someone like Fate-san.]","Or maybe spending time with Amel-san awakened some dormant chuunibyou instincts inside me...... w- well, it’s nothing worth worrying about. If I ever get the chance to meet her, I can ask then.","[......Well, setting that aside, Sieg-san, shall we keep drinking here? Or should we head home and continue there?]","[Let me think. I do feel bad making Bell-chan be my backrest this whole time, so perhaps we should head back for now...... and we still haven’t tried the fruit liquor, so let’s continue after we return.]","[Then shall we drink in my room?]","[That sounds nice. It also aligns with my objective...... ah, no, I mean, your room is more spacious than mine. If it’s all right with you, I’d love to.]","Both Sieg-san and I are the type to drink slowly, so there was still plenty of wine left, and we still hadn’t tried the ripple liquor Sieg-san first suggested. We agreed to go back and drink a fresh round.","Honestly, it wasn’t just that I wanted to drink more, the desire to spend more time drinking with Sieg-san was strong, so I was fully in favor of continuing in my room.","Having decided on our course of action, Sieg-san and I did a quick cleanup and then called out to Bell.","Around that time, in a far, faraway world...... a world separated by countless dimensional walls, a certain World Creator suddenly jolted upright from her chair.","[I just felt as if my First Star called out to me!?]","『Outputting exasperation...... <No, I’m pretty sure he absolutely didn’t call you. I mean, you two haven’t even met, right?> ......To my knowledge, Polar Star God has yet to meet Kaito-sama.』","[N- No, well, that may be true...... but just now, somehow, it felt like my heart resonated with my First Star’s...... like our hearts connected...... the resonance of love, perhaps?] ṜâNȪʙƐS̈","『Outputting additional exasperation...... <You should probably leave the delusions there. A lot of people are going to get mad at you.> ......At the very least, the fan club won’t stay quiet.』","[Gnnghh...... h- hmmm, I see, that’s unfortunate...... If it were my First Star’s request, I was thinking I could skip ahead in the order and go see him...... number 238 huh...... When will I ever get to meet my First Star......]","Electrone, who happened to be nearby, told her this in an exasperated tone, and the small, childlike World Creator...... Polar Star God slumped her shoulders in defeat.","『If you were to skip the order, you’d be facing the enraged Bipolar God next, you know......』","[......Right, the next one was that monster...... even if I could skip ahead, I’d rather be after the Bipolar God...... No, not that I can skip in the first place......]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......I- It stopped at 70%...... b- but the way the story just slid smoothly into drinking together in his room...... this is bad, really bad......]","Makina : [......\"Setting-change beam so the remaining part of Serious-senpai turns into fruit jam\"...... Alright!]","Serious-senpai : [The heck are you changing me into jam for!?]"]},{"number":2431,"title":"Chapter 2431: Chapter 2432: Stargazing Wine 7","paragraphs":["After returning home, we decided to have another drink in my room, but just as we arrived, Sieg-san made a suggestion.","[Kaito-san, if we start drinking again now, it will get fairly late, so how about we both take our baths first?]","[Ah, right. We just got back from outside anyway, so taking a bath first sounds good...... Will an hour later in my room work?]","[Yes. Well then, I will see you later.]","And so, we agreed that we should both bathe first. Since we had already finished dinner, by the time we finished drinking, it would be late enough that going straight to bed wouldn’t be strange, so having a bath beforehand really was the best choice.","I went into my home and straight toward the bathroom, lightly touching the magic tool installed at the entrance before heading to my room. That device was a bath magic tool that automatically filled the tub when activated, a very convenient invention.","The same applies to Lilia-san’s mansion, but the bath in my house is quite large. From my old-world perspective, it feels like unbelievable water waste, but with magic tools, things change a lot.","The bath magic tool in my house creates the hot water with magic, and after use, performing a certain operation converts the water back into magic power. Thanks to this extremely eco-friendly function, I can enjoy the first bath of the day not just once, but as many times as I want.","And since filling the tub only takes a few minutes, it’s incredibly convenient.","Incidentally, this bath magic tool is also installed in the bath of Lilia-san’s mansion. Heck, it seems to be a popular magic tool among high-ranking nobles, and households of Count rank or higher almost always have one.","Well, it is extremely convenient, but it’s also a large-scale magic tool, so naturally it’s expensive. On top of that, shrinking it is apparently difficult, meaning the bathroom inevitably becomes large, so only nobles with considerable financial means can afford to install one.","These kinds of large-scale magic tools might be considered the specialty of magic tools. But when it comes to fine, delicate functions, machines still win. Air-conditioning in particular is hard for magic tools, you can’t do detailed temperature control or quick switching. Even a magic tool on the level of an electric fan costs about the same as an air conditioner, so while Symphonia has a stable climate year-round, general citizens in cold countries like Archlesia Empire have a hard time with it.","Well, if you can use magic, learning a spell that adjusts the temperature around your body might actually be cheaper.","Thinking about such things, I returned to my room, checked the area around the sofa where I would probably be drinking with Sieg-san, and since everything looked fine, I headed to the bath and washed up.","Sieg-san might need more time, but I definitely don’t need an hour to bathe. Should I prepare something? But Sieg-san already made the snacks, and between the leftover wine and the ripple liquor, we have more than enough to drink.","In that case, there’s nothing special to prepare...... Ah, right. I received that cat-ear device, the one that plays music, from Electrone-san as a birthday present. Playing some nice music could make the atmosphere feel stylish.","A room filled with elegant music, holding a wine glass, spending the evening with one's lover...... that sounds really good. The only problem is that for me, \"elegant music\" basically just means classical music. Someone like Ozma-san would probably pick something that fits the mood perfectly without effort......","(Please excuse the sudden intrusion into your mind. Outputting apology and explanation...... <I’m sorry for suddenly interrupting you, Kaito-sama. I sensed that you thought of me for a moment, and I reflexively confirmed it with omniscience.> ......I apologize for startling you and for rudely peeking into the situation without permission.)","......Good evening, Electrone-san. Well, I’m pretty used to Shiro-san doing this sort of thing, so it’s fine. Is this some sort of cross-world communication? In any case, I’m happy we get to talk again.","(Outputting deep emotion...... <My oshi is endlessly kind! I’m so smitten it hurts......> Now outputting the main point...... <I’m sorry. Let me get to the point. About the device I gave you, even if you don’t specify a song title or genre, it has a mode that plays music that fits the atmosphere. It automatically chooses something suitable based on Kaito-sama’s mental state and mood. Just think \"auto mode\" when you turn it on and press the switch!> ......Explanation complete.)","I see, so it has such a convenient function...... Thank you for taking the time to tell me. I imagine things must be complicated since we’re in different worlds, but if you ever have the chance, please come visit again.","(Outputting overwhelming emotion...... <My oshi’s preciousness is overflowing. With the way I am now, I could probably beat ten Omnipotent and Omniscient beings at once.> ......Thank you for your kind words. When that time comes, I would be very happy to speak with you again. Thank you for taking the time to talk with this unit...... This concludes the transmission.)","Thank you as well.","......So she can communicate from another world too...... Well, for an Omnipotent and Omniscient God, that’s probably nothing. Rather, starting the conversation with an apology really shows how remarkably normal and considerate she always is.","<Afterword>","Virtual Angel : [Outputting intuition...... <Hah!? My oshi is thinking about me!!!>]","Noja Loli : [......Aren’t you saying almost the exact same thing I just did?]","Virtual Angel : [Please refrain from equating this with your delusions of grandeur. In this case, there is an undeniable fact that this unit’s name actually was thought of.] RåNốBĘŝ","Noja Loli : [I see...... Guess I’ll call the gorilla......]","Virtual Angel : [Cease your interference. For the noble purpose of answering Kaito-sama’s question, this unit must obtain interworld-communication authorization from Shallow Vernal. Should the summoning of a dangerous creature cause a delay in delivering my answer to Kaito-sama, that responsibility shall be attributed to the Polar Star God. Do you accept that?]","Noja Loli : [Ugh...... I can’t trouble the First Star...... Fine. I’m jealous, but I’ll just sit here and watch with my fingers in my mouth......]"]},{"number":2432,"title":"Chapter 2432: Chapter 2433: Stargazing Wine 8","paragraphs":["After getting out of the bath and doing only the simplest preparations, I relaxed and read a book while waiting. About five minutes before the promised time, there was a knock at the door.","Certain that it must be Sieg-san, I answered, put the book away into the Magic Box, and headed for the door to greet her. When I opened the door...... just as expected, Sieg-san was standing there.","[Sorry to keep you waiting.]","[No, your timing was perfect. Come in.]","[Excuse my intrusion.]","As I let Sieg-san into the room, I found myself a little shaken. The reason was her outfit. The sleeveless top was nothing unusual for her, but this one seemed loose and relaxed, perhaps meant as sleepwear. It was slightly oversized, and she wore short pants so brief they didn’t even reach halfway down her thighs. She was dressed far more lightly than I had imagined.","No, it suited her, and she looked incredibly cute...... but Sieg-san was on the tall side with long legs, and with her in short pants, my eyes kept flicking toward those beautiful legs.","And her top was also rather risky. Being both sleeveless and oversized, whenever she moved it felt like her chest might be visible from the side, leaving me nervous and on edge.","[Ah, this sofa over here, please.]","[Yes. I’ll go ahead and set the food out on the table.]","[Thank you. Then I’ll take care of this......]","[That is...... the one Kaito-san received from Electrone-sama, if I recall......]","[Yeah. Apparently, it has a function that automatically plays music to match the atmosphere, so I thought it’d be nice to drink while listening to something classy. This room is well-insulated, so sound won’t leak and bother anyone...... or well, even if it did leak, there’s no one using the rooms within hearing distance anyway......]","My house was simply too large for the number of people living in it, leaving plenty of spare rooms. The rooms around mine were also currently unused.","At some point, they might end up as hobby rooms, the way Lilia-san made her collection room, so it seemed that several rooms, including the ones next to mine, were being intentionally kept empty by people like Anima or Illness-san.","Well, even without that, the house wasn’t built in a way that would let sound leak outside or into neighboring rooms, so playing music at night wasn’t a problem at all.","I activated the cat-ear device in automatic mode, and before long, a calm and beautiful melody started to play. The audio quality was extremely good, like listening to a live performance, and was wonderful...... but it suddenly began playing an incredibly moody piece......","[That’s a nice song.]","[It is. Something you’d expect to hear in a bar, fits well.]","It had the atmosphere of a mature evening, perfectly suited for the situation of drinking together with a lover.","[Well then, shall we start with the rest of the wine?]","[Yes. A toast?]","[Good idea, since the mood’s right...... then, cheers.]","[Cheers.]","We lightly tapped our glasses and began our evening drink once again. It was strange, though it was the same wine, the shift in atmosphere changed how it tasted. Compared to drinking it on the hill beneath the stars, it now felt deeper and more serene.","At that moment, Sieg-san leaned lightly against me just as she had on the hill.","Maybe because she had just bathed, she smelled wonderful, and her body was slightly warm. Her touch also felt softer. No, it made sense, she was dressed far lighter than when we drank on the hill, so her warmth and the feel of her body were much easier to sense.","With the pleasant music blending into the atmosphere, everything took on a soft, intimate tone...... No, honestly, having an evening drink alone with my lover, in my own room, with nothing pressing the next day and the mood being absolutely perfect, at that point, not being conscious of it would be impossible.","[It’s delicious.]","[It is...... errr, Sieg-san.]","[Yes?]","On top of everything, the emotions coming through Sieg-san via Sympathy Magic were familiar...... the same kind I had felt when she invited me to stay out with her before.","Thinking back, she had prepared everything that time too, guiding the situation forward, and it felt like things were happening in a similar way tonight.","Considering that, I could guess what she meant earlier on the hill when she said she would tell me \"later\"...... but rather than waiting for her, I felt like it was something I should say myself. Maybe it was just my imagination, but I had the feeling Sieg-san was waiting for me to speak up.","[......Would you like to stay in my room tonight? There’s only one bed, but it’s big enough for the two of us.]","[......Yes. I was hoping it would turn out that way...... so I’m happy.]","Pushed forward by the mood and everything around us, I finally said it. Sieg-san smiled softly, looking genuinely pleased, and relaxed against me, leaning in even closer.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai (Cookies & Jam) : [........................]","Makina : [munch munch...... When you pair it with the jam, it’s a solid 90 points...... munch munch...... hmph!]","Serious-senpai : [Hah!? M- My body is turning ba——— gwaaah!? T- This sugar content! Why would you revive me at a time like this...... I- Isn’t this like turning me into something like that Stomachache Warrior who’s been forbidden from fainting......?]"]},{"number":2433,"title":"Chapter 2433: Chapter 2434: Stargazing Wine 9","paragraphs":["We had already finished most of the wine back on the hill, so before long we shifted over to ripple wine. I’d had it once before, when we went to Rigforeshia, and its refreshing taste felt pleasant.","[Speaking of ripple, today I heard something about a golden ripple.]","[Golden ripple? That’s something I’ve never heard before. Is it supposed to be a gold-colored ripple?]","[No, it seems to be more like a rumor spread for marketing purposes. It apparently doesn’t actually exist, but people say it’s the most delicious ripple in the world. If, just hypothetically, it did exist, do you think ripple wine made from it would taste good?]","[There’s a certain romance to the idea. But in reality, it might be difficult. I’m not an expert, so I can’t say for sure, but something that tastes good to eat doesn’t necessarily make good wine.]","[Ah, right, like grapes. Wine grapes tend to have stronger acidity or stronger flavors, so personal tastes vary. Ripples might be the same.]","Just as Sieg-san said, a ripple that’s delicious to eat and a ripple that’s delicious as a wine probably aren’t the same, and the world’s tastiest ripple wouldn’t automatically make the world’s best ripple wine......","Well, the golden ripple itself is basically an urban legend, so this was just idle chatter anyway......","[Kaito-san, you said you like ripple pie, but do you also like ripple as a fruit?]","[It might be my favorite among fruits. Otherwise, mikan...... errr, oranges are good too. Maybe I just like fruits with a bit of sourness. Ah, but I like strawberries as well, so it’s hard to narrow it down to just one.]","[I see. I like fruits in general too, but if you ask me which is the best, I’d have to think about it. Among fruit wines, though, ripple wine is my favorite......]","[Really? Now that you mention it, you were drinking ripple wine in Rigforeshia too.]","Sieg-san usually drinks either fruit wine or simple wine, and it seems ripple wine is her favorite. I don’t know much about fruit wines myself, but I’ve seen orange, muscat, peach, strawberry...... and apparently there are mixed varieties as well.","But now that she mentioned it, I realized she really is almost always drinking ripple wine.","[......To be precise, it became my favorite because of the ripple wine we had that day in Rigforeshia.]","[Eh?]","[It was the drink we shared during the memorable trip where I became your lover. Thanks to the happy memories, I’ve grown to love it even more than before.]","[......I see...... But now that you say that, the ripple wine I drink with you does feel especially delicious.]","[Fufufu, then we feel the same.]","Sieg-san leaned against me happily, and I wrapped an arm around her shoulder, pulling her close. She was lightly dressed, so the closeness felt intense, and whether it was the alcohol or simply being aware of her warmth, I felt my heart racing.","It’d be a lie to say there wasn’t anything about it that made me overly conscious, but including that, it was a warm, blissful moment with someone I loved, a comforting happiness shared between lovers.","We spent a while drinking and chatting, and when we finished the bottle of ripple wine Sieg-san had prepared, our evening drink came to an end.","After that, we each got ready for bed in a simple, quick way, then got under the covers together and dimmed the lights. The only light left was the small illumination magic tool by the bedside, set to its weakest glow, so it wasn’t completely dark.","[......Come to think of it, when we went back to Rigforeshia, we also slept in the same bed.]","[Yeah, thanks to Rei-san and Fia-san fooling around...... It feels kind of nostalgic now.]","We did indeed sleep in the same bed when I stayed at Sieg-san’s home. Back then, we slept back-to-back, both of us trying desperately not to be conscious of the other.","Now we were lying face-to-face, and as my eyes adjusted to the darkness, I could clearly see Sieg-san’s face looking at me.","[I asked a strange question back then...... Do you remember?]","[Yes. I remember being at a complete loss for how to answer.]","I remembered that conversation clearly. Because Rei-san had teased her about her underwear, Sieg-san ended up asking me something like \"If you hypothetically saw me in my underwear, would you get excited?\" and I had been forced to answer. ꭆä₦oʙÊș","At the time, Sieg-san’s self-esteem had been pretty low. She seemed to think she didn’t have much charm as a woman. Well, I also got called out for having low self-esteem myself.","[Back then, we were both kind of lacking in confidence, weren’t we?]","[Fufu, that’s true. But now, I fully understand, through experience, that what you said at the time was true. So perhaps...... I’m able to feel just a little more confident than before.]","[You can have all the confidence in the world...... Sieg-san, you were charming even back then, but now you’re even more charming, an absolutely wonderful woman.]","[......I’m sure...... it’s because you made me that way.]","As her gentle, sweet voice drifted to me, I felt Sieg-san’s arm slide around my back...... And from there onward, no further words were needed.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Fugwah...... ah...... ggh...... I- I can’t...... I’m gonna die...... wait, what the heck!? My body, turning into liquid!? And even though it’s liquid, my body's still properly shaped!?]","Makina : [......Well, I was thirsty, so I turned you into mixed juice......]","Serious-senpai : [You——— You can’t just mess with people’s bodies however you want! Hey, stop that!!! Don’t stick a straw in me!!! You’re always treating people like snacks...... wait! I- Is the reason my body sometimes turns into sugar...... because of you!?]","Makina : [No, I don’t know anything about that. I didn’t do anything.]","Serious-senpai : [......Ah...... o- okay then......]"]},{"number":2434,"title":"Chapter 2434: Chapter 2435: Spreading Aftermath 26","paragraphs":["The first thing she saw when she opened her eyes was a completely unfamiliar sight.","[......A ceiling I don’t recognize. W- Where am I......]","Sitting up in the bed, Marie darted her gaze around restlessly. The room she was in was easily more than twice the size of her bedroom back at the Barony, and every piece of furniture was clearly of high quality at a glance.","Her clothes, too, were an elegant set of nightwear, and the bed itself was far larger and finer than anything she was accustomed to. Every detail of her surroundings was on a different level from her usual life.","At the very least, this was not her family home, the Ritch Barony, and it didn’t seem like a luxury inn either. The Ritch Barony simply didn’t have the wealth to rent such a room for lodging.","(......Eh? Seriously, where am I? What happened to me......? I- I remember meeting up with Father...... and then...... losing consciousness in the carriage......)","Marie, who had just begun to sort through her thoughts to understand the situation, was startled out of her attempts when someone knocked on the door and politely asked for permission to enter. Grateful for the chance to get information, she immediately granted it.","A maid stepped inside and bowed to her.","[Good morning, Marie-sama. I’ve come to assist you with preparing for the day.]","[Ah, errr...... I’m sorry. I don’t really understand the situation. Where is this?]","[This is a guest room in the main residence of the Hamilton Marquisdom. You lost consciousness in the carriage, and at Lady Eris’s instruction, we prepared this room for you. You seemed quite exhausted, Marie-sama, you slept soundly through the entire night.]","[A- Ahh...... I see...... M- My apologies for troubling the Marquis and for Eris-sama......]","[Not at all. His Lordship and the young lady both said it was entirely understandable, so please don’t worry. However, they would like to ask you for more details about your circumstances, so once you’re ready, you’ll be escorted to the conference room. If you’re hungry, I can bring you a light meal......]","Marie nodded, accepting the explanation. It made sense, what she’d managed to tell Baron Ritch in the carriage was fragmented, and the part involving Kaito, which was surely the most concerning, could only be clarified by asking her directly.","Thanks to a full night’s rest, Marie had regained some of her emotional stability; at the very least, she was in a better state to explain things than she had been yesterday.","[......No, I’m not very hungry...... i- if anything, my stomach feels like it’s only going to hurt even more soon, so I’ll pass on the food. I’m so sorry. If I could have a drink instead......]","[I’ll prepare it at once.]","The maid left briefly, then returned with tea. Marie moved to the table near the bed and took a sip, letting out a small breath as the warmth calmed her. The maid then presented her with exceptionally fine clothing...... although still within a range that wouldn’t be inappropriate for a Baron’s daughter. 𐍂ÁɴO͍βƐꞩ","[Lady Eris requested that you wear these today...... The clothes you wore yesterday will be washed and sent to the Ritch Barony, so please use these for the day.]","[T- Thank you very much.]","[Would you like assistance changing?]","[Ah, no, it’s fine. I usually dress myself......]","[As you wish. I’ll step out for now. If you require anything, just touch the magic tool there and I’ll come immediately.]","The maid bowed and departed.","Left alone, Marie stared into the distance as her thoughts drifted toward what awaited her next.","After finishing her tea and getting dressed, Marie followed the maid’s guidance to the conference room. Inside, the key figures were already gathered: Baron Ritch, Marquis and Marchioness Hamilton, and Eris.","[Oh, Marie. How are you feeling?]","[I’m alright. I’m very sorry for the trouble I’ve caused you, Marquis Hamilton, Marchioness, and Eris-sama.]","[Please don’t worry about that. We truly understand what you must be feeling...... If anything, I’m sorry we had to summon you when you should still be resting. We’ve gathered some information on our end, but there are many things only you, the person involved, can clarify. Please tell us in detail about your exchange with Kaito-sama.]","Eris, with whom Marie had at least some prior acquaintance, stepped in gently to ease her tension, and the Hamilton couple nodded in agreement.","[Errr...... would it be all right if I explained everything from the beginning?]","[Yes, that would help very much...... I’m sorry, but the circumstances have changed somewhat...... This matter involves Divine Protections, so we need to coordinate with Her Majesty Chris. Her Majesty has no direct involvement in the situation, of course, but she does wish to hear your account personally. So we will need to move to the Imperial Castle first, and you can give your explanation there.]","[Eek...... I- I understand.]","Feeling overwhelmed by Eris’ words, Marie nodded, unconsciously placing a hand over her stomach. This would be her very first time entering the Imperial Castle, and her first time speaking directly with the Emperor, Chris. Her stomach already hurt just thinking about it.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Breaktime is over...... Let us resume.]"]},{"number":2435,"title":"Chapter 2435: Chapter 2436: Spreading Aftermath 28","paragraphs":["Since Chris was the one who originally summoned everyone, the key figures gathered in one of the Imperial Castle’s rooms with remarkable smoothness. This time, the attendees were Marie, the person directly involved, and her father, Baron Ritch. Then there was Marquis Hamilton, the head of Hamilton Marquisdom and the one expected to support the Ritch Barony in this matter, and Eris, the Archlesia Empire noble who, after Chris, had the most contact with Kaito. Aside from those four, only Chris and a few of her close aides were present, making for a very small meeting.","[My apologies for calling you here on such short notice. But I judged that, as Emperor, I needed to understand the circumstances of this matter. Anything related to Miyama-sama has the potential to turn into a major incident if handled poorly, so I’d like us to coordinate properly and deal with this carefully. Also, for the sake of keeping matters smooth, I’ll omit the house names and titles of Eris Dia Hamilton and Marie Ritch here, and simply address them as Lady Eris and Lady Marie. Lady Marie, this is the first time we've met, but formal greetings aren’t necessary, and no one will be reprimanded for lapses in etiquette or speech. Please speak freely without fear. The same applies to everyone else present, feel free to speak your mind.]","Chris briefly stated this at the beginning, noticing how tense Baron Ritch and Marie, both low-ranking nobles, were in the Imperial Castle, and reassuring them that their conduct wouldn’t be judged.","Before long, the discussion everyone here most wanted to hear began, Marie’s account. Nervous as she was, she explained everything she remembered, starting from the moment she first encountered Kaito.","As for the content itself, Baron Ritch repeatedly went pale, but the others remained calm throughout.","[......I see, I understand the situation. First, let me ease your worries, Lady Marie. Based on what you told us, there was nothing that could be considered disrespectful toward Miyama-sama or anyone around him.]","[R- Really......? B- But I accepted so many incredibly expensive gifts......]","[It’s natural you’d feel that way, Marie-sama, but when actually compared to Kaito-sama’s assets, those things wouldn’t strain him in the slightest. Considering his personality, I imagine he’s simply pleased that you accepted his goodwill honestly.]","Regarding her fear of having accepted goods worth more than three white gold coins, Chris and Eris both assured her it was not an issue. Hearing that, Marie and Baron Ritch visibly relaxed.","But only for a moment, Chris’s expression sharpened immediately after.","[......However, it’s possible this matter could lead in a rather troublesome direction.]","[Eh? Ehhh......]","[First, let me confirm something. Lady Marie, is there any fact indicating that you and Miyama-sama have become lovers, or even have some relationship close to that?]","[N- No! Absolutely not! I- I don’t mean that Kaito-sama lacks masculine charm or anything like that, but we’ve known each other for less than 10 days, and we’ve only met twice, including yesterday......]","Hearing Marie’s panicked answer, Chris nodded once and continued.","[It seems one of my subordinates happened to see Miyama-sama giving Lady Marie clothing at the store, so I asked just to be sure.]","[Y- Your Majesty, then...... are you saying rumors have already spread of Marie being romantically involved with Miyama Kaito-sama......?]","[No. Even though it only happened yesterday, there isn’t the slightest sign of such rumors circulating.]","When Chris gave that answer, the pale Baron Ritch and Marie looked relieved...... while Eris and Marquis Hamilton both grew grim.","[......Your Majesty Chris, in other words...... despite Kaito-sama and Marie-sama being seen in a high-class shopping district and a café, places where nobles and related individuals often appear...... no one is talking about it?]","[Yes. Of course, there’s always a chance it spreads later...... but I believe we can safely assume that Alice-sama has intervened.]","[......This is an even worse situation than I imagined.]","[Indeed. Things actually would’ve been simpler if the rumors had just spread normally.]","[ [ Eh? ] ]","Chris nodded at Eris’ serious question, and even Marquis Hamilton stated gravely that the situation was bad. Baron Ritch and Marie, who didn’t understand why that was, looked confused.","Seeing this, Eris turned toward Marie and began to explain in simple terms.","[Marie-sama, for you, if rumors spread through high society that you and Kaito-sama are romantically involved, you would certainly attract curious attention and life would become troublesome...... However, such rumors spreading in noble society would have almost no effect on Kaito-sama himself. He has virtually no involvement with noble society, and at this point, even if people whispered that he’d gained another noblewoman lover, it’s doubtful anyone with ulterior motives would dare approach him.]","[E- Errr, in other words?]","[In this situation, even if the rumor spreads among the nobility, the ones who would suffer trouble would just be Baron Ritch and Lady Marie...... not Kaito-sama. Meaning, there should be no reason for Phantasmal King-sama to intervene. But according to Her Majesty Chris, Phantasmal King-sama has intervened.] ṛАNobÊS̩","[......Alice-sama normally just remains an observer when a matter poses no harm to Miyama-sama. But on rare occasions, even when it doesn’t directly affect him, she steps in to assist our side. And that only happens when she sees a situation so unfortunate that even she can’t help feeling pity...... In other words, something else is happening here. Something in this case has caused Alice-sama to feel that Lady Marie deserves at least a bit of her help......]","After hearing Eris and Chris’ explanation, Marie and Baron Ritch finally grasped the meaning, and their faces turned deathly pale. There was a sense that something far greater was in motion, though they had no idea what it might be. That eerie tension hung in the air...... until a voice cut through it, sounding almost exasperated.","[Well, that’s exactly it~~ If this were just some silly rumor spreading around, I’d be sitting back laughing and enjoying a glass of wine......]","[ [ [ [ [ ! ? ] ] ] ] ]","Without anyone noticing, Alice had somehow appeared and taken a seat at the table where Chris and the others were discussing the matter. Everyone in the room felt shock, and an indescribable sense of dread.","Not only had she manipulated the information flow, she had personally appeared...... That alone suggested that something far more serious was unfolding than they had imagined......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Ah, so you actually intend to explain it properly.]","? ? ? : [Well, if we don’t warn them in advance, it’ll probably turn into a huge uproar, and Marie-san’s stomach might disintegrate from the stress......]"]},{"number":2436,"title":"Chapter 2436: Chapter 2437: Spreading Aftermath 29","paragraphs":["Alice’s sudden appearance shocked everyone, but only for a moment. Chris realized first, Eris right after, that this meant something serious. For Alice to come in person could only mean the matter was monumental beyond words......","And for her to arrive at this exact timing implied that Chris and Eris also needed to hear it...... in other words, the subject likely had major implications for the country itself.","[......Alice-sama, the fact that you’ve come all the way here...... may we interpret that to mean you intend to provide us with information we have not yet learned?]","[Correct. You’ve been more flexible lately, very impressive, Chris-san. At this rate, I could give you an appraisal worth three white gold coins. Well, dragging this out would be pointless, so let’s get straight to the main topic...... Everyone, are your stomachs prepared to be punctured?]","None of them wanted to have that kind of resolve, but it was already certain the topic was disastrous. Even the inexperienced Baron Ritch and Marie, though late to catch on, sensed the severity of the situation and looked ready to faint at any moment.","But this would almost certainly be a matter deeply tied to Baron Ritch and Marie. They couldn’t afford not to listen, so they forced themselves to stay conscious and paid close attention to Alice’s words.","[First of all, it’s not that Marie-san did anything wrong. Really, the only way to describe it is...... she had terrible luck. Anyway, about the issue, Marie-san, you talked about golden ripples with Kaito-san in the café, right?]","[......Eh? Ah, yes.]","[......Golden ripples?]","Marie nodded at Alice’s words, but the others, everyone but Marie and Baron Ritch, wore puzzled expressions, unable to recall what golden ripples referred to.","Seeing this, Baron Ritch began a simple explanation.","[The golden ripple is a kind of legend from my territory...... or rather, a story a former lord tried to spread to help sell ripples, but as you can tell by the fact none of you know it, it never became widespread. It only survives as a tale occasionally brought up in part of the territory.]","[......Ah, I see. I’ve heard that kind of story before. Something promoted as part of a marketing strategy that fails, gets forgotten by most people, and then much later someone recalls it as \"I don’t remember where I heard this, but......\", and eventually it becomes a sort of local legend.]","Hearing Baron Ritch’s explanation, Chris nodded in understanding. There had been several such cases in the past, where someone tried to spread that sort of thing but failed, and only the story itself ran off on its own, eventually turning into something like an urban legend.","[Yes, exactly. It was really nothing but a silly story, and Marie explained that properly to Kaito-san too. It’s not like he misunderstood anything. It should have been harmless small talk...... but the problem is, someone was eavesdropping on that conversation...... and she got interested in those golden ripples...... Someone up in the Sanctuary.]","[ [ [ [ [ ...................... ] ] ] ] ]","In that instant, the room fell into a silence so deep it felt as though time had stopped. Chris, Eris, Marie, Marquis Hamilton, and Baron Ritch...... not a single one of them could even react. They only stared wide-eyed.","And of course they did, Alice had said \"in the Sanctuary\"...... Anyone living in this world could immediately imagine who that referred to.","All color drained from their faces, and they began to tremble. Even so, Chris somehow managed to force out his voice.","[......A- Alice-sama...... t- that means......]","[......Yeah, I'm talking about Shallow Vernal-sama. And if it had ended there, things would’ve still been simple, but apparently, Shallow Vernal-sama handed all matters regarding the golden ripple over to Life-san. Heck, even added \"I’m looking forward to it\" when she passed the command...... So now Life-san is fired up to an absolutely terrifying degree.]","No words came out. Their minds were unnaturally clear, so clear it only emphasized how impossible it was to process what Alice was saying.","The five of them, Chris included, felt as if the words were just circling around inside their hollowed-out heads.","[......And so, with that being the situation, I expect that within the next few days, a \"golden ripple tree created by the full combined power of the Gods\" will be delivered to the Ritch Barony...... or rather, directly to Marie-san. And it’ll probably come with instructions like \"Present the first golden ripple to Shallow Vernal-sama\"...... So please brace yourselves.] ȑÁNꝋbΕŝ","Those words, as merciless as a death sentence, made Marie and Baron Ritch instantly pass out, eyes rolled back and foam bubbling from their mouths.","......And a few seconds later, Alice revived them without the slightest mercy using a Resuscitation Magic.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see, so they're not just gonna receive it huh...... She also has to offer a golden ripple they've grown on Shiro...... Marie’s stomach is done for......]"]},{"number":2437,"title":"Chapter 2437: Chapter 2438: Spreading Aftermath 30","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Due to personal matters, there will be a break tomorrow. The next update will be on the day after tomorrow.","After fainting from sheer shock and being mercilessly revived by magic several times, Marie was left slumped over with an expression that practically screamed \"So this is what despair feels like\".","She wanted nothing more than to escape reality the way she had when she went shopping with Kaito, but that had only worked because she’d been in a dreamlike daze back then. In her current state, there was no way...... More than that, even if she tried to convince herself this was all a dream, the intense pain stabbing through her stomach insisted with everything it had that this was, without a doubt, reality.","[......M- Marie-sama...... please, get a hold of yourself......]","[T- Thank goodness I didn’t eat breakfast...... If I had, I definitely would’ve thrown it all up...... E- Eris-sama...... w- w- what...... w- what am I supposed to do......]","Eris offered words of concern, and Marie looked up at her with desperate, pleading eyes. This situation was already far beyond anything she could handle. She had no idea how to deal with it, or even how she should be acting.","That was why she desperately wanted advice, anything that might help her break through this madness, from Eris, a noble of far higher standing and an undeniably gifted young woman.","But hearing Marie’s question, Eris had a painfully troubled expression on her face.","[......My apologies. But in this case...... even I can’t begin to imagine what should be done......]","If this were about one of the Six Kings, they could still work with it. Of course, that would still be a tremendous ordeal, and Marie’s stomach would still be screaming, but Eris would at least be able to offer some amount of practical advice.","But Shallow Vernal was on an entirely different tier. There were very few who had ever even spoken with Shallow Vernal directly, so there was simply no answer Eris could give.","Particularly if matters escalated to offering a golden ripple to Shallow Vernal, it would no longer be just a matter for nobles or nations. It could even affect temple authorities and believers of the Godism Church. This could easily become a situation on a global scale.","In fact, not only Eris but Chris as well was holding her head in distress. There was no avoiding the fact that a golden ripple tree would be bestowed upon Marie, and of course, there was no way to avoid having its fruit presented to Shallow Vernal.","Naturally, there was also no way for them to step in as intermediaries. They couldn’t think of a single method to help Marie in this impossible situation.","[......Ah, well, I’ve already thought of a few ways to handle this. It’s not like I came here to bully Marie-san after all......]","[P- Phantasmal King-sama......]","A saving hand extended from an unexpected direction...... hearing Alice’s words, Marie’s eyes brimmed with tears as she turned toward her.","Seeing that, Alice gave a sympathetic, wry smile before beginning her explanation.","[First of all, there’s no avoiding the fact that a golden ripple tree will be granted to you, so just accept that part. As for the very first golden ripple it produces...... give it to Kaito-san.]","[To Kaito-sama......?]","[Yes. I’ll explain everything to him myself, and then we’ll have Kaito-san deliver it to Shallow Vernal-sama. That way, Marie-san won’t have to deal with Shallow Vernal-sama directly.]","Alice paused there, raised her gaze toward the ceiling, and spoke upward.","[......That works for you, right, Shallow Vernal-sama? You’re monitoring things since I stepped in anyway, and you’re listening to this conversation too, aren’t you? I’m sure you’d be happier receiving it from Kaito-san rather than Marie-san, and afterward, you two can eat it together or whatever you want. So no issues, right?] ꭆÃNồβÊṩ","As soon as Alice finished speaking, glittering particles of light appeared on the ceiling. They gathered, forming the shape of a hand, which gave a firm thumbs-up and then vanished.","[......Well, since it seems Shallow Vernal-sama is fine with that, let's go do it that way. As long as we toss anything related to Shallow Vernal-sama at Kaito-san, he’ll handle it nicely somehow.]","[U- Understood.]","In truth, if anyone was suited to dealing with Shallow Vernal, it was Kaito. In the first place, Shallow Vernal wanted the golden ripple because she wanted to eat it with him, so if he brought it to her, she would have absolutely no complaints.","With the biggest concern, the offering to Shallow Vernal, settled at last, Marie allowed herself the smallest hint of relief but......","[......Well, do your best with everything afterward. With this being an item to be presented to Shallow Vernal, you guys will probably only be able to grow them in very small numbers, so as for what you'll do with the golden ripples afterward, you could just discuss that with Chris-san. I’ll help with some information control...... but I don’t think you’ll be able to avoid becoming the center of attention worldwide......]","[A- Abuh......]","[Well, if things get completely hopeless, you can always go cry to Kaito-san, you know?]","[S- Such discourtesy...... I- I- I- I could never......]","[......To be honest, crying to him really is the optimal solution here...... but I’ll leave that choice to you.]","In reality, Alice's suggestion, \"crying to Kaito\", might very well be the best possible solution. If Marie abandoned shame and pride and begged him outright, things would almost certainly move in the best possible direction.","Depending on how things went, Kaito might even offer to take the golden ripple tree off her hands entirely...... but whether because she was too inherently earnest, or because she still hadn’t grown close enough to him for that level of reliance...... Marie didn’t choose that optimal answer.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Hmm, but honestly, if you think about it, clinging to Kaito in tears might be the fastest and cleanest way to resolve everything...... If Kaito moves to help Marie, Alice won’t just give advice, she’ll step in with full force to support him...... and there’s also a certain God who can pretty much fix anything after something happened......]"]},{"number":2438,"title":"Chapter 2438: Chapter 2439: Spreading Aftermath 31","paragraphs":["Once Alice had finished delivering the necessary information, she vanished as if to say she had conveyed all that needed to be said. The room returned to how it had been before her appearance, though the atmosphere certainly did not.","Before Alice appeared, the discussion had mostly been Chris and Eris advising Marie on how to handle the situation. But now, that dynamic had shifted dramatically.","Given the weight of any matter involving Shallow Vernal, neither Chris nor Eris could remain uninvolved.","[......Even if we can finally see a ray of hope regarding the tribute to Shallow Vernal-sama, we will need to act with extreme caution when dealing with the golden ripples afterward. With it being a mystical fruit created by the Gods, it will inevitably carry religious implications, and there’s a chance the Godism Church might move as well. The easiest route for the country would be to give Lady Marie a title and establish her as independent under some pretext...... but that is rather unrealistic, isn’t it?]","[Y- Yes. Marie hasn’t received any of the education required of a noble family head. She’s only been trained enough to behave properly as a lower noble’s daughter. To enter political and social circles as a family head would be......]","[......It would only increase Lady Marie’s burden instead. Even if she were to start learning now, it would take too long. It would never even be in time to handle golden ripple confections popping around, so that option is impossible.]","As Emperor, Chris would have preferred to handle the golden ripple matter separately from the broader affairs of the Western Region, but from the difficult expression on Baron Ritch’s face and her own thoughts, it was clear this could not be done.","Since Marie is a young lady of the Ritch Barony, factional considerations within the nobility also came into play, which complicated the procedures further.","If Marie had already received the education necessary for a family head as Eris had, Chris would have liked to grant her a title and place her under the direct protection of the state as an important figure.","[......Complaints will arise that a high noble is interfering with the affairs of a lower noble, but in the matter of the golden ripples, the Hamilton Marquisdom should take the lead.]","[That’s true. It will cause Marquis Hamilton some trouble, but for Lady Marie and the Ritch Barony, that would be the solution with the least burden.]","Chris agreed with the words Marquis Hamilton muttered while thoughtfully touching his chin. Eris, who immediately understood their intention, also spoke after a moment of reflection.","[......At least publicly, we can present the golden ripple as a joint undertaking between the Ritch Barony and the Hamilton Marquisdom, while ensuring the impression that the Hamilton Marquisdom is leading the effort. That way, if any demands for the golden ripple are addressed to the Ritch Barony, they can refuse by saying \"The distribution rights are held by the Hamilton Marquisdom; please direct inquiries there\". If people believe the Ritch Barony holds the authority, it wouldn’t be surprising if someone attempted to pressure them by force.]","[Ahh, regarding the matter with the Sharon count family, I stayed out of it because they have enough power to handle it themselves...... but the Ritch Barony cannot possibly handle this alone.]","[Yes...... It’s embarrassing to say this, but although I am the family head, I have little experience with noble bargaining and negotiations. I can’t hope to navigate this skillfully...... If the Hamilton Marquisdom is willing to take the lead, it would be a tremendous help.]","Hearing Eris and Marquis Hamilton’s words, Baron Ritch nodded visibly in relief. This matter had long since exceeded what he could manage himself, so Hamilton Marquisdom stepping in was more than welcome.","[We’ll work out the specifics later, but the Hamilton Marquisdom will support you regarding the golden ripples. However, when it comes to the western development issue, that cannot be led by us.]","[ [ ......Western development? ] ]","Both Baron Ritch and Marie wore identical expressions, their faces clearly saying \"This is the first we’ve heard of that\".","It was natural for Marie, but Baron Ritch, with few connections to merchants and a weak information network, also had not yet learned anything about western development.","Seeing their reactions, Chris nodded lightly and began to explain the matter to Baron Ritch and Marie.","[It isn’t confirmed, merely a deduction based on the current situation...... but it appears that the Lord Trading Company is preparing for western development. Specifically, they seem to be moving toward constructing a Teleportation Gate in the Ritch Barony.]","[A- A Teleportation Gate!?]","[Eh? Ehhh...... the Lord Trading Company...... Eh? I thought it was about purchasing ripples......]","Both Baron Ritch and Marie looked utterly stunned, as though cold water had been dumped over their heads. At the same time, they remembered the letter they had received, one requesting a meeting with the Lord Trading Company.","To them, it had simply been about negotiating the purchase of ripples...... the idea that a matter as enormous as a Teleportation Gate might be involved had never even crossed their minds, so they could not keep up with the situation.","Chris then explained, along with her own predictions, the movements suggesting development in the western region and what the future might hold...... By the time she finished, Baron Ritch and Marie had gone pale as sheets, trembling uncontrollably.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Is that okay? At this rate, Marie’s stomach might not even exist anymore.]","? ? ? : [What’s really terrifying is that, timeline-wise, it hasn’t even been 10 days since Kaito-san and Marie-san met.]","Serious-senpai : [The Stomachache Devil is way too devilish......]"]},{"number":2439,"title":"Chapter 2439: Chapter 2440: Spreading Aftermath 32","paragraphs":["The discussion to set a general direction ended with an agreement: the Hamilton Marquisdom would take charge of matters concerning the golden ripples, while the Archlesia Empire would support the construction of the Teleportation under the banner of western regional development. With that finally settled, Baron Ritch and Marie at last, one could almost say finally, returned home.","[.....Somehow, it feels like it’s been ages since we were last here.]","[I feel the same...... Anyway, Marie, you must also be exhausted. Take your time and rest today. There are plenty of things we still need to discuss, but that can wait until tomorrow.]","[That would be great. I’m really at my limit......]","Both Baron Ritch and Marie wore utterly worn-out expressions. For impoverished frontier nobles like them...... finding themselves caught up in a situation on a national, perhaps even global, scale had clearly taken a heavy toll.","Even so, with people like Chris, Marquis Hamilton, and Eris, individuals far more experienced and capable than the two of them, promising their cooperation, a faint glimmer of hope could be seen in the future.","[......At this rate, Father might even get promoted in rank, don’t you think?]","[Despite having accomplished nothing? Well, Her Majesty could attach whatever reason she wished if she felt like doing it...... but honestly, I’d rather she didn’t. A higher rank means more responsibilities, and I really don’t have the time or the leeway for that. Besides, there’s no real advantage in promoting me. If anything, formally granting you a title seems far more likely.]","[That is something I truly wish to avoid. My head already feels like it’s going to explode. I don’t want an even more demanding position. No, seriously......]","[Hahaha...... well, for now, let’s just focus on getting some rest.]","After exchanging these weary words, Baron Ritch and Marie parted ways and headed toward their respective rooms.","Once Marie finally reached her own room, she took out the clothes and accessories Kaito had given her, and as if to confirm they were truly real, she stared at them with an indescribable expression on her face.","She couldn’t believe things had turned out like this. Her mind felt unsteady, still floating in a dreamlike, unreal haze, unable to settle.","Right as she was lost in thought, her room door was knocked on, and her older sister, the third daughter, stepped inside.","[Marie, are you alright? You look completely exhausted......]","[If you’re asking whether I’m alright, then the answer is no. This has turned into something unbelievable...... Look, Sister, these clothes and accessories......]","[Wow...... In the blink of an eye, Marie’s become the richest person in the entire house. Beautiful, high-class clothes, gorgeous accessories, all of them things anyone would dream of owning. And yet...... strangely enough, I don’t feel even a little jealous. If anything, I’m overflowing with relief that it’s not me.]","The outfit, something even the eldest sister likely didn’t own, and the obviously expensive accessories were indeed objects a noblewoman would naturally long for...... but given Marie’s current situation, they did not inspire envy in the slightest.","[Sister, maybe you should brace yourself too. You might get approached with some political marriage offer.]","[Can you not...... I was planning to become a librarian in a small town......]","[If our territory develops, we might even get a library, you know?]","[......Are things really turning out that big?]","[According to Her Majesty the Emperor and Eris-sama, the western region might undergo rapid development from here on out......]","[If that happens, Marie, you might end up being remembered as one who restored Ritch Barony.]","[Ahaha, my name might end up in the history books then...... haha...... If only...... if only this were all just a joke......]","She tried to laugh off her sister’s teasing words, but Marie’s expression stiffened, because it wasn’t impossible. It could genuinely happen.","Still, Marie was a woman who had grown up hardy in a poor frontier barony, and she was quick to adapt. After a moment, she shook her head to reset her thoughts and forced a smile back onto her face.","[......But well, we shouldn’t just dwell on the negatives, right!? Sure, there are tough parts, but these are luxury clothes I’ve always dreamed of! And they’re not even hand-me-downs from you or my other sisters.]","[Fufu, that’s true. But Miyama Kaito-sama really is amazing, isn’t he? Just from a glance, anyone can tell these clothes are extremely high-end, and he just gave them to you without hesitation, didn’t he?]","[He didn’t even show the slightest reaction to the price. If anything, it was like he was buying something cheap. I really realized how different rich people are. According to Phantasmal King-sama, clothes and accessories of this level were genuinely just small purchases for him......]","[Maybe he took a liking to you, and hoped to make a good impression by giving her a gift?]","[No, no, I’m not beautiful or anything. Someone like Kaito-sama could have his pick from countless far prettier girls, you know?]","[Which is exactly why he might prefer someone with a gentle, natural cuteness! Besides, you’re definitely beautiful...... after all, you take after me the most among us sisters!]","[Fufufu, I see......]","Drawn in by the cheerful words of the third daughter, Marie, too, let a bright, delighted smile slip out. Sure, things had turned into something outrageous, and there were probably plenty of stomach-aching troubles waiting for her from here on out...... but honestly, she was happy about the clothes and accessories, and in the end, the time she spent shopping with Kaito and visiting a café had been fun as well. And so, she kept a smile on her face, thinking positively that there had been good things mixed in after all.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [W- Well, as expected of a charge-type, that was some truly fearsome stomachache. But at least she's worked through all the flags she’d been carrying, so it feels like things have settled down a bit...... There's still Cornelia’s flags ahead though......]"]},{"number":2440,"title":"Chapter 2440: Chapter 2441: Spreading Aftermath 33","paragraphs":["In the conference room of the Archlesia Empire’s Imperial Castle, alongside Emperor Chris, stood Ryze, the current King of the Symphonia Kingdom, and Laguna, the King of the Hydra Kingdom.","A few days had passed since the talks concerning the Ritch Barony. Ryze and Laguna had requested a venue for a trilateral discussion, and preparations for the meeting were completed with a speed unimaginable before Kaito arrived in this world.","This discussion had nothing to do with the golden ripples. Even Chris herself hadn’t known about it until Alice informed her, so there was no way Ryze or Laguna would know either. Their request this time concerned the developments in the western region of the Archlesia Empire.","Both Ryze and Laguna possessed strong intelligence networks, and having acquired information suggesting a high likelihood of Kaito’s involvement, they entered the meeting prepared but...... what Chris explained far surpassed what either of them had imagined.","[Good grief, the Archlesia Empire has been advancing at a remarkable pace lately. The economy seems to be flourishing, quite enviable.]","[......Do you seriously find it enviable?]","[No, if anything, I’m ashamed of my past self who carelessly envied the Symphonia Kingdom and young Ryze...... But well, in terms of national profit, it is impressive.]","Seeing the fatigue written all over Chris’s face, Laguna spoke with a wry smile. Chris, normally calm and unwilling to show weakness, was visibly exhausted, proof enough of how overwhelming the situation had become.","[......If these events occurred one at a time with proper intervals, I would welcome them wholeheartedly...... b- but they’re happening one after another everywhere, and we don’t have the time or manpower to keep up. We’re still only at the stage of finalizing the budget proposal for redeveloping that tourist city......]","[Ah yes, the city the Founder visited, was it? So the state has decided to take charge of its redevelopment huh......]","Ryze asked, having already heard rumors, since when Olivia went on a date with Kaito, she hadn’t used Recognition Inhibition, making it a topic of discussion, and Chris nodded while holding her head.","[The place had already been stagnating as a tourist destination. With the Founder’s visit, and our increasing interactions with the God Realm recently, we were preparing to shift in that direction...... but then major activity appeared in the west, Dragon King-sama and War King-sama visited another trade city as tourists, both the Victor Trading Company and Sharon Trading Company began showing unclear movements, God of Fertility-sama strengthened her Divine Protection, and then the golden ripples...... all within less 10 ten days...... t- there’s just far too much to do.]","[......Kaito truly is overwhelming. From the standpoint of national interest, I’d love for him to visit the Hydra Kingdom as well...... though I’d also desperately hope he goes easy on us. But still...... Chris seems completely at her limit, while when all sorts of things were happening in the Symphonia Kingdom, young Ryze, you didn’t seem nearly this cornered.]","Glancing at Chris, whose stomach was clearly suffering, Laguna recalled that despite being the ruler most affected by Kaito’s influence, Ryze had not seemed so frantic in the past. Hoping to gain some insight, she asked...... and Ryze responded with a wry smile, an indescribable expression on his face.","[......No, in our kingdom’s case...... whenever something happens, it almost always converges on Lilianne. So I rarely end up taking action myself, or rather...... by the time the information reaches me, it’s already too late......]","[I see. Since everything centers around young Lilia's place, it means you can simply keep watch around her, making things easier to handle...... but still, sacrificing your sister’s stomach for the nation’s sake is hardly admirable......]","[......If I could do something about it, I would. But when it comes to Miyama-kun, any sort of precautionary measures are pointless...... Well, I don’t think Lilianne is particularly unlucky, but somehow, she just pulls troublesome situations toward herself with full force, or rather, every inconvenience seems to head straight for her......]","[Life rarely goes the way you want, does it?]","Yes, this is exactly why Ryze never looked especially exhausted whenever some new incident involving Kaito occurred in the Symphonia Kingdom...... Nearly every stomachache‐inducing problem ended up converging on Lilia instead.","And since Lilia drew in those situations like a black hole, all they needed to do was keep watch around Kaito’s home and Lilia’s estate. That made gathering information easier and dealing with the aftermath more manageable, allowing Ryze a surprising amount of breathing room. ṝαŊꝋBÈS","[There's also that...... Now that Kaito has established a home and become more settled here, his lifestyle has stabilized, and his range of movement has broadened. Even when we spoke earlier, he seemed interested in cities outside the capital...... it’s very possible his activity range will expand even further.]","[......Next time, I’ll recommend that Miyama-sama take a sightseeing tour of a city in the Hydra Kingdom.]","[Can you not, young Chris. That borders on terrorism...... No doubt the national profit would skyrocket, but...... stomachaches would be rough for this old body......]","Seeing the chaos that had erupted in just a short time after Kaito expanded his activities into the Archlesia Empire, it was all too easy to imagine what might happen if he did the same in the Hydra Kingdom. Laguna could only wear a deeply conflicted expression on her face.","<Afterword>","<Symphonia Kingdom>","Thanks to the ever‐consistent stomachache black hole, the royal palace remains relatively peaceful.","<Archlesia Empire>","A recently hot stomachache hotspot, where even Chris is being thoroughly tormented.","<Hydra Kingdom>","With interests in spicy food, the presence of Shigenobu living in Hydra, and a moderate liking for fishing, one could feel a premonition that Kaito might extend his activities there if given the chance. The day Laguna suffers from stomachache may be approaching......."]},{"number":2441,"title":"Chapter 2441: Chapter 2442: Spreading Aftermath 34","paragraphs":["Sanctuary, God Realm...... More specifically, a small floating island created by Shallow Vernal located just near it. On this island, where later she would go on a hot spring date with Kaito and had even built the entire hot spring town, Shallow Vernal was making detailed adjustments.","Though it was described as a small island, it was large enough to fit a whole hot spring town, so creating it with care would naturally take some time. This time, Shallow Vernal was in the middle of copying a hot spring town from Makina’s world and then adjusting it to fit Trinia’s culture.","[Hmmm, if we’re going for a Trinia-style, maybe the buildings could be bricks. The image of the buildings is pretty important, so as it stands, it feels a bit too Japanese.]","[I see...... However, we still want to leave enough of the original look so that Kaito-san can recognize it as a hot spring town at first glance.]","[For example, what if we extended that river over here and built a bridge?]","[That’s not bad, but if we put a bridge there, the view from it wouldn’t be great. Should we adjust the height......?]","Hearing Makina’s words as she sought advice, Shallow Vernal flicked her fingers lightly, altering the terrain of the hot spring town.","For both Shallow Vernal and Makina, they could truly reshape the terrain and environmental conditions as they pleased, giving them many options, but that also made it hard for them to settle on a single direction.","[......By the way, you mentioned that Otherworld Gods will come to see my beloved child, right? I suppose Electrone is an exception, but who’s next?]","[The God known as Bipolar God is scheduled to visit next.]","[Ugh, that insanely powerful god...... By the way, has the order after that been decided?]","[Originally it would be Virtual God, but she’s already been granted free visitation, so after that, I don’t know. It seems the other Otherworld Gods have various arrangements among themselves, but I don’t know the details. The order could also change depending on my or Kaito-san’s intentions.]","[......Fumu.]","Hearing Shallow Vernal’s indifferent explanation, Makina looked thoughtful for a moment.","[......Shallow Vernal, I’m consulting with you like this, but as payment, there’s a God I’d like to come a bit earlier. Could you adjust the order for me......? Ah, of course, she can be after Bipolar God.]","[That’s fine, but that’s a bit unexpected. I assumed you’d ask to use the completed hot spring town for going with Kaito-san...... I would have refused that though.]","[I don’t particularly need that. If I want to go on a hot spring trip with my beloved child, I can always go to the real deal anyway.]","[..................]","Watching Makina speak with such confidence, Shallow Vernal wondered \"Why does she assume Kaito-san would agree to a hot spring trip?\", but she didn’t feel like asking and just let it slide. ꞦaꞐȪBÊS","[So, who is this God?]","[Polar Star God, \"Astraea Tryst Meteor\"...... well, an obnoxiously cheeky midget of a God. Lacks any sense, but seems to have enough common sense to appreciate how wonderful my beloved child is, so I thought I’d show off my beloved child a bit.]","[You’re close with her?]","[Not at all! No sense, bad taste, and just the other day, when I showed her a movie I made of my beloved child, she cried, but then she had the nerve to say something like \"For the likes of you, it seems you’ve managed to make something somewhat decent\", a sore loser's bluff is what it is! It's totally not because she was feeling down because her turn to see my beloved child was still a long way off, okay!!!]","[......I see.]","Shallow Vernal swallowed the words \"So basically, you are close?\", and simply nodded. Saying it aloud would probably provoke a troublesome reaction, which would waste time and delay the hot spring town adjustments.","[Changing the order is fine. Once Bipolar God has visited, tell her to call out to me. In return, you’ll be helping me out with various things until the hot spring town is completed.]","[Yeah, yeah. Well, if my beloved child is going on a trip, I want it to be a good place, so I’ll cooperate properly.]","[......Even so, you’ve started speaking in a much more casual tone than before.]","[I’ve gotten used to you by now. Rather, the way we are before is more on you. It’s just that Shallow Vernal speaks too indifferently, so our exchanges naturally ended up sounding very formal.]","Since Makina now had two terminals constantly active in this world and had conversed with Shallow Vernal many times, she had begun to understand how to interact with her, and her speech had become more casual than before.","At the very least, with Shallow Vernal having grown under Kaito’s influence, she had this sense of reassurance that she wouldn’t irrationally use Epilogue against anyone.","[......By the way, what will you do with this hot spring town after the trip with my beloved child?]","[Fumu...... guess I’ll just pass it to Lilia.]","[Ah, that’s nice. Could be used for tourism and stuff, so if you drop the whole island somewhere in Symphonia Kingdom as a gift, it won’t go to waste.]","While the World Creators converse as if it were an ordinary casual chat...... Just like that, in a place completely unrelated to the Ritch Barony that had recently stirred up the Human Realm, to the Sharon County, to the rapidly-rising Archlesia Empire, or to the maneuvers of various trading companies...... It was decided that an immense stomachache was about to rain down on Lilia.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [No matter the occasion, the strongest would always be the strongest...... The Ultimate Stomachache Warrior is on a whole different level. With no context or reason whatsoever, an absolutely ridiculous top-class stomachache flag just got planted in the most outrageous place......]"]},{"number":2442,"title":"Chapter 2442: Chapter 2443: Requested Item 1","paragraphs":["On a clear, sunny afternoon, after finishing brushing Bell, I suddenly thought I’d check out the special space in the backyard and headed over.","The door in my backyard connects to a space created by Canalis-san. Inside, there’s a workshop where Nebula and Illness-san do their crafting, and fields with tea trees and cacao trees.","Although Nebula, Illness-san, and Canalis-san use it most often, I was told I could come and go freely, so I decided to check out the fields to see what they were like.","Incidentally, there’s only one door, and by sliding the plate above the doorknob, you can switch between the workshop, the fields, or other connected spaces.","When I reached the backyard and checked the plate...... Arehh? Have the options increased? There used to be just two, the workshop and the fields, but now there was a third one.","I had planned to look at the fields, but the mysterious third space caught my attention, so I set the plate to it, turned the doorknob, and passed through a thin, membrane-like barrier that obscured the view ahead...... and found myself in a wide, grassy meadow.","[Oya? Welcome, Kaito-sama.]","[Hello, Canalis-san...... is this a new space?]","Inside, Canalis-san appeared after the space shimmered like noise before my eyes, so I greeted them lightly and asked about this new area.","[Yes, it’s a space I made recently. How should I describe it...... it’s kind of like a ranch.]","[A ranch? You mean you raise cows and stuff?]","[Rather than raising them, it’s more like the place where I do selective breeding. Tahaa~~ I’ve been creating dairy cows for use in Nifty’s dairy products, experimenting to see if I can improve them.]","[Fumu, selective breeding huh? With Canalis-san's skills, you could probably create cows that produce amazingly delicious milk instantly......]","[That’s true. I could use my God Power to create cows that produce super tasty milk, but that isn’t necessarily the best approach. Sure, the milk would be delicious, but it lacks surprises. Sometimes, unexpectedly tasty flavors emerge by accident or through natural variation. If you create a perfect flavor from the start, those surprises never happen, so it can feel a bit uninspired. Tahaa~~ I apologize for prioritizing romance over efficiency.]","I see...... Comparing it to Kuro’s baby castella might be a bit rude, but it’s like Kuro’s idea of infinite potential. There’s the possibility of new flavors emerging accidentally in ways the creator didn’t intend. If you start with a \"finished product\", you might overlook those accidental delights along the way.","[Also, tastes vary widely. Even if you make something most people find amazing, it isn’t an absolute “correct” taste. Well, you could theoretically imbue it with a property that changes the flavor to match whoever’s tasting it, but even then, it would vary with the person’s mood, so there may be no absolute answer.]","[That’s true. In terms of flavor, there might be tastes most people enjoy, but there isn’t a universal perfect taste. That’s why you keep experimenting.]","[Exactly. Since I’m a God, I can shorten the time needed for selective breeding, which normally takes a long time. That way, I can make various improvements in a short period. Tahaa~~ I apologize for prioritizing efficiency in a modern way!]","After giving Canalis-san, who spoke in their usual expressionless yet brisk tone, a wry smile, I suddenly thought of something and decided to ask.","[......Canalis-san, by the way...... do you happen to have any really good water?]","[Leave it to me! Well then, here's the God-Approved Mineral Water, trusted and proven. This water...... is incredibly delicious! That’s all it does, no other effects whatsoever! Would you like a cup?]","[Thank you...... oh, wow, it really is quite good.]","[Well, it’s just good as water, so don’t expect an emotional, mind-blowing taste or anything like that.]","The water Canalis-san offered was indeed delicious. Well, as Canalis-san said, it was just good water, nothing overwhelmingly amazing or emotionally stirring. It was simply high-quality, easy-to-drink water...... no more, no less.","[Actually, someone I asked a favor of is coming tomorrow. She hardly eats anything and mostly just drinks water, so I thought giving her good water as a thank-you would be nice...... and honestly, your water tastes better than the stuff I bought.]","[Tahaa~~ Well, that’s because it’s God-Approved. As water, it’s second to none. Though, as I said, it’s just good water...... Oh, but since I pride myself on being perceptive, Kaito-sama, I understand exactly what you’re thinking. How much would you like me to prepare?]","[Errr...... quantity......]","Talking about water had been by chance, but since the person coming tomorrow had agreed to an urgent favor, it made sense to give something of good quality as thanks. And so, I decided to prepare Canalis-san’s delicious water as a gift. ℞aNɵBƐS","I hope she’ll be pleased, though I don’t know her very well yet, so there are still many things about her I’m unsure of.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Who is it? Someone who only drinks water sounds like a Spirit...... but someone he hasn’t talked to much?]"]},{"number":2443,"title":"Chapter 2443: Chapter 2444: Requested Item 2","paragraphs":["I stepped out of the house through the front door and touched the pillar-like object right beside it, then sent a Hummingbird to the person I had an appointment with. This pillar was crafted by Canalis, and by having someone pre-registered, like me or Anima, touch it, the area right in front of the entrance temporarily loses its Teleportation Obstruction effect, allowing Teleportation Magic to reach the front of the house.","I first learned about this when Megiddo mentioned it: apparently, the Recognition Inhibition Magic around my house is so strong it’s on par with the Sanctuary, to the point that even Megiddo, one of the Six Kings, cannot ignore it to teleport through.","Moreover, this Teleportation Obstruction is specially made so that residents like me and Anima are completely unaffected. Thanks to Canalis’ God Power, I can freely return home using my teleportation magic tools without any trouble.","So, anyone not living in my house normally teleports to the gate first before entering. The alternative is temporarily disabling the Teleportation Obstruction effect right in front of the door, as I did, to teleport directly there. The distance between the gate and the entrance isn’t huge, but if teleportation is possible, it’s better to come closer.","About a minute or two after sending the hummingbird, a magic circle appeared on the ground slightly ahead of me, and soon the person I had arranged to meet appeared.","[Hello, Lanza-san.]","[Hello! I’ve come to accept your envitation...... infetation...... invatation...... I- I’ve come!!!]","A woman with short, rust-colored hair tied in a ponytail, who seemed to try to phrase herself politely but gave up midway in confusion and then cheerfully announced her arrival with a liberated expression...... she was Lanza, the Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree, one of the World King's subordinate and a subordinate of Camellia-san.","[I’ve been eagerly awaiting the day I could meet Kaito-san again! If I'm not mistaken, in the Otherworld, you say each mommy felt like...... each monument is like...... each monkey...... errr......]","[......Are you thinking of \"each moment felt like eternity\"?]","[That’s it! That’s exactly how I felt while waiting!]","As always, she was full of energy. Though Camellia-san’s subordinate, she somehow gave off a vibe similar to Blossom-san.","Her appearance and outfit had a kunoichi-like style, and alongside Blossom-san, the Japanese aesthetic felt even stronger.","[......Wait, am I the one who kept you waiting?]","[No, no, we insisted on this meeting, so it’s fine.]","The purpose of Lanza-san’s visit was regarding a previous request: I wanted to purchase matsutake mushrooms...... called Spearmash in this world.","Lanza-san had agreed to sell them, but the Spearmash harvest and sales are carefully regulated by Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree. She said it was fine to sell, but they had to wait until the harvest season.","Of course, I had no objection. I had been looking forward to the harvest...... and now that the season had arrived, Lanza-san had come to deliver the Spearmash.","[The payment was made in advance, so this time, we only need to hand over the goods, correct?]","[By the way, was it really okay to sell at such a low price? Aren’t these high-grade mushrooms?]","[Hmmm, they’re considered high-grade because we rarely sell them publicly. Basically, the Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree, myself included, only need a minimal amount of money, so we have no intention of excessive business. We sell a fixed number once a year, so they end up being expensive by default.]","[I see......]","Lanza-san doesn’t eat or drink, and her hobby is training herself, so she hardly spends money. Other Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree are similar, they earn only what’s necessary to maintain their habitats and environment. And so, since only a small number of their Spearmash ever enter circulation, their rarity gives them high value.","[Of course, if it’s Kaito-san’s request, I have no problem giving them to you, and I could even waive the payment...... but Camellia-sama said, she said that Kaito-san might feel ereasy...... greasy...... sleazy? ......She said you might feel bad!!!]","[T- That’s true. I’d feel bad accepting them for free, so it’s actually better this way.]","[But! Don’t worry! Since it was none other than Kaito-san’s request, I used my authority to provide full service!!! I received payment for 100 mushrooms, but as a special freebie, I brought an additional 9,900, making it a nice round total of 10,000 mushrooms!!]","[10,000 mushrooms!?]","I was stunned at Lanza-san’s words, announced with a triumphant pose as if throwing a guts pose. Wait, what kind of world even has someone give 99 times the purchased amount as a freebie...... no...... she’s standing right in front of me...... grinning from ear to ear.","Also, even though we haven’t really talked much...... Lanza-san’s affection toward me felt unusually high. Her personality is straightforward and refreshing, but through Sympathy Magic, a strong sense of goodwill was clearly being conveyed.","W- What should I do? She’s smiling happily and seems to be expecting me to be pleased, so there’s no way I can say I don’t need 10,000 mushrooms.","[......Thank you. I’m really happy.]","[I’m glad to hear that, Kaito-san! That makes me happy too!]","She really is a good person...... undoubtedly cheerful, full of energy, and kind...... but somehow, there’s this slightly scatterbrained side to her......","<Lanza>","She isn’t the type who, like Blossom, stops listening when she gets excited or becomes stubborn through sheer conviction...... She's simply stupid, and her personality is extremely straightforward.","Because she immediately acts on whatever pops into her head without thinking deeply, her ability to take action is extraordinary. The day after the idea occurred to her, she once visited Lillywood’s castle alone to challenge her, and when she was moved by Camellia’s strength and kindness, she promptly talked things over with her companions and joined the World King’s faction to become Camellia’s subordinate. She truly lives by “strike while the iron is hot”.","Naturally, the Spirits' affection revision is in full effect...... or rather, since her personality is fundamentally simple, her affection toward Kaito, who is naturally adored by everyone, is ridiculously high. She approaches him with the mindset of “Kaito is loved by nature = as a part of nature, I also love Kaito”, so her affection for him is practically maxed out right from the start."]},{"number":2444,"title":"Chapter 2444: Chapter 2445: Requested Item 3","paragraphs":["The sheer number, 10,000, is staggering. Even if I shared them with the Otherworlders I know, there would still be an enormous surplus, so I need to think of ways to consume them.","After all, they are high-quality mushrooms in this world as well, so sharing them with acquaintances should at least reduce the quantity somewhat. Well, for now, I accepted the Spearmush that Lanza-san brought, and Lanza-san gave a firm thumbs-up and smiled.","[The harvest season has ended for this year, but if you let me know, I can bring more during next year’s harvest season!]","[T- Thank you very much.]","......W- Well, Lanza-san’s thoughtfulness is truly appreciated, but there’s no way I could finish consuming them by next year. After all, that’s 10,000 mushrooms. Even if I consumed 10 a day, I wouldn’t even get through half. No matter how I think about it, there’s no way I’ll run out by next year. If anything, this batch could last not just a few years but over a decade.","[Oh, right. It’s simple, but I prepared a little gift to show my thanks. I heard that you don’t eat meals and only drink water, so I prepared some high-quality water for you.]","[I’m sorry to trouble you, but I like water, so I’m happy! To show such consideration...... it makes me exemptly...... exseenly...... ex...... errr...... thank you very much!!!]","She seemed to be trying to use a somewhat complicated expression but kept stumbling. She was probably trying to say something like \"it makes me extremely pleased\".","(T/N: Kyouetsu shigokudegozaimasu/恐悦至極でございます)","I thought she might be similar to Blossom-san, but this kind of charm is closer to Tir-san or Raz-san, perhaps.","[Since I couldn’t figure out anything else you like, I only brought water......]","[No, water is more than enough. I am a Spirit, so I don’t need solid food.]","[You don’t even enjoy them as a taste preference?]","[......Enjoy as a taste preference?]","[Eh? Well, I mean...... it’s not necessary for living, but you could enjoy flavors and such for fun......]","Arehh? She looked as if she had just heard an unfamiliar concept. Lanza-san, clearly surprised by my words, paused for a moment and muttered quietly.","[......I never thought of it that way.]","Could it be that Lanza-san is...... no, even thinking that might be rude. Y- Yes, stoic! She’s probably the stoic type, with little interest in anything unnecessary.","[I see, so that’s why Camellia-sama drank tea.]","[Ah, errr...... until you became Camellia-san's subordinate, have you not interacted with other Spirits?]","[Indeed. Aside from the Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree, I almost never interacted with other Spirits! We Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree are content as long as our dwelling remains comfortable, and we have no interest in the outside world. Should I say we’re closed-off? So, until recently, I wasn’t even under Lillywood-sama’s command, and the only interaction we had with the outside was the annual Spearmush sale...... so we only interacted with the outside once a year.] RÂƝꝋbÈṨ","[I see. Then it makes sense that you didn’t know what other Spirits were doing. But in that case, being Lillywood-san’s subordinate must have been a significant change.]","The Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree are somewhat like Wingeds...... perhaps even more closed-off than them. From what she said, they hardly interact with the outside world and seem to live solely to protect their own territory.","[Yes. I went to challenge Lillywood-sama, was defeated by Camellia-sama, and became inspired by her strength and kindness. I immediately returned to my dwelling and suggested we become subordinates of Lillywood-sama.]","[......Were you opposed?]","[Yes, I was opposed quite strongly. However, there were a few who agreed. And those who opposed didn’t just deny me outright, they considered the history of the Spear-branched Forest and presented the pros and cons of joining Lillywood-sama’s command, in a lolically...... loracally...... lojecally com...... errr......]","[Logically consistent?]","[That’s it! They presented their opposition in a logically consistent way.]","[I see. So you discussed it thoroughly and got everyone to understand.]","She’s talking about it so casually, but I think that’s actually pretty incredible. I don’t know exactly how old Lanza-san is, but among the Spirits where the older ones are said to be stronger, and given that she has the ability on the level of a Count-rank, she must be a very old Spirit. Changing the mindset of the Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree, who had stuck to their long-standing, rigid traditions and avoided outside contact until now, must have been incredibly difficult.","They must have had a pretty heated debate......","[No, I didn’t really understand the discussion because it was too complicated, so I just \"beat up all the opposition\" and passed it with a majority vote! And the day after I challenged Camellia-sama, we successfully became Lillywood-sama’s subordinates!!!]","She solved it with violence!? And she became her subordinate the day after proposing it...... is she some kind of initiative powerhouse?","Honestly, rather than being the World King's subordinate, I feel like she'd be more suitable being the War King's subordinate......","<Afterword>","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree A : [I acknowledge that the World King possesses the power befitting the King of Spirits, and I won’t deny that there are benefits to submitting, but a major change comes with a commensurate burden.]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree B : [In the first place, the Spear-branched Forest is functioning fine as it is. There’s no need to force a change.]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree C : [Exactly. If we go into detail and list the pros and cons, each point......]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree D : [Couldn’t it depend on the conditions? If we maintain the current state and only nominally become subordinates, I don’t see a problem.]","Lanza : [......I see...... I understand everyone’s opinions (she doesn't). Now, those who oppose my proposal, clench your fists...... show your strength to express your opinion!!!]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree E : [Gah, wait, wait, wait......]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree F : [Stop! You’re an idiot, yeah, but an idiot who’s explosively strong, which is why you’re our representative as the Great Spirit. No one can match you......]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree G : [That’s why I said just agree for now...... there’s no way this idiot can have a proper debate......]","Spirit of the Spear-branched Tree H : [Well, in the end, that idiot is the strongest, so it’s best if the idiot decides the policy and we focus on supporting them.]"]},{"number":2445,"title":"Chapter 2445: Chapter 2446: Requested Item 4","paragraphs":["Once our business was done, Lanza-san took the water from me and waved cheerfully as she headed off. How should I put it...... she really was like a storm blowing through.","As for the 10,000 spearmush, I do need to think about how to use them all...... but for now, since I have the chance, I’d like to try eating one.","Matsutake rice or a clear soup would be good, but for now I’ll just grill it. And if I’m going to grill it, I’d really like to use a shichirin and charcoal......","[......Alice, do we have a shichirin and some charcoal for grilling?]","[Kaito-san, are you maybe confusing me with a convenient tool bag you can pull anything out of?]","[You say that, but you’re already holding a shichirin......]","I called out to Alice, deciding we’d eat together, and of course, her preparations were impeccable, shichirin already in hand. Since grilling matsutake in front of the entrance would be a bit much, we decided to move to the backyard.","[......You’re not supposed to wash them, right?]","[That washes away the aroma. You wipe the dirt lightly with a damp cloth like this, cut off just the tip of the stem...... then make a small slit and tear it by hand, and it comes apart nicely.]","[Ohh, it already looks delicious. Do I just grill it like this?]","[Lightly spray it with sake, sprinkle a little salt...... something like that. Once it’s done grilling, eating it with mixed soy sauce, or sudachi, or dashi ponzu is great.]","As expected of Alice, she explained while handling everything with practiced efficiency. Meanwhile, I took out two small camping chairs, lined them up, and set out a compact table.","[Let’s bring out some sake too......]","[Nice idea~~ Ah, once moisture starts rising to the surface, it’s ready to eat.]","Before long, small beads of moisture began forming on the matsutake grilling on the shichirin. I squeezed a bit of sudachi, added just a little soy sauce, and took a bite.","The unique fragrance of matsutake filled my nose, and the combination of freshness, crisp texture, and rich flavor spread in my mouth. Mm...... it’s been a while since I've had them, and it really is delicious.","[This is great. Actually, I feel like it’s been ages since I last ate matsutake.]","[Well, they basically don’t exist in this world. I’ll grill about five more......]","[You’re eating way too fast......]","Actually, if there are too many left over, maybe I could just have Alice eat them all? When trying to clear out the massive amount of food stored in the magic box, that might honestly be the most efficient method.","[......Are you maybe thinking of using me to dispose of leftover food?]","[......Ah, no...... hmm...... Alice, how about eating around a hundred more?]","[You gave up, didn’t you!? You tried to dodge it at first, but halfway through you gave up and switched completely to making me deal with them!!! I feel like you’re treating me a bit too casually here...... but well, spearmush are tasty, so I’ll eat them.]","Watching Alice eat spearmush at an impressive pace, looking slightly exasperated, I gave a wry smile. Still, I should also think about who to share them with.","Of course, I’ll share some with Kaori-san and the others I talked with about matsutake earlier, but the other Otherworlders might want some too.","I can check with Aoi-chan and Hina-chan, and with my parents right away. As for Akane-san, Seigi-kun, and Shigenobu-san, I’ll confirm with them and share some if they want.","What about Neun-san? Kuro mentioned she prefers shiitake to matsutake, but that doesn’t mean she dislikes matsutake. I’ll check, and if there’s no issue, I’ll share some.","And then...... wasn’t Miyabi-san staying at Epsilon-san’s place? I’ve never met her, but she gave me pickles for my birthday, so sending some to Epsilon-san to pass on to her might be a good idea. ṝАŊOВĚṥ","But since these are extremely delicious and high-quality matsutake...... or rather, spearmush, maybe I should put them in a luxurious wooden box or something, it would really help set the mood.","[......Alice, do we have some kind of nice wooden box?]","[I feel like you’re using me way too conveniently...... Here, a wooden box suitable for holding spearmush, along with hida and hiba leaves for lining it.]","[And why did you bring out all that then......? And the front of the box even has \"Matsutake\" written on it......]","I’d tossed the question out casually, following the same mood as earlier, yet she really did produce a box perfectly suited for holding matsutake, complete with \"Matsutake\" written on it in elegant calligraphy. As always, her ability to anticipate things was impressive...... she must have predicted I’d ask for something like this and prepared it beforehand.","[......By the way, these leaves that are usually used for lining the box, they're called hida or hiba? What are these?]","[Those got lots of names. Sometimes they’re called urajiro or hoda, but generally, you spread out some kind of fern and hiba...... hinoki leaves. They have antibacterial and insect-repelling properties.]","[Hehh, is that so......]","Listening to Alice’s explanation with interest, I placed a light layer of leaves inside the box she handed me and arranged the matsutake. In an instant, it gained a refined, high-class feel.","Looks good. I’ll deliver them to the people I know in this form.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see, so that’s an option...... Just feed any leftover ingredients to Alice.]","??? : [Aren't you guys treating Alice-chan a bit roughly?]","Serious-senpai : [Says the one who gets excessively embarrassed if you treat her too courteously......?]"]},{"number":2446,"title":"Chapter 2446: Chapter 2447: Requested Item 5","paragraphs":["Friendship City Hikari, on the second floor of the diner Suiren...... After waking up and taking a light shower, Kaori was toweling herself off in the changing area when her gaze drifted to the large mirror.","She’d bought a high-quality full-length mirror recently, thanks to having a bit more financial leeway. But as she looked at the reflection staring back at her, her expression turned thoughtful.","(......Hmmm...... my skin really is pretty, isn’t it? I mean, I’ve noticed it before, but it feels like it’s getting even prettier......)","Even taking into account that she’d just gotten out of the bath, the skin reflected in the mirror looked beautiful, clearly different from how she’d looked before.","(That little wrinkle at the corner of my eye I was worried about disappeared before I knew it, and my skin looks...... fresh? Firm? Did that new toner and lotion I switched to really suit me that well? No, this isn’t the kind of improvement you get just from skincare. This is something else...... that glow you only get from youth itself...... and it’s not just my face, right? Even my hands...... they’re pretty now?)","Running a diner by herself meant Kaori constantly worked with water, cooking, washing dishes. Even with her skill in water magic to simplify things, she always had to worry about her hands getting rough.","But now, her hands showed no sign of dryness at all. If anything, no one would believe she spent most of her day doing chores involving water.","(I mean, I am happy my skin is getting prettier but...... this obviously isn’t something I achieved through effort. It’s not skincare, not my diet...... it feels like something supernatural got involved...... arehh? Wait. I feel like I’m forgetting something important...... errr......)","As she examined the changes in her own body, Kaori pressed a finger to her forehead, certain she’d forgotten something significant.","———–As thanks for everything you do on a daily basis, I’ve given you something close to a Blessing.","And then, like a message from above, the words Olivia told her through telepathy during that earlier three-person date with Kaito and Olivia rose to the surface of her mind.","(A- Aaahhh!? I- I remember now! Right, Olivia-sama said something weird back then! And I was going to ask her for details later, but after that the date kept throwing surprises at me, and all my attention got dragged away, I completely forgot!)","Yes, Olivia had said something that sounded very much like she had bestowed a blessing upon Kaori. Kaori had intended to ask her more about it later.","But after being dragged around, acting practically like lovers, and ending the day with a hug with Kaito, even if it was just how things naturally flowed, she’d completely forgotten.","(So this is that, right? That has to be what’s causing this. I- I need to properly confirm this with Olivia-sama...... but how? I don’t want to ask her while she’s at the diner. There are always other customers around, and I already draw too much attention. If it becomes obvious that I received something like a Blessing from Olivia-sama...... n- no, asking at the diner is out.)","Olivia visited her shop regularly for meals, so meeting her wasn’t a problem, but given the sensitive nature of the subject, Kaori didn’t want to ask her somewhere others might overhear.","(In that case, the best option is to go to Olivia-sama herself and talk. Today is a regular day off, so I have time. Olivia-sama will definitely be at the Central Cathedral, and if I go see her...... she’ll probably meet with me...... I think......)","Olivia may hold the extremely high position of Founder, but Kaori felt confident that their relationship was close enough that, if she went to visit, Olivia would likely make time to meet her.","So the chances of meeting her by going to the cathedral were high...... but the Grand Cathedral, the central seat of the world-spanning Godism, was an enormous and overwhelmingly majestic structure.","(......Still, going there and asking someone to arrange an audience with Olivia-sama feels intimidating, or maybe I’m just anxious about going alone...... If only Kaito-kun could come with me...... If he did, I’d feel so much more comfortable......)","If Kaito accompanied her, Olivia would undoubtedly be delighted, and Kaori herself would feel more at ease. And if anything happened, she had the comforting thought that Kaito might help her.","As she pondered these things, a hummingbird arrived from Kaito, abruptly and at the perfect moment.","[......From Kaito-kun? What’s this about?]","Murmuring to herself, she checked the contents: he had something he needed to talk about and wanted to meet. For the current Kaori, it was exactly the opportunity she was hoping for.","She didn’t know what Kaito’s matter was, but even if meeting today wasn’t possible, she could at least ask him to accompany her to the cathedral another day. Kaori had no reason to refuse.","(If Kaito-kun has some time, I’ll ask him to come with me to the Cathedral. But well, putting that aside...... my skin really has gotten pretty. I- I’m looking pretty good, aren’t I? Not like a world-class beauty or anything, of course, but maybe...... cute? Or even kind of pretty? I think I might actually pull off that level now?)","Though she was uneasy due to not knowing the details of the Blessing, the clear improvement in her skin, something she’d been worrying about a lot as she approached 30, made her honestly happy. And so, gazing at her reflection, Kaori wore a bright, pleased expression for a good while.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [T- This...... which one is it? Is this going to lead into stomachache development because of the Blessing or because of the matsutake, or into a date...... W- Which one is it......?]"]},{"number":2447,"title":"Chapter 2447: Chapter 2448: Requested Item 6","paragraphs":["To start, after bringing up the whole matsutake conversation and seeing how much Kaori-san seemed to want some, I contacted her via hummingbird to share a bit with her.","Today should be her shop’s day off, so there was a chance it wouldn’t be convenient. I checked first, and she replied right away that there was no problem even if I came immediately, so we agreed I’d visit her shop at 10.","For now, the wooden box Alice gave me can hold around 10 pieces, so giving her 10 as a share should be fine.","(T/N: Just searched, matsutakes apparently have 5-20cm caps wide and sturdy stems 4-16cm long. Can apparently grow larger and thicker than that, sometimes over a pound.)","[Why not just supply Kaori-san’s shop and let her use them for set meals?]","[Ah, that might be a good idea...... Aside from having someone like Alice, who can eat infinite amounts, handle them, consuming 10,000 of these is pretty hard. In that sense, letting a diner use them may be good. But, is that even allowed?]","[Even if the freebie was too much, you did purchase them from Lanza-san, so supplying them elsewhere is no problem. The Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree aren’t exclusionary, just closed-off and uninterested in the outside world. They don’t care what happens to the Spearmush once shipped out.]","[Ahh, so they’re that type...... It’s hard to imagine from Lanza’s personality, but now that I think about it, until I pointed it out, she didn’t even have the concept of enjoying things like food as a luxury. And she had no intention of joining the Realm King’s faction until she met Camellia-san. If you say she isn’t interested in the outside world, that does make sense......]","The Wingeds, if anything, simply doesn’t want much involvement with others, buys only the bare minimum, and basically doesn’t let outsiders into their village, giving off an exclusionary vibe. In contrast, the Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree are the type who have almost no interest in anything outside their own habitat.","Lanza-san only began interacting with the outside world because she met Camellia-san and joined the World King’s faction. Before that, she’d apparently been living solely within their territory for tens of thousands of years. Whether it's good or bad, it seems they’re Spirits whose entire lifestyle is practically self-contained among their own.","Anyway, just to be sure, I used hummingbird to send a message to Lanza-san stating: \"This isn’t certain, but if it turns into that kind of arrangement, would it be all right to let me supply them?\"","A response came back immediately: \"THERE IS ABSOLUTELY NO PROBLEM! THE SPEARMUSH I GAVE YOU IS ALREADY YOURS, SO YOU ARE COMPLETELY FREE TO HANDLE THEM HOWEVER YOU WISH!!!\"","The text on the hummingbird was ridiculously huge...... Maybe she poured extra magic power in to enlarge the message? How should I say this...... She really is just overflowing with energy.","[......Well, it looks like from now on you’ll probably be able to get Spearmush outside their usual season too.]","[......Eh? Why?]","[Want to hear it?]","[I do, but why are you taking out a wine glass?]","[Well~~ as usual, you unconsciously trigger weird flags here and there, and Alice-chan just can’t stop laughing.]","A bad feeling ran through me as I watched Alice merrily take out a wine glass and sip wine. If it were something that would harm me, she would stop me beforehand, so that probably isn’t the case.","Most likely, something I did...... turned into something weird, but in a good way.","[......Kaito-san, you gave Lanza-san that delicious water made by Canalis-san, right?]","[I- I did......]","[For you or anyone else, it’s just tasty water. But for Spirits, it’s the best water imaginable, delicious enough to make them addicted. To put it simply, it’s like handing top-grade Glorious Tea to someone who’s only ever had teabag tea.]","[......T- That means?]","[Kaito-san is already insanely well-liked by Spirits. Then you gave them the best possible present. Naturally, the Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree’s affection for you skyrockets...... Honestly, if you said next month that you wanted to visit their home, they’d probably welcome you with open arms.]","[..................]","I see, there really is no downside for me. What Alice is saying is that the Spirits of the Spear-branched Tree’s affection for me will shoot up dramatically, and if I ever want more Spearmush in the future, I might be able to trade Canalis-san’s water for them even outside their harvest season.","But the important part here is this...... Even right now, I’m already in a ridiculous situation where buying 100 gets me 9900 as a freebie. I’ve only just met Lanza-san, yet even then, I already felt like her affection for me was absurdly high...... and now it’s going even higher?","[......Next time, they might round it off to 100,000, y’know~]","Watching Alice drink wine and cackle like it was the funniest thing in the world, I couldn’t help making a complicated face. No, being liked is a good thing...... but I can’t help feeling a little uneasy.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [And then, add with that the fact that the affection of all the Spirits rises together...... Let's stop there. There are already plenty of Spirits who’ve been sending looks his way as it is, don’t go boosting their affection any more than this......]"]},{"number":2448,"title":"Chapter 2448: Chapter 2449: Requested Item 7","paragraphs":["I arrived at Kaori-san’s shop using my teleportation magic tool and was let in through the back door. Since the shop was closed today, Kaori-san was in casual clothes, wearing an outfit she had bought back in the Hydra Kingdom.","[Sorry for coming on your day off.]","[No, it’s actually better that it’s a day off. You don’t have to worry about opening hours, so we have plenty of time...... But what brings you here all of a sudden?]","[Ah, well, actually, I managed to get the thing we talked about before, so I brought it right away...... Here it is.]","[Whoa, m- matsutake!]","When I pulled out the wooden box labeled \"Matsutake\", Kaori-san’s eyes lit up. After all, she had been the one to first bring it up, and she had probably been longing for matsutake.","[And these are really good matsutake...... Ah, they’re Spearmush here, right? But you can tell just from their size and aroma that they’re top quality.]","[Yes, I tried one earlier, and it was really delicious. So, well, I brought these for Kaori-san......]","[Thank you! I’m happy, but is 10 of them okay?]","[Well, actually, I wanted to consult with you about that......]","[U- Unn?]","As Kaori-san looked at me with a slightly puzzled look on her face, I explained my conversation with Lanza-san and told her that I had nearly 10,000 Spearmush mushrooms on hand, and asked if she could stock them in her shop.","[......I- I see...... 10,000 certainly is insane. Definitely, no individual could consume that many, so having them sold wholesale could work. And having them in my shop...... hmmm...... that could actually be a good idea.]","[Do you think it’s doable?]","[Recently, my shop has become more well-known and we have more customers, but many are tourists. They want something nice to eat as a souvenir of their trip, so I’ve been thinking of adding a few pricier set meals. Spearmush is a rare and high-end mushroom even in this world, so I think there’s a good chance it would sell.]","[I see. Indeed, if people come to Friendship City Hikari and try Otherworld Cuisine, many might be willing to splurge a bit.]","Kaori-san’s set meals are relatively inexpensive, with the most expensive one under 20R. That’s great because it offers affordable, delicious meals, but having a high-end option would also give customers more choices.","Since Kaori-san now has a large-capacity magic box, she has room to expand her menu, which is a plus. Overall, the response regarding the Spearmush was very positive.","[Matsutake rice, matsutake soup, matsutake chawanmushi, grilled matsutake...... a full matsutake set could be nice. We also have the good seasonings from Neun-san and rice from Raz-sama, so it should be a delicious set...... Oh, but first, I need to ask the wholesale price...... Kaito-kun, if you were to supply my shop, what price would you sell them at?]","[H- Hmm, let's see...... errr...... maybe 100R for 100 mushrooms......?]","[That’s way too cheap! Isn't that only 1R per mushroom!!! That price won’t work! Spearmush is a luxury mushroom, and if you offer it at that price, it would be problematic for me!] ᚱÄNꝊ𐌱ΕṦ","[W- Well, I guess so but...... I actually paid Lanza-san 100R per mushroom, which makes it 10,000R...... just one gold coin for 100 mushrooms. And I got 9,900 freebie mushrooms...... So if you look at the ratio, it comes out to 100 mushrooms for 100R......]","[Ah, I see. From your perspective, Kaito-kun, the effective cost per mushroom is 1R, so it makes sense you’d hesitate to set a high wholesale price.]","That’s right, it was just as Kaori-san said...... expressed in Japanese yen, one Spearmush would be 10,000 yen, but I only paid 100,000 yen for mushrooms worth 10 million yen, making the effective cost per mushroom about 100 yen...... So setting a price appropriate for a luxury mushroom feels a bit awkward.","[......Hmm...... then how about we do it on consignment?]","[Consignment?]","[The idea is, I’d take a bulk of Spearmush and sell it as set meals. Then we split the revenue from those sets 50/50.]","[I see......]","[Considering these mushrooms are hard to get for anyone other than Kaito-kun, it might be fair for you to take a bigger share. But if we start arguing about shares, you might bring up the effort for cooking and selling...... So let’s just keep it simple and split profits half and half. How about that?]","[That makes sense. That way, both of us can be satisfied...... Okay, can we go ahead with that?]","[Unn! Leave them to me!]","Thanks to Kaori-san’s suggestion, we settled on the plan where I would supply the Spearmush, she would cook and sell them, and we’d split the profits evenly.","[Then, should I hand over about a thousand mushrooms for now?]","[That’s too many. We don’t even know how well they’ll sell yet, so let’s start with a hundred. Once those sell, we can do the next batch.]","[Understood.]","[Is that everything regarding the Spearmush, Kaito-kun? Then...... errr...... I actually have a favor to ask of you as well......]","Although the Spearmush matter was settled, it seemed Kaori-san had something she wanted to discuss with me too, opening her mouth with a somewhat serious expression.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [With the Spirits' affection being racked up, the question is———–who will be the first to make it...... in other words, who will become Kaito-san’s girlfriend first? So, Love Expert Serious-senpai, who do you see as the most likely candidate?]","Serious-senpai : [Who the heck's a love expert!? I'm the embodiment of seriousness! The serious of the serious! There’s no way I’m a love expert!!!]","? ? ? : [Ah, yeah, yeah. So?]","Serious-senpai : [......For now, let’s assume all the Spirits have extremely high affection for Kaito. For example, Camellia or Ariel should have very high affection for him, but whether romantic flags are actually set? That’s a bit uncertain. I mean, their affection is very strong, so given some trigger, things could quickly turn that way, but at the moment, I don't see things turning out like that yet...... With that in mind, the three I’m watching closely in terms of danger are Lillywood, Rosemary, and Jutia.]","? ? ? : [Oh? And why is that?]","Serious-senpai : [First, Lillywood has been with Kaito the longest among the Spirits and has gone through a lot of events together. It's just, Lillywood herself seems not to fully understand romantic feelings. She spent a long time thinking of herself as just a tree, and she’s quite stoic, focusing only on work and not much on personal preferences, so she doesn’t really grasp romantic emotions. However, she does seem happy being seen as a woman by Kaito and sometimes struggles with her own impulsive actions. So the feelings are budding, but for now it’s an unfamiliar sensation for her. That means that with some trigger, the relationship could progress very quickly.]","? ? ? : [That’s a surprisingly detailed explanation......]","Serious-senpai : [Next, Rosemary has extremely high affection for Kaito and does have romantic feelings, but I think she doesn’t realize it herself. At this point, if Kaito were to confess, she’d probably accept immediately due to her high affection. But she’s naturally shy, inexperienced with social interactions, and even with those she trusts, like Camellia, her sense of distance can get messed up, so she’s not aware of her romantic feelings. If you asked her how she feels about Kaito, she’d probably say \"she loves him\" without hesitation, but she doesn’t realize that includes romantic love...... With this type, once Rosemary becomes aware of her feelings, the relationship could progress.]","? ? ? : [......And Jutia?]","Serious-senpai : [Jutia, on the other hand, is quite self-aware. From her words and actions, it’s almost certain she likes Kaito romantically, and she knows it herself. But because of her personality, she expresses affection straightforwardly and cheerfully, so Kaito probably doesn’t realize her feelings are romantic. Also, she’s not in a rush and doesn’t seem intent on advancing things quickly. It’s like she enjoys being close to Kaito, hoping slowly that he notices her feelings, taking a long-term, relaxed approach. So in her case, unless Kaito realizes that her actions mean love, not just like, it will take time to develop. But if he does notice, Jutia would express her feelings straightforwardly, and things would likely progress smoothly.]","? ? ? : [Fumu fumu...... No, isn't that clearly establishing yourself as a love expert?]","Serious-senpai : [No! I am the embodiment of seriousness!!!]"]},{"number":2449,"title":"Chapter 2449: Chapter 2450: Requested Item 8","paragraphs":["Since Kaori-san said she also had something she wanted to consult me about, after putting away the matsutake I’d brought, I decided to listen in detail while drinking the tea she served.","[......Errr, you see. I’m not sure how to put this, and if I’m just being full of myself you can laugh, but lately...... my skin, or rather my whole body just feels like it’s gotten prettier somehow...... younger, maybe? Don’t you feel like there’s something like that going on......?]","[Kaori-san has always looked young and beautiful, but it does feel like you’ve been even more polished lately...... Before, you already gave off an impression of looking like you were in your early 20s, but now, if someone told me you were a teenager, I might actually believe it. You’ve always had this youthful vibe while still feeling properly adult because you’re overflowing with vitality, but...... now that you mention it, your skin really does feel rejuvenated to a degree that can’t be explained by just that.]","[......It's because you're like this, seriously, this exact thing! Because you always give answers that are a perfect 100 points every single time, you end up inviting weird misunderstandings! I’m seriously going to start shifting toward making you take responsibility for that already......]","When I honestly answered what she asked, Kaori-san’s cheeks twitched, looking ard to tell whether she was happy or angry.","However, after taking a deep breath, she quickly composed herself and reset her expression.","[......No, if I keep throwing tsukkomis at Kaito-kun’s womanizing tendencies, we’ll never get anywhere. I mean, it really does feel like I’m strangely getting younger...... It’s a level of change that can’t be explained just by trying harder with skincare or paying attention to my diet. My height and everything else feel the same, but it’s like only my skin is reverting to a younger state.]","[Hmmm...... Does it feel similar to Life-san’s Blessing? If I remember right, Life-san’s Blessing is supposed to bring a person’s age or physique closer to the ideal state they themselves envision.]","Well, even if it’s an \"ideal\" physique, it seems to be limited to something the person actually was in the past, or could realistically reach through effort. Otherwise, my height should’ve grown too......","So it’s like you can return to a past state, but you can’t arrive at a future one. Fate-san’s \"Critical Point of Fate\", which uses her Authority of Fate at full power, is apparently something that lets one temporarily reach a future endpoint, but Life-san’s Blessing doesn’t go that far.","More than that, the Blessing itself doesn’t possess power on the level of a God’s own Authority, so what it can do is inherently limited. Of course, from the perspective of Humans like Kaori-san and me, its effects are still far beyond common sense......","[Indeed, I guess it's close to that? Actually, I did think of something along those lines.]","[You got something in mind?]","[Unn. You remember when Olivia-sama, you, and I went out together before? Olivia-sama spoke to me via telepathy then, right? You seemed to hear it too, so maybe you remember, but at that time, Olivia-sama said she had given me something like the Gods' Blessing.]","[......Ah, now that you mention it, she did casually say something like that. Olivia-san is technically outside the Gods' hierarchy, but she’s essentially a being close to the Gods, so it wouldn’t be strange for her to be able to grant a Blessing. In that case, Kaori-san’s changes might be due to Olivia-san’s Blessing?]","[That’s what I thought was most likely, and seeing Kaito-kun's reaction, it really does seem like that’s the strongest possibility.]","[Yeah. I don’t know how much the recipient can adjust it themselves, but the Supreme Gods' Blessings tend to share effects like eternal youth, and Olivia-san’s abilities are said to rival those of a Supreme God. In that case, it feels like she could easily make Kaori-san ageless or rejuvenate your youth.]","In Olivia-san’s case, the abilities that correspond to her Authority are the kind that can be exercised within the Friendship City...... but those are really just her original powers with usage restrictions applied outside Friendship City. That doesn’t mean Olivia-san’s inherent strength changes.","Even at my birthday party, her restrictions were temporarily lifted and she was able to use her full abilities in another world. Since those limitations are imposed on Olivia-san herself, not on her Authority, it doesn’t feel like the effects of her Blessing would disappear outside Friendship City.","[......So, moving on to what I wanted to consult you about...... I want to ask Olivia-sama about this in more detail, but going to the Central Cathedral by myself makes me hesitate a bit...... Would you come with me, Kaito-kun?]","[I don’t mind at all, but wouldn’t it be possible to ask her via telepathy?]","If it were possible to talk with Olivia-san through telepathy, that would probably be the quickest way to ask...... or so I thought.","[Well, you see. Errr, how should I explain this...... It might be easiest if you imagine it like a phone call? Olivia-sama calls me, and if I pick up, we can freely talk until the call ends...... but I don’t know Olivia-sama’s phone number, so I can’t call her from my side.]","[Ahh, I see. So unless Olivia-san connects the line from her side, you can’t telepathically talk to her. In that case, yeah, going to see her directly really would be faster.]","Communicating through hummingbird takes time, and apparently, Olivia-san usually doesn’t check hummingbird while she’s in the middle of prayer, so if she’s praying, there’s a chance the reply would be delayed.","......When I send messages, she always replies at lightning speed, but considering Olivia-san’s personality, that’s probably because it’s me, she prioritizes responding to me over prayer.","Given that, if Kaori-san wants to ask about the Blessing, going to see her in person really does seem like the best option......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [There is a potential stomachache flag, but...... it's rather weak? She’s already on good terms with Olivia to begin with, and Kaori herself has always yearned for eternal youth and having her youth restored, so if she’s given a proper explanation, she’ll probably accept it without much trouble...... And if that’s the case, what awaits after that is a Friendship City date with Kaori, who has a day off and plenty of time on her hands......]"]},{"number":2450,"title":"Chapter 2450: Chapter 2451: Requested Item 9","paragraphs":["The Central Cathedral isn’t all that far from Kaori-san’s shop, so we decided to head there on foot. Leaving the store behind, I walked alongside Kaori-san towards the Cathedral, chatting as we went.","[By the way, Kaori-san, do you usually come to the Central Cathedral?]","[Hmmm, I do attend the Heavenly Light Worship at least, but that’s really about it. In this world, there are quite a few people who worship once a month or so, so I think I’m on the low end.]","Heavenly Light Worship refers to a form of worship held twice a year...... during the Heaven Month and the Light Month. In other words, you participate in Godism's prayers once every half year, making it the most common style of worship in this world.","It’s basically like New Year shrine visits in Japan, so it seems most people living in this world do observe Heavenly Light Worship. That said, it’s more of a custom than an obligation, there’s no fixed rule about which day you have to go, and there are surely people who don’t go at all.","During the Heaven Month and the Light Month, the areas around the temples fill up with extra stalls catering to worshippers, so the atmosphere really does feel a lot like a New Year’s visit.","Incidentally, the Light Month came to be called that thanks to Neun-san’s achievements. Before that, it was known as the Earth Month, and prior to the friendship treaty, the practice was apparently called Heaven-and-Earth Worship.","[So, Kaito-kun, do you do Heavenly Light Worship?]","[Nope. If I go, complaints start coming in......]","[Complaints? If you showed up, I’d think the temple staff would be thrilled......]","[No, not from them...... It’s more like complaints from the Sanctuary saying \"If you’re going to a temple to pray anyway, wouldn’t it be better to just come here?\"......]","[A- Ahh, I see...... so that's what you meant......]","Yes, rather than complaints coming from temple officials, it’s from the one way higher up...... complaints from the God of the world herselves, the one on the receiving end of worship. If I'm going to go to the trouble of heading to a temple and offering prayers to God, then just come directly to the God instead, that’s the complaint she lodges.","(Of course, that’s a perfectly reasonable request. I’d be much happier if Kaito-san came to visit me than if you prayed at a temple, so that’s what you should do.)","......And so, because the God being prayed to makes that demand, I go to the Sanctuary for tea instead of attending Heavenly Light Worship.","While chatting about such things as we walked, we soon arrived at the Central Cathedral. No matter how many times I see it, it’s an enormous building, truly befitting of the center of the Friendship City.","There wasn’t any particular event going on today, but even so, there were quite a lot of people around, which really shows just how strong the faith of this world’s inhabitants is.","When Kaori-san and I entered the Cathedral, a priest who had been standing near the entrance approached us and bowed.","[Thank you from the bottom of our hearts for visiting the Central Cathedral. Shall I announce your arrival to Founder-sama?]","[Ah, yes. Please do.]","[Certainly. This way, please. We will prepare a room for you.]","After giving a small nod, we were led into what seemed to be a staff-only corridor and guided along it. Ever since my first visit, whenever I come to the Central Cathedral, a nearby priest or cleric usually approaches me right away and offers to take me to Olivia-san, making things extremely smooth.","If anything, no, without a doubt, it’s something Olivia-san herself has thoroughly arranged.","[......As expected. You’re basically on face-recognition terms with the Central Cathedral. As always, this kouhai of mine is just absurd.]","[It’s definitely on Olivia-san’s instructions though.]","[Yeah, probably. There’s no way Olivia-sama wouldn’t have informed the priests about how to handle anything involving you, Kaito-kun. When you put it that way, it certainly makes sense.]","Apparently, while we’re being guided like this, Olivia-san is already getting a rapid report, because I’ve never had to wait even 5 minutes. It’s incredibly thorough, an astonishing level of VIP treatment, but considering Olivia-san is at the top, I can see why Kaori-san would find it perfectly reasonable.","[Please wait here. Founder-sama should arrive in about 2 minutes.]","[Understood. Thank you very much.]","[You’re too kind.]","It’s great that everything is handled so smoothly, but if I had to point out one problem, it would be that nearly everyone affiliated with Godism in the Central Cathedral, including ordinary priests, treats me with such reverence that it’s like they’re dealing with a God herself. I can’t help but give a wry smile at that.","Well, if you include that sort of thing too, it's certainly just like Olivia-san but still......","[......So, uh, what kind of position do you think I’m being seen as here?]","[Ah, right, your interactions with Olivia-san are almost entirely at your shop, aren’t they, Kaori-san?]","[Unn. So I doubt the priests know who I am, and unlike Kaito-kun, there’s no reason for Olivia-sama to have issued any instructions about me to the clergy. In that case, am I being seen as just some unfamiliar civilian you brought along?]","[Maybe...... they think you’re some outrageous existence they just don’t know about yet?]","[Eeeeh...... please cut that out. Seriously. I’m begging you......]","It’s hard to say for sure, but in reality, Olivia-san and Kaori-san do get along quite well. Even if she were introduced simply as a friend of the Founder...... that would probably still result in a fairly high level of VIP treatment anyway.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well, even if it turns into some absurd level of VIP treatment with total face-pass privileges...... once you think about Olivia being the one in charge here, it somehow just feels like \"yeah, figures\". It’s strange...... So is this faith......?]"]},{"number":2451,"title":"Chapter 2451: Chapter 2452: Requested Item 10","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I'm on a business trip tomorrow, so the next update will be the day after tomorrow.","We were shown into a room, and, almost certainly timed to exactly at two minutes, Olivia-san arrived with a quiet \"Excuse my intrusion\".","She walked straight up to me, then smoothly, almost fluidly, assumed a posture of prayer.","[May I offer my gratitude for the blessing of being able to meet Miyama Kaito-sama...... Today, I thank you from the bottom of my heart for making the journey to the Grand Cathedral. Simply by Miyama Kaito-sama’s visit, it feels as though the very air of the Grand Cathedral grows more sacred.]","[A- Ahaha, sorry for dropping by so suddenly.]","[No, not at all. There is never a moment when the Central Cathedral would close its doors to Miyama Kaito-sama. And speaking for myself personally, I feel an abundance of happiness simply from Miyama Kaito-sama’s visit. Please feel free to come at any time.]","How should I say this...... she was Olivia-san as usual. Starting with a prayer right out of the gate and being overly grand about everything, I'd gotten pretty used to that by now.","After giving me a light bow and lifting her gaze, Olivia-san glanced toward Kaori-san and opened her mouth.","[Mizuhara Kaori, you have come as well. Your visit is welcome.]","[Ah, yes. Sorry for intruding...... The difference in how warmly you treat me compared to Kaito-kun really feels like you, Olivia-sama.]","Kaori-san might say that, but honestly, Olivia-san’s attitude toward Kaori-san feels a bit gentler. If it were anyone else, she’d probably just say a brief \"Your visit is welcome\" and leave it at that. The fact that she added \"you have come as well\" likely comes from their everyday familiarity, and it gives the impression that she holds Kaori-san in higher regard than most.","Of course, since the point of comparison here is me, someone offering a frankly ridiculous level of devotion, her treatment of Kaori-san only seems comparatively curt.","[Once again, welcome. What business brings you here today?]","[Errr, this time it’s not so much about me...... Kaori-san is the main focus. When the three of us went out together before, you mentioned that you’d given Kaori-san something close to a Blessing. We’d like to hear the details about that.]","[I see...... Ahh, my apologies. To leave Miyama Kaito-sama standing for so long is a grave sin worthy of being recorded in history...... Please, have a seat here.]","[There’s no such grave sin...... Well then, if you'll excuse us.]","At Olivia-san’s urging, Kaori-san and I took our seats. Olivia-san then bowed to me with a slightly tense expression.","[......Miyama Kaito-sama. If it would not inconvenience you, may I prepare tea and sweets before we begin our discussion?]","[Yes, thank you.]","[No, it is I who should thank you from the depths of my heart for granting me this opportunity. Since the time I previously had the honor of hosting Miyama Kaito-sama, I have continued my studies. I will devote myself wholeheartedly so that you may be satisfied.]","With an expression that looked like she was about to head into a decisive battle, Olivia-san began preparing the tea. From the looks of it, she was making hōjicha. She had set out ceramic, distinctly Japanese-style containers, and it was clear she’d studied far more than before. rἈ₦ȯʙƐⱾ","Before long, cups of fragrant hōjicha were placed in front of Kaori-san and me, followed by some tea sweets. Last time, Olivia-san had prepared cookies, but this time it was something green that looked like a Baumkuchen...... At a glance, it seemed to be matcha Baumkuchen.","[Olivia-sama, is this matcha Baumkuchen?]","[Yes. I studied what you once taught me, these Japanese sweets, and through trial and error, using reference materials and all the knowledge I’ve gathered so far, I created this...... I- I do hope it suits Miyama Kaito-sama’s palate......]","[It looks delicious. Then I’ll dig in right away.]","She was unbelievably tense...... Staring straight at me with an expression like a prisoner awaiting a verdict, with a level of seriousness that made it seem like she might start talking about disemboweling herself on the spot if the evaluation were bad.","That said, just from a glance, it looked extremely appetizing, so there shouldn’t be any problem.","Thinking that, I took a bite...... It seemed there was a layer of chocolate inside, and the matcha flavor paired beautifully with the chocolate. It was really delicious, and it went exceptionally well with the hōjicha too.","[......It’s really delicious. The chocolate pairing is outstanding, personally, it’s very much to my taste.]","[Ahh...... Hearing Miyama Kaito-sama say that makes me feel as though everything has been rewarded. Of course, I am still quite immature, but I am pleased that what I have learned was put to good use. As for the chocolate, after Miyama Kaito-sama graciously guided me to Dia Royal Chocolate before, I purchased it personally and adjusted it so it would suit this confection. Naturally, when serving something to Miyama Kaito-sama, it may still be far from perfect, but even so, knowing that it suited your palate fills my heart with joy.]","......She looked incredibly happy, no, the moment I said it was delicious, her expression changed in an instant, like a ray of light piercing through an overcast sky, and she became noticeably more talkative. Combined with her small stature, she looked unbelievably adorable.","<Afterword>","~~This time’s easy-to-understand summary~","Olivia : [Doki doki (; •̀ ~•́ )]","Kaito : [It’s delicious.]","Olivia : [・:*:・✧*。(ˊ▽ˋ*)✧*。・:*:・]"]},{"number":2452,"title":"Chapter 2452: Chapter 2453: Requested Item 11","paragraphs":["After finishing preparing the tea, Olivia-san said a brief \"Excuse me\" and took her seat.","[......Well then, let us begin anew. This is about Mizuhara Kaori, correct? A Blessing...... although, strictly speaking, I am not a God, so perhaps another term would be more accurate. Still, for the sake of keeping this discussion smooth, I will refer to it as a Blessing. That Blessing is what you wished to ask about, yes?]","[Y- Yes. When I think about it, I realized I never properly confirmed the effects with you, Olivia-sama. No, it’s my fault for not asking sooner, but...... various changes have started to appear......]","[I see. And those changes, could you be more specific?]","At Olivia-san’s question, Kaori-san began explaining, much the same way she had earlier explained things to me. She felt that her skin had become clearer, that she seemed to be growing younger, and she wondered whether this might be the influence of Olivia-san’s blessing, hence why she had come to ask for details.","[......I understand the situation. The changes you’ve sensed are indeed the effects of the Blessing I bestowed. As for the effects themselves, I have been adjusting them as we go, and at present they are in what could be called a Provisional state.]","[Provisional?]","[First, let me give a basic explanation of Blessings. This may be redundant for Miyama Kaito-sama, but Blessings bestowed by Gods come in two types: Provisional Blessings and True Blessings. Put simply, a Provisional Blessing is the act of applying Auxiliary Magic on a person using Authority to a target. A True Blessing, on the other hand, involves bringing the recipient within the bounds of one’s Authority...... granting permission to use a portion of that Authority. The case of Lilia Albert is an easy example. She has received a True Blessing from God of Time and Space Chronois, and through that grace she is able to use the Authority of Time, but only with regard to acceleration.]","......There was a lot in that explanation I was hearing for the first time, but there were also parts that made sense. In short, Lilia-san can use a power that stands above magic, Authority, but only for accelerating time, and because it is Authority, not magic, that acceleration cannot be nullified by ordinary Time-Space Magic.","The same goes for Fate-san’s True Blessing, she had explained it as \"becoming luckier\", but more accurately, it must be that the Authority of Fate activates in certain elements tied to luck.","[For this reason, when the Gods bestows a True Blessing, they always use the phrase \"to be inscribed in conjunction with my name\". Authority is the law of the world, the rules themselves. You can say those who receive a True Blessing gain the power to interfere with those laws, though only in very limited aspects. And the scope of these effects, whether Provisional or True, can be adjusted by the god who bestows them. What kind of effect to bring about, how much authority to grant...... all of that can be adjusted, as long as it remains within what that God’s Authority allows. As long as you understand that much, you’ll be fine.]","[Errr, then Olivia-sama’s authority would be......?]","[The power I possess, my Authority, is somewhat unusual. I have influence over all phenomena that occur within the Friendship City. Therefore, as long as it is an event that can occur within the Friendship City, it falls within the scope of my Authority. The effects are wide-ranging, but in exchange, they have no effect outside the city.]","Olivia-san’s Authority really was a bit special. It’s restricted to the Friendship City, but within that range, it can exert overwhelming power.","The conditions are limited, but within those conditions, it feels almost invincible.","[In addition to that, there are also the effects common to Blessings in general. A low-ranking God’s Blessing can prevent illness; a high-ranking God’s Blessing can prevent more serious diseases and extend one’s lifespan; and a Supreme God’s Blessing prevents all illness and grants eternal youth. These effects apply even with Provisional Blessings, but they only last for about a year. As such, lifespan extension or eternal youth doesn’t mean much unless it’s a True Blessing. And as for my Blessing...... it has effects nearly identical to that of a Supreme God.]","[H- Hyiihh......]","[At present, what I am doing for Mizuhara Kaori is closer to a Provisional Blessing, so it will expire in one year. However...... deciding on the final, official effects won’t even take that long, so there is no problem.]","Unn? Arehh? Kaori-san seemed too overwhelmed by the sheer scale of the discussion to notice, but something about Olivia-san’s wording just now felt...... odd.","What Kaori-san currently has is a Provisional Blessing, an experimental bestowment that’s being adjusted, since within the city it could potentially produce many different effects, and the final form hasn’t yet been decided.","But from the way Olivia-san phrased it just now...... didn’t it sound like once she decides what effects her Blessing should have, she’ll switch it over to a True Blessing?","H- Hmmm...... This feels like it’s taking a strange turn, but for now, I’ll just listen until the end.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [You know, I was just thinking about this...... Isn’t Olivia’s evaluation of Kaori way higher than Kaito or Kaori themselves imagine? I mean, the point of comparison is Kaito, whose favorability level is so broken it doesn’t even function as a reference, and from Kaori’s perspective it’s more like \"The person Olivia is fond of = Kaito\", so she probably hasn’t noticed, but I think her favorability towards Kaori is probably on a level that can’t even be compared to that of an ordinary person......]","? ? ? : [Right, so let’s take a moment here to recall their interactions up to now. With people like Kuro-san or Neun-san, Olivia-san basically just gives them a brief remark, almost a single sentence, and has zero intention of holding a conversation beyond what’s necessary. But with Kaori-san, whether it was during their date or even at the ship party, she’s the one starting conversations, asking things like how to eat certain dishes. In other words, she actively talks to her.] RаΝO͍฿ΕṠ","Serious-senpai : [Now that you mention it, it’s kind of hidden because her treatment of Kaito and Shiro is on a completely different level, but even compared to the others, her attitude towards Kaori really is noticeably different huh......]","? ? ? : [As a reference, we’ve prepared a favorability chart for you, so please take a look~~]","~ ~ ~ Olivia’s Favorability ~ ~ ~","People unrelated to Godism","10/100","Affiliated members of Godism","12/100","Acquaintances","15/100","Kaori","80/100","Kaito & Shiro","∞/100 (almost constantly increasing)"]},{"number":2453,"title":"Chapter 2453: Chapter 2454: Requested Item 12","paragraphs":["After finishing her explanation about Blessings, Olivia-san paused for a moment before resuming.","[......Now then, with the basic explanation of Blessings for Mizuhara Kaori concluded, I will explain the Blessing that I personally performed. To begin with, I would like to explain why I decided to bestow a Blessing upon Mizuhara Kaori in the first place.]","Both Kaori-san and I already knew this well, but Olivia-san was serious to an almost excessive degree. Since we had asked her for a detailed explanation this time, it seemed she intended to explain everything thoroughly, including the true reasons why she had performed the Blessing at all.","The explanation was likely to be fairly long, but both Kaori-san and I wanted to understand even the smallest details. Important information could be hidden in parts we hadn’t heard before, and for Kaori-san especially, since it concerned her personally, it was only natural that she would want to know everything in detail.","[Since being guided by Miyama Kaito-sama, I am keenly aware that I have been helped by Mizuhara Kaori in many different ways. Regarding meals at the diner, I pay the appropriate monetary compensation for the food provided, so there is no issue there. However, beyond that, I have sought Mizuhara Kaori’s advice on personal matters, and she has explained things to me or guided me in practice when my own knowledge was insufficient. In many respects, she has provided me with extensive assistance, and for that, I am deeply grateful to Mizuhara Kaori.]","[N- No, it’s not anything that grand...... I just happened to help out or listen once in a while, that’s all......]","Kaori-san scratched her cheek shyly, but in truth, she was quite good at looking after others. Apparently, she had given Olivia-san a lot of advice about date-related matters as well, so from Olivia-san’s perspective, she must have felt greatly indebted.","[In response to this various assistance, I wondered whether there was something I could do to repay her. From our daily conversations, I determined that Mizuhara Kaori primarily harbors concerns regarding aging, skin, youth, and romance. With regard to youth and romance, there are many abstract elements, and due to my own immaturity and differences in race, I judged it difficult to present concrete solutions. Therefore, I excluded those. Instead, I considered whether I might be able to address, with my own power, the matters of aging and skin, which Mizuhara Kaori seems to be particularly concerned about.]","[I- I see...... u- umm, Olivia-sama...... when you analyze it that seriously, it’s kind of...... embarrassing, or rather......]","[Mizuhara Kaori frequently speaks about aging and skin, but what she mentions most often is...... first, the influence of aging. Regarding this, there have been multiple statements about a decline in physical ability, such as being unable to push herself as hard as in the past. When examined in light of the characteristics of Humans, it does feel somewhat early for the influence of aging to appear, but I judged it to be within the range of individual variation. Next, regarding skin, there were cases where she expressed concern over deterioration due to aging, as well as mentions of skin trouble caused by work involving water or other external environmental factors...... However, comparatively speaking, there were many statements that used aging as the reference point..... From this, I arrived at the conclusion that Mizuhara Kaori may be more susceptible to the effects of aging than other Humans.]","[That’s not...... haaah...... h- how embarrassing...... I’m going to die of shame......]","I don’t know why, but although Olivia-san was speaking in an extremely serious manner, it felt as though Kaori-san was being subjected to public humiliation.","Well, it was true that there were effects of age, but from Kaori-san’s perspective, it was probably just casual chatter, things like \"My skin doesn’t have the same firmness it did when I was a teenager~~\" or \"Pulling all-nighters is harder than it used to be~~\", the kind of everyday remarks people make when they start to feel they’re getting older.","However, ultra-serious Olivia-san had taken those remarks as genuine worries, compared them against her knowledge, and concluded that \"Kaori-san has a constitution that is particularly susceptible to the effects of aging, and she is troubled by that\".","From Olivia-san’s point of view, human aging probably only truly begins at stages like middle age or early old age.","In reality, this was simply a difference between races and couldn’t be helped...... but Kaori-san, whose harmless small talk had been subjected to such earnest analysis, covered her face with both hands, looking overwhelmingly embarrassed.","[I did consider granting a Blessing with an effect that would resolve those concerns. However, since I do not possess the concept of aging, I cannot judge the deterioration caused by it, and because I do not know Mizuhara Kaori’s prior condition, I was unable to accurately grasp what state she herself desired. Therefore, I concluded that it would be best to leave that judgment to Mizuhara Kaori herself. By linking it to my Authority, I experimentally bestowed the following effect: while she is living within the Friendship City, any condition that the individual herself judges to be the result of aging will gradually return to her ideal state.]","[......Errr, so in other words, it’s not just a simple rejuvenation kind of thing?]","[Yes. To use Mizuhara Kaori as an example: if her skin has become more youthful...... that would be because she recognized its previous condition as being \"due to aging\". Conversely, the fact that her height has not changed would be because Mizuhara Kaori herself recognizes an increase in height not as aging, but as growth. The effects manifest gradually, and the influence of the individual’s own will is also significant. The reason the effect on her skin is particularly noticeable is, I believe, because Mizuhara Kaori strongly felt the effects of aging in regard to her skin.]","[......That’s true...... I was worried about my skin, but...... hearing it said out loud by someone else...... it’s really...... so embarrassing I could die......]","Olivia-san calmly explained the effects of her Blessing, but Kaori-san, whose worries about her skin had been unintentionally laid bare, had turned bright red all the way to her ears.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I think she's probably more embarrassed because Kaito himself had heard it. She talked about it with people like Akane, but in front of Kaito, she never said things like wanting to get younger or anything like that...... d*mn it, isn't she totally acting like a heroine!?] ꞦáNÓ฿ΕS"]},{"number":2454,"title":"Chapter 2454: Chapter 2455: Requested Item 13","paragraphs":["Kaori-san was being calmly exposed for having worried about her skin, and though she was sinking into a sea of embarrassment, Olivia-san continued her explanation in an equally calm manner.","[Not only the external factors, but I believe that the things Mizuhara Kaori perceives as the effects of aging, such as matters concerning her internal organs, have also been improved. How does that feel to you?]","[......Y- Yes, that’s true. I’ve been feeling energetic lately, and my physical condition is really good.]","[Fumu...... These effects were only provisionally granted, but how would you describe your actual experience of them? I intended to ask you eventually, but since we have the opportunity now, let us hear your impressions.]","[Ah, errr...... let’s see. Well, I do feel like something incredible is happening, but...... h-honestly...... I’m happy that my skin has become younger. I was starting to worry about a lot of things with thirty just around the corner, so...... if you put aside the embarrassment, I’m truly, genuinely grateful.]","Kaori-san was the type who switched gears quickly, so she gathered herself and shared her honest thoughts. She had been bewildered to learn that a Provisional Blessing had been applied to her without her noticing, and having it explained so matter-of-factly was embarrassing, but she was clearly happy that her skin and other aspects had become younger, and she expressed her thanks to Olivia-san.","[......If Mizuhara Kaori is satisfied, then this effect should pose no problems.]","[Eh? A- Ahh, so does that mean you might put it on me again? Even if it only lasts for a year, not aging during that time would be nice, and being able to maintain this skin would be wonderful too...... By the way, if I leave the Friendship City, will the changes revert?]","[Changes that have already occurred will not revert. To use another Blessing as an example, the Provisional Blessing of the God of Life, Life, allows the recipient to rejuvenate to a specific age at the time they receive it, but even after a year passes and the Provisional Blessing expires, the changes do not revert. My Blessing is the same. Moreover, the effects that prevent aging and illness will not disappear even outside the Friendship City.]","[Oh, that’s a relief.]","Hearing Olivia-san’s words, Kaori-san smiled. Seeing that, Olivia-san nodded once and then smoothly rose to her feet.","[By my name———- By the name of Olivia———- I hereby proclaim. In this realm that belongs to none and yet to all, the city where the ties of the three realms converge, God, Human, and Demon———- there I stand. Names are examined, names are recorded, names are guides, and at the end of that guidance stands thee. As one who belongs neither to Apostle, Divine Servant, nor Disciple———- by the name of Olivia, I grant permission for the name of Mizuhara Kaori———– to be inscribed in conjunction with my name.]","[......O- Ohh...... T- That sounds amazing. It’s cool, or rather, is that Godism's baptism?]","......Eh? Wasn’t that just now a True Blessing? The phrasing was different from that of the Gods, but she said something about Kaori-san's name being inscribed in conjunction with her name...... Didn’t she just casually bestow a True Blessing!?","Kaori-san, who likely didn’t even know the wording of a True Blessing to begin with, seemed not to fully understand what had happened and clapped in admiration, but it wasn’t my imagination, her body had glowed for an instant just now.","Probably, no, definitely, she performed a True Blessing.","[......Um, Kaori-san.]","[Unn?]","[That was probably a True Blessing.]","[................................................Wha!?]","At first, Kaori-san stared blankly, as if she couldn’t process my words, but after a moment her expression shifted into something I could only title \"A Bolt from the Blue\".","[T- T- T- True Blessing!? Eh? W- Why? What...... O- Olivia-sama!?]","[Yes? What is it?]","[Eh, just now...... did you...... that is...... perform a True Blessing?]","[If we apply the terminology of the Gods, then yes, calling it a True Blessing would be accurate. The reason I initially kept it close to a Provisional Blessing was to observe what effects would be appropriate for you, including how they progressed over time. Since Mizuhara Kaori has taken a liking to effects focused on improving aging, there is no longer any need to leave it as a Provisional Blessing.]","[Eh? Ah...... yes...... errr...... thank you very much?]","Though Kaori-san asked in a flustered state, Olivia-san remained calm and spoke as if it were the most natural thing in the world, leaving Kaori-san no choice but to nod along.","Most likely, Olivia-san had intended to perform a True Blessing from the beginning and was merely adjusting its effects...... Since Kaori-san judged those effects to be acceptable, Olivia-san must have decided there was no need to keep it in a trial phase and upgraded it to a True Blessing. From Olivia-san’s perspective, nothing had changed from her original plan.","Of course, I could understand Kaori-san’s bewilderment at suddenly receiving a True Blessing out of the blue......","[......Olivia-san, in the case of the Gods, the effects differ between a Provisional Blessing and a True Blessing, the True Blessing is stronger, right......? Does the Blessing you gave Kaori-san also have any differences?]","[The effects I mentioned earlier remain unchanged. However, since my powers relate to the Friendship City, there will be additional effects concerning that. It’s a modest change, but while Mizuhara Kaori is within the Friendship City, her abilities and such will receive a boost.]","[A- Ahh, errr...... so, while I’m in the Friendship City, it’s like I can become stronger?]","When I asked about the difference in effects between a Provisional and True Blessing, Olivia-san explained that there isn’t a major change, but while Kaori-san is inside the Friendship City, her abilities receive a buff.","It’s probably similar to the Blessings of Sky-san or Gaia-san, where a buff applies only under specific environmental conditions. Compared to the sky or the earth, the Friendship City feels like a smaller range...... and somehow, the smaller the range, the stronger the effect might feel......","[Quantifying strength is difficult, but if we express it in terms of magic power...... let’s see. While within the Friendship City, Mizuhara Kaori’s magic power will probably be about \"50 times\" her normal level.]","[Modest!? That’s not modest at all!?]","Hearing Olivia-san say it as if it were a trivial matter, Kaori-san let out a soul-stirring scream.","......For Olivia-san, at the level of a Supreme God, a fiftyfold increase in Kaori-san’s magic power is probably a minor change...... but for Kaori-san herself, it’s an extraordinary transformation.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Every now and then, Olivia gives off that sheltered lady vibe that comes from having so little social interaction......]","? ? ? : [Well, from the perspective of Olivia-san, who’s at the level of a Supreme God, even if Kaori-san’s magic power increases fiftyfold, it’s really just within the margin of error. Though, this is just an example using magic power...... There are other things that increase as well, you know.]","Serious-senpai : [Ah......]"]},{"number":2455,"title":"Chapter 2455: Chapter 2456: Requested Item 14","paragraphs":["Olivia-san used magic power as an example, but since this Authority has effects on many different things as long as one is within the Friendship City, it’s probably not just magic power that increases.","In fact, it wouldn’t be strange if each of her abilities were multiplied fiftyfold.","[There likely won’t be much of an impact.]","[No, no, that’s ridiculous enough, you know!? I mean, it’s fifty times we're talking about here, fifty times! That means I’ve basically gained incredible combat power, at least within the Friendship City......]","[But there are hardly any opportunities to fight within the Friendship City, are there? So wouldn’t the impact be negligible?]","[Ugh...... th-that’s...... y-yeah...... that’s true......]","That was an overwhelmingly sound argument. Even if combat power were multiplied fiftyfold within the Friendship City, there would hardly ever be a chance to fight there in the first place. And if an opponent that Kaori-san would need fifty times her strength to defeat were to go on a rampage inside the Friendship City, Olivia-san would surely deal with it herself.","Seen that way, there really doesn’t seem to be much opportunity to make use of fiftyfold combat power. Of course, it probably isn’t only about combat power, but still......","After hearing Olivia-san’s words, Kaori-san put on a thoughtful expression for a moment. Since she's the type to switch gears quickly, she was probably organizing her thoughts and preparing to come to terms with it.","Then, as if she’d finished switching gears, she turned toward me and flashed a sly grin.","[......Fufufu, look, Kaito-kun. It’s a coincidence, and it’s location-limited, but it’s still an incredible power-up...... I can definitely feel power welling up inside me...... This is it, the overwhelming magic power multiplied fiftyfold!]","[No, since it should be adjustable at will, I believe Mizuhara Kaori’s magic power hasn’t changed at the moment though?]","[......................]","[It also affects physical abilities, and a sudden change would cause confusion when adjusting your strength and so on, so I’ve made it possible to switch it on and adjust it at Mizuhara Kaori’s discretion. You’ll need some getting used to it, but you should be able to fine-tune the multiplier as well, and even focus the increase on specific abilities only. If necessary, I can instruct you on that, though it’s also fine if you simply grow accustomed to it naturally as you use it.]","[................................................]","Olivia-san is fundamentally calm and logical, so it seems she had properly considered the effects of a sudden increase in ability and taken countermeasures in advance.","That really is wonderful, and the fact that it can be kept off when not needed is reassuring too, there’s no worry about accidentally breaking things with suddenly increased strength.","......That said, if I had to point out one problem...... Kaori-san, who had jokingly talked about things like \"this overwhelming power\" to psych herself up, ended up crouching down and covering her face after thoroughly embarrassing herself.","Combined with Olivia-san’s calm, matter-of-fact tsukkomi, that embarrassment must have been pretty severe.","[......U- Umm, Kaori-san? Are you okay?]","[......I’m so embarrassed I’m going to die, yeah, you might as well kill me...... When you think about it, for something that’s supposed to be fifty times, things in my life didn’t really feel like it changed that much...... I even thought maybe the effect hadn’t been applied yet...... This is so embarrassing......]","It’s not that Olivia-san meant any harm, but somehow it feels like Kaori-san has been put through one embarrassing situation after another today.","Well, after writhing around with a bright red face for a while, Kaori-san recovered and stood back up.","[......Errr, Olivia-sama. Would it be alright if I try it out?]","[Yes. Just thinking about it should cause your abilities to increase. Fine adjustments will require some practice, but at maximum effect, no adjustment is necessary.] RåΝôΒĘs","[O- Okay. I’ll try it...... mmh...... o- oh......]","As Kaori-san clenched her fist as if focusing her resolve, even I could tell that her magic power was steadily growing larger.","[S- So this is fifty times my magic power...... Kaito-kun, what do you think? Amazing, right?]","[It certainly is impressive magic power......]","[......Ah, that look. That’s the face that says \"There are too many amazing people around, so compared to them it doesn’t seem that huge\".]","Kaori-san’s magic power after being multiplied fiftyfold...... just going by feel, it was about on the same level as Eta or Theta. I’m not very good at measuring magic power, so I can only tell roughly, but compared to Lilia-san or Anima, it felt considerably smaller.","I mean, compared to me it’s on a completely different order of magnitude, but still...... Incidentally, when compared with the likes of Isis-san or Megiddo-san, their magic power is so immense that I can hardly measure it at all.","It’s like looking out over the ocean with the horizon in view, you can tell it’s unimaginably vast, but you can’t really gauge how vast it is.","Well, there are plenty of powerful individuals who usually suppress their magic power, so maybe it’s only natural that I can’t really tell.","When it comes to people like Kuro, Shiro-san, or Canalis-san, I can’t tell at all anymore. It’s like looking up at the stars from the ground, you can see them, but you have no sense of how vast the universe really is. That kind of feeling.","[No, compared to me it’s an absurdly huge amount of magic power, and...... errr, since you weren’t in charge of cooking, you might not have talked much with them, Kaori-san, but I have two red-haired maids at my house named Eta and Theta......]","[Ahh, errr, the two who look like twins, right? I had a brief greeting with them at the ship party.]","[Yes. Those two are Baron-rank Demons, and your magic power felt to be about on par with theirs.]","[I see. From your perspective, Kaito-kun, that’s nothing special...... no, wait, it is special, isn’t it!? In other words, doesn’t that mean my current magic power is on par with Peerage Holders!?]","......Now that she mentions it, that’s true...... Lilia-san and Anima are on the level of Count-ranks, so there’s naturally a difference there, but considering that Baron-rank Demons themselves number fewer than fifty thousand across the entire world, making them truly among the elite upper echelon, having her magic power rise to that level is nothing short of extraordinary.","Unnn, it’s just that my sense of scale has completely gone numb.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well, he's recently started getting acquainted with Otherworld Gods, so even though he was already interacting mostly with people at the top before, his range of interactions has now expanded even higher. It’s only natural that his sense of scale would end up getting numb.]"]},{"number":2456,"title":"Chapter 2456: Chapter 2457: Requested Item 15","paragraphs":["For the moment, it felt safe to say that the discussion had wrapped up, and there was no doubt that Kaori-san had learned what she wanted to know.","She certainly hadn’t expected the True Blessing to be bestowed right here on the spot, but at least Kaori-san had been able to receive it...... or rather, she’d muttered under her breath \"But still, eternal youth really is nice\", so all things considered, it didn’t seem like a bad thing for her.","[......Ah, that reminds me, Olivia-sama. This whole thing got me thinking, if I wanted to contact you myself, what should I do? I mean, not cases where it’s fine to send a hummingbird and wait for a reply, but times when I’d like to get in touch as quickly as possible. Is it possible for me to use the Blessing to do something like telepathy from my side too?]","[It is possible, yes, but unlike hummingbirds, telepathy via mana wavelength requires the skill to project one’s mana wavelength over long distances. At close range, it can be done naturally, but if there is significant distance between us...... with Mizuhara Kaori’s current abilities, it may be somewhat difficult.]","[Ahh, I see. So for me, telepathy is more of a short range problem then.]","[That would be correct. Or rather, if you have business with me, there is no problem if you simply come to the Central Cathedral as you did this time. I have already \"issued notice to all priests\" about you, so if you give your name, they will relay you to me.]","[......Oof.]","Kaori-san had merely been trying to confirm a method of contact in case something similar happened again, but Olivia-san’s unexpected remark left her wearing an indescribable expression on her face.","What mattered here was how Olivia-san had informed the others about Kaori-san. There was no doubt that Olivia-san’s evaluation of Kaori-san was high, but when notifying other priests, had she really said something like \"She’s a friend of mine\"?","[......O- Olivia-sama? When you say \"issued notice\"...... h- how exactly did you put it? I- I mean, I’m not affiliated with the Godism Church or anything, so I was wondering how you explained me to the other priests......]","[Ahhh...... I told them \"She is a woman who shares a close relationship with Miyama Kaito-sama, and who also has frequent personal exchanges with me, often offering advice. Therefore, should she visit, she is to be directed to me directly.\"]","[......S- Something’s not right, my stomach hurts...... Didn’t my stomach toughness get multiplied by fifty too?]","Not a single lie had been told. It was true that Kaori-san and I came from the same place, and it wasn’t wrong to say we shared a close relationship. It was also true that she had frequent exchanges with Olivia-san and had offered advice to her many times.","That advice, however, was mainly about date plans and things along those lines...... but judging from how Olivia-san had informed the priests, it sounded as though Kaori-san was some remarkable figure who had deep ties with me and was capable of offering counsel even to the Founder, Olivia-san.","Even if Olivia-san hadn’t intended it, it felt like the other priests were probably recognizing Kaori-san as an important person within the Godism Church.","Kaori-san had her head in her hands, but since there was technically no falsehood involved, it would be difficult to ask Olivia-san to \"correct\" anything.","Or rather, if she did try to correct it...... there was also the very real possibility that the ultra-serious Olivia-san would explain things in meticulous detail and end up turning Kaori-san into an even stranger kind of important figure.","Kaori-san probably understood that too. She looked like she couldn’t say anything more, so I decided to step in and wrap things up.","[......Ah, errr, Olivia-san. Thank you very much for answering all our questions. I think Kaori-san got everything she wanted to know. You must have been busy with work as well, sorry for dropping by so suddenly.]","[Not at all, please don't mind it. For me, there is nothing that takes precedence over matters concerning Miyama Kaito-sama and Shallow Vernal-sama. Attending to this as my highest priority is only natural.]","[The tea and the Baumkuchen were delicious too. Thank you very much.]","[N- No, if Miyama Kaito-sama was pleased, there could be no greater happiness for me. Though I am still quite inexperienced, if I am granted another opportunity like this, I will further hone my skills and offer you even better hospitality next time.]","Olivia-san, speaking with genuine delight in response to my words, was incredibly endearing, she even had an almost puppy-like air about her.","......And at that moment, something suddenly occurred to me.","[......Ah, right. The exact date isn’t decided yet, but I’m thinking of holding a tea party at my place. Shiro-san is planning to attend as well, would you like to join us too, Olivia-san?]","[Me, at a gathering where Miyama Kaito-sama and Shallow Vernal-sama are both present!? O- Of course, it would be an honor far beyond my station, but...... w- would that be alright?]","[Yes. We’re still in the process of inviting people, so if you’re willing, I’d love for you to come.]","[To bestow such an honor upon me, my heartfelt gratitude for Miyama Kaito-sama’s vast and profound benevolence...... Though I am a person of many shortcomings, I will gratefully accept your invitation.]","[Alright then. I’ll let you know once the details and schedule are finalized.]","I’d invited her thinking that if Shiro-san was attending the tea party, Olivia-san would surely be pleased, but her reaction surpassed my expectations. She looked as though she were about to attend a truly sacred rite.","As a side note, when I briefly glanced over at Kaori-san, she was shaking her head vigorously from side to side, her face deathly pale, so it seemed best not to invite her.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Kaori got away...... but Eris’s stomach is about to give out......]","? ? ? : [Errr, as of now, the confirmed participants are Shallow Vernal-sama, Eris-san, Olivia-san...... and, well, Lilia-san will probably get dragged in too.]","Serious-senpai : [Lilia's naturally getting a spot on the participant list huh...... no, well, I guess she probably would......]"]},{"number":2457,"title":"Chapter 2457: Chapter 2458: Requested Item 16","paragraphs":["Leaving the Central Cathedral, I walked side by side with Kaori-san as we talked. She did look worn out, as expected, but since she had said she was happy about things like becoming eternally youthful, her expression was an odd mix, she seemed exhausted and pleased at the same time, making it hard to put into words.","[......By the way, Kaori-san. I can already tell your answer from how you reacted earlier, but I’ll ask just in case. Do you feel like attending the tea party?]","[Kaito-kun, can you imagine this? If my stomach gets a hole in it, I won’t be able to drink black tea, you know. If you’re going to invite me, do it only when there aren’t gods or kings or people like that around.]","[Got it. Still, when all’s said and done, Kaori-san, you’ve really ended up becoming something amazing.]","[Seriously! Even if it’s limited to the Friendship City, having power on par with a Peerage Holder...... that’s just insane.]","[Hmmm, but that part’s only based on my own sense of it, so it’s not exactly certain, you know?]","She did feel close to Eta’s and Theta’s amount of magic power, but whether that directly meant her strength was on par with a Baron-rank Demon was hard to say.","[No, I feel about the same...... Even if I don’t know the exact benchmarks, I do think I’ve reached around that level. More than anything, the fact that my magic power increased fiftyfold is just way too ridiculous.]","[So that really is the most important part?]","[You probably already know this, Kaito-kun, but magic power has the biggest impact on combat strength and it’s also the hardest thing to increase.]","[Now that you mention it, my own magic power hasn’t really increased at all either.]","[Same here. I’ve been living here for over 10 years, but it’s honestly only gone up a little since the moment I was summoned.]","As Kaori-san said, magic power is extremely difficult to increase. At the very least, I haven’t felt any growth myself, and apparently, Kaori-san’s hasn’t grown much either since she was summoned as a Hero Actor.","Magic power has a major influence on the power of spells and the multiplier of physical enhancement, so it’s no exaggeration to say that magic power directly translates into combat ability. The reason my own physical enhancement is so lackluster is, quite simply, because my magic power is low.","[Magic power is heavily affected by innate talent, and it only increases bit by bit. Even Eta-san and Theta-san from your side must’ve taken hundreds, or even thousands, of years, on top of their natural talent, just to finally reach Peerage Holder levels of magic power. That’s why Olivia-sama’s blessing, which lets someone reach that level instantly even if it’s region-limited, is so incredible.]","[If your magic power becomes fifty times higher, then the actual increase in combat strength wouldn’t just be fiftyfold, right?]","[Exactly. The more magic power you have, the stronger your spells become, and the higher your physical enhancement multiplier goes...... Well, of course, there are exceptions, cases where, due to aptitude, someone can use magic far beyond what their actual magic power should allow. My Water Magic falls into that category. My magic power is only moderately high for a human, but when it comes to Water Magic alone, I can unleash power and scale that should be impossible for my magic power. That’s why I was able to push through even when I had a mock battle with Frau-san, who had more magic power than me and superior physical abilities. Without that special aptitude, I think I would’ve lost normally.]","That probably applies to Hina-chan as well. In terms of magic power alone, Aoi-chan has more, but thanks to the sharp, Otherworlder-specific aptitude she has, Hina-chan’s physical enhancement is overwhelmingly stronger.","In fact, Hina-chan’s physical enhancement, in terms of multiplier alone, is said to rival people like Sieg-san and Luna-san, who are among the strongest of the Humans. It really shows just how extreme the specialization of Otherworlder aptitudes can be.","[With magic power multiplied by fifty, I might actually be able to use Maximum Magic, at least when it comes to water magic.]","[I’m not very knowledgeable about that stuff, but is Maximum Magic really that difficult?]","[Of course it is. Maximum Magic refers to spells that go beyond the frameworks of lower-, middle-, and upper-tier magic. Their scale and power are on a completely different level. Most Maximum Magics probably have enough power to wipe out a small city. I think you'd have to be on the level of a Count-rank before you could use them. Normally, even if my magic power increased fiftyfold, I still wouldn’t be able to use them, but since my aptitude for Water Magic is so specialized...... maybe it’s possible?]","[I see...... Isis-san was firing them off like nothing though.]","[No, no, isn't your comparison there ridiculous!? Death King-sama’s magic power is on such a different dimension that even comparing it to Count-ranks doesn’t make sense! Even if my magic power increased a hundred million times, I still wouldn’t come close, so of course she can spam Maximum Magic like that.]","In truth, the only time I’ve clearly seen Maximum Magic with my own eyes was during the battle between Isis-san and Iris-san. Well, it’s possible I’d seen it even before that, but that was the first time I’d witnessed it being used with it explicitly stated to be Maximum Magic.","Isis-san had used it so casually, but that was only because she herself is absurdly strong. Under normal circumstances, that kind of scene would be completely unimaginable.","[So the Six Kings really are on a whole different level huh......]","[The Six Kings are in a league of their own, sure, but from our perspective, even Count-ranks are already monsters. Baron- and Viscount-ranks aren’t at a level I can stand up to, of course, but I can at least understand that level of strength. But once you get to Count-rank, they're people who are like \"being able to react to light speed is just a given\", you know? That’s a whole different dimension...... Light speed is something you’d expect from only the very top-tier characters in battle manga, yet for them it’s basically the bare minimum. People say there’s a huge wall between Viscount- and Count-ranks, and honestly, I totally get it~~]","[......Maybe someday, Kaori-san might reach that realm too......]","[I won’t!? Or rather, I can’t!!! ......I shouldn’t be able to, at least. As long as you don’t do anything weird...... Whatever it is you're thinking, can you not? I feel like I'd get involved with some strange god or something and get super-buffed...... I'm just someone who runs a set-meal diner, okay!? I don’t need to be able to react at light speed!!!]","[No, I don’t plan on doing anything like that......]","[Even if you don’t plan to, that kind of thing just ends up happening anyway, that’s what’s scary about you, you know]","At Kaori-san’s words, delivered like a cry from the soul, I could only give a wry smile. Well, honestly speaking, if I were to ask Shiro-san or Makina-san, it might actually be possible for Kaori-san to gain strength on the level of a Count-rank...... but there was no reason to do something like that.","Alternatively, if some Otherworld God were to take a liking to Kaori-san and grant her some kind of Blessing, something like that might happen as well...... but well, realistically speaking, that was almost certainly never going to happen.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Wasn’t there a god who’s really close with Makina, and who was supposed to show up after the Berserk Gorilla?]","? ? ? : [But would that person even have any reason to personally take a liking to Kaori-san?]","Serious-senpai : [......Yeah, probably not.]"]},{"number":2458,"title":"Chapter 2458: Chapter 2459: Requested Item 17","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Tomorrow is Christmas Eve, but I'm on a business trip, so the next update will be the day after tomorrow.","For now, I’m heading toward Suiren with Kaori-san, but we haven’t really made any concrete plans for what to do afterward. I do want to do a bit of sightseeing since I'm in the Friendship City, but Kaori-san is probably tired and would want to take it easy.","Of course, I could wander around on my own, but somehow that feels like a waste.","[......Ah, right. Kaori-san, do you want to watch a movie together?]","[Eh? A movie? Have recording magic tools developed that much already? Last time I heard, they could only handle about three minutes of footage at most......]","Kaori-san is right, recording magic tools, which are equivalent to video cameras in our world, are still a work in progress.","From what I’ve heard from Mom and Dad, magic crystals are good at storing magic power, but they’re not suited for keeping video data. Even high-purity crystals can’t store long footage.","The reason is that, by their nature, magic crystals constantly absorb ambient magic power, which affects the recordings they store. To protect against that, additional protective magic formulas need to be inscribed, which nearly eliminates the storage capacity.","So, in other words, developing something like a Blu-ray disc or other storage media equivalent is necessary, and various trading companies are already pursuing development in that direction.","I’m sure the profits for the first successful company are enormous, but it’s clearly difficult. Even Kuro struggled with it, and it seems hard unless new materials or processing techniques appear.","Well, that’s not related to what we’re talking about now. The reason I invited Kaori-san has nothing to do with recording magic tools.","[Ah, no, not a recording tool...... errr, it’s understandable if you don’t know, but at my birthday party, Canalis-san gave me something like a tablet that lets me watch movies from our world. I can pay to watch everything from the latest films to old classics.]","[Eh, eeeh, you can even watch the latest movies!? That’s amazing! I really like movies, especially romance films. There are works that hadn’t been released yet when I was summoned here that I wanted to see...... and some I haven’t seen in ages...... Eh? Wait, can I watch them too?]","[Yes. You can project them as an SF-style monitor in the air or use a projector-like setup on a wall, both the visuals and sound are amazing.]","[That’s perfect! I want to watch! If you’re okay with it, Kaito-kun, let’s watch it at my shop!]","Hearing the word \"movie\", Kaori-san’s mood clearly brightened, and she smiled as she said it. Her reaction exceeded my expectations, but thinking about it, this is probably her first movie in over 10 years, so it makes sense that she’s excited.","Kaori-san also said she enjoys theater, so she likely likes narrative entertainment. Either way, I’m glad she looks happy.","[Then, shall we head straight to the shop?]","[Yeah...... ah, no, since it’s a movie, let’s buy some snacks too!]","[That’s true, snacks would be good...... and wow, you’re really excited.]","[Of course, I’m excited! It’s a movie we're talking about here! Theater is fun too, but it’s been ages since I watched a movie, so it’s thrilling. Thanks to magic tools, this world isn’t inconvenient at all...... but when it comes to entertainment, it doesn’t compare to that world with smartphones, computers, and the internet. The game we played for your birthday was fun too, it had been a while.]","[Ah, that’s true. Entertainment-wise, our former world definitely wins. Of course, this world will continue developing, but as of now......]","I think part of it is due to the contract between Shiro-san and Makina-san, which placed global restrictions on reproducing mechanical products or misappropriation of technology.","Now, those restrictions have been relaxed, and recording magic tools and other new technologies are appearing. So, there’s a possibility that these fields will develop further in the future, and maybe something akin to the internet could eventually be created, but that’s still a long way off.","[Ah, you can choose which movie we watch, Kaori-san.]","[Thanks! Wow, I’m excited! What should I watch? I could go for the latest release I wanted to see, or an old favorite...... it’s hard to decide! Kaito-kun, do you have a favorite movie?]","[My favorite works are mostly older ones. I guess the ones I watched as a child left the biggest impression...... for example......]","[Ah, those are classics for sure. They were often shown on TV...... I remember them pretty well too. And then there’s......]","While talking about our favorite movies with Kaori-san, we moved along to buy snacks in a cheerful mood. It was a spontaneous suggestion, but seeing her so happy made it completely worth inviting her.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......So, it's the start of a movie date?]","? ? ? : [Oui.]","Serious-senpai : [U- Uwaahh......]"]},{"number":2459,"title":"Chapter 2459: Chapter 2460: Christmas Extra - : The Scenery I Wanted to See - Part 1","paragraphs":["Christmas was originally the celebration of the birth of Jesus Christ, and I’ve heard that the origins of the date itself trace back to ancient Roman Sol festival...... but that’s a story that belongs strictly to the world we once came from.","In this other world, Trinia, Christmas feels more like a festival handed down from the past Hero Actors, a kind of exotic celebration from the Otherworld. It isn’t recognized as having any particularly deep origins or intent, and is understood simply as a festive event, much like a holiday.","Well, even in the Japan of the world I came from, Christmas was mostly treated as a once-a-year event without much concern for its original meaning, so in that sense, maybe there isn’t much difference after all.","If there is one clear difference, it’s that Christmas in Trinia involves decorations going up all over the cities, and in the capitals of each nation, stalls line the streets, creating a lively scene...... Rather than spending it quietly at home with family, the atmosphere is closer to a winter festival.","[It’s really lively, isn’t it?]","[......Unn...... decorations go up in lots of cities, but...... the capital has stalls and events, so...... it’s especially lively.]","Walking down a street crowded with people, but not so packed that you can’t move, I held hands with Isis-san. In the past, because of the influence of her magic power of death, participating in events like this would have been completely impossible for her. But now, thanks to an item she received from Canalis-san, as long as she maintains a barrier that prevents anyone below a certain level of power from coming within a 50 cm radius, she can walk through the city without any problems.","With Isis-san’s level of magic power control, excluding just me from the barrier is effortless, and as for the issue of her being a well-known figure as one of the Six Kings, using Recognition Inhibition Magic takes care of that as well.","She isn't exactly as skillful as Alice, so if she directly speaks with someone fairly strong, there’s apparently a chance they might notice something off. Still, unless they’re of noble rank or higher, it seems extremely unlikely she’d be discovered, so we can relax and enjoy our date.","The only remaining concern is that if I call Isis-san by name, others might notice, but that’s handled by a portable magic tool, modified so that voices don’t carry to the surroundings.","[But still, I’m really happy we can come enjoy the Christmas streets together like this with you, Isis-san.]","[......I’m really happy too...... of course, I’m glad people aren’t afraid of me when I come into town...... but being together with Kaito...... being able to see so many things...... even more than before...... that’s what makes me the happiest.]","As she said that, Isis-san smiled with pure happiness. She was so adorably angelic that just seeing that smile made me feel inviting her out on this date today had been completely worth it.","[Oh, there’s a Christmas tree in the plaza.]","[......It’s beautifully decorated...... come to think of it...... Eul and the others were making a Christmas tree at the castle too.]","[They’re getting ready for the party, right? I’m looking forward to tonight.]","[......Unn...... together with Kaito...... and everyone else...... I’m really...... looking forward to it.]","That night, we were scheduled to have a Christmas party at Isis-san’s castle with the Six Stars, and it sounded like Eul and the others were enthusiastically preparing for it. I couldn’t help but feel excited already.","[Well, we can buy presents later...... for now, let’s just enjoy the date.]","[......Unn...... together with Kaito...... I want to go...... to lots of places.]","[Let’s go around as much as time allows. Why don’t we start with that park over there? It looks like they’re holding some kind of event......]","When Isis-san and I stepped into the park, filled with a festive buzz, the first thing that caught my eye was a large stage, and atop it, people who looked like members of a musical ensemble lined up.","[......It looks like they’re singing in a chorus.]","[......A traditional winter song...... the stage is big too...... maybe they’re holding something like a choral competition.]","[That makes sense. There are a lot of groups gathered off to the side of the stage, so it really does feel like a competition.]","The Christmas here had nothing to do with Christianity, so it wasn’t a church choir or anything like that, but the group currently up on stage happened to have outfits and a song that gave off exactly that kind of atmosphere.","As I stood a little distance away from the bustling stage, holding hands with Isis-san and watching, I noticed the bright, genuinely delighted smile on her face.","[Isis-san, you look like you’re having fun.]","[......Unn...... being able to see...... so many people enjoying themselves like this...... makes me happy...... The old me would’ve...... just frightened them......]","Back then, whenever Isis-san visited a city, it would practically trigger a state of high alert. Naturally, she would never have had the chance to watch events like this up close.","In a way, that couldn’t be helped. If things hadn’t been handled that way, the Humans would have been terrified, fleeing in panic, and Isis-san would have been hurt even more deeply.","But that’s exactly why, now that those worries have been eased to some extent, I want Isis-san to enjoy all the things she was never able to enjoy before.","[......Of course, Isis-san has suffered for so long, so I wouldn’t say it’s a good thing...... but still...... being able to see the scenery you always wanted to see for the first time, together with you like this...... does make me a little happy.]","[......Kaito...... Unn! ......That’s right...... seeing the scenery I was never able to see before...... together with the person I love most in the world, Kaito...... makes me incredibly happy...... fufu...... I’m really looking forward to what comes next.]","[We still have plenty of time today to walk around and see things, so let’s look at lots of different scenery together.]","[......Unn...... Kaito...... I looove you.]","Hearing my words, Isis-san smiled blissfully and wrapped her arms tightly around mine, whispering her love in a sweet voice. The fact that Isis-san was so happy from the bottom of her heart made me incredibly happy too...... my heart felt warmly filled to the brim.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I- Impossible, an ambush!? M- Moreover, there are p- parts!? ......Ghk...... too...... sweet......! F- Fast......! Eve...... Can’t dodge!!! Endure? Can I make it out alive? No! I- I'll die...... kuh...... \"Sugar Sage: White Serious\"!!!]","Makina : (......An ability that swaps positions with sugar prepared in advance? But the object she swapped with was supposed to be sugar, and yet, after being hit by the lovey-dovey waves, it turned into a shortcake loaded with fresh cream...... That means the image Serious-senpai received from witnessing this round of lovey-dovey...... If she hadn’t swapped, she herself would definitely have become the shortcake. That image won’t be easy to shake off...... The mental damage Serious-senpai must have taken is huge.)","Serious-senpai : [......Hah...... hah...... d*mn it......]","Makina : [Well, putting that aside, I’m in the mood for chocolate cake right now!]","Serious-senpai : [......Huh?]","Makina : [So then...... hnng! \"Choco Sage: Black Serious\"!]","Serious-senpai : [Hey, don’t mess ar...... gyaaaaaah!?]","Merry......"]},{"number":2460,"title":"Chapter 2460: Chapter 2461: Christmas Extra - : The Scenery I Wanted to See - Part 2","paragraphs":["After watching the choral competition in the park, I walked once more along the bustling street together with Isis-san. There were plenty of Christmas-like decorations, and Isis-san kept darting her gaze around curiously, as if everything were new to her.","[......Christmas is...... a festival from Kaito’s world...... right? ......Compared to the Christmas in this world...... how is it?]","[Well, the decorations and the overall atmosphere feel pretty similar, I think. But the Christmas I can think of is more like having a party at home. You prepare things like turkey...... a whole roasted poultry, cakes, and spend time with people close to you, exchanging Christmas presents, that’s the image I have.]","[......You don’t really...... go out much around that time then?]","[No, not necessarily. A lot of people do spend it at home with their families, but there were also plenty who went on Christmas dates with their lover.]","When I think of my own Christmas memories, it’s mostly from when I was little..... nothing as grand as a party, really, just a day with slightly fancier food than usual with Mom and Dad. The main event was always the Christmas present waiting by my pillow the next morning.","I believed in Santa Claus until around the third grade, but even after I learned the truth, waking up to a neatly wrapped present by my pillow still made me happy.","Well, as for things like a lovers’ Christmas or a holy night, I never really had much connection to that sort of thing. So if you asked me what couples actually do on a Christmas date, I honestly don’t know all that well......","[......Then...... today...... it’s...... a Christmas date...... for me and Kaito...... right?]","[Yeah.]","Isis-san smiled shyly, and she was unbelievably adorable. Right, in the past things were different, but now I had a girlfriend so cute she could practically be called an angel. It made this Christmas feel like I was enjoying something entirely different from my childhood holidays.","[......There are lots of food stalls too. Since we’re here, should we eat something?]","[......Unn...... we eat chicken...... right? ......Then...... how about that stall?]","[......W- Well, we certainly eat chicken...... let’s stop by that one.]","The stall Isis-san pointed to certainly was selling chicken———- a yakitori stand. It wasn’t wrong; eating grilled poultry certainly counted. Still, whether yakitori should be considered a particularly Christmassy dish was a bit debatable.","That said, plenty of people eat fried chicken instead of turkey or roast chicken anyway. And as street food, yakitori on a skewer is easy to eat, so maybe it was actually the right choice.","As we moved in front of the yakitori stall, a pleasant, basil-like aroma drifted over. Instead of sauce or salt, it seemed more like basil chicken, and it looked delicious in its own way.","Since Isis-san said she didn’t eat very much, we bought one large skewer of yakitori with the intention of sharing it, then stepped away from the stall.","[......Kaito can...... eat first...... After Kaito eats...... I’ll eat too.]","[Got it. Then I’ll take a bite...... Oh, it’s light and really good. Go ahead, Isis-san.]","[......Thank you...... I’ll have some.]","The chicken on the skewer was fairly large and satisfying, and the basil-chicken-style flavor was really tasty. After I took one piece, I lightly held the skewer and offered it to Isis-san...... She moved gracefully, gently holding her hair aside so it wouldn’t touch the food, and took a bite.","Of the piece of chicken I’d eaten in one mouthful earlier, she only ate about a third, then smiled cutely.","[......It’s delicious...... But maybe the order was a mistake...... I should’ve eaten first...... and let Kaito eat the rest...... It’s...... a little big to eat in one bite.]","[That’s true...... Then let’s do it this way, Isis-san takes a bite, then I’ll eat the rest.]","[......Unn.]","Sharing a single skewer of yakitori like this felt surprisingly romantic...... it really made me feel like we were on a Christmas date.","Of course, even if it was a big skewer, it was still just one, so we finished it quickly. I tossed the skewer into the trash and started thinking about which stall to visit next, when suddenly Isis-san seemed to have noticed something.","[......Ah...... Kaito...... you’ve got a little sauce on you.]","[Huh? From the yakitori? Errr......]","[......Hold still.]","Before I could even ask \"Where?\", Isis-san told me not to move. She gently placed a hand against my cheek, leaned in close, and lightly kissed me.","The kiss landed slightly off-center from my lips, followed immediately by the sensation of her tongue lightly licking the spot...... When she pulled back, Isis-san, somehow already holding a handkerchief, softly wiped beside my lips, smiling as she did so.","[......Ehehe...... now...... it’s clean.]","[Thank you...... Ah, but maybe there’s some on the inside of my lips too?]","[......Ah...... that might be true...... then...... I’ll clean it...... one more time.]","Perhaps realizing my intention from my words, Isis-san leaned in again, her face lit up with a delighted smile.","<Afterword>","Bûche de Noël : [......Even with the Recognition Inhibition Magic, getting all lovey-dovey right out in the open like that, so you’ve grown up, protagonist!!! D*mn it!!! Thanks to that crazy god, I got turned into a log cake, you know!!!]","Makina: [Fufufu~n♪ Fufufu~n♪ Fufufu~n fufu♪]","Bûche de Noël : [Don’t hum cheerfully while you’re slicing me up! And also, Jingle Bells isn’t originally a Christmas song, it’s a horse-sleigh song, isn’t it?!]","Makina : [......The cake is talking.]"]},{"number":2461,"title":"Chapter 2461: Chapter 2462: Requested Item 18","paragraphs":["Thinking back on something calmly afterward is something anyone can experience. Kaori, who had readily agreed to Kaito’s invitation to watch a movie, found herself thinking as they went to buy snacks.","(I’m really looking forward to it, watching a movie for the first time in ages. What should we watch? A romance film, probably...... ah, but would Kaito-kun get bored? Maybe an action movie would be better. It’s been so long since I’ve seen a movie that I could enjoy any genre...... n- no, horror is a hard pass. I don’t mind scary themes, but the kind that relies on jump scares really isn’t my thing......)","For Kaori, it truly had been over 10 years since she’d last seen a movie, and she felt a buoyant excitement as she pondered what to watch.","Then, at that moment, she casually shifted her gaze to Kaito walking beside her...... and a word flashed through her mind like a sudden spark.","(......Arehh? Wait, is this...... a date? M- Maybe? A movie date feels like the most classic of classics, but...... ah, no, we’re not going to a theater, we’re watching it at my shop...... so would that be a stay-at-home date? A young man and a young woman...... young...... well, I'm still barely in my 20s, and with Olivia-sama’s Blessing, I've essentially regained my youth, so I should still count as \"young\", right? A- Anyway, a young man and woman watching a movie alone at home...... isn’t that totally a date?)","Her excitement over watching a movie for the first time in ages had kept that thought from occurring to her until now, but today was Kaori’s shop’s regular day off. Once they returned, it would be just her and Kaito alone, and once she started thinking of it as a stay-at-home date, she couldn’t see it any other way.","One could say she was overthinking it, but once her thoughts tilted in that direction, more and more ideas kept bubbling up.","(S- So what is this, really? Watching a movie together was Kaito-kun’s idea, so does that mean I basically got asked out on a date? No, but I was the one who suggested watching it at the shop, so it’s not like Kaito-kun necessarily intended it as a home date. Ahh, but we didn’t just part ways after meeting Olivia-sama either...... so maybe he wanted to spend a bit more time with me? That possibility...... might exist?)","Of course, Kaito himself didn’t have any particularly deep intentions, and based on their past interactions, Kaori thought that was probably the case. Still, she couldn’t say with absolute certainty that he had no intention of dating her at all. There remained the possibility, however small, that he might.","She had already held quite favorable feelings toward Kaito to begin with, and on top of that, Olivia-sama’s Blessing had resolved her long-standing worry about nearing her 30s and starting to see her age reflected in her appearance.","She’d thought about it that morning while looking at herself in the mirror during her shower. She didn’t flatter herself enough to think she was a peerless beauty, but at least to the extent of thinking \"Aren't I kinda cute?\", she could feel some confidence. Her skin condition had improved dramatically lately, and because of that, it was fair to say her awareness had drifted oddly in a romantic direction.","(......H- Hmmm, considering Kaito-kun’s personality, it’s probably right to think he just invited me as a way to help me refresh my mood...... b- but, maybe, just maybe, he’s a little aware of me as a woman...... I can’t say the chance is zero...... s- so what do I do? What kind of mindset am I supposed to go in with?)","Kaori understood that the correct course of action was to not be weird about it and act as she normally would...... but once she started thinking about it, the thoughts stubbornly refused to leave her head.","[......Um, Kaori-san? We’ve passed several shops already, where are we heading?]","Her thoughts kept circling without an answer. Unlike Kaito, Kaori didn’t have Sympathy Magic, and she wasn’t confident in her romantic experience either, so reading someone’s intentions was difficult. Still, she liked romance stories and had a fair amount of knowledge about love-related matters, which only made it harder for her thoughts to reach a conclusion.","(I mean, fundamentally, there’s a huge gap between my romantic experience and Kaito-kun’s. If he were serious about it, I could easily get swept along in no time, and there’s even a chance we’d cross the line. It’s not that my guard is loose or anything; it’s more like Kaito-kun is just too much of a playboy, or rather, he’s naturally cool and kind. Over the course of knowing him, I’ve thought he’s...... ah, no, actually, I’ve thought he’s really great. So if he came on strong, I feel like I’d just get overwhelmed and give in.)","At her core, Kaori’s affection for Kaito was high, and even if Olivia had been with them, she had gone on a date with him before. Part of her wanted to take the lead as the older one, yet another part of her felt that being pushed assertively wouldn’t be so bad either. With those conflicting feelings, Kaori wore a deeply conflicted expression.","[......You’re not hearing me? Errr, if we keep going, there’s also Carriage Street ahead, so......]","Perhaps because she was so lost in thought, Kaori didn’t respond to Kaito’s calls, continuing to walk on with the same troubled expression.","(I mean, I know Kaito-kun isn’t the aggressive, carnivorous type, but sometimes he suddenly has this dependable, cool way about him that really gets to you...... and getting led along like that wouldn’t be so bad either, I guess...... N- No, that’s too big a leap! We’re just watching a movie together at home, that’s all, ahaha, wow, I really let my imagination run wild there......)","Still lost in thought, Kaori continued walking straight toward the road meant for passing carriages. Judging it dangerous if things continued as they were, Kaito grabbed Kaori’s hand and forcefully pulled her back toward him.","[Kaori-san!]","[......Fwah!? Ah, eh? Eeeh, w- what, what!? K-Kaito-kun, you’re really going into beast mode......]","[No, you looked like you were about to step out onto the carriage road because you were thinking too hard...... sorry it ended up looking like I was pulling you into my arms.]","[......Huh? Eh? A- Ahh...... I see...... so that’s what it was......]","Having suddenly been pulled close by Kaito, Kaori’s thoughts were instantly blown away and her face flushed bright red, but his explanation finally made her understand what situation she was actually in.","And then, what came surging up next was an overwhelming sense of embarrassment.","[......I’m going to die of embarrassment.]","[Ah, errr, I’m really sorry.]","[No, that’s not about you pulling me in like that...... honestly, I’m grateful you stopped me]","[U- Unn? Then what is it about......?]","[Please, I’m begging you, don’t pry any further. My face is seriously going to explode......]","Realizing in hindsight just how deeply she’d been engrossed in what was basically romantic delusion, the embarrassment was enough to make her feel like flames were shooting out of her face. In front of the puzzled Kaito, Kaori stood there for a while, covering her bright red face with her hands.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [D- D*mn it...... this bûche de Noël is way too sweet...... I feel like I’m taking damage here. Isn’t there something more bitter!?]","Makina : [I like sweet cakes better. I mean, bitter chocolate has its own kind of appeal too, but when it comes to chocolate cake, I think it’s better when it’s nice and sweet.]","Serious-senpai : [Just when I thought the Christmas side story was over, this one’s turning sweet too...... does my personal hell never end......? Black coffee, please.]","Makina : [Here you go.]","Serious-senpai : [Thanks......]"]},{"number":2462,"title":"Chapter 2462: Chapter 2463: Requested Item 19","paragraphs":["I gently but somewhat forcefully stopped Kaori-san, who seemed lost in thought and completely oblivious to any sound around her. Stepping onto the carriageway was dangerous, and I didn’t even know where she was heading, so I think my decision itself was correct...... but because I moved suddenly, it ended up looking like I was pulling her close.","[......I’m really sorry for stopping you so abruptly.]","[No, it’s completely my fault. Honestly, it was a relief you stopped me...... the shop I was planning to go to, we’ve already passed it, so let’s go back.]","[Understood. But, what’s the matter? You seemed deep in thought.]","[......How should I put it...... not exactly long ago, but it feels like some long-forgotten youth of mine is acting up again, or something like that......]","[U- Unn?]","[No, it’s nothing. It’s just that it’s been a while since I’ve been to the movies, so I was thinking about what kind of movie would be good.]","Indeed, since it’s been over 10 years since her last movie, it makes sense that she would struggle with deciding what to watch. Since she said \"youth\", maybe she was thinking about romance movies. She did say she liked them......","[Indeed, it’s been a while since I’ve gone to the movies, so I’m also not sure what to watch..]","[Unn. It’s not just the genre, but whether to watch a movie I liked before or something I’ve never seen...... it’s a tough choice.]","[Kaori-san, you like romance movies, right? Among the newer ones \"Love Raised in the Evening Sky\" is the latest.]","[Eh? No way, that’s already out!? Ah, I see, that makes sense...... timing-wise, more than a year has passed in that world since I was summoned, so it’s not strange that it’s released. I saw the first trailer and wanted to go watch it, but I got summoned to this world before it came out.]","[Right, I haven’t seen it, but I remember reading some online news that said it did well at the box office.]","Naturally, there’s a time gap between the time when Kaori-san was summoned and when Seigi-kun and I were summoned. The movie that came up in conversation is relatively new, released around spring, but it seems it hadn’t been released yet when Kaori-san was summoned.","[I definitely want to see it. But, hmm, realizing that kind of time gap...... it’s kind of a strange feeling, isn’t it?]","[What do you mean?]","[Well, considering my age when I was summoned, when you calculate based on that world, Kaito-kun is not only older than me, but even older than Akane-san. But here, I’m older, so...... you really notice the time difference.]","[Now that you mention it, meeting someone from the same hometown really makes you feel it. Even Shigenobu-san, in that world, would be just a little older than me.]","Indeed, assuming Kaori-san was 16 like Hina-chan and Aoi-chan when she was summoned, one year later...... when I was caught up in the summoning, she would be 17-18, so clearly younger than me. By the same calculation, Akane-san would be around 20, and Shigenobu-san around 23-24, so their ages aren’t far from mine.","Of course, after being summoned, they’ve lived in this world for several years, so Kaori-san and the others are definitely older than me...... but the phenomenon of age being overtaken, which shouldn’t normally happen, makes the time gap feel very real.","[See? It’s interesting, isn’t it? Maybe that’s why...... talking with someone from the same hometown brings back memories of my youth...... or at least, it makes me feel like it...... I was summoned just after becoming a second-year high school student, so maybe I didn’t really feel much of my youth...... N- Not only that, I've been busy with all sorts of things back in my first year...... even after being summoned it was hectic...... where did my youth go......]","[H- Hmmm, being a high school student doesn’t automatically equal youth, but that age does carry that image strongly.]","[Right. By the way, Kaito-kun, how were things back then for you? Guess you must be popular huh?]","If we define youth as high school life, then I’ve had absolutely none of it. Back then, high school was almost entirely a commute between school and home, and I spent most of my time playing online games, so I hardly talked with any classmates.","It’s not like I was bullied or ostracized, but I was probably more like part of the mob...... I think the person I talked to the most was Akira.","[No, not at all. I hardly had any friends and was in the go-home club, and at school, I just slept most of the time.]","[Eh? That’s surprising. I would have thought you were already a ladies’ man back then......]","[Even back then, or rather, both in the past and now, I’ve never once been a ladies' man......]","[Heehh~~ hoh~~ Hmmm.]","[Eh? W- What’s with that slightly skeptical look......?]","I received a sidelong glance that seemed to say \"Who are you to say that?\", but unfortunately, I have no idea what she meant...... I mean, in this world, I do have plenty of lovers, so you could say I’m popular but...... it’s not like I’m a ladies’ man or anything like that.","Feeling somewhat awkward, I gave a wry smile in response to Kaori-san’s gaze.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Yeah, who are you to say that!? The guy who sets up flags with almost every woman he meets, what the hell are you saying!!!?]","? ? ? : [Well, Kaito-san is a bit clueless when it comes to distinguishing between like and love, so even if he senses that someone has positive feelings toward him, he often doesn’t realize it’s romantic until the other person makes a fairly direct approach. On the flip side, progress with those kinds of people tends to be fast, like with Isis-san or Vier-san...... well, going in too aggressively, like Gorilla-san, can backfire......]"]},{"number":2463,"title":"Chapter 2463: Chapter 2464: Movie Watching with Kaori 1","paragraphs":["When I came to a shop that sold sweets and snacks with Kaori-san, I found that they actually had a pretty wide selection. There were things that felt like old-fashioned dagashi, items more like modern snack foods, and even bottled cookies and dried fruits, it was surprisingly well stocked overall.","[......It’s kind of unexpected. I never really had the chance to visit shops like this before, and I haven’t had many opportunities to eat these kinds of sweets in this world, so it feels really fresh to me.]","[Ahh~~ Kaito-kun, before you bought your own house, you were staying with that noble family...... Lilia-san’s place, right? There’s no way a Duchy would serve these kinds of commoner snacks, so it can’t be helped. When you go on pilgrimages as the Hero Actor, you actually end up eating them pretty often, though. These kinds of sweets are aimed at commoners, so a lot of them keep for a long time and are good for snacking.]","[I see. When you think about it that way, the existence of the magic box probably has a big influence too, doesn’t it?]","[Yeah, that’s true. If you have a magic box, you don’t really need to worry about expiration dates, and you can even store freshly made sweets. So you end up drifting away from more everyday, commoner-style snacks.]","There are, of course, things like factories in this world as well. They use large-scale magic tools to mass-produce goods, and when it comes to sweets, the variety didn’t feel all that different from my original world.","Come to think of it, Nifty’s products are also made with mass production in mind...... but those are a different story. They’re special items made by Canalis-san. After all, they’re practically cheat-level products that don’t consume any energy at all, so they’re fundamentally different from ordinary factories.","Or rather, when it comes to the separate space he’s creating in the backyard, the contractual restrictions with Shiro-san seem to be fairly loose. As long as whatever is made there isn’t taken outside that space, it’s apparently possible to produce all kinds of items that would be completely inconceivable by ordinary standards.","[......Oh, and another big reason is simply that my magic box is already packed full of sweets. I mean, I’ve got about 800 of ripple pies alone......]","[......What kind of mental lapse leads someone to buy 800 ripple pies? You should just buy more after you finish eating them......]","[No, I didn’t buy them, they were a gift...... a thousand of them...... I’ve reduced the number quite a bit already.]","[1000 ripple pies as a present...... I really want to retort it’s way too many...... but with this related to Kaito-kun, if I react carelessly, there’s a high chance the giver is some incredible person, so I can’t say anything.]","[Would you like one too, Kaori-san? They’re really delicious.]","[Thanks. In that case, I’ll have one.]","The huge number of ripple pies I got from Ein-san, I’ve been giving them to acquaintances and eating them as snacks, and I’ve managed to go through about 200 so far. Even so, I haven’t even reduced them by half yet.","I mean, the taste is insanely good, and since they’re in the magic box, I can eat them freshly made at any time, which is wonderful...... but there are just too many. Well, I’ll take my time and work through them.","[Kaito-kun, your magic box has all kinds of things in it, doesn’t it?]","[Yeah, most of the things I get end up going straight into the magic box. I do tidy it up once in a while, but it’s so convenient that there are quite a few things I’ve left in there and completely forgotten about.]","[Ah, I get you. I got a large-capacity magic box too, and I often just toss things in with a \"for now, into the magic box you go\" mindset. Sometimes I even forget what I put in there. I mean, if you touch the magic box and picture it, you can tell what’s inside, but unless you consciously check, you don’t really know.]","A magic box has a function that lets you see, or rather...... recall what’s inside it. When the owner touches the magic box and declares that they want to check its contents, a list-like image of everything inside floats up in their mind.","[By the way, changing the subject, or maybe going back to it...... but Kaito-kun, do you have any favorite kind of sweets?]","[I think I prefer chocolate-based sweets over snack foods. Anything that combines chocolate and cookies is a guaranteed hit.]","[Ah, yeah, those are good. I like snack foods too, but if I eat too much with the same mindset I had when I was younger, my stomach gets upset, which is a bit of a problem.]","[......But with Olivia-san’s Blessing, wouldn’t you be fine now?]","[Oh, right, does it work on things like that too? I don’t plan on overeating or drinking excessively, but being able to eat as much as I could when I was younger might be nice......]","Indeed, back when you’re in high school, there are times when you feel like you could eat endlessly...... of course, that’s just a sensation, not like you can actually eat infinitely...... though well, there are people like Alice who really can eat without limits......","[Come to think of it, High-ranking Demons convert the food they eat directly into magic power, so it seems they really can eat as much as they want.]","[I see...... that would mean their calorie intake is basically zero, right? H- How nice. Being able to eat a lot without worrying about gaining weight sounds so nice...... You really can't help caring about things like your weight, you know.]","[From my perspective, Kaori-san is slim and is really beautiful, but I understand why you’d worry about it.]","In fact, thanks to Shiro-san’s blessing, I don’t gain weight no matter how much I eat either, but even so, when I have a late-night snack, I sometimes find myself worrying about my weight anyway.","Things like height and weight are exactly the sort of obsessions that other people can’t really see, but everyone has them in one form or another. It’s a tricky thing.","[......Geez, you really just say things like \"beautiful\" so casually, like it’s straight from the heart...... I’m doing my best not to be conscious of it, you know...... You really are......]","[Unn?]","[It’s nothing! Come on, let’s pick out some snacks!]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [W- Wait, the subtitle is...... are you planning to flirt? Are you seriously planning to flirt!?]"]},{"number":2464,"title":"Chapter 2464: Chapter 2465: Extra - : Connections Found in Unexpected Places","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I’m working flat out even on New Year’s Eve, so I haven’t been able to secure any time for writing. Because of that, this side story will be the final update of the year.","Thank you very much for everything this past year, and I hope you’ll continue to support me next year as well.","Okura Shigenobu, once a Hero Actor and an immigrant to this world, could be called the oldest of the still-living Otherworlders, setting aside special cases like Neun and Miyabi, who had reincarnated as Demons. Now, he lived a semi-retired life in a quiet rural backwater of the Hydra Kingdom.","Shigenobu had two children with his wife, Hannah, one son and one daughter, and a total of four grandchildren.","One day, one of those grandchildren came to visit the home Shigenobu and Hannah lived in.","[Grandpa, Grandma, I’m here~~]","[Oh, you made it, Nicole.]","[Welcome. Wasn’t it hard, coming all this way from the teleportation gate?]","[I’m fine, I’m fine. I usually travel much longer distances as an adventurer, so this is nothing.]","The visitor was Nicole, Shigenobu and Hannah’s granddaughter, who was currently working as an adventurer based in the Archlesia Empire.","After exchanging words with Shigenobu and Hannah with a bright smile, Nicole stepped into the house and handed over the paper bag she had brought with her.","[This is a souvenir from Dad.]","[Sorry about that. Tch, so he sent his daughter in his place while he stayed behind to work?]","[He said he couldn’t get any long stretches of vacation. He was complaining that where you live is way too rural, and just visiting is a pain.]","[Well, it is the middle of nowhere.]","Nicole’s father, Shigenobu’s son, was currently employed at a trading company in the Archlesia Empire. Since it dealt in foodstuffs and related goods, business connected to the Ritch Barony was especially lively right now, making this a busy season. Because of that, he hadn’t been able to take a long break.","Seeing Shigenobu’s wry smile, Hannah brought tea over to Nicole, who was wearing a similar expression.","[So, Nicole-chan, how’s life as an adventurer?]","[Oh, you know, Leo is just so stupid and reckless. I mean, he’s skilled and has guts, I’ll give him that, but he rushes into things without thinking, and that’s such a headache. Seriously, he’d be hopeless if I weren’t around~~]","[Fufufu, is that so?]","Nicole worked as a duo with an adventurer named Leonhardt. Though she spoke as if complaining, her expression was cheerful, making it easy to tell that, one way or another, she harbored feelings for Leonhardt.","Watching her endearing granddaughter, Hannah smiled warmly as well.","[Is Leo-kun not with you today?]","[Apparently, he got a letter from his family telling him to show his face once in a while, so he went back home with the grumpiest look on his face. He always looks really unhappy whenever his family comes up, so I didn’t ask. But he’s oddly knowledgeable about noble affairs, so maybe Leo’s from a noble house? Lately, he’s been saying that the nobles of the Archlesia Empire are in quite a panic or something like that.]","[Hehh. Well, it doesn’t really concern us, but nobles have their own messes to deal with, I suppose...... Oh, that aside, Nicole, you came at just the right time. I’ve got something good.]","[Unn? What is it?]","As Nicole tilted her head in curiosity, Shigenobu took out a finely crafted wooden box and placed it on the table.","[......I got this from an acquaintance not long ago. It’s Spearmush.]","[Eh? No way!? Spearmush, it's that, right? That super-rare high-grade mushroom from the Demon Realm? Hehh, it’s my first time seeing it...... and there are 10 of them!? Your acquaintance is incredible, Grandpa.]","[Well, there’s no doubt he’s something else entirely...... Anyway, it’s a bit too much for just Hannah and me. You should eat some before you go.]","[Yay! Thank you~~!]","Spearmush was an ultra-high-end mushroom. Nicole had known the name, of course, but this was the first time she had ever seen the real thing. Not only was it expensive, but it was also extremely hard to obtain simply because so few ever made it onto the market.","She did find herself wondering how Shigenobu had managed to get his hands on it, but Nicole also knew that her grandfather had an unusually wide network of acquaintances. Concluding that he must have acquired it through one of those connections, she accepted it happily.","[By the way, how’s Emiru doing these days?]","[My sister? I saw her a little while ago, but...... errr...... she looked really busy with work.]","[Unn? Emiru’s a monster scholar, right?]","[Unn. Apparently an abnormal variant of a White Dragon was confirmed, so she’s swamped with research. That White Dragon seems to be the pet of some extremely high-ranking noble, so direct investigation is difficult. She begged them to give her even a single scale, and she’s been desperately studying it ever since, but reproducing the mutation seems almost impossible, so she was saying it’s hard to even write a paper and didn’t know what to do, just holding her head in frustration.]","[I don’t really get it, but...... I guess if a new species turns up, scholars are bound to be busy.]","[She also said some really important Count contacted her, and that her posting might change too~~]","As for Nicole’s older sister, Shigenobu and Hannah’s other granddaughter, it seemed she was too busy with work to spare the time to visit them. After nodding in understanding, Hannah turned toward Nicole and smiled mischievously.","[......More importantly, I’d like to hear more about Nicole-chan and Leo-kun. How is your romance progressing?]","[Bfuh!? G- Grandma!? W- W- What are you saying......? I- It’s not like that between Leo and I at all......! He’s just, you know, like a troublesome little brother or something, no romance or anything like that!]","[Ara ara...... then have you been on any dates?]","[In a sense, our usual adventurer work is kind of like a date...... no, wait, that’s not it at all!!!]","Watching their granddaughter blush furiously as she protested, both Shigenobu and Hannah wore amused smiles.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [O- Oh, this is an unexpected connection...... Nicole is the granddaughter of Shigenobu and Hannah...... And Emiru?]","??? : [A monster researcher employed exclusively by the Victor Trading Company. The one that made the appraisal when Kaito-san went there to buy brushes.]","Serious-senpai : [Ah, I see......]"]},{"number":2465,"title":"Chapter 2465: Chapter 2466 - Movie Watching with Kaori 2","paragraphs":["<Author’s Notes>","Happy New Year. I look forward to working with you again this year.","Kaito and Kaori returned to the shop after stocking up on snacks and immediately began preparing to watch a movie.","[Can’t you project it like a projector?]","[That’s possible too, but we can also bring up a kind of sci‐fi-looking monitor in midair. So we’ve got a fair amount of freedom.]","[Ah, then how about using this table here? If we project it on the other side, it should look pretty good, right?]","After some discussion, they decided to use a four-person table. While Kaori arranged the drinks and snacks on top of it, Kaito got everything ready for the movie.","He powered up the device he’d received from Canalis and set up the film they’d chosen together...... a romance movie that had come up in conversation while they were out.","[I’m all set on my end.]","[Same here.]","[Alright, once you sit down, Kaito-kun, I’ll turn off the lights.]","They turned the lights off to make the screen easier to see. Of course, it was still daylight outside, so the room didn’t become pitch-dark, but without any large windows, the izakaya-style interior grew dim enough to feel pleasantly close to a movie theater atmosphere.","Kaori took the seat beside Kaito, and before long, the movie began.","(......Even being alone together in a dark room with the opposite sex, he doesn’t seem flustered at all. If anything, he even feels relaxed, like he’s used to being in this kind of situation. S- So this is what a romance pro looks like......? Or maybe I’m just overthinking it.)","She let her thoughts wander briefly like that, but soon found herself absorbed in the movie. It was something she’d wanted to see for a long time, and for her, it was her first film in well over a decade, which made the experience all the more moving.","The story was a romance between a widow who had lost her husband at a young age and a college student. In terms of the age gap, it might even be somewhat close to Kaori and Kaito’s situation.","(Hmm, this is really good. Total jackpot. I like how the heroine’s age is close to mine. I can relate to her in so many ways, and it really pulls you in. And a romance with a younger guy has that youthful, coming-of-age feeling, it’s the best.)","Since it perfectly matched her tastes, Kaori watched with a cheerful smile on her face. Then, at one point, she casually glanced over at Kaito beside her.","His profile, lit by the glow of the screen, showed him completely engrossed in the film, unaware of her gaze. That serious expression looked somehow gallant, and she felt a faint flutter deep in her chest.","(......Life really is unpredictable. Being able to sit like this and enjoy a romance movie...... when was the last time again? Middle school, maybe? Back then, I used to think, without any real reason, that once I became a high schooler, I’d naturally get to live a sparkling, wonderful youth...... but that never happened.)","Kaori had lost her parents shortly after entering high school. After that, she’d been rejected by relatives and passed around, swept along by rapidly changing circumstances, with no room in her life for something as leisurely as watching movies.","(After losing Mom and Dad, there were days when I didn’t even understand what was happening around me. I was rejected everywhere and even thought it might be better if I just disappeared...... Then, just when it was almost decided that I’d be sent to a children’s care facility, I was summoned to this world, and spent years traveling. I never even had the luxury to think about “youth”.)","Looking back, even she herself felt she’d lived a remarkably strange life. She didn’t regret her choices. There were things she felt she might have handled better, but even so, she genuinely felt that the life she’d arrived at now was a happy one......","(Seriously...... you never know how life will turn out. I never imagined that the youth I’d completely given up on after all that would come rushing back to me at a time like this.)","Kaori continued watching the movie, occasionally shifting her gaze toward Kaito sitting beside her and letting out a small, wry smile.","(......Still, maybe I was born under a weird star? In this belated youth, the person I end up liking...... is someone just as weird, definitely not easy on the stomach. What a troublesome boy.)","Her days had already been fairly fulfilling, having found things she wanted to do, but since meeting Kaito, life seemed to have gained even more color.","Her happiness had grown larger, but with it came more chaos, more times being thrown about, and her stomach had ached more than once.","Yet even so, she didn’t feel that her current days were bad...... On the contrary, there were many moments when she felt like she was truly living her youth.","(......Well, maybe love and youth are meant to not go as you wish. There are still so many things I don’t fully understand, but...... for now, hard on my stomach you may be...... My cool and dreamy belated youth, please continue taking care of me here on out.)"]},{"number":2466,"title":"Chapter 2466: Chapter 2467: Movie Watching with Kaori 3","paragraphs":["The romantic movie I was watching together with Kaori-san came to an end, and the ending credits began to play. Romance movies weren’t something I had many opportunities to watch, or rather, even when they were an option, they were a genre I rarely chose but...... it was more interesting than I had expected.","There wasn’t much of the kind of overly clichéd “passing each other by through misunderstandings” that I had imagined. Instead, the story unfolded at a good pace, and it felt like the bond between the protagonist and the heroine gradually deepened as it went on.","There was no sense of the creators’ intention to forcibly make it tragic just to move the audience, either. It was a straightforward happy ending, neatly wrapped up, and it left me feeling good after finishing it.","[......Mm~, that was fun! Watching a movie after so long really is the best.]","[It was interesting enough to become a topic of conversation. I don’t really watch romance movies, but it was quite absorbing, so I’m glad we watched it.]","[Well, it’s certainly a genre women tend to prefer more than men. But I’m glad you enjoyed it...... though, when it came to choosing the movie, it kind of ended up with me pushing my preference......]","Kaori-san said that with a wry smile, but it wasn’t as if she had forcefully pushed a romance movie on me. Rather, she’d been considerate of me, asking beforehand things like “Would an action movie be better?”","It was just that she clearly seemed like she wanted to watch the romance movie that came up, so it ended up being me who suggested watching it.","[Honestly, if it were just me, it’s not something I’d normally choose, so thanks to watching it together with you, Kaori-san, I feel like I lucked out by discovering an interesting movie. The story was more refreshing than I expected, too, and it wasn’t overly messy or blatantly trying to make you cry, which was nice.]","[There sure are a lot of works like that huh. You know, the really clichéd ones where, around the middle, the heroine suddenly finds out she has an illness, and you immediately realize “Ah, this is going to end with them being separated by death”. They’re fun in their own way, and in a sense they feel like the classic formula, but...... personally, I like happy endings. Those merry bad endings do move you, but after finishing them, they leave you feeling pretty heavy......]","[Yeah, sad endings or bitter endings do stick in your memory, and of course there are works that are so interesting you want to watch them again, but... I also prefer happy endings, since they leave you feeling better afterward.]","[Unn, unn. In that sense too, this movie really was good. I’m close in age to the heroine, so there were a lot of scenes I could really empathize with, and toward the end, I even teared up a bit.]","Exchanging impressions after finishing a movie is supposed to be one of the real pleasures of watching one together...... well, so I heard. Since going to see movies with my parents back in elementary school, I hadn’t really watched one together with anyone, but now that my conversation with Kaori-san was getting so lively, that had to be true.","[Come to think of it, the couple in the movie had about the same age gap as us.]","[Oh, right, Kaito-kun, you’re a university student, right?]","[Well, I already dropped out, so technically a former one......]","[I’ve never gone to university, so I don’t really know...... are the depictions of university in movies pretty accurate?]","[Hmmm, I think it depends on the university. For example, at the university I went to, there was a shop that sold textbooks and stationery, but there wasn’t one like the one in the movie that sold food and drinks. Instead, there was a convenience store right near the university, so we bought drinks and food there.]","[Ahh~, I see. If there’s a convenience store nearby, that does make sense.]","[Apparently, there are universities that even have convenience stores inside the campus.]","[Hehh~, I guess you could expect pretty stable sales, so from the convenience store’s side it might be good...... though there might be issues with staffing......]","Since there were still snacks we’d bought left over, I chatted idly with Kaori-san while drinking tea. Maybe because we’d just finished an enjoyable movie and were still riding that high, it felt like our conversation was livelier and more fun than usual.","[......The movie was really interesting, but I guess the downside is that watching one makes a lot of time pass.]","[Yeah, that one was about an hour and a half.]","[It’s around lunchtime, are you hungry, Kaito-kun? I can make something.]","[Ah, well, since you’re offering...... we did eat some snacks, so I’m not that hungry. Something light would be fine.]","[Leave it to me then. I’ll make some sandwiches.]","[Oh, I’ll help.]","[Now that won't do, maybe you should leave this to the professional. It’s not a dish that takes much effort, so don’t worry about it and just relax while you wait.]","After saying that with a gentle smile, Kaori-san went into the kitchen and put on an apron. Somehow, she seemed to be in an even better mood than usual, cooking with an air of cheerful enjoyment.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Midday...... r- right, Kaito went to Kaori’s shop around 10, then went to Olivia’s place and came back, and even after watching a movie it’s still only a little past noon...... which means...... this arc...... isn't over yet?]"]},{"number":2467,"title":"Chapter 2467: Chapter 2468: Movie Watching with Kaori 4","paragraphs":["We eat the sandwiches Kaori-san deftly prepared, and while taking a light post-meal break, we talk about what to do next.","[What should we do? Time-wise, it looks like we could still watch two more movies, but...... wouldn't watching films back-to-back be tiring?]","[Hmm, yeah. I do feel like watching one more, but I think I want a bit of a break in between. How about we just chat for a while...... Kaito-kun, do you have any movies you’d recommend?]","[Let’s see. I watched one at home the other day that was pretty interesting. I thought it was horror, genre-wise, but it leaned heavily into comedy, so rather than scary, it was more fun......]","With Kaori-san prompting me, I talk about a movie I’d seen before, carefully avoiding spoilers. She listens with interest, nodding along, occasionally asking questions, and our idle chatter continues on pleasantly.","Then, when the conversation reaches a natural pause, Kaori-san suddenly changes the subject, looking as if she’s just remembered something.","[......Speaking of which, I just realized something at home earlier, but...... now that I think about it, I’ve never been to your place, Kaito-kun.]","[Ah, that’s true. Akane-san has come over a few times, but you haven’t, Kaori-san.]","[Unn. I’ve heard from Akane-san that it’s an absolutely enormous mansion, though.]","[The exterior is basically a copy of Lilia-san’s estate, so...... it’s pretty much the same as a ducal mansion. There’s no doubt it’s a huge place. Well, we have way more rooms than we can use, so it’s hard to say we’re making full use of its size, but......]","The interior is different, but from the outside it looks almost exactly the same as Lilia-san’s estate, so calling it a mansion is certainly accurate. That said, compared to Lilia-san’s estate, which employs a large number of servants, my house has an overwhelming number of empty rooms.","Not everyone actually lives in the estate, but Lilia-san’s place has dozens of servants and a security force that might as well be private soldiers. Compared to that, the number of residents in my house is overwhelmingly small.","Me, Anima, Caraway, Eta, Theta, Mom, Dad, Aoi-chan, Hina-chan, and Canalis-san, ten people in total...... Nebula is at the World Tree, so there’s no room for her, and Illness-san has a room at Lilia-san’s estate, so she doesn’t live at my house either.","Other than that, I sometimes rent out rooms to servants from Lilia-san’s estate whom I’m particularly close with.","Living at one’s workplace can be mentally exhausting, but commuting from outside can be tough in its own way. Lilia-san’s estate is located in a high-end residential area of the central district, so even renting a place nearby is expensive. If you rent a cheaper room in another district, the distance to the estate becomes considerable, making the commute difficult.","Luna-san, for example, also commutes from another district, but since she can effectively be considered one of Lilia-san’s close aides, she was given a pair of registered teleportation magic tools, one for her home and one for the estate. Thanks to that, commuting from another district isn’t an issue for her.","However, it’s not feasible to lend such expensive teleportation magic tools to ordinary servants, so commuting servants apparently have it pretty rough.","It all started when I was consulted by one of those servants I get along with and talk to often, and I rented out a room in my house at a low price. Apparently, just having a single covered walkway between work and home makes a big psychological difference, and it was well received. After that, I suggested the same arrangement to other commuting servants I was close with, and as a result, a few of them now rent rooms in my house...... Even so, it’s only 5 people, so with a total of 15 residents, we still have rooms to spare everywhere.","[......Kaori-san, are you interested in my place?]","[Unn. How should I put it, kind of like wanting to see something scary out of curiosity...... I do want to see what kind of place it is.]","[Then, how about we move to my house and watch the next movie there? We can get there instantly with my teleportation magic tool, and if we register the coordinates on your teleportation magic tool, it’ll be easier for you to drop by in the future if you ever have business there......]","[That’s a really tempting proposal, and I definitely want to go, but...... wouldn’t it be sudden and inconvenient?]","[Not a problem at all.]","[Then, since we're at it, I guess I’ll take you up on it and come visit......]","Since Kaori-san usually has her shop to run, until now I’ve always been the one going to see her, but today is her regular day off, and timing-wise, it feels just right.","[Then, shall we head out right away?]","[Unn...... ah, Kaito-kun, if it’s okay, this might be a bit selfish of me, but could I ask you for a favor?]","[A favor?]","[Unn. I was thinking of asking Akane-san next time, but...... I’d really like you to take me to the Archlesia Empire once. I think I mentioned before that Chris-san took really good care of me in various ways, but even when I wanted to see her, the Archlesia Empire is far away, so I haven’t really had many chances to visit. Since I finally got a teleportation magic tool, I was thinking it’d be nice to register the capital of the Archlesia Empire as a destination.]","[Ah, I see. In that case, how about we stop by the Archlesia Empire once before going to my house?]","[Thanks, that really helps.]","Hmmm...... if that’s the case, maybe we could even go and see Chris-san briefly. Of course, that would depend on checking her schedule first, but for now, I’ll just try proposing the idea to Kaori-san.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Sliding from a home date straight into another home date!? N- No way, t- that can’t be real...... Is something so outrageous really allowed!?]"]},{"number":2468,"title":"Chapter 2468: Chapter 2469: Movie Watching with Kaori 5","paragraphs":["At Kaori-san’s request, we moved to the capital of the Archlesia Empire. The teleportation point I have registered is a plaza a short distance from the imperial castle. Walk straight down the main avenue from here and you’ll reach the castle; head off in another direction and you’ll quickly arrive at the upscale shopping district where the pet-related shops I frequent are located. It’s a place with excellent access all around.","[Lately, it feels like we’ve been coming to the Archlesia Empire quite often.]","[......Yeah. you’ve kind of been bullying Archlesian nobles recently.]","[N- No, I wouldn’t say bullying...... I think......?]","[If even the person himself doesn’t sound confident, then that pretty much answers it.]","I can’t deny it very strongly, everything involving Marie-san lately has unquestionably been my fault. I did apologize to her and gave her some clothes as a present, which made her happy, so that eased my mind a little, but there’s no doubt it’s still been rough in various ways. If I get the chance, I should probably do something again......","[The Archlesia Empire really does get a bit chilly around this time of year. It’s not quite winter yet, but compared to Friendship City, the temperature is lower.]","[Yeah, it definitely feels different from Friendship City.]","As for me, thanks to Shiro-san’s blessing, my body is kept at a comfortable temperature whenever it’s extremely hot or cold. Still, at this current...... how should I put it, temperature that feels like the transition from summer to autumn, I can sense it normally.","Compared to Friendship City, it’s a little cooler. If the Friendship City still retains a summer climate, then the Archlesia Empire feels like it’s fully in autumn.","[......Oh, that reminds me, Kaori-san, would you like to go see Chris-san? Of course, that would be after checking Chris-san’s schedule......]","[Hmmm. If we can meet, I’d like to at least see her once, but Chris-san is the Emperor and must be busy, so on short notice it might be...... Ahh...... With Kaito-kun here, then maybe it’ll work out somehow...... Hmm. Let’s ask about Chris-san’s schedule, and if she has some leeway, I’d be happy to meet her for a bit.]","[Then let’s check via hummingbird.]","If I were to ask directly for time, I’m sure Chris-san would force her schedule open for us. But that wouldn’t really be what either Kaori-san or I want, so for now, we decided to check Chris-san’s availability through hummingbird and only go see her if she truly has time to spare.","Well, Chris-san is sharp, so if I send a hummingbird asking about today’s schedule, she might figure things out immediately...... Still, if I phrase it indirectly, she should grasp our intent and let us know if it’s inconvenient.","[......Ah, we got a reply. It looks like a meeting ended a little while ago, and she has a bit over an hour free. I’ll let her know our situation and ask if she’s available to meet.]","[Meeting...... I guess being an Emperor means having all kinds of meetings.]","Since she happened to be free right now, I told her that I was with Kaori-san and asked if a brief greeting would be possible. Chris-san kindly replied with an OK, so we headed toward the imperial castle together.","[By the way, Kaori-san, you were summoned to the Archlesia Empire, right? Was the imperial castle where you stayed first?]","[Unn. After briefly greeting the Emperor at the time, Chris-san explained a lot of things and prepared a room for me inside the castle. Though, I set out on a pilgrimage pretty soon after, so I only stayed there for about 10 days.]","[That was the Emperor before Chris-san, right? From what I’ve heard secondhand, his reputation doesn’t seem very good.]","[Hmmm, I’m not sure. I barely spoke with him, so I don’t really know. But I did get the sense that he looked down on commoners, maybe?]","As for the Emperor before Chris-san, from everything I’ve heard so far...... Chris-san called him \"like a pathogen infecting the nation\", Risti-san called him \"a petty villain with a timid heart\", and Megiddo-san outright called him \"trash\". It seems he's someone getting absolutely trashed by everyone.","[I hear Chris-san’s reputation is extremely good.]","[Apparently, it’s gotten even better lately. I’ve heard that the entire Archlesia Empire is booming economically, and that Chris-san’s leadership is being praised to the skies.]","[Hehh. I have heard that she’s been implementing all sorts of policies and being called the Wise Emperor, so I guess those efforts are really bearing fruit.]","I remember that when I met Risti-san before, she said something along the lines of how the Archlesia Empire as a whole was on an upward trend, and that they wanted to make it a sure thing and push straight into a full economic boom. The fact that this has been properly realized is something you really have to admire.","[.......................]","[Eh? Um, Kaori-san? Why are you giving me that look?]","[Well, when it comes to the biggest trigger behind the Archlesia Empire’s economic boom, I think things like the God of Fate's Divine Protection, or the Supreme God attending their Founding Festival, played the largest role......]","[......How strange. That sounds oddly familiar.]","[You really are a kouhai who’s bad for my stomach.]","I see, so this is another case where I’m the cause...... N- No, but Chris-san was already working hard to bring about an economic boom in the first place, and all the stuff involving me was just a tiny little push in the right direction...... Couldn’t we just leave it at that? I- I don’t think anyone’s actually suffering because of it...... Errr, let’s see, I think there should still be about two tins of tea that helps with stomachaches left in my magic box......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......This guy, is he planning to inflict stomachache like he's giving away a tip......? This feels like one of those cases where, as an apology to Chris, he ends up handing over some dangerous thing that’s been lying dormant in the magic box, doesn’t it?]"]},{"number":2469,"title":"Chapter 2469: Chapter 2470: Movie Watching with Kaori 6","paragraphs":["When I headed toward the Imperial Castle together with Kaori-san, it seemed everything had already been arranged. Waiting in front of the gate was the person assigned to guide us...... or rather, Alexandra-san, no, Aria-san.","With Aria-san leading the way, we entered the castle. As we walked down the corridor, Kaori-san muttered with a deeply moved look on her face.","[......Being escorted inside without even a body check, even though we’re outsiders...... as expected of Kaito-kun.]","[Ah, now that you mention it, normally if you’re meeting the Emperor, they’d check whether you’re carrying any dangerous items, right? ......But wouldn’t that be pointless if you just put them into a Magic Box?]","[Eh? No, there’s the Box Lock Magic......]","[......Eh?]","Just when I thought a body check would be meaningless if dangerous items were hidden in a Magic Box, it seemed there was actually a magic designed specifically for that situation.","[There’s a magic called Box Lock that, with the owner’s consent, renders a Magic Box unusable for a fixed period of time. It’s a special Enchantment Magic that has no effect without the other party’s agreement, but it’s also used during ceremonies like the Festival of Heroes.]","[I- I see...... I’ve never had it cast on me even once though......]","[Must be because you’re treated like a VIP......]","From a security standpoint, it certainly made sense that there would be a magic capable of temporarily restricting a Magic Box. Still, I had visited all three nations’ castles before, and not once had I been subjected to Box Lock, no one had even suggested it.","[I apologize for interrupting your conversation, but there are mainly two reasons for that...... First, any magic that imposes such restrictions simply doesn’t work on Miyama-sama, who bears the God of Creation's Blessing. In the first place, Miyama-sama...... or rather, Phantasmal King-sama who guards you could wipe out everyone in this castle in mere seconds if she wished. So if Miyama-sama intended to attack with malicious intent, we couldn’t have prevented it in the first place, making such restrictions meaningless.]","[......Ah, I see.]","Having overheard my conversation with Kaori-san, Aria-san explained why no one had ever proposed casting Box Lock on me.","The two reasons were that Shiro-san’s Blessing rendered it ineffective, and that sealing my Magic Box wouldn’t accomplish much anyway.","[Shallow Vernal-sama's Blessing sure is amazing, isn’t it?]","[It is, but I still don’t fully understand what effects it actually has.]","I’d been told that Shiro-san’s Blessing stood above all other Blessings, but I didn’t really know its detailed effects. Even Shiro-san herself had just tilted her head and said \"Who knows?\", so I simply assumed it came with all sorts of effects.","Chatting like that as we walked, we soon arrived at the reception room. When we entered, Chris-san was already there.","[Miyama-sama, Kaori-san, welcome. Thank you as well, Head Maid, for escorting them. Please prepare tea for three......]","[Certainly.]","[Please, both of you, have a seat here.]","Prompted by Chris-san, who welcomed us with a smile, we sat down on the sofa in the reception room.","[Hello, Chris-san. Sorry for coming so suddenly today.]","[You weren’t busy with work, were you?]","[No, not at all. I happened to be free when I received your message, so there was no problem whatsoever.]","I hadn’t come with any particular purpose in mind, but Chris-san welcomed us warmly, chatting lightly with Kaori-san with a calm expression.","Once their conversation reached a natural pause, I spoke up.","[......Chris-san, it seems things have gotten pretty noisy in Archlesia lately because of me. I’m sorry about that.]","[Oh no, it’s true that it’s been surprising, but in terms of the nation’s interests, the benefits have been tremendous, so much so that I’m actually grateful...... if they’d happened one at a time, that is.]","[Huh?]","[No, pardon me. It’s nothing.]","It felt like she added something under her breath at the end, but her voice was too quiet for me to make it out. In any case, it seemed to be benefiting the nation, which was a relief.","[In truth, it’s only that the timing was moved up a bit. I’d already thought that we would eventually need to make changes to western logistics.]","[Hmmm, I don’t really understand that sort of thing, but wouldn’t it cost a lot of money?]","[Certainly, it does require a budget. However, with the land under God of Fate's Divine Protection and the Founding Festival, the overall economy is booming, and the national treasury is well supplied. That said, when it comes to an organization as large as a nation, moving money and personnel requires approvals and meetings from all sides, so the number of meetings has increased somewhat compared to before.]","She is busy, but from Chris-san’s perspective, maybe this is also a development she’d been hoping for?","[Ah, Chris-san. Here...... you might not need it, but consider it an apology, or maybe a souvenir. It’s a tea made by Canalis-san that’s effective against stomachaches caused by mental stress, so if you’d like......]","[......This is a most welcome gift. My heartfelt thanks...... I shall drink it regularly.]","......Arehh? For just a moment, it felt like her expression turned extremely exhausted...... Maybe she really is quite busy after all? Still, it’s not like there’s anything specific I can do to help, and if I tried something half-baked and ended up inviting a new round of trouble, that would be disastrous. Better not pry unnecessarily.","[......Ahh, speaking of tea, I’m actually thinking of organizing a tea party soon.]","[............................Huh?]","[......Kaito-kun, are you trying to make Chris-san drink that tea right away? You trying to solve a problem you're now trying to instigate?]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The currently confirmed participants are Shiro, Olivia, Alice, and Lilia (she hasn’t even been invited yet, but her attendance is basically settled), and he’s trying to drag her into what can only be described as a banquet from hell.]"]},{"number":2470,"title":"Chapter 2470: Chapter 2471: Movie Watching with Kaori 7","paragraphs":["This must be what they meant for one's blood to drain from a person’s face. It would not be an exaggeration to say that Chris Dia Archlesia, Emperor of Archlesia Empire, was now facing a terrifying situation.","[......Errr, well, it’s a personal thing, something on a small scale, but I was thinking of organizing a tea party...... I’m just at the stage of reaching out to people I thought of.]","First of all, Chris, renowned as the Wise Emperor and possessing extraordinarily high intelligence-gathering capabilities, was already fully aware of the exchange that had taken place during the tea party with Eris.","She therefore knew that Kaito had made remarks at that gathering about possibly organizing a tea party if the opportunity arose. However, his current words indicated that the situation had changed drastically.","(......At the tea party with Lady Eris, it sounded like nothing more than \"I might plan one if I get the chance\", but if he’s already at the stage of inviting participants...... that suggests there’s a high possibility that, in Miyama-sama’s mind, the decision to actually hold the tea party has already been finalized. Since it’s strictly Miyama-sama’s personal tea party and not an official event, there’s no need to consider the balance between the Three Realms or the Three Nations......)","Though shaken, Chris' thoughts began racing at extraordinary speed. More than the fact that the tea party would be held at all, what truly mattered was who would attend, and that was precisely the point Chris cared about most.","[I’ve only just started inviting people, but for now, the ones who are confirmed are Shiro-san, Eris-san, and Olivia-san. Of course, there’s no pressure, but Chris-san, would you like to join as well?]","For a brief instant after hearing the confirmed participants, the thought crossed her mind that \"Eris has been thrown alone into hell\", but there was something far more important that needed to take priority.","(Shallow Vernal-sama and Founder-sama alone already make this overwhelming, and I highly doubt it will end there. Miyama-sama is envisioning this as a small-scale tea party...... most likely with fewer than 20 participants. And though this is only speculation, at this stage Miyama-sama probably isn’t selecting participants based on any deep considerations, he’s simply inviting people he happens to meet or think of. That makes the randomness of the attendees extremely high. My guess is that once it exceeds around 10 people, he’ll start thinking about who else he should invite.)","Chris' reading of the situation was remarkably accurate. At present, Kaito wasn’t extending invitations based on specific reasons or logic like \"this person should be invited alongside that one\". The reason he had invited Chris now was simply because he happened to meet her at this moment and remembered the tea party.","And for Chris, this invitation was like having heaven and hell spread out before her eyes at the same time. Speaking frankly from her personal feelings, she had no desire whatsoever to attend a tea party that was all but guaranteed to give her a stomachache.","However, as the head of a nation...... as an Emperor...... the benefits to be gained were simply too enormous for her to even consider declining.","Even with only the confirmed participants, Shallow Vernal and Olivia were figures with whom it would normally be difficult to maintain even proper diplomatic contact. Considering that the nature of a tea party would allow for at least some degree of conversation...... the gains to be had in exchange for a stomachache were nothing short of tremendous.","(If this is merely a spur-of-the-moment, casually planned event in Miyama-sama’s mind, then the randomness of who gets invited is high, but even so, there are certain individuals we can reasonably predict. First, Duchess Lilia's attendance is practically guaranteed. Given her position, there’s no way she could skip a tea party being held next door with so many notable figures in attendance.)","Regardless of Lilia’s own will, or the damage it might do to her stomach, her participation could be considered virtually certain. Even setting aside such reasoning, it was difficult to imagine Lilia not getting dragged into a situation like this, so Chris judged her attendance as almost assured.","(Considering her relationship with Miyama-sama, her past participation in Lady Eris' tea party, and the fact that she heard about the plan to organize one, the likelihood of Kuromu-sama attending is also high. And if it’s a tea party hosted by Miyama-sama, then Eden-sama or Makina-sama...... I don’t know which one would come, but there’s a strong chance that that individual would want to participate as well. And if Eden-sama does attend, then Phantasmal King-sama would likely join as a stopper.)","The individuals Chris immediately thought of as having a high probability of attending were Lilia, Kuromueina, Makina, and Alice, four people...... Adding the three already confirmed participants and Chris herself brought the total to 8. By her estimation, there were only about two remaining slots left in the high-randomness participant pool, but predicting who those might be was difficult.","(This is a terrifying prospect. No matter how you look at it, the participants are all extraordinary figures, and accordingly, the benefits to be gained from interacting with them would also be extraordinary......)","What lay ahead was both hell and heaven. Not hell \"or\" heaven, hell and heaven existed simultaneously. In exchange for an unimaginable stomachache, one would obtain overwhelming rewards.","In other words, the choice before Chris now was between a 0 or 100...... Reject the invitation like Kaori and gain a momentary peace, or accept the stomachache in exchange for profit...... In a sense, there was practically no choice at all.","[......It’s truly an honor. Since this is such a rare opportunity, I’ll gratefully accept the invitation.]","[Got it. Then I’ll contact you once the detailed schedule is decided.]","Smiling towards Kaori, who looked at her with a worried expression, Chris conveyed her decision to participate in the tea party to Kaito. As she did, she silently vowed that once the two of them left, she would immediately brew and drink the tea she’d been given, said to be effective against stomachaches......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Even knowing that hell awaits her ahead, as the head of a nation, she simply can’t choose not to participate, given the lineup involved...... how terribly pitiful.]","? ? ? : [Kaito-san really is still at the stage of inviting people on a whim, so being invited at all is something rare...... you could even say it’s good luck, in a way. Also, can everyone please stop naturally recognizing me...... Alice-chan as Makina’s handler?]"]},{"number":2471,"title":"Chapter 2471: Chapter 2472: Movie Watching with Kaori 8","paragraphs":["Since it had originally only been meant as a brief visit, a short meet-and-greet of sorts, after chatting casually for a while, Kaito and Kaori thanked Chris and took their leave.","After seeing the two of them off, Chris returned to her office, checked the clock, and confirmed that she still had a bit of leeway before her next meeting. With that confirmed, she let her thoughts wander.","Naturally, what occupied her mind was the tea party being hosted by Kaito. At present, no concrete schedule has been decided yet; the date and time would be announced later. Taking that into account, Chris decided to leave some flexible room in her schedule for the foreseeable future. She roughly adjusted her plans in her head, then jotted them down in the memo at her desk.","(......Since this involves Miyama-sama, and the benefits to the nation are simply too great, adjusting my schedule itself won’t be an issue. Honestly, I could probably make it work even if they said it was the very next day, but considering things like a party held aboard a ship, they should allow for a certain amount of preparation time...... In that case, assuming it’ll be held around next month seems reasonable.)","At this point, Kaito already seemed to have firmly decided on holding the event itself. Once he began reaching out to potential participants and waiting for the final number to be set, preparation would inevitably take some time.","That said, when it came to preparations, Kaito had the overwhelmingly capable Canalis on his side. Because of that, the “next month” estimate was based on the assumption that only the period up to deciding the participants would take time, while the actual preparations would be finished almost instantly or at most in a few days.","(As for the participants Miyama-sama might invite on a whim, it’s hard to predict...... but once the number exceeds ten, it becomes possible to anticipate who he might approach next. When a certain number has already gathered and he starts wondering whom else to invite...... given the nature of a tea party, the first people to come to mind would naturally be those who enjoy black tea.)","As expected of someone called the Wise Emperor, Chris possessed both keen intellect and flexible thinking. Taking into account the information currently available, as well as Kaito’s personality, she began simulating the list of participants for the tea party.","(Among Miyama-sama’s acquaintances, the ones who stand out as particularly fond of tea would be Ein-sama and Jutia-sama...... but Ein-sama will probably not participate. She has an extremely strong fixation on being a maid, so she would happily take part if it were as part of the serving staff, but she would dislike attending as a guest. Miyama-sama surely understands that, and he wouldn’t invite Ein-sama knowing she’d be reluctant. On the other hand, the chances of Jutia-sama participating are quite high. She openly declares herself a fan of Nifty, and her relationship with Miyama-sama is good, if invited, she would undoubtedly accept.)","Chris' reading was spot-on. Jutia’s favorability towards Kaito was quite high, and even outside the context of a tea party, if Kaito invited her to anything at all, she would almost certainly accept without hesitation. If invited, her participation was all but guaranteed.","Another tea enthusiast would be Sieglinde, but Sieglinde would likely refuse to take part in a gathering where influential figures were seated side by side. Instead, it could be expected that she would remain in the rear as Lilia’s bodyguard.","(As for the other rulers of the Human Realm...... of course, as in my own case, there’s always the possibility of running into Miyama-sama by chance and being invited, so it’s not zero, but aside from that, the likelihood of them being invited is low. Regarding His Majesty Ryze, it’s unlikely that Miyama-sama would even consider him when thinking of candidates. Rather, the one who might come to his mind would be Prince Orchid, whom he is on friendly terms with. However, Prince Orchid would probably decline even if invited. In his case, appearing to hold more authority than Princess Amalie, the crown princess, could become the seed of a succession dispute, so he would avoid that. In fact, although he gets along well with Miyama-sama, he always seems careful to maintain an appropriate sense of distance, and he would not participate while leaving Princess Amalie out.)","From there, Chris' thoughts shifted to other figures of power and high standing. In this area, there was always the chance that Kaito might invite someone on a whim, so she gave it some consideration, but she felt that most of the individuals who came to mind had rather low chances of actually being invited.","(As for Her Majesty Laguna, she doesn’t particularly like tea to begin with, so the chances of Miyama-sama extending an invitation are low. As for the Supreme Gods of the God Realm, they would feel ill at ease sharing a table with Shallow Vernal-sama, so the likelihood of their participation is also low. As for the Goddess of Fate...... since she is his lover, there is a chance that the Goddess of Fate might be invited, but that one tends to find such gatherings troublesome. More likely, she would promise to have tea with him separately and either not participate in the tea party at all or opt to assist Shallow Vernal-sama instead.)","Her reading regarding the Gods was also quite accurate. In reality, Fate would very likely consider a tea party to be a hassle, and if she were to have tea with Kaito, she would much rather enjoy it alone with him. As such, she would not participate.","(As for the Six Kings other than Kuromu-sama and Alice-sama...... World King-sama does not consume anything other than water. A tea party is not the sort of setting War King-sama would enjoy. Dragon King-sama though, he might participate if invited. As for Death King-sama...... I wonder? With Lady Eris and myself present, the issue of the magic power of death would come into play. But with figures such as Shallow Vernal-sama, Makina-sama, and Canalis-sama present, it might be possible to suppress it by some means...... and in that case, participation might be possible......)","At this point in time, Isis had already received an item from Canalis during Kaito’s birthday party that could suppress the magic power of death. However, since Chris was unaware of the existence of that bracelet, she assumed that Isis might also participate if the issue of her magic power of death could be resolved.","Having thought that far, the time for her next meeting drew near. Chris cut off her train of thought, rose from her seat, and headed for the conference room.","......Incidentally...... her failure to account for the “Otherworld Gods besides Makina” would later come back to her in the form of a stomachache.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Hm? If it’s written this way, then...... does that mean there’s a chance that World Creators besides Electrone might participate? Either way, those stomachache flags are popping up all over the place......]"]},{"number":2472,"title":"Chapter 2472: Chapter 2473: Movie Watching with Kaori 9","paragraphs":["Since Chris-san also had plans, we didn’t linger for a long conversation. After talking for a bit, Kaori-san and I left the castle together, exited beyond the imperial castle grounds, and then used a teleportation magic item to move to my house.","We could have teleported directly into my room, but Kaori-san said she wanted to see the exterior, so we teleported to the area in front of the entrance instead.","[Ooh...... this is amazing. I mean, when I was brought here by Illness-san before, we teleported into the entrance hall, so I knew it was big, but...... seeing it from the outside is overwhelming. It’s like a mansion, or rather, it’s about the size of a luxury hotel.]","[I’m completely wasting all that space, though......]","[Ahaha, yeah, at this size you’d really need to employ a ton of people or you’d never make full use of it. And not just the house itself...... the garden is incredible too! It’s so well-maintained it feels like a stylish garden park, almost like a tourist attraction. Even though the house itself is the same shape, the atmosphere is totally different from Lilia-san’s residence.]","As Kaori-san said, the exterior of the house is almost identical to Lilia-san’s mansion, but the garden is completely different. Nebula and Illness-san carried out a large-scale renovation here, so it bears no resemblance to the garden at Lilia-san’s estate.","The garden at Lilia-san’s residence has a very aristocratic feel, carefully arranged in symmetrical patterns, complete with fountains, and wide enough for carriages to pass through from the gate. Because of that, there are comparatively fewer flowers and trees.","In contrast, my house is designed with the assumption that you enter on foot rather than by carriage. There are grassy areas and gentle hills so that Bell and Lynn can play easily, giving it a feel closer to a natural park.","[......Kaori-san, since we're at it, would you like to take a look around the garden?]","[Really? Unn, with such an amazing garden, I’d love to walk around and see it properly.]","[Then let’s take a light stroll around.]","She seemed genuinely interested in the garden, so before going inside the house, we decided to walk around it together.","The garden at my house is quite large, so even one lap covers a fair distance, but since Nebula and Illness-san paid close attention to the scenery, you can enjoy it like sightseeing, looking at beautiful flowers along the way, which I think is really nice.","Kaori-san looked like she was having fun, occasionally stopping to admire flowerbeds and the like.","After strolling together for a while, I spotted Bell and Lynn a little distance away. I couldn’t see Sela, so she was probably in Sieg-san’s room right now.","[O- Ohh, so those are the pets you’re so proud of, Kaito-kun. A Behemoth really does have an incredible presence......]","[They’re both good kids. Bell, Lynn, come here~~]","[Gau!]","[Kyui!]","Both Bell and Lynn are smart, so when they saw that I was with Kaori-san, they didn’t come over on their own, probably to avoid getting in the way, but when I called them, they both came trotting over, looking happy.","[Behemoths really do have insane amounts of mana, don’t they? Way more than you’d ever see in monsters from the Human Realm...... E- Errr, is it okay if I touch them? They won’t bite, will they?]","[It’s fine. Lynn only dislikes being touched around her neck, but anywhere else is no problem. Bell has...... preferences, you could say. She’s a bit prideful, and especially when it’s someone with less mana than her, she tends to make a slightly displeased face. There are exceptions though......]","[Ahh, a lot of high-ranking monsters are like that. If anything, White Dragons are also high-ranking monsters, so their pride should be pretty strong too...... Errr, then can I start by petting Lynn-chan?]","[Kyukui!]","Since I’ve properly trained Bell, she won’t growl or bite, but depending on the person, she could look visibly displeased. At first, I thought she simply rejected anyone she didn’t like, but it turns out she seems to judge people based on mana capacity. In general, she dislikes being touched by those with low mana...... people weaker than herself.","That said, there are a few exceptions. For example, she’s known Aoi-chan and Hina-chan for quite a while now, so she doesn’t mind being petted by them. She’ll even let them ride on her back, making a face that clearly says \"Good grief, I guess it can’t be helped\". Because of that, it seems that mana capacity mainly affects her first impression when meeting someone for the first time.","Lynn, on the other hand, has no such issues. Perhaps due to Dragon instincts, she doesn’t like anyone other than me, whom she recognizes as her mate, touching the area beneath her neck where her reverse scales are. Aside from that, she doesn’t mind people petting her at all.","Even now, as Kaori-san reached out and stroked her head, Lynn looked thoroughly content.","[They’re really friendly and cute.]","[Probably because Lynn used to belong to a Flying Dragon Flight, so she’s simply used to people.]","[I see...... errr, then what about Bell-chan...... is it okay if I pet her?]","[......Gau.]","[Eh? Is this really okay? My mana is lower than Bell-chan’s, but...... she doesn’t seem to dislike it?]","[No, if anything, with that reaction there’s absolutely no problem...... That’s surprisingly a good first impression...... Ah, I get it!]","When Kaori-san asked cautiously, Bell let out a short cry and lowered her head slightly. This reaction was unexpectedly favorable, similar to how she reacts to someone with greater mana than herself...... In other words, someone she considers stronger than her.","Of course, if you look purely at mana capacity, Kaori-san’s mana shouldn’t exceed Bell’s, who already possesses an enormous amount of mana even for an adult Behemoth...... And yet, that was when I realized that Kaori-san met one of the exception conditions.","[It’s not confirmed, but it seems that she also recognizes people who possess a True Blessing as being above her.]","[Ah, that must be because I have Olivia-sama’s blessing.]","That’s right, another of the exceptions is a True Blessing. It isn’t completely certain, but Bell is relatively obedient around Mom and Dad, and she doesn’t make an unhappy face when they pet her either.","I had suspected that this might be due to their having received Fate-san’s True Blessing, and seeing how Bell behaved around Kaori-san this time pretty much confirmed it.","I don’t know whether it’s True Blessings in general or specifically True Blessings from a Supreme God, but at the very least, Bell seems to recognize Kaori-san as someone above her and allowed herself to be petted calmly.","[Ooh! Amazing, this feels incredible. I’d heard about it, but you can really tell how particular you are, Kaito-kun.]","[Oh......?]","Of course, Bell’s coat is something I’m very proud of, it’s the ultimate texture, refined through extreme attention to detail. But the fact that Kaori-san noticed it with just one stroke shows that she has an excellent sense for discerning quality.","[As expected of Kaori-san. I’m very particular about Bell’s coat gloss, you know. If I go into detail......]","[Eh? Into detail? Ah, why do I feel like I just set myself up for a dangerous topic......?]","[First of all, the fur in this area is slightly softer than elsewhere......]","Given the opportunity, I figured I’d explain a bit about those particular details......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [His affection may shoot through the roof, but anything related to his pets are topics you absolutely must not casually bring up with Kaito. It’s the same as the okonomiyaki talk with Akane, but Kaori really does step on conversational landmines without thinking sometimes......]","? ? ? : [When it comes to topics like that, his doting-parent switch flips to ON instantly, after all.]"]},{"number":2473,"title":"Chapter 2473: Chapter 2474: Movie Watching with Kaori 10","paragraphs":["The pet-related topic that Kaori had casually brought up turned out, in a sense, to be a landmine. Kaito absolutely doted on his pets, Bellfreed and Lindwurm, and when it came to pet-related subjects, his level of enthusiasm was on an entirely different plane.","That said, unlike a certain God who would talk nonstop in such overwhelming volume that it felt like being crushed, Kaito still retained enough rationality to consider the other person’s circumstances.","This time as well, he didn’t go on so long that it ate into their movie-watching time. If one were to measure it purely by length, Kaito’s talk about his particular obsessions, such as Bellfreed’s coat texture, wasn’t actually all that long.","However, the intensity was something else entirely...... In any case, you could keenly feel just how overwhelming his fixation was. Even though he was speaking in a perfectly normal manner, there was something almost oppressive about it.","[......I’ve learned something today. Talking about Kaito-kun’s pets is like bringing up takoyaki or okonomiyaki when it comes to Akane-san, something you really shouldn’t do lightly......]","[S- Sorry. I got a bit too fired up......]","[Well, I get how you feel. If I started talking about my cooking preferences, I’d probably get carried away too...... When it’s something you love, you just can’t help but put passion into it, right?]","Once Kaito calmed down and realized his enthusiasm had gotten the better of him, he apologized, and Kaori replied with a wry smile, saying she understood how he felt.","Granted, her passion probably didn’t reach the same level as Kaito’s did with his pets, but since Kaori herself had plenty of particular preferences when it came to cooking, there were parts she could sympathize with.","[It ended up taking longer than planned, but shall we head to my room now?]","[Alright. Well then, Bell-chan, Lynn-chan, thanks for playing with me. See you later~~]","[Gau.]","[Kyuu!]","After lightly waving to Bellfreed and Lindwurm, Kaori went inside the house together with Kaito. As they walked down the hallway, their conversation about the pets continued.","That said, it was just ordinary small talk, not the kind of discussion that would send Kaito’s enthusiasm skyrocketing again.","[Lynn-chan was surprisingly affectionate, but Bell-chan felt cool and aloof right up until the end.]","[Bell has a pretty strong sense of pride, so that’s how she is with anyone outside a very select few...... That said, since she’s still a kid, she’s incredibly spoiled with me and Alice......]","[Alice-sama...... Unn? She behaves like a spoiled child around Phantasmal King-sama too?]","[Yes. Alice was the one who named Bell, so she adores her almost like a mother. Also, since Bell’s a smart kid, when she plays with me, she holds back, taking my physical abilities into account, but with Alice, she doesn’t need to restrain herself at all, so when she shows up, she happily pounces on her with everything she’s got.]","In truth, Bellfreed viewed Kaito as something like a father figure and Alice as a mother figure, and around the two of them, she behaved just like a child, clinging to them with all her might.","Especially with Alice, there was no need for restraint, so she would literally go all out...... using power that could turn not only an ordinary person but even an average monster into mincemeat in an instant. Still, to Alice, it was no more troublesome than a kitten playfully pawing at her, so she handled it without any issue.","[Alice is surprisingly good at taking care of others, you know. It seems she plays with Bell quite often. Because of that, Bell listens to Alice more than anyone else after me. Lynn, on the other hand, is friendly with just about anyone...... though lately, she’s been talking to Nebula a lot.]","[Hehh~~ yeah, I kind of get her. Nebula-chan is cute, but she also feels really dependable and attentive...... Like, she’s got this aura where even her cuteness comes with a kind of charisma, so it makes sense that Lynn-chan would get attached to her.]","[It also helps a lot that Nebula can perfectly understand Lynn’s magical wavelength as actual conversation.]","[Arehh? Didn’t you say you could do that too, Kaito-kun?]","[Well, that’s the thing. With Frea-san...... errr, Nidzveld-san, one of the Dragon King’s subordinates, her magical wavelengths come across to me as normal conversation. But with Lynn’s, I can sort of grasp the general feeling, but it’s not that clear-cut...... I think it’s because Lynn is still a child, so her ability to convey intent through magical wavelengths isn’t as refined as Frea-san’s yet. Once she grows more, I think I’ll be able to understand her clearly.]","[I see~~ The fact that you casually use one of the Four Great Demon Dragons as an example is just so like you, Kaito-kun.]","Lindwurm was still very much a young child. While her total magic power was quite large, partly due to the influence of her diet, her ability to communicate through magical wavelengths was still immature, very much a case of waiting for her to grow.","[But Nebula-chan can understand her already huh. That’s amazing. She’s really incredible. She’s good at crafting things, right?]","[Yes, Nebula is amazing. Not just with crafting, she’s talented in a lot of areas, actually......]","[Eh? Arehh? This feeling...... Eh? Don’t tell me, this too!? Talking about Nebula-chan is another one of those topics!?]","She’d spoken lightly, without much thought, but there was no mistaking it, Kaito’s voice now carried almost the same level of passion as when he’d been talking about Bellfreed’s coat earlier. Having dug her own grave in the most unexpected way, Kaori could only watch Kaito launch into another enthusiastic explanation with a wry smile.","(But still, seeing him like this makes him feel like a cute kouhai, no matter how far outside common sense he might be sometimes...... When you look at it that way...... maybe this isn’t so bad either.)","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [She’s got a comical side, but at the end of the day, Kaori properly has that neighbor lady vibe too, doesn’t she...... As expected, she’s a heroine you really can’t let your guard down around......]"]},{"number":2474,"title":"Chapter 2474: Chapter 2475: Movie Watching with Kaori 11","paragraphs":["Although she ended up listening once again to Kaito’s passionately charged explanation, this time they were still in transit, and there was a kind of time limit in place, the conversation would be cut off once they reached Kaito’s room. Because of that, Kaori listened to his talk about Nebula with a wry smile.","Before long, they arrived in front of the room. The conversation came to a pause there, and, prompted by Kaito, she stepped inside.","[......Huge!? It’s like on the level of a hotel suite, with the bed being king-sized too...... The rich-person aura is just way too overwhelming......]","[This room was arranged based on the guest room I was using at Lilia-san’s mansion while I was staying there after all.]","[Ahh, if it’s modeled after a Duchy's guest room, then I guess a suite-like size makes sense. I mean...... it’s still amazing though.]","The one who built Kaito’s house was Alice. To make it easy for Kaito to live in, the interior design of Kaito's room was modeled after the guest room he had used in Lilia’s mansion, but since he was the homeowner, the room itself had been expanded in size.","It was a room so spacious that an ordinary person like Kaori would almost never have a chance to see one like it, and the items displayed inside radiated an overwhelming sense of luxury as well.","Even if it was the room of Kaito, someone she was fairly close to, it was only natural that she would feel a bit overawed by the sheer opulence.","[......Ahh, you got the birthday photos too. Arehh? And this painting on the wall...... is this Japan? It kind of feels like a festival stall scene.]","[Ah, that one’s...... hard to explain. It’s a painting of a festival from a dream...... I guess you could say?]","[U- Unn?]","[That painting was a gift from Alice, but...... how do I put it, there was this thing where, in a dream-like state, or maybe a world of consciousness only, Alice and I went around a festival together. This is a painting of the scenery from back then.]","[H- Hmmm...... I don’t really get the situation, but if it’s you, Kaito-kun, I guess it wouldn’t be strange for something like that to happen...... Still, I should probably say it’s amazing, like, as expected of the Phantasmal King-sama. It’s an incredible painting. It really pulls you in...... I don’t know anything about art, but it feels really captivating somehow...... Yeah, it’s a really nice painting~~]","[It’s warm and cheerful, but there’s also a hint of loneliness to it...... It really feels like it captured the atmosphere of a festival just as it was. I like it a lot too.]","Kaito and Kaori’s impressions were fairly simple, but if someone knowledgeable about art, like Rosemary, had been there, they would have been utterly engrossed in the painting.","After all, this painting had been created using the same paint as the legendary artwork Seven Planet.","The paint used to create Seven Planet was a mysterious kind of paint Alice had made long ago after defeating the Seven-Star Demon Beast, a magical beast born of the stars, using its materials. It was something that could be said to be almost impossible to recreate.","After finishing her true masterpiece, Blue Earth, and then Seven Planet with the remaining paint, Alice had kept what little was left...... an amount not even enough to finish a single painting as a keepsake.","Later on, she realized that Makina’s Heart Tool, Factory Gear, could be used to increase the amount of paint. Using copied and multiplied paint, she painted this festival scene and presented it to Kaito as a gift.","In other words, this was, in a sense, the newest...... a work that could be called the ninth iteration of the Seven Planet series. It was an artwork of tremendous value, but since Kaito wasn’t particularly well-versed in art, and Alice herself had simply painted a nostalgic scene as a gift without bothering to explain anything about the paint, its true worth was still unknown.","If Rosemary were to visit Kaito’s room, she would notice it immediately. However, the last time she visited the house, they had tea on the garden terrace, and afterward it was usually Kaito who went to visit Rosemary’s home instead, so she still hadn’t laid eyes on this painting.","[But festivals really are nice huh~~ Maybe there are festivals with a similar vibe in this world too.]","[There probably are...... actually, the thing Kuro produced for the first Six Kings Festival was kind of festival-like, so I think it’s pretty likely.]","[Searching for them sounds fun. Lately I’ve had a bit more financial leeway too, so I’ve been thinking that traveling could be fun. Well, it’ll probably be a little different from Japanese festivals, but that’s part of the fun too.]","[True. Ah, though, if you use that gate over there, you can go to Japan too.]","[....................................Excuse me?]","Hearing the words Kaito said so casually, Kaori stared blankly back and forth between the gate in the room and Kaito’s face.","[Errr, that gate is something I received from Shiro-san, and it can be used to travel to the Otherworld. It seems that, basically, no one other than me can make the trip to the Otherworld...... but if someone is holding my hand or in physical contact with me, we can move together. So if you really wanted to, you could go to Japan too. Well, there are restrictions, like you can’t bring things from over there to this side, that sort of thing.]","[....................................H- Hehh...... You know, when you say something that incredible, could you at least say it with a \"I’m about to say something amazing\" kind of face? My heart almost stopped...... So that means if I’m with Kaito-kun, I can go to the Otherworld...... Well, my existence over there, including official records and all, has already been erased, and I don’t really think about going back at this point, but...... that’s still a pretty shocking fact.]","Kaori didn’t have any particular lingering attachment to the Otherworld, so even after hearing about the existence of a gate that allowed travel between worlds, she didn’t really feel like going there. Still, a certain thought crossed her mind.","(......But if you think about it that way, doesn’t that mean something like a Harajuku date, the thing I always dreamed about, would also be possible? Ahh, no, but since I can’t travel unless you’re with Kaito-kun, that basically means my boyfriend would have to be Kaito-kun...... which means...... which means...... w- well...... that’s n- not really a problem either...... a- and besides, that’s not what this is about right now anyway...... I- I mean, it’s just, you know, as a reference for the future...... just the possibility that a dream-like youth date could happen someday...... Y- Yeah! Just a possibility!!! A possibility, that’s all!!!)","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well, to begin with, Heroes are summoned through the Hero Summoning ritual that targets people who already harbor desires like \"I want to disappear from this world\" or \"I want to go to another world\". After being summoned, they go on a pilgrimage and live in the other world for about a year before weighing the options and choosing whether to return or stay, so I guess it makes sense that she doesn’t really have much lingering attachment to her original world...... That aside...... somehow, the sugar content is going up again...... This is bad. It’s not a good trend.]"]},{"number":2475,"title":"Chapter 2475: Chapter 2476: Movie Watching with Kaori 12","paragraphs":["Letting her gaze wander around Kaito’s room with a sense of curiosity, Kaori absentmindedly let her thoughts drift.","(The bed’s over there...... so it’s not the type with a separate bedroom, more like several rooms knocked together into one? Judging by where the doors are...... it feels like at least three rooms were merged. No, even then it still feels too big...... It’s not just wide from side to side, everything about it feels incredibly spacious and massive. It really gives off the image of one of those luxury apartments where an entire floor is a single unit...... Ah, did this place have some kind of spatial expansion?)","Just as Kaori had guessed, Kaito’s room had indeed been spatially expanded, making the interior far larger than could ever be inferred from the house’s floor plan. Even so, it was far too spacious for Kaito to use alone, so a lot of the space tended to go unused. That excess space was often tinkered with on a whim by frequent visitors like Kuromueina and Alice. As a result, the room had gained more and more hidden functions over time......","(......Wait, hold on. I kind of just came all the way here on momentum and flow...... but now that I think about it, I’m in a guy’s room right now, aren’t I? And not just any guy’s, but someone I’m a little interested in...... N- No, it’s fine, totally fine...... W- Well, I’m a grown woman who’s accumulated a fair bit of life experience, so it’s not like I’d get flustered over something like this...... Well, okay, if we’re talking experience points, I lose horribly to Kaito-kun, but still.)","As she suddenly regained a bit of composure, Kaori seemed to realize just how unusual her situation was. With that awareness in mind, a faint sense of agitation welled up inside her as her thoughts continued to spin.","(Still, I wonder...... what’s Kaito-kun’s intention here? We’re watching a movie, so I get why a private room would be better than something stiff like a reception room or guest parlor, and honestly, I’d prefer that too. But...... but! A young man bringing a woman whose age close to his into his own room...... I mean, you’d think there’d be, like...... at least a little intention to seize an opportunity, right? Just a little...... just a little...... But from how he looks, it's like he doesn't even have a fragment of that kind of ulterior motive. And that, in its own way, makes me feel kinda complicated......)","Being alone together in the room of a man she was interested in, Kaori was aware that her thoughts were jumping ahead a bit, but as usual, Kaito had absolutely no such intentions.","If anything, Kaito still hadn’t quite shed his down-to-earth sensibilities. Unless it was for negotiations or something similar, the idea of ushering someone who came over to play into a guest room or reception room barely even crossed his mind.","In fact, even with people who visited often like Kuromueina or Amel, he usually spent time with them in his private room. Somewhere in his head, the equation \"inviting a friend over = showing them my room\" may have already been firmly established.","[Kaori-san, is it fine if we sit on this sofa to watch?]","[Unn, that’s fine...... By the way, Kaito-kun, this has nothing to do with the movie at all, but can I ask you something? Just for reference.]","[Sure, what is it?]","[U- Umm...... Kaito-kun, you say fairly often that I’m a charming woman, right? W- Well, it’s probably flattery mixed in and all, but you do say things like that.]","[Eh? Well, I don’t really think of it as flattery......]","[So, you know, just as a reference...... could you be a bit more specific? I- I mean, in what way do you think I’m charming as a woman?]","To be honest, even Kaori herself didn’t really understand why she had asked such a question. Was it because she wanted to be praised as a woman by Kaito, who would surely respond kindly...... Or was it because she wanted the extremely natural, almost too-composed Kaito to see her a little more consciously as a woman...... Even she couldn’t say for sure.","Faced with that sudden question, Kaito blinked in surprise for a moment, then quickly opened his mouth to reply.","[Hmmm, there are honestly so many that it’d be hard to explain everything, but...... if we’re talking about appearance, for example, you give off the impression of an older woman who also has a cute side. Your facial features lean toward the cute end, but at the same time you have a calm, dependable air about you. I usually see you with your hair tied up for cooking, but I think the way you have it down like this right now has an elegance to it too, it really suits you.]","[Ahh, r- really? T- Thank you...... I mean, I think you’re exaggerating a bit, but......]","[As for your personality, personally, what I find most charming is how enjoyable you are to talk to. Kaori-san is bright and sociable, incredibly easy to talk to, and you’re also considerate and kind, so I can relax and speak openly with you.]","[Y- You’re praising me too much, um, t- that’s enough already......]","[And you’re great at cooking, with that warm, homey feel too. Kaori-san’s food isn’t just delicious, there’s this warmth to it, a comforting taste that makes you want to eat it again and again......]","[S- Stoooop!!! I get it! I get it, okay!? That’s more than enough!!! I’m sorry for asking something weird! If this keeps going it’s going to feel kind of strange, so stop!!! Sorry for changing the subject, let’s watch the movie, the movie!!!]","[Eh? Ah, yes.]","She’d only meant it as a \"it’d be nice if he praised me a little\" kind of thing, but he’d gone far beyond that...... so smoothly and thoroughly that it almost felt like he was trying to woo her. Flushing bright red, Kaori forcibly cut off the conversation while turning her face away.","As for the grin that had crept onto her lips without her noticing, she desperately covered it with her hand.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Ahh, hey, this is kind of not okay...... Doesn’t her heroine power feel absurdly high? They’re not even lovers yet, and the sugar content is already off the charts, at this rate I’m going to mutate again...... Couldn’t you show a little restraint, seriously......]","Makina : [......................]","Serious-senpai : [See? Now even this deranged thing has spawned and is waiting in the back with that predator look on her face......]"]},{"number":2476,"title":"Chapter 2476: Chapter 2477: Movie Watching with Kaori 13","paragraphs":["For the time being, they decided to pull themselves together and watch a movie. When Kaito walked over to the wall of the room and pressed his palm against it...... the sofa and table slid aside, rearranging themselves into a layout suited for watching a movie projected onto the wall, almost like a projector screen.","[......Eh? What was that just now...... Arehh? Wait, I thought this world had more of a fantasy vibe, but does it have some kind of sci-fi elements too?]","[No, in this case it’s actually much more on the pure fantasy side. When I touch the wall and imagine \"theater mode\" in my head, it changes into a layout where that wall is treated as a screen......]","[H- Hehh...... errr, can I throw a tsukkomi here? Why did you even think of installing a function like that when building the house?]","[Ah, well, how should I put it...... This room has a lot of functions that Alice installed when she built it. There seem to be plenty I don’t even really know about myself...... but this theater mode, at least, is something that was added very recently.]","[......You can add a feature that literally slides the room layout around after this place was built?]","[Well, the one who installed it is omniscient and omnipotent, so......]","[This guy really does live outside the bounds of common sense huh......]","Listening to Kaito’s explanation, Kaori had an expression of indescribable exasperation on her face. Just as Kaito had said, the theater mode function that automatically adjusted the room layout had been added recently so the tablet Canalis gifted would be easier to use.","For that matter, neither of them really understood how it worked, power source included. According to Canalis, it ran on \"God Power\", making it an unknown function by this world’s standards, which means it couldn't even be considered a magic tool...... but then again, when it came to Kaito’s house, Shallow Vernal had loosened the restrictions, so there were already quite a few things that lay outside common sense in this world: the door in the backyard that led to a multilayered dimensional special space, the gate to Kaito’s room, and so on. At this point, it was hardly surprising anymore.","[......Well, anyway, let’s watch the movie. I picked the last one, so you can choose this time, Kaito-kun. I’m interested in seeing what kind of movies you pick too.]","[Got it. Since the last one was a story-focused romance, how about something with more action this time?]","[Sounds good. I like famous action movies too.]","It was decided that Kaito would choose the next movie. As if prompted by him, Kaori sat down on the sofa. While glancing sideways at Kaito as he browsed movies on the tablet, she suddenly found herself thinking.","(......So, how much distance is appropriate here? We’re sitting together on a sofa, what’s the normal distance between Kaito-kun and me? We’re not lovers or anything, so getting too close would be weird, right? But then again, we’re sitting on the same sofa, so putting a ton of space between us also feels kind of rude. F- For now, I’ll just sit here and leave the rest up to Kaito-kun.)","Since it was her first time ever sitting side by side on a sofa with someone of the opposite sex, Kaori couldn’t quite get a sense of the right distance.","This was mainly due to her lack of romantic experience, but even if she left it up to Kaito, whether the distance would actually end up appropriate was...... honestly rather questionable.","It was true that Kaito had plenty of experience sitting next to women like this on a sofa, but the person he most often sat beside was Kuromueina, who had been extremely close in terms of personal space since the day they first met. Because of that, Kaito had come to think that level of closeness was normal.","[Ah, Kaori-san, how about this movie? It’s a pretty famous one, but I’ve never seen it myself.]","[Hoehh? Y- Yeah, that’s the one that won awards, right? I know the title, but I haven’t seen it either, so that might be perfect.]","Finding a prospective movie, Kaito moved closer to Kaori and showed her the tablet screen.","(......Eh? Um, isn’t this kind of close? He closed the distance so naturally that I couldn’t react at all. T- This is a bit too close, or rather...... isn’t this basically a lover’s distance!? N- No, maybe he’s just getting closer to show me the tablet screen right now?)","Fundamentally lacking in romantic experience, Kaori was unsure whether the current sense of distance, while not quite close enough to be called pressed together, it was at least close enough for her to clearly see the tablet screen in his hands, was actually appropriate.","[It looks like there’s both a subtitled version and a dubbed version. Which do you prefer?]","[As for me, I think I’d rather watch the dubbed version...... I mean, subtitles have their own appeal, but I like the dubbed version because I can watch it more relaxed.]","[I usually watch the dubbed version too. Then let’s go with that......]","With the movie decided, an image appeared on the wall in front of Kaito and Kaori like a monitor, and the room lights automatically dimmed to a level that made it easy to see.","(......I see...... so we’re going with this distance...... N- No, it’s not like I can’t handle it or anything...... I mean, we even held hands while watching a play before, so this kind of distance is totally fine. Are we supposed to hold hands here too......? N- No, wait, calm down, me!? This isn’t a date! ......But coming to a guy’s house and watching a movie alone together is basically a date already, isn’t it......? N- No, no, let’s not think about weird things.)","As her thoughts spun in circles, Kaori decided that, at the very least, she was glad the room had gone dark, since it meant Kaito wouldn’t be able to see how red her face probably was.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [That’s totally the reaction of someone who’s fallen in love, isn’t it!?]","Makina : [A date between my beloved child and one of my other children...... beautiful...... the preciousness is overflowing. Ah, Serious-senpai, caramel popcorn, please.]","Serious-senpai : [You’re telling me to just become one!? I’m not mutating on purpose, you know! Even if you request it......]","Makina : [It’s fine. I’ve already \"determined it so\".]","Serious-senpai : [Are you a devil or what?]"]},{"number":2477,"title":"Chapter 2477: Chapter 2478: Movie Watching with Kaori 14","paragraphs":["The action movie that had started was, as expected of an award-winning film, thoroughly engrossing. Kaori found herself able to forget her tangled thoughts for the moment and simply enjoy the movie.","Feeling a little thirsty, she kept her eyes on the screen as she reached out toward the cup on the table...... only for her hand to bump into Kaito’s hand, which had been reaching out at the exact same time.","[Ah, s- sorry!? That was yours, wasn’t it, Kaito-kun!]","[No, it’s fine. I wasn’t paying attention either. If it’s placed between us, it’s easy to mix them up.]","The one who had mistaken it this time was Kaori. The two of them were sitting on the sofa facing the screen, with Kaito on the left and Kaori on the right. From Kaori’s perspective, her own cup was placed slightly forward to her right.","But because she had been so focused on the movie, she mistook the cup that entered the edge of her vision, Kaito’s, for her own and reached out with her left hand, resulting in their hands colliding.","(H- How cliche is this!? I’ve seen this exact development in romance movies! N- No, but when it actually happens to you, it’s way more embarrassing than you’d expect. I mean, it was my mistake, but still...... it makes me weirdly self-conscious...... Meanwhile, Kaito-kun looks totally unfazed, calm, even. Guh, is this the difference in experience......?)","Though the unexpected mishap left Kaori a little flustered, Kaito didn’t seem particularly bothered. After their brief exchange, he simply turned his attention back to the movie.","From Kaito’s point of view, after all, the two of them had previously spent nearly an entire day holding hands on a date, so a brief brush of hands was nothing to get worked up over.","But for Kaori, perhaps because she was more consciously aware of Kaito than she had been during that date, when she’d mostly gone along with Olivia’s lead, she felt an inexplicable, awkward embarrassment lingering in her chest.","After the movie ended, Kaito and Kaori lightly stretched and moved their stiff bodies from sitting so long, chatting about their impressions of the film.","[The plot felt pretty by-the-book, for better or worse, but the action was incredible.]","[Unn. It was super intense and really fun. Though when you think about it...... I kind of felt like that level of movement might actually be possible with Body Strengthening Magic. Magic really is amazing.]","[For me, those kinds of moves would be a bit tough.]","[Not very good with Body Strengthening?]","[......At max, I can only do about one-and-a-half times.]","Incidentally, Kaito’s \"max 1.5 times\" was after being boosted by things like the Fruit of Nebula's World Tree; using it in his normal state, the multiplier would be even lower.","[Yeah, 1.5 times is definitely on the low side. Well, magic has its strengths and weaknesses.]","[By the way, Kaori-san, how far can you go?]","[Hmmm, I think I could manage around 30 times but...... I’ve never really had a reason to push it that far, so I haven’t actually tried. Against monsters at the level you’d find in the Human Realm, even fairly strong ones can usually be handled with about 5 times. And honestly, I was more of the type to fire off high-output magic from mid to long range.]","Kaori had once worked as an adventurer in the past, but since monsters in the Human Realm weren’t particularly powerful, there was rarely any need to crank Body Strengthening Magic up to extreme levels.","Of course, when it came to top-tier Human Realm monsters like Wyverns or Black Bears, that was a different story, but subjugating monsters of that class was mainly the knights’ job, so adventurers were seldom called upon.","[I see. Being able to use such powerful Body Strengthening Magic is enviable, but...... now that you mention it, there really aren’t many chances to use it, are there?]","[Even when you’re active as an adventurer, it’s rare to go all-out. In everyday life, you basically never use it to that extent. At the very least, there aren’t many situations where it helps with cooking.]","[Ah, speaking of cooking...... Kaori-san, if you’d like, would you stay for dinner? You treated me to lunch, so this would be my way of returning the favor......]","[Eh? Really? Are you sure? Wouldn’t that be a bother on such short notice......? I mean, if you ask whether I’m interested or not...... I definitely am. I’m really curious about what kind of food would come out. I’m interested, but......]","[If we let them know now, it shouldn’t be a problem. If I ask, they can bring it to the room, so we can just eat here...... I’ll check real quick.]","Hearing Kaito’s proposal, Kaori, who enjoyed cooking as a hobby, seemed genuinely intrigued by the idea of noble-house cuisine, responding that she’d be happy to if it wouldn’t cause any trouble.","Seeing that, Kaito used hummingbird to check, then looked slightly thoughtful as he read the reply he received.","[Ah, if it’s difficult, don’t force it, okay?]","[No, dinner itself seems to be no problem at all. It’s just something else......]","[Something else?]","[Yes, errr...... if you’re okay with it, Kaori-san, would you like to stay over tonight?]","[..................]","At Kaito’s sudden question, Kaori's expression turned blank, as though he’d abruptly started talking about outer space.","(......Stay over? I-I mean, I did say I wanted to enjoy my youth, and I admit I’m really interested in romance. But isn’t the development kinda skipping several steps at once......? Eeeeeh!?)","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Cut it out! Don’t try to turn this into some sugary development! This is that, right!? He probably just checked with someone like Illness and got asked something like \"If Kaori is staying over, should we prepare a room?\", that’s all!!! Kaito, don’t phrase it in a way that causes weird misunderstandings!!!]"]},{"number":2478,"title":"Chapter 2478: Chapter 2479: Movie Watching with Kaori 15","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I'm on a business trip tomorrow so I won't be updating tomorrow.","Kaori had been thrown into confusion by the abrupt turn of events, but thanks to her natural ability to switch gears quickly, she pulled her thoughts back together.","(C- Calm down...... I’m a woman who’s seen plenty of romance stories. I may have zero real experience, but I’ve got knowledge...... This pattern is that one! The other person has absolutely no ulterior motive, and if I panic and overreact, I’ll just jump to conclusions and embarrass myself! Just now, Kaito-kun looked thoughtful while reading hummingbird’s reply and then asked whether I wanted to stay over, so......)","Drawing on the romance stories she’d consumed so far, and judging from Kaito’s personality that he probably had no hidden intentions, Kaori tilted her head slightly and asked,","[When you say \"stay over\", you mean me staying at Kaito-kun’s place, right?]","[Yes. I just got a message from Illness-san asking whether we should prepare a guest room if Kaori-san is staying over, so......]","[Ahh, I see......]","Listening to Kaito’s explanation, it seemed that when he’d asked Illness to prepare dinner, she’d inquired whether a guest room was needed, and that was why he’d brought it up to Kaori.","(Well, if I had to nitpick, maybe think a bit more about the order you explain things in!? I mean, I know Kaito-kun has absolutely no ulterior motive...... but still, somehow that makes it feel a little unsatisfying too...... Normally, when a guy suggests an overnight stay to a girl his age, wouldn’t he at least think about the possibility of something happening? No, I know Kaito-kun isn’t that kind of person, and I know I’m being selfish here, but part of me wants him to see me as a woman just a little......)","To begin with, the plan was for her to stay in a guest room, not in Kaito’s own room. Even so, the fact that he gave off an air of having zero ulterior motives was reassuring, yet at the same time left her with a faint sense of dissatisfaction. A maiden’s heart certainly is complicated.","(......I won’t say it out loud, but there is a chance, you know. I like Kaito-kun enough that if he seriously pushed, I’d probably end up going along with it. I know full well how unreasonable I’m being, but at least let me complain a little in my own head...... Wait, no, that’s not the point. First I need to decide whether I’m staying or not......)","Realizing her thoughts were drifting in a strange direction, Kaori temporarily tucked away the part of her maiden’s heart that was overreacting to romance and brought her focus back to the matter at hand.","[If you’ve got your shop to worry about and it’s difficult, then please don’t feel pressured......]","[Ahh, no, the prep is already done, and my place only opens from lunchtime, so that’s not a problem at all.]","All the preparations for the set-meal shop were already finished, and the dishes were stored in the magic box, so staying over itself posed no issue.","(As for clothes, I can just go back and get them once with my teleportation magic tool, so that’s fine. If I stay over, I could probably watch two more movies, which is nice, and more than anything, there’s something really appealing about this...... something that makes my expectations rise.)","After thinking for a moment, Kaori’s expression turned serious as she asked Kaito,","[......Kaito-kun, there’s something I want to ask...... The bath at your place...... is it big?]","[It’s ridiculously spacious.]","[T- Then, would it be okay if I stayed over......? To be honest, I really wanted to soak in a big bath.]","[Ahh, baths are magic tools too, so they’re certainly rather expensive.]","[Exactly. As a Japanese, I can’t live without a bath, so I pushed myself and bought one...... but it’s not very big. I can’t fully stretch my legs or anything. Even if I bought a new one, there’s the issue of space in the house, and remodeling just for the sake of a bath feels a bit much...... So I’ve been wanting to get into a big bath. You know, there aren’t many hot springs in this world...... I mean, they do exist, but they’re all really far away, like in remote frontier areas, so going there is a hassle.]","[Yeah, now that you mention it, I’ve heard hot springs are pretty minor here.]","Just as Kuromueina had mentioned before when they were making bath additives, that hot springs were a minor thing, hot springs were indeed relatively uncommon. All of them were located far from the friendly city where Kaori lived, so she’d rarely had the chance to soak in a spacious bath.","[There aren’t many public bathhouses either, I guess?]","[A lot of people are fine with just a shower, and even those who want a bath can usually buy one themselves if they stretch their budget a bit, even if it’s a magic tool, like I did when I first opened my shop. So there probably isn’t much demand for public bathhouses? Plus, quite a few people see soaking in a big bath as something from noble culture.]","[Well, they do say the Japanese are obsessed with baths. I guess there’s a difference in sensibilities compared to people in this world.]","[Exactly. So, well...... that’s why. I really want to soak in a big bath, so if Kaito-kun doesn’t mind, I’d love it if you let me stay over.]","[Yes, that’s fine. Then I’ll let Illness-san know to prepare a guest room.]","[Thanks!]","And so, it was decided that Kaori would be staying one night at Kaito’s house. With the time constraint eased for the moment, once they finished sending messages, Kaito and Kaori started talking about watching one more movie and began choosing what to watch next.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Her heroine power is too high...... the sweetness level too...... hah!? T- This is...... my hands are swelling......]","Makina : [......Maybe just a little more before you pop?]","Serious-senpai : [You mean I actually have to pop to turn into popcorn!? Isn’t that gross!? Won’t I end up all gory!? We’re rated R15 here! My body going bang is not okay!!!]"]},{"number":2479,"title":"Chapter 2479: Chapter 2480: Movie Watching with Kaori 16","paragraphs":["After finishing their third movie, Kaori went back once to pick up a change of clothes and other things, then returned to Kaito’s house. Time-wise, it was already approaching dinner, making the timing just right.","[Kaori-san, about dinner, would you like to eat here or in the dining hall?]","[H- Hmmm, the dining hall is over at Lilia-san’s mansion, right? I remember you usually eat dinner over there, Kaito-kun...... b- but eating in a noble’s mansion surrounded by servants and such feels like a pretty high hurdle for me.]","[We can use the dining room in my house too, you know? Well, in that case it’d probably just be me and Kaori-san, so it wouldn’t be much different from eating in the room.]","[Yeah. If that’s the case, then as long as you don’t mind, Kaito-kun, I’d feel more at ease eating in this room.]","[Got it. Then I’ll have them bring it over here.]","Kaori was acquainted, to some extent, with the residents of both Kaito’s house and Lilia’s mansion. She could at least be considered familiar with Aoi, Hina, Lilia, Illness, Anima, Caraway, and Eta and Theta, since she had gotten to know them when she gave cooking advice at the party on the ship.","However, there were still many people she didn’t know, and given that Lilia’s mansion was a full-fledged noble residence, it was only natural that she would feel a bit hesitant.","[By the way, Aoi-chan and Hina-chan live at your place too, right, Kaito-kun?]","[Yes, but today they went to the trading city where the Adventurers’ Guild branch is, for some kind of adventurer training course, so they’re staying the night over there.]","[Training at a branch in another city...... that means Aoi-chan and Hina-chan passed the intermediate adventurer exam!]","[Yeah. It seems they gained experience as lower-rank adventurers and passed the monthly exam.]","[Ahh, that brings back memories. The training you get when you rank up takes a whole day, so it’s really long. Well, everything they teach you is important though.]","[Come to think of it, Kaori-san, you used to be an adventurer too, right?]","Aoi and Hina had been working steadily as adventurers, and since they already knew magic, they had the ability to rise to intermediate rank. However, due to their lack of experience, they spent a certain period working as lower-rank adventurers to get used to adventuring. After that, they applied for the promotion exam, passed without issue, and went to the Adventurers’ Guild branch to receive the training required to advance to intermediate rank.","[When you become intermediate rank, you start getting requests from cities other than the one you’re based in, so your range of activity expands a lot. Since there are many differences compared to being lower rank, you go to a branch in a different city from your home base to take the training. When you move up to upper rank, on top of that, you also study things like movements assuming joint missions with the knight order, and the basics of operating under their command, so you even go to the knight order’s headquarters.]","[Ah, I’d heard about that, but joint missions only start from upper-rank adventurers, huh?]","[Depending on the scale, intermediate adventurers can get involved too, but in those cases there’s always at least one upper-rank adventurer present, and you form a temporary team. In the first place, joint missions don’t happen that often. I was technically an upper-rank adventurer too, but as for joint missions with the knight order...... I only had one, when a stampede occurred. Well, in my case, I was moving around from place to place a lot, so those kinds of requests probably didn’t come my way very often anyway.]","In Kaori’s case, since she had worked as an adventurer as a means of funding her travels around the world, she hadn’t operated out of any specific base city.","For adventurers like that, joint missions, which often had the potential to drag on for many days, were relatively unlikely to be assigned, and the only such experience Kaori had in the past was an emergency request triggered by a stampede.","As an aside, thanks to her performance during that incident, Kaori came to be known by the alias \"Water Blade\". If she had continued working as an adventurer, she would have soon been recognized as a top-tier adventurer...... however, shortly after that stampede, Kaori retired from adventuring, so she was never called a top-tier adventurer.","[Come to think of it, Kaito-kun, you never became an adventurer, did you? Well, it’s not like you need to make money through adventuring, and I know you’re not great at combat, but I thought you might have at least registered just to accompany Aoi-chan and Hina-chan.]","[Ah, no, I actually can’t register as an adventurer......]","[Eh? Why not?]","[......Errr, apparently it’s because I, personally, fall outside the scope of the laws of the Three Human Nations, so it would cause various complications. I have gone along on requests as a companion before, though. Well, it’s not like I particularly want to be an adventurer anyway, so it’s not really a problem.]","[The laws don’t apply to you? You’re not secretly some kind of fixer who rules the world from the shadows, are you?]","[I’m not.]","Faced with Kaori’s wry, somewhat exasperated smile, Kaito responded with a similarly wry smile of his own.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I- It wasn’t a sugar-sweet episode. Did the flow just change!?]","Makina : [You can punch harder if you pull your fist back before striking.]","Serious-senpai : [.................]"]},{"number":2480,"title":"Chapter 2480: Chapter 2481: Movie Watching with Kaori 17","paragraphs":["After it was decided that Kaori-san would be staying the night and I asked Illness-san to prepare a room, we spent the time watching another movie and chatting. When it was time for dinner, we had the meal brought to my room.","Since my room is about the size of three regular rooms put together, eating together with the two of us was no problem at all.","[Ohhh, it’s not a course meal, but there’s a lot of dishes and it’s really luxurious...... Is this soup potage? It looks delicious.]","[They sometimes serve it like a course, but since Aoi-chan, Hina-chan, and I aren’t really used to that style, they often arrange everything like this instead. It seems the head chef puts a lot of thought into it and makes various improvements.]","[Hehh. When you say head chef, you mean the one from Lilia-san’s mansion, right? She wasn’t directly involved in cooking for the ship party, but she was interested in otherworld cuisine, so we talked quite a bit and taught each other different cooking methods.]","[Ohh, now that you mention it, I do feel like since the ship party, they’ve started serving meals that incorporate a bit of the flavor style from the world we were in.]","During the ship party, I was technically the host, and it was mainly handled by the staff from my household and the hired maids, so the cooks from Lilia-san’s mansion, including the head chef, weren’t very involved.","However, the head chef is apparently quite eager to absorb new cooking techniques. Out of personal interest, she observed the menu planning and such, and it seems she became acquainted with Kaori-san as well.","[As expected of a Duchy’s head chef, her skills are incredible...... Unn! This potage has been strained so carefully, the texture is amazing.]","[From what I’ve heard, she originally worked at the royal castle. Apparently there’s a kind of competition where court chefs compete in cooking techniques, and she once made it into the top four.]","[Hehh, so there’s a tournament like that.]","[It seems it’s only held within the royal castle though.]","Since I talk with the head chef fairly often, I’ve heard stories about her time working at the royal castle a few times. As part of daily training, there are apparently competitions like that as well.","Even if you just say \"royal castle chef\", there are many people working at the castle, and the number of cooks is quite large. Some prepare meals for the servants, while others are in charge of devising dishes for parties and the like, it seems to vary a lot.","......Well, apparently the winner of that competition was Beatrice-san, so it seems even maids, not just cooks, are eligible to participate......","[This is delicious...... Is it the preparation that’s different? No, maybe it’s this slightly sour sauce that makes the difference......]","While eating the food with obvious enjoyment, Kaori-san would occasionally put on an expression that looked like a professional’s, serious and thoughtful, as if she were analyzing the flavors. She might be thinking about trying to recreate seasoning combinations she liked.","It seems she’s been experimenting with new dishes quite a lot and putting a great deal of passion into cooking. Well, in any case, as long as she’s having fun, that’s what matters most.","After finishing dinner and taking a short break, I suddenly spoke up to Kaori-san.","[By the way, Kaori-san. Do you drink alcohol?]","[Alcohol?]","[Yeah. There’s a bar in the basement.]","[I see, a bar in the basement...... in the basement...... Unn? Why is there a bar in the basement of your house?]","[If you ask why, all I can say is that Alice built it on her own...... By the way, the shop manager is the Death King's Head Subordinate.]","[Ah, just like always, this kid's living outside the bounds of common sense...... W- Well, I am interested in bars, so I’d like to check it out. I haven’t really gone to bars before, so I’m looking forward to it.]","Thinking that Iris-san is also good at cooking and that they might have things to talk about, I made the suggestion, and although Kaori-san looked puzzled, she replied enthusiastically.","We left the room together and headed toward the bar in the basement. Going down the stairs and getting close to the bar, Kaori-san tilted her head and just like Amel-san did when I brought her here, she looked in the opposite direction from the bar.","[......Kaito-kun, if that way is the bar, then what’s this way? A food storage room or something?]","[Ah, no...... that’s a weapon shop.]","[A weapon shop? You mean...... that kind of shop that sells swords and spears?]","[That very kind of weapon shop.]","[......Why is there a weapon shop inside your house?]","[All I can say is that Alice built it on her own...... But well, lately Aoi-chan and Hina-chan have been using it, so it’s not completely pointless......]","[Ah~~ for adventurer activities, you definitely need weapons and armor. And if it’s Phantasmal King-sama’s shop, the quality should be guaranteed......]","[If you’re interested, want to take a quick look?]","[Honestly, I am a little interested. As long as it’s not a bother to Phantasmal King-sama......]","Kaori-san seemed interested when she heard it was the Phantasmal King’s shop, though she also looked slightly hesitant, but that shouldn’t be a problem. If anything, she might already be preparing to try to sell something.","Thinking that, I went with Kaori-san to the weapon shop and stepped inside, where, as usual, Alice wearing a lion mascot costume greeted us.","[Welcome...... Somehow it feels like this place gets more customers than the general goods shop......]","[That’s because your general store is in an alley and you close it on a whim, so your business days aren’t stable......]","[S- Sorry to intrude, Phantasmal King-sama! Your costume is really cute today too.]","[......Cute, you say?]","[Eh? It is cute! That brazen-looking face, and the cat costume was cute too, but I think the lion costume is cute as well......]","It had been that way since the Founding Festival, but Kaori-san was fairly positive about Alice’s mascot costume, either it matched her tastes or she genuinely thought it was cute.","Somehow, it even felt like Alice was nodding in satisfaction...... Maybe it’s because, including Kuro and others, there are many people who rate it poorly? Well, but if you look closely, it does seem like a design that could be popular with women......","[......But it’s still the person inside that’s the problem. When you include that, the evaluation ends up being \"annoying\"......]","[Isn’t that cruel!?]","[Kaito-kun, you really show no mercy to the Phantasmal King-sama. I- I guess that just means you two are really close?]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Alice, showing up here? W- What’s going to happen? Kaori isn’t the type to seriously take weird things at face value like Isis does, and Kaito is with her too, so it doesn’t really feel like a situation where things can be stirred up......]"]},{"number":2481,"title":"Chapter 2481: Chapter 2482: Movie Watching with Kaori 18","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Sorry to have kept you waiting for so long. The release date for the Light Novel's Volume 15 has been set for February 20! The preorder page and the cover are already up as well, so I’ll attach them in the afterword.","We had come to Alice’s weapon shop for the time being, but it wasn’t as if Kaori-san actually needed any weapons. It wasn’t like she needed some amazing kitchen knife either, so there wasn’t really anything to buy at a weapon shop when...... whoa, there was an obviously strange corner set up next to the counter.","Wasn’t that the series of mini plushies based on the costume Alice usually wore......? Come to think of it, the miscellaneous goods store had sold original goods like that too......","[Ahh, how cute! Phantasmal King-sama, is it okay to buy these plushies?]","[Yes, any of them are 5R each.]","[Errr, then I'll have one of each type......]","And just as Alice had planned, Kaori-san, who had been praising her costume nonstop, immediately latched onto the plushies and bought the entire lineup on display.","[......Ah, but seeing them in plush form, they do seem kind of cute.]","[Right? This chubby, stubby look is the best.]","[......So the problem really is what’s inside.]","[Hey now, Kaito-san?]","The smaller plush versions were indeed pretty cute, and Luna-san would probably like them too. While thinking that and watching Kaori-san shop, Alice suddenly spoke up as if something had just occurred to her, right as the payment was finished.","[......Even so, Kaori-san will be staying overnight...... so Kaori-san is going to fall prey to that dirty trick as well huh.]","[D- Dirty trick?]","[Oi, Alice, what the heck are you......]","Somehow, things are heading in a bad direction. The atmosphere was exactly the kind she had when she was about to mess around, so I had a bad feeling she was about to say something weird.","Sure enough, my prediction came true, and in the next instant, Alice started spouting something outrageous.","[Allow me to introduce this Kaito-san here! He is a mixed-bathing meister who burns with an incredible passion for bathing together with women!]","[Eeeeeh!?]","[Hey, what are you suddenly saying...... Kaori-san, please don’t take this seriously. She’s just messing around......]","[But at the very least, you’ve bathed together with all of your girlfriends, right?]","[..................]","[Kaito-kun?]","......It’s true. Unfortunately, as a matter of fact, I had done so. I- I mean, it’s not like I was usually the one actively pushing for it, but when she puts it that way, I can’t even muster a retort.","[On top of that, if we include the women who aren’t your girlfriends, the number of women you’ve bathed with together reaches fifteen, doesn’t it?]","[........................]","[......Kaito-kun? ......You’re an outrageous carnivore type, aren’t you!? N- No, you’re way past carnivore, that's practically a debauched paradise there!!!]","[N- No, um...... i- it is true, but...... there are misunderstandings too, you know......]","Honestly, it’s hard to argue when it’s fact...... If we’re talking numbers, it really does reach fifteen......","[And furthermore! At most, he’s even decided to bathe together with four women at the same time!]","[Eeeeeh!? You’re even pulling stuff like those shady power stone ads!?]","It’s true that those kinds of ads often show someone bathing with multiple beautiful women, but...... d- d*mn it, Alice was clearly saying this for fun, but the troublesome part was that she wasn’t lying at all.","Also, while Kaori-san was clearly surprised, she didn’t seem turned off by it. If anything, it felt like she had roughly guessed that I’d been swept along into those situations and was deliberately putting on an exaggerated reaction.","Well, even so, it wasn’t like I could just leave the misunderstanding as it was......","[K- Kaori-san...... please let me explain myself. What Alice said is technically true, but I’m not some mixed-bathing meister or anything. In the first place, there have been almost no times where I actively went out of my way specifically to bathe together with someone. Most of the time, it was more like I got dragged into it......]","[Unn, well, considering Kaito-kun's personality, I figured you weren’t the type to go \"Alright, time for mixed bathing!\" on your own. But even so, isn’t it insane that you’ve bathed together with fifteen people without actively trying?]","[......I think I’m probably cursed...... by baths.]","Indeed, it was as Kaori-san said. Despite not intentionally trying to do it, it was strange that I’d ended up bathing together with so many people.","Even if you subtract the inflated numbers caused by the Six Kings Festival’s pre-eve mixed-bathing system, there were still plenty of other situations where things somehow turned into shared baths.","[Seriously, I’ve lost count of how many times I’ve been humiliated in the bath by Kaito-san......]","[No, in your case, they're basically all self-inflicted......]","If anything, despite being an extremely shy person, there was even reason to suspect that Alice was actually number one when it came to the total number of mixed baths I had with. Shiro-san was probably second, but...... I feel like Alice was ahead by one.","[......So, Kaito-san. Are you going to bathe together with Kaori-san too?]","[Why did that become the topic!?]","[Kaori-san, please steel yourself. This is an unavoidable fate that eventually befalls every woman who becomes close to Kaito-san.]","[I- Is that so......? If it’s with swimsuits on...... I might manage somehow......]","[Kaori-san, don’t go along with this! Alice, if you don’t knock it off, I’m seriously pulling out my piko-piko hammer!]","It was obvious that both Alice and Kaori-san were just playing along and having fun, but from my side, it was awkward in a weird way. Once the topic came up, it made me uncomfortably conscious of things, and honestly, it was just troublesome all around.","But, was it just my imagination? Kaori-san somehow looked like she was having a bit of fun...... no, more like she seemed faintly happy about it.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Listen up, Kaito...... what this really is...... is Kaori wanting to be seen at least a little as a woman, and then seeing you, who wears your emotions all over your face, flustered like that, realizing that you’re looking at her in that way even a bit, and getting happy about it...... in other words, what looks like teasing is actually an absurdly high-level display of flirting...... If it weren’t me, I’d have missed it...... d*mn it!!]","Makina : [She exploded!? Not in some gross way, but in a gag-manga-style, pop, over-the-top explosion!?]"]},{"number":2482,"title":"Chapter 2482: Chapter 2483: Movie Watching with Kaori 19","paragraphs":["Since the situation was unfavorable, no, more like the flow of things was going very badly, we decided to leave Alice’s weapon shop as quickly as possible.","Kaori-san was already done with her shopping anyway, and our original destination was the bar, so there was no problem. Just as we stepped outside the weapon shop and were about to head toward the bar, Kaori-san called out to me with a mischievous-looking smile.","[......So, what are you going to do? As the mixed-bath meister, Kaito-kun, are you aiming to take a mixed bath with me too?]","[Kaori-san...... you seem unusually cheerful.]","[Ahaha, sorry, sorry. It’s just that it’s rare for me to be on the advantageous side of this kind of topic compared to Kaito-kun, so I ended up having a little fun with it. Well, if you suddenly got over your hesitation and went all in, I’d be the one in trouble, so I’m kind of walking on thin ice here.]","She was clearly joking, but Kaori-san looked like she was enjoying herself. Well, just as she said, if I suddenly blurted out \"Then let’s take a mixed bath\", it would put her at a disadvantage instead......","[......But honestly, how is it? Putting aside whether you’d actually do it or not...... errr, from your perspective, Kaito-kun, does it sound appealing at all?]","[Expanding on that topic is pretty embarrassing, but...... I mean, I’m a guy too. If I got to take a mixed bath with a beautiful woman, of course I’d feel happy about it.]","[......Even if that woman were me?]","[I think your self-evaluation is a bit on the low side, Kaori-san, but without any flattery, I do think you’re beautiful. So when this kind of topic comes up, I end up getting strangely self-conscious and embarrassed...... shouldn’t we stop here? This topic, I mean.]","[Ahaha, yeah. I’m starting to feel awkward too, so let’s leave it at that.]","Kaori-san might rate herself a bit low, but there’s no doubt she’s beautiful. Rather than \"beautiful\", her face gives off a cute impression, and with her playful demeanor, she’s undeniably charming as a woman.","She seems to admire a cool, model-like image of femininity, but in reality, she gives off much more of a playful, cute onee-san vibe.","Talking about mixed baths with someone like that, it’s only natural to become conscious of her. In fact, I even ended up picturing the scene a little in my head, which only made the embarrassment worse.","[I’d be too embarrassed to actually do something like a mixed bath anyway, so...... well, that’s something for when we’re closer.]","[Yeah. For now, let’s go to the bar.]","[Unn.]","......Arehh? The way she said that just now made it sound like she was assuming something like that would happen later on...... No, I’m probably overthinking it.","Anyway, even though we had that oddly embarrassing exchange, Kaori-san was in good spirits, and with this atmosphere, it felt like we’d be able to enjoy our drinks.","When we went inside the bar, Iris-san greeted us with a calm demeanor.","[Welcome. Take any seat you like.]","[Thank you very much.]","[S- Sorry to intrude.]","Guided by Iris-san, we sat side by side at the counter. Perhaps because I had told her beforehand that Iris-san was the Death King's Head Subordinate, Kaori-san looked a little tense.","[Do you have any preferences?]","[Errr, since we’ve already eaten, I’d like something with a refreshing taste. What about you, Kaori-san?]","[For me, errr...... ahh, since I have to open the shop again tomorrow, I’d rather avoid anything too strong......]","[Oh, about that, you can probably nullify it with Olivia-san’s Blessing.]","[Eh? You can?]","All of the True Blessings from the Supreme Gods come with an effect that completely nullifies status ailments, similar to the Blessing from Shiro-san that I have.","In fact, Lilia-san, who has received Chronois-san’s True Blessing, was able to adjust how drunk she got from alcohol, so I figured Olivia-san’s Blessing should work the same way.","[They said the basic effects of the Supreme Gods’ True Blessings are the same, so it should be fine...... If you think beforehand something like \"I don’t want to get more than lightly tipsy\" before you start drinking, you won’t go past that point. And if you want to sober up, the alcohol will leave your system immediately and the intoxication will fade.]","[I- Is that so? True Blessings sure are amazing.]","[It may be easier to imagine it in terms of oxygen. For humans, oxygen is not poisonous as long as it is taken in within the normal range of breathing. However, if taken in excessively, it can become a poison that damages the body. Alcohol is recognized in the same way. You can determine in advance from which point it is considered harmful and should be nullified. This is not limited to Blessings, High-ranking Demons can achieve the same effect through magic.]","[I- I see......]","With Iris-san adding to my explanation, Kaori-san nodded in admiration.","[Then I shall prepare something with a refreshing mouthfeel.]","[Please do.]","[P- Please take care of us.]","[Kaori-san, Iris-san is a kind person, so you don’t need to be so nervous. Also, cooking is her hobby, so you might actually get along pretty well?]","Kaori-san still seemed a little tense, but although Iris-san’s manner of speaking had an air of haughtiness, she was actually kind and attentive, so I thought Kaori-san would quickly feel at ease.","If anything, since they both liked cooking, I even felt that they might end up hitting it off and becoming good friends.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [S- So you made it so that after exploding, I respawn on the spot......?]","Makina : [Munch munch...... No, it’s not like I did anything...... I think it’s just the gag correction reviving you on its own.]","Serious-senpai : [There’s no way a once-in-a-generation serious character would have something like gag correction...... More importantly, Kaori...... she’s a pretty terrifying one. To naturally pull off something as high-difficulty as making Kaito become romantically conscious of her...... Could it be that among the Otherworlders, Kaori will be the first to advance all the way to becoming his girlfriend......?]"]},{"number":2483,"title":"Chapter 2483: Chapter 2484: Movie Watching with Kaori 20","paragraphs":["After enjoying a light drink at Iris’ bar, Kaori was shown to the guest room she would be staying in, and then headed to the bathroom to take a bath.","To avoid any accidents like unexpectedly running into each other in the bath, they had discussed things beforehand: Kaori would contact Kaito after she finished bathing, and only then would Kaito go in.","[......It’s huge.]","Having undressed and moved into the bathing area, Kaori muttered involuntarily. She had been told in advance that the bath was large, but seeing it in person, it was bigger than not only a private home’s bath, but even an average public bathhouse’s, giving off an overwhelming presence.","(......Whoa, I knew it was big, but this is amazing...... And it’s ridiculously clean too. Even the magic tools like the shower, these aren’t the kind you’d find in a normal household. It's that type where you can finely adjust the water pressure and everything.)","After looking around with admiration, she first moved in front of the shower to wash her body and hair.","[Errr...... touch the magic crystal next to the magic tool......]","She was told that there’s a storage-type magic tool right beside the shower’s magic tool in the bathroom, and she's free to use whatever shampoo, treatment, and other items are inside as she likes.","When Kaori touched the magic crystal, part of the wall slid aside, revealing shelves lined with shampoo and treatment bottles.","(So many kinds!? Errr, Kaito-kun said the one he uses is in an orange container...... Ah, is it this one?)","Since everyone living in Kaito’s house used this bathroom, there were many different kinds of shampoos and such. Among them, Kaori picked up the shampoo and treatment that Kaito had said she could borrow.","(......Come to think of it, I didn’t ask, but could this be some amazing high-end shampoo? Maybe I should’ve checked beforehand...... Well, it’s too late now, so I’ll just use it.)","In fact, it might have been better not to ask about the ingredients. After all, the shampoo and treatment Kaito used were made by Alice, who had suggested making some for Kaito while she was creating pet shampoo. While the ingredients differed from the pet version...... they shared one common element: fruit from Nebula’s World Tree.","(Mmm, it smells so good...... The foam is so fine and smooth too. This is really nice shampoo. If it were sold commercially, I’d totally buy it...... though it’s probably expensive.)","Ignorance truly is bliss. Unaware of the raw materials, Kaori washed her hair and body without a second thought and then moved to the bath.","Soaking up to her shoulders and stretching out both legs, Kaori smiled in contentment.","[Mmm~~ a big bath really is the best~~ the sense of openness is totally different.]","Murmuring to herself, she narrowed her eyes comfortably...... and after a short while, a somewhat amused smile appeared on her face.","(......No, this is bad. I can’t stop grinning...... I keep thinking about that conversation with Kaito-kun from earlier.)","What came to Kaori’s mind was the conversation she’d had with Kaito shortly before going to the bar. When the topic of mixed bathing came up, she’d known it wasn’t good to tease him too much, yet she couldn’t help herself and ended up dragging the conversation out because she was happy.","She did reflect on that afterward, but even more than regret, a sense of joy welled up inside her.","That was because, to Kaori, Kaito was someone who far surpassed her in romantic experience, and she viewed him as someone well-versed in dealing with women.","He often naturally told her that she was beautiful or charming, which made her very happy...... but at the same time, somewhere deep down, she had also wondered whether he truly saw her as a woman at all.","One reason was that Kaito’s lovers and acquaintances were all beautiful women, but more than that, it was because up until now Kaito had never once shown any behavior toward Kaori that hinted at ulterior motives.","Even when he invited her to the house this time, and when he suggested that she stay overnight, Kaori hadn’t sensed any hidden intentions from him. She understood that he was interacting with her purely as a friend, without any improper thoughts, and from Kaori’s perspective, that was reassuring.","However, at the same time, it was also true that feeling like she wasn’t being seen as a woman at all was, in its own way, not very satisfying.","That was why she remembered it. When the topic of mixed bathing came up, Kaito’s reaction, easy to read because he tended to show his emotions on his face and had been flustered at the time.......","(......At the very least, he does see me properly as a woman...... as that kind of person, too. He was clearly conscious of it and looked embarrassed......)","Of course, she didn’t think it was in a romantic sense, but she could at least understand that she fell within the range of people he could feel desire toward.","For Kaori, who harbored affectionate feelings toward Kaito yet also felt that someone with her level of looks might not be taken seriously, that reaction made her happy and inexplicably raised her spirits.","(Ehehe, this is bad...... I’m acting just like a maiden in love. Ahaha, but well...... I guess it’s hard to completely deny it either.)","Perhaps because no one else was around, Kaori bathed the entire time with a slightly softened, relaxed smile on her face, looking cheerful throughout.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Not \"like\", you’re completely a maiden in love there! And wait, my body’s swelling up again!? How many times is this going to happen!?]","Makina : [Next time, let’s mix some chocolate with you before eating.]"]},{"number":2484,"title":"Chapter 2484: Chapter 2485: Movie Watching with Kaori 21","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I got home late due to overtime work, so today's chapter is short.","After enjoying the spacious bath, Kaori left the bathroom, dried her hair, then went to Kaito’s room once to let him know she had finished bathing before moving to the guest room.","The room was so large it felt like a suite, furnished with multiple magic tools and arranged in a way that made it seem very comfortable to stay in.","(Ah, even looking at it again, it’s an amazing room...... It’s twice the size of my bedroom...... no, three times at least. With a place this big, cleaning must be a lot of work...... though, come to think of it, Illness-san is said to be a Count-rank Demon. If they used some kind of limited State Preservation Magic that keeps the room in a fixed state from the end of cleaning until the next time the door is opened, then maybe it wouldn’t need cleaning when it’s not in use?)","Kaito’s house had originally been built modeled after Lilia’s mansion, so many aspects of the room layouts were similar. In other words, this was the kind of room prepared for guests staying with a Duchy, and for Kaori, who could be considered an ordinary citizen, it was an opulence that felt almost overwhelming.","(The bed is huge, and the room itself is just plain spacious...... T- This is a bit too much in its own way. It’s so big it’s hard to relax...... I’m the type who can’t fall asleep right after a bath, so I was planning to wait a bit before going to bed, but...... what should I do? F- For now, maybe I’ll go back to Kaito-kun’s room after he finishes bathing? I’ll send a hummingbird so he can reply once he’s out of the bath......)","She planned to stay up for a while longer, but since she felt restless, she thought it would be nice to chat with Kaito, so she sent a hummingbird asking him to contact her once he finished bathing.","If Kaito replied after getting out of the bath, she could just go visit his room and chat, that was what she was thinking as she sat down on one of the chairs in the room and let out a small sigh of relief.","(......How long do boys usually take in the bath? I’ve heard it’s shorter than women’s, so maybe around 45 minutes? Well, I’ll just relax a bit. Today was fun, but there were also a lot of surprising things, like Olivia-sama’s story, and we watched three movies too...... I feel like I’m fairly tired. Once I actually get ready for bed and lie down, I’ll probably fall asleep right away.)","She felt a moderate sense of fatigue, but at the same time a certain pleasant comfort, probably because the day had been full and enjoyable.","When she woke up that morning, she had never imagined she would spend her day off like this, but unexpectedly, spending the day with Kaito had been a lot of fun.","(Well, by the time Kaito-kun finishes bathing, it’ll probably be pretty late, so we won’t be able to talk for long, but in Kaito-kun’s room...... in his room...... fumu......)","At that point, Kaori’s thoughts abruptly came to a halt. After pausing for a moment, they began to turn again, this time in a different direction.","(......Arehh? Staying over at the house of a guy I’m fairly conscious of, visiting his room late at night right after he gets out of the bath, and I’ve even had a bit of alcohol? Doesn’t this completely look like the kind of flow that leads to “morning-after coffee”? N- No, Kaito-kun wouldn’t let things go in that direction, but still...... am I doing something outrageous here?)","Considering the current time, if she went to visit after Kaito finished bathing, it would likely be past 10 PM. Of course, Kaito would actually finish earlier than Kaori expected, making it a bit sooner...... but that was within the margin of error.","Feeling a slight unease about having acted on impulse, yet with the hummingbird already sent and no way to take it back, Kaori quietly waited for Kaito to finish his bath.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Wha, i- impossible! From canceling the mixed bath straight into a sharing-the-bed flag......!? T- There’s no way such lawless behavior should be allowed...... n- no, more importantly, how would it even lead to sharing a bed? Given Kaito and Kaori’s personalities, that kind of development shouldn’t happen...... A- Am I overthinking it? N- No, but still......]"]},{"number":2485,"title":"Chapter 2485: Chapter 2486: Movie Watching with Kaori 22","paragraphs":["After finishing my bath, I wiped myself down and headed to the changing room, where I noticed the hummingbird magic tool I had left there blinking. The hummingbird magic tool has something like what you’d call \"sleep mode\" on a smartphone...... a standby mode.","When you leave it in this state while sleeping and the like, any incoming hummingbirds are stored inside the magic tool, and the magic tool itself blinks faintly so it isn’t too bright.","If you touch the magic tool in this state, the received hummingbirds will appear, so you can just touch it to check them.","When I checked, it turned out to be a message from Kaori-san. She wanted to visit my room, so she asked me to contact her after I got out of the bath.","I dried my hair and changed clothes, taking them out of the magic box. Originally, I was planning to go straight to bed, so I had intended to put on sleepwear, but since Kaori-san was coming, casual everyday clothes would be fine.","After changing, I used the hummingbird to tell her that I was heading back to my room now, then returned to my room. About 5 minutes later, Kaori-san came by, so I opened the door to welcome her.","[Welcome, Kaori-san.]","[Sorry for coming so suddenly...... well, you see, I can’t really fall asleep right away after getting out of the bath, and if Kaito-kun doesn’t mind, I was hoping you could keep me company for a bit of casual chatting...... and also, my room is so big that it’s kind of hard to relax when I’m alone.]","[Ah, I see. That’s fine.]","I understood how Kaori-san felt. I’ve gotten used to it by now, but when I first came to this world, the room I was assigned was so spacious that it made me feel strangely unsettled too.","It might be a little different from not being able to sleep because your pillow is different, but when the atmosphere of a room, or the mood itself, so to speak, is different, it’s natural for anyone to feel at least a little uneasy until they get used to it.","[Ah, Kaori-san, would you like something to drink? Since it’s night, coffee might not be a great idea, so how about some cocoa?]","[If you have some, I’d love to, but is that okay?]","[Of course. Please wait a moment. I’ll get it ready right away.]","Since I had some cocoa that Aria-san gave me for my birthday, I decided to use that and took the can out of the magic box.","[Unn? Isn’t that a tea can?]","[It looks like a tea can, but the contents are cocoa. It was a gift. And then there’s this milk......]","[Is that milk something amazing?]","[Well, amazing in a sense...... you know Canalis-san, right?]","[Unn. The Omnipotent and Omniscient God who’s staying with Kaito-kun, right?]","I prefer making cocoa with milk rather than hot water, so I took out the milk Canalis-san gave me, put it into the heating magic tool, and answered Kaori-san’s question at the same time.","[Yes, that Canalis-san has been doing all sorts of selective breeding experiments with dairy cows lately......]","[Selective breeding...... of dairy cows......]","[Why are you repeating that with a face like you just heard some incomprehensible words?]","[Well, if you tell me that an Omnipotent and Omniscient God is raising dairy cows, I’m bound to react like this......]","[She was raising chickens too, you know. W- Well, anyway, after a lot of trial and error, she ended up making a kind of milk that seems to pair well with cocoa, so she gave it to me as a present. I was thinking of using that......]","[Hehh, I see. So this is milk that a God produced through trial and error...... I wonder if the fence called \"common sense\" even exists around Kaito-kun...... well, at least I get that it’s amazing milk.]","[She personally said it was more like something that just happened by accident though.]","Rather than using her God Power to do everything instantly, Canalis-san is the type who enjoys experimenting and tinkering with things, so the milk I was using this time also felt like something that came about by chance.","If I remember right, at first she was trying to create milk suitable for sweets sold at Nifty, so milk tailored specifically for cocoa was a different concept altogether...... especially since Nifty is a tea brand...... well, personally, I’m just happy to have good milk for drinking cocoa, so I have zero complaints.","[Here you go.]","[Thanks! Mmm, it smells great! Cocoa at night really is nice. It’s kind of soothing, and it feels like it’d help you fall asleep more easily.]","[How is your sleep usually, Kaori-san? I fell asleep pretty quickly myself......]","[I think I’m pretty good at falling asleep too. When I decide to sleep, I can doze off right away. Today was really fun, but it was also pretty tiring, so I might fall asleep the moment I get into bed.]","I handed Kaori-san the cocoa in a mug, and just like when we were watching a movie, the two of us sat side by side on the sofa and chatted.","Maybe because she had just taken a bath, but a soft, pleasant scent drifted from Kaori-san, different from the smell of cocoa.","Just like that, we continued drinking cocoa and making idle small talk. The atmosphere was relaxed and unhurried, and as we slowly exchanged words, I felt a comfortable sense of ease.","From time to time, the conversation would trail off into silence, but it wasn’t awkward. It felt more like a pause born of mutual relaxation, and I had the sense that we were spending a genuinely pleasant time together.","[......By the way, Kaori-san, do you have any preferences for breakfast tomorrow morning?]","[.......................]","[......Kaori-san?]","Since Kaori-san was planning to eat breakfast here, I asked in case she had a preference for bread or rice, but unlike usual, she didn’t respond right away. Tilting my head in confusion, I turned toward her, and at that exact moment, Kaori-san gently leaned over against me.","[......Huh?]","[......Zzz...... zzz......]","......Eh? Arehh? Hold on a second...... could it be that Kaori-san...... fell asleep?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [This is bad, bad, bad...... This is not a good development, this is really not good......]","Makina : [Go! My beloved child!! That’s it, princess carry!!]","Serious-senpai : [Don’t go saying unnecessary cr*p, d*mn it!]","Makina : [My beloved child giving my child a princess carry, this is a MAX-tier blessed scene just for me!! Go~~! Do your best, my beloved child!!]"]},{"number":2486,"title":"Chapter 2486: Chapter 2487: Movie Watching with Kaori 23","paragraphs":["It wasn’t so much a \"weight\" as it was the sensation of someone gently leaning against me, accompanied by the faint, steady sound of regular breathing. To be honest, it took me a moment to fully grasp the situation.","No, once my thoughts started moving, I understood immediately what was going on. It was just that the unexpected turn of events made my mind go blank for an instant, and that description fits better.","Putting it into words was simple enough. Kaori-san was leaning against me and sleeping, that was all there was to it. The reason was also easy to guess.","She had said earlier that she might fall asleep as soon as she got into bed, so she was probably already tired. Then we drank cocoa and chatted for a bit, and once she relaxed and let her guard down, the drowsiness must have hit her all at once and she drifted off.","In a way, it meant she trusted me enough to feel safe sleeping beside me, and if I were to say how I felt about that, it did make me happy...... but still, what should I do now?","Waking her when she was sleeping so comfortably felt cruel, but leaving things as they were was also a problem. If she stayed in this position and kept sleeping, she might end up straining her neck.","What to do......? There was a chance she’d wake up soon, so should I just wait like this? Or should I lay Kaori-san down properly?","She was only leaning on me lightly, so I could probably support her with my hands and separate our bodies, and I thought I could lay her down without waking her.","But if she ended up sleeping for a while, it would probably be better to carry her to the bed rather than letting her sleep on the sofa.","Carrying her all the way to the guest room would be tough, but I could at least manage putting her on my own bed. Unn. Let’s put her on the bed for now. I can sleep on the sofa, or even use another room’s bed if needed.","Having made up my mind, I first gently laid Kaori-san down on the sofa, then cleared the comforter off the bed to make space to lie her down. After that, I lifted the softly sleeping Kaori-san in a princess carry.","......Part of it was thanks to using Body Strengthening Magic, but I was able to lift her smoothly, feeling surprisingly light in my arms. Still...... mm, she smells really nice, and the softness I can feel through my hands is making my heart race.","Maybe it was because she was in sleepwear, but the fabric was thinner than I’d expected, and I could feel her body heat coming through...... perhaps it was a bit hasty to carry her in a princess carry.","Doing this to a woman in her nightwear when we’re not even lovers might have been reckless, but I’d already picked her up, so it was too late to turn back now.","For the time being, I tried to empty my mind as much as possible and carried her over to the bed without letting myself dwell on it.","There’s one more important point here: where on the bed to lay her down. Obviously, it’s best to place her near the center so she won’t roll off while turning in her sleep...... but because the bed is unnecessarily large, it’s impossible to reach the middle while standing at the edge, so I climb onto the bed on my knees and carefully, as gently as I can, lay Kaori-san down near the center.","Her peaceful sleeping face is adorable, and now that she’s lying on her back, the slight rise and fall of her chest almost draws my gaze toward it...... but I grit my teeth and hold myself back, then reach out mechanically for the comforter.","As gently as possible, I pull the blanket over Kaori-san.","[......Mmm.]","[ ! ? ]","Did I wake her up? ......No, it was probably just her turning in her sleep...... alright, cover her properly with the blanket......","I panicked, thinking she might have woken up when Kaori-san turned over, but since there didn’t seem to be any real problem, I went ahead and properly covered her with the blanket...... and then, right after that, the incident happened.","[......Huh?]","To explain the situation, in order to tuck the blanket around her properly on such a large bed, I had to take a position where I was straddling over Kaori-san’s body.","And at that moment, even if only briefly, my body ended up very close to hers. Then Kaori-san, who had turned onto her side while sleeping, suddenly hugged my waist, which happened to be right next to her.","Yes, she wrapped both arms around me tightly, just like hugging a body pillow......","And as a result, what kind of scene did this create......? It was me, straddling over the sleeping Kaori-san, completely unable to move.","W- What do I do now!? This is really bad...... She’s got my waist locked down tight, so I can’t move carelessly. That said, staying in this position isn’t good either.","It’s bad for my peace of mind, sure, but more than that, it’s simply exhausting to remain frozen in this posture.","Breaking free...... i- is that even possible? Changing my body’s orientation...... maybe if I do it very carefully? Using the held waist as a pivot and somehow turning my body...... no, but if I change direction like that...... won’t I end up lying down right beside Kaori-san? N- No, but since it’s hard to keep supporting my body with my arms like this, I don’t really have any other choice......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Fwah!? Sleeping together in that position...... y- you’re being loved...... by the God of Romcom...... d- d*mn it, my body’s swelling again...... guaaah!?]","Makina : [......Making sure my child doesn’t wake up, but also making sure their bodies don’t separate...... no, at the moment my beloved child shifts into a lying-down position, adjusting causality so that the place being hugged changes from the waist to the chest......]","Serious-senpai : [You b*staaard! What the hell are you doing!!! Just because it’s a romcom event between your children, you’re manipulating fate from the outside with illegal interference......]","Makina : [Calling it fate manipulation, y- you're exaggerating it a bit too much. It’s just lightly giving a push to one of the perfectly plausible futures that could normally happen...... I’ve already confirmed that they both have a certain level of affection for each other...... so...... errr...... I just want to see the precious sight of my children sleeping side by side in harmony!]","Serious-senpai : [Can you not double down on itttt!?]"]},{"number":2487,"title":"Chapter 2487: Chapter 2488: Movie Watching with Kaori 24","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I’ll be taking tomorrow off from updating due to personal matters, so the next update will be the day after tomorrow.","If you ask whether the situation is good or bad, it’s obviously not good. Still, I feel like I’ve overcome plenty of hardships up to now...... or at least it feels that way. It’s been quite a while since I last found myself in this kind of flustered situation, but it shouldn’t be something I can’t handle.","Come to think of it, I’ve somehow built up quite a bit of experience in romance too, and I’ve gotten better at responding calmly to all sorts of situations. Even this situation, if I compare it with my past experiences, I should be able to deal with it calmly...... there’s no way I can!","If the other person were my girlfriend, I’d probably have a bit more mental leeway. Heck, it was more like...... no, of course, considering she’s asleep, it wouldn’t be good...... but still, I might feel that even if my thoughts drifted in a strange direction to some extent, it could be forgiven.","But the one clinging to my waist right now is Kaori-san, and though she isn't my girlfriend, she's still a cute, cheerful, and charming woman. I absolutely must not make any weird moves on her, as depending on what happens, there’s even the possibility that I’d be burdened with an enormous sense of guilt in our future relationship.","For now, I carefully moved my body and managed to get into a position where I could avoid the disastrous outcome of falling on top of Kaori-san.","Still, I can’t deny that we’re practically sleeping side by side. At this point, I have to make a new decision...... I need to decide what to do next.","Right now, Kaori-san and I are lying on the bed facing each other on our sides, with Kaori-san firmly holding onto my waist. Aside from the fact that her face is around the level of my navel, it’s basically spooning.","There aren’t many options I can choose from in this situation. One is to wait...... she’s gripping my waist tightly right now, but I doubt a sleeping Kaori-san will keep that up forever. If I wait a while, her hold might loosen, so I could wait for that moment and then slip away.","Next, there’s the option of just waking Kaori-san up. This would resolve the situation all at once, but...... waking her up when she’s suddenly hugging the waist of a man feels awkward, and I’m worried about whether I could even explain things properly. Plus, part of me thinks that as long as I can just get free, things will somehow work out.","Lastly, there’s the option of forcefully twisting my body a bit to break free from her hold. There’s a risk of waking her up, but if it goes well, I could escape quickly without waking Kaori-san, a sort of best-of-both-worlds solution.","However, this method might be the most dangerous of the three.","If I reconsider the current situation, Kaori-san is clinging to my waist, with her face around my navel. Given that positioning, areas like her chest are in an extremely dangerous zone, and with how tightly she’s holding on, being aware of that area is exceptionally risky.","Right now, I’m barely managing to hold on by desperately trying to empty my mind, but moving carelessly here would be far too dangerous.","......In that case, is waiting really the best option after all......? There’s also the possibility that Kaori-san might turn over in her sleep and free me on her own, so for now, I’ll observe the situation a little longer......","[......Mmm~~]","As I was thinking that, Kaori-san immediately started to move. The strength of the arm wrapped around my waist loosened a little, and at the same time, she made a wriggling motion with her body.","She was probably unconsciously searching for a more comfortable spot to hold onto, or something like that. But this was a once-in-a-lifetime chance. If I quickly pulled away at the moment Kaori-san loosened her grip even more, I could escape......","[......Mm.]","However, as if mocking my thoughts, the situation took an unexpected turn. Kaori-san, who had been moving her hand as if feeling around my back, slid it from my waist up to my back...... or rather, around my shoulder area. Then she twisted her body and shifted upward slightly...... and after hugging me even tighter than before, she stopped with her face buried against my chest.","What’s more, she even wrapped her legs around me...... clinging on like a koala gripping a tree.","......The level of contact just skyrocketed, didn’t it!? We’re practically pressed together head to toe now, and on top of that, she’s holding me even more tightly than before, to the point where I can barely move at all!?","No, no, this is bad. This is definitely bad! The closeness is outrageous, and combined with the fact that Kaori-san is wearing sleepwear, the softness and warmth I can feel are seriously not okay.","A- As expected, this is no time to hesitate anymore.","[......K- Kaori-san. Please wake up, Kaori-san?]","[......Zzz...... zzz......]","I tried calling out to wake her up...... but there was no sign of her waking at all. Come to think of it, I remember her saying she falls asleep easily...... Should I raise my voice more? N- No, maybe there’s no need to panic like that...... She’s already moved this much in such a short time, so she should move again soon. In that case, it’s probably better not to force her awake right now.","The worst thing in a situation like this is panicking and acting rashly. On the contrary, precisely because it’s a situation like this, I should calm my mind and relax.","In other words, as long as I don’t harbor any impure thoughts and keep my mind empty, I should be fine...... How should I say this...... it’s been a while since I last had to fight against my own self-control, but if I can just get through those situations back then, I’ll probably do just fine here.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Oi, you did something, didn’t you!? You definitely did something, didn’t you!?]","Makina : [I- I didn’t.]","Serious-senpai : [You absolutely did. That last part was just unnatural! You messed with Kaito’s thoughts, didn’t you!?]","Makina : [W- Wait, calm down and think about it. If I really manipulated my beloved child’s thoughts, Shallow Vernal and the others wouldn’t stay silent, and I myself wouldn’t want to do something like that either. That’s impossible.]","Serious-senpai : [Ggh, w- well, that’s true...... If you went as far as mind control, even Canalis and Nebula would probably step in......]","Makina : [......Unn. I didn’t manipulate my beloved child’s thoughts. I just made it so that when my children are being hugged, their heart calms down and they feel relaxed, that’s all. So it’s not manipulation. Even if they relaxed and their thinking leaned slightly toward optimism, that’s not because I controlled them, but because my beloved child did so on his own...... haa haa...... my beloved child sleeping together with my other child...... it’s so precious......]","Serious-senpai : [T- This god is hopeless. When it’s a lovey-dovey event between her own children, she uses every dirty trick in the book to give illegal support. W- We have to do something about this fast......]"]},{"number":2488,"title":"Chapter 2488: Chapter 2489: Movie Watching with Kaori 25","paragraphs":["Experience has a major impact on one’s state of mind in times of crisis. When you encounter something you’ve already experienced before, compared to something you’re facing for the first time, it goes without saying that you’ll have far more emotional leeway in the former case.","That said, humans are also creatures who fail because they grow accustomed to things. There’s even a term called “human error], and it’s quite common for people to let their guard down precisely because they’ve dealt with the same situation countless times before, only to end up making a mistake as a result.","I’ve gone through all sorts of unexpected incidents in my own way, and I’ve had romantic experiences too. In terms of sheer age, I’m still far from seasoned, but I do take some pride in thinking that I’ve accumulated a fair amount of experience.","Yet now, I was keenly realizing that perhaps, without even noticing it myself, I’d grown too used to situations like this and let my guard down mentally.","At present, Kaori-san has completely turned me into her body pillow, pressing up against me closely enough that I can fully feel the warmth and softness of her body.","What’s more, while I think we get along reasonably well, she’s a woman of marriageable age of whom we're not lovers or anything like that, so under normal circumstances, it wouldn’t be strange for me to be far more flustered.","No, in fact, at the beginning I was pretty panicked, wracking my brain over how I should deal with this from here on out.","But after some time passed, I realized something. For some reason, I was relaxing in this situation...... or rather, I was feeling a sense of comfort and peace.","There’s a part of me that thinks I should urgently search for a way to escape, and another part that thinks that since things have already turned out this way, it can’t be helped and I might as well stay like this for a while. Caught between these two impulses, I’ve been hesitating over which way to steer myself as time continues to pass.","Kuh, Dr. Vier also talked about how hugging causes some kind of substance to be released that creates a feeling of happiness, and maybe human body heat really does bring a sense of calm to the heart.","In reality, it’s soft, it’s warm, it smells nice...... and if I let my guard down even a little, I feel like I might reflexively hug her back. That kind of comfort might be exactly what’s causing this strange sense of relaxation in my mind.","Also, the fact that the other party is Kaori-san might be helping to suppress my emotional agitation. I wouldn’t say we’ve known each other for a particularly long time yet, but we talk often, and I think I have a decent grasp of what kind of person she is.","At the very least, I trust her enough to be confident that even if Kaori-san were to suddenly wake up right now, the situation wouldn’t spiral into something awkward or complicated.","Of course, it’s easy to imagine that Kaori-san would be mortified with embarrassment if she woke up like this, but she’s the type who switches gears quickly and doesn’t dwell on the past. I think she’d recover after a while, and there shouldn’t be any need to worry about things becoming strangely stiff between us afterward.","If this situation were something that caused Kaori-san to feel instinctive disgust, that would be a different story...... but I think we get along well enough that it probably won’t come to that. After all, even if it was under Olivia-san’s prompting, we’ve already hugged once before......","Unn, Kaori-san really does have a great personality, she’s someone I can trust, so I’m not worried about that at all. What I’m more worried about is that if I end up directing my awareness to my lower half, which I’m desperately trying not to think about right now, I might have a reaction that only makes the situation worse.","I mean, come on, if someone as cute as Kaori-san is pressed up against me this closely, there are parts of me that are bound to react, as a man.","So for now, I’m doing my best not to think about it, trying to empty my mind as much as possible...... but when I do that, my ability to think also dulls a bit...... and combined with how comfortable this feels, I think I’m starting to get sleepy.","I just took a bath, I drank some cocoa, I’ve calmed down from the initial shock and ended up relaxing in a weird way...... and now that I’m aware of it, the drowsiness is hitting me all at once...... this is bad, I feel like I might actually fall asleep.","But well, realistically speaking, the only way to escape this situation would be to wake Kaori-san up. Even if I used a teleportation magic tool, since we’re pressed together, Kaori-san would just get teleported along with me, so there’s no point.","There’s also the option of asking someone for help, but I’m being held tightly enough that moving my hands to send a hummingbird would be difficult, and if some third party were to see us like this, even if I could handle it, Kaori-san’s embarrassment would probably reach catastrophic levels. Thinking about that, I’m not even sure that method would be the right choice.","W- Well, I’ll wait just a little longer...... and then...... errr...... yeah, once the restraint on my hands loosens...... I’ll somehow manage something clever...... ah, cr*p, I’m so sleepy......","<Afterword>","Makina : [And now, right here! If I lock in a future where my child wakes up before my beloved child...... alright, perfect!]","Serious-senpai : [Don’t mess arou......! T- This bastard, when it comes to herself, she only ever goes full rampage mode, but when it’s supporting other people’s romance, like during Alice’s festival and now again, she always steers things into a perfectly crafted romcom development! D- D*mn it...... m- my body is swelling up again......]","Makina : [Now then, I’ll watch the rest while eating my victory popcorn.]"]},{"number":2489,"title":"Chapter 2489: Chapter 2490: Movie Watching with Kaori 26","paragraphs":["In the haze of drowsiness, Kaori’s consciousness slowly floated to the surface. The first thing she felt was a pleasant warmth, and as her fuzzy mind gradually woke, she slowly opened her eyes.","(It’s kind of warm and feels nice...... Does that mean I slept well? Arehh? But it’s still dark...... I can’t quite open my eyes yet———-)","The room was still dark, but since she had been asleep until just now, Kaori’s eyes had adjusted somewhat to the darkness. Whether it was starlight or moonlight she couldn’t tell, but with the faint light filtering in, she was able to see a little.","And what jumped into Kaori’s view when she opened her eyes was, first, what looked like the chest of a man wearing loose clothing...... and when she raised her gaze, there was Kaito’s sleeping face.","(................................................?????)","When one speaks of one’s thoughts to freeze, this must be it. Faced with such an utterly unexpected situation, Kaori’s brain temporarily shut down all thinking.","If this had been a computer screen, an hourglass icon would probably be spinning in circles. It wasn’t just that her thoughts couldn’t keep up or that she couldn’t understand the situation, her thinking had completely stopped, leaving her unable to think about anything at all.","Just like that. Kaori remained in that total mental shutdown for several dozen seconds, but before long, her frozen mind rebooted and started moving again.","(......Huh? Eh? W- What is this!? W- W- What’s going on...... J- Just what kind of situation am I in right now!?)","The reason she desperately held back from screaming out loud might have been because, somewhere in her unconscious mind, there was still consideration for the sleeping Kaito.","That didn’t ease her confusion in the slightest though. Without making a sound, Kaori panicked visibly, darting her eyes around at an incredible speed as she checked her own condition.","There were parts she couldn’t see clearly because of the darkness, but from what she could see and the sensations in her body, she was able to grasp the general situation. Right now, Kaori was sleeping while clinging to Kaito’s chest, and one of Kaito’s arms was wrapped around her back...... In short, they were sleeping while embracing each other.","(Eh? T- This can’t be...... Did I speed-run our relationship not just with a triple jump, but at rocket-launch speed and end up on the “morning coffee after waking up] course!? N- No, wait, calm down, me...... It’s true I drank alcohol, but it was only enough to get lightly tipsy. Sure, my thinking ability might’ve dropped a little, but I wasn’t drunk enough to make a one-night mistake or lose my memory. I remember properly...... So if I recall what happened before we went to sleep......)","For a moment, her shaken state caused her thoughts to leap ahead wildly, but she desperately forced herself to calm down. Strangely enough, being held by Kaito gave her a sense of relaxation. Her face was burning hot, as if her blood were boiling from embarrassment, but she still managed to get her thoughts moving.","After considering the situation before sleeping, the current situation, and the likely chain of events connecting the two...... Kaori's cheeks twitched with an indescribable expression on her face.","(......Ah. This is totally the pattern where I messed up and caused trouble for Kaito-kun. J- Just a guess, but after drinking the cocoa, I must’ve fallen asleep...... And since it’s Kaito-kun, I bet he didn’t try to forcefully wake me and instead tried to lay me down on the bed. He’s kind, after all, so he probably planned to let me sleep on the bed and then go sleep on the sofa or in another room himself, right?)","Kaori knew Kaito’s character well and trusted him. At the very least, he wasn’t the kind of person who would vent his base desires on a sleeping member of the opposite sex. She could reasonably assume that their current state of sharing a bed was largely the result of circumstances beyond their control.","And when she tried to think about what those circumstances might have been...... no matter how she looked at it, it seemed the cause lay with herself.","(It’s probably that, right? Based on all the romance stories I’ve seen, this situation is the type where I, while asleep, unconsciously grabbed Kaito-kun’s hand or clung to him. And honestly, I feel like I was sleeping really deeply, so I probably didn’t wake up at all, right? Or maybe he thought it’d be cruel to wake me, so he waited for me to naturally wake up or let go, but in the meantime, he got sleepy too and just fell asleep like that.)","Considering both the situation and Kaito’s personality, she could make a fairly solid guess, and it was close enough to the truth to be called basically correct.","(......Unn. I get the situation. I get it, but...... putting that aside...... what do I do now......? It’s probably, no, definitely me who hugged him first, and I think I’m the one at fault here, but...... while I was asleep, Kaito-kun ended up holding me back too, so...... I can’t move.)","Just because she understood the situation didn’t mean she could break out of it. Right now, Kaori was clinging to Kaito while also being held by him in return. Their bodies were almost completely pressed together, making it quite difficult to move.","No, of course, she could forcibly pull herself away if she was willing to wake Kaito up, but being certain that she was the one who had caused him trouble, she couldn’t bring herself to take an action that would wake him up in what was clearly the middle of the night.","(......B- But still, this is kind of not okay, you know, Kaito-kun!? It feels...... way too intimate, and t- this level of closeness is insane...... Errr...... does this mean I just stay like this until Kaito-kun wakes up......? Arehh...... what time is it now?)","For the record, the current time was 2 AM, and if she were to wait for Kaito to wake up naturally, there was still a long, long time to go.","<Afterword>","Makina : [Magnificent! Right now!! I am!! Overwhelmingly moved!!! You were being considerate of my beloved child, weren’t you!? My child cherishing my beloved child, swallowing her embarrassment to show tenderness!! Showing respect!! Deepening their love!! The world I desire is right here before my eyes!!!]","Caramel Popcorn : [......Isn’t that exactly the kind of line said by someone who’s about to get blown away by pure love......?]"]},{"number":2490,"title":"Chapter 2490: Chapter 2491: Movie Watching with Kaori 27","paragraphs":["Even as she restlessly shifted her gaze at the current situation of being held in Kaito’s arms, the fact that she still had some leeway to think was, after all, because she had experienced a hug once before.","Of course, a hug and sleeping in the same bed were completely different things, but even so, the fact that she had once experienced being pressed this close together became a faint source of emotional support.","(......No matter how I think about it, dawn is still far away. Kaito-kun looks like he’s sleeping soundly too, and getting out of this situation without waking him up would be difficult. I could pull away if I used Body Strengthening Magic, but after causing him so much trouble already, waking him up in the middle of the night would be......)","In terms of physical ability, if magic were included, Kaori far surpassed him, so it wasn’t that she couldn’t break free from being held.","However, considering that she had fallen asleep herself and unconsciously clung to Kaito, restraining him for at least long enough that he gave up and fell asleep, she couldn’t bring herself to choose that option.","(Using Teleportation Magic is impossible too. Taking magic tools out of the magic box would require moving around a lot, and besides, Kaito-kun’s house has powerful teleportation interference, so teleporting itself isn’t possible...... h- hmm...... so that means...... there’s no way out?)","After thinking that far, Kaori glanced at Kaito’s face. It was too dim to see clearly, but the faintly visible sleeping face somehow felt cute.","(......W- Well, in that case...... it can’t be helped, right? It’s not like I dislike this situation or anything...... somehow, it feels really reassuring, like I can relax here...... for now, I guess it’s fine to stay like this.)","Of course, she felt embarrassed, but she didn’t feel any discomfort at being held by Kaito. If anything, she even felt a certain sense of comfort.","From Kaori’s perspective, towards Kaito, the person she was interested in...... the one she had come to recognize she had feelings for, her guard had become quite loose. And on top of that, since Kaito was fast asleep right now, even if she was embarrassed, there was no worry about him seeing her reddened face.","Under the noble excuse of “it would be bad to wake Kaito up”, a desire to enjoy this situation just a little longer also welled up inside her.","(......W- We’re practically pressed together with almost our whole bodies anyway...... and if I try to pull back the hand I’ve wrapped around Kaito-kun’s back, I might wake him up...... y-yeah, that’s right. This can’t be helped...... I already caused trouble, so waking Kaito-kun up in the middle of the night would be bad...... it can’t be helped, and thinking about the posture too, sticking a bit closer is more natural anyway......)","Thinking up excuses for herself, Kaori gently pressed her reddened face against Kaito’s chest. She wasn’t tightening her embrace or anything like that, but she still felt as if the degree of closeness had increased, feeling like she could hear the pounding of her rapidly beating heart.","(O- Ohh...... Kaito-kun gives off such a gentle vibe that I always had the impression he was kind of slender, but...... h- he actually has a pretty solid chest, or rather, it feels like he does some exercise too...... h- he really has the body of a boy...... u- ugh, my heart’s racing.)","Kaito didn’t really engage in combat all that often, and in his daily life he preferred relaxed, loose-fitting clothes, but he frequently accompanied Hina on her early-morning runs and at least kept up the bare minimum of exercise.","On top of that, he was constantly doing various kinds of maintenance work, such as brushing Bellfreed’s nearly 5-meter-tall body, so he does have a fair amount of muscle. From the impression she got while hugging him, he felt sturdier than she had imagined.","That contrast became a kind of gap, making Kaori’s heart pound even harder.","(T- This is troubling...... I mean, it’s like I’m getting way more serious about this than I thought...... u- uwahh, what should I do, this feeling is, I- I'm really happy...... n- no, it’s not like Kaito-kun and I are lovers or anything, and normally, this kind of thing isn’t very appropriate, but given the situation right now, it can’t be helped......)","Along with a sense of peace, a faint happiness welled up inside her, and Kaori let out a small smile while keeping her face buried against Kaito’s chest.","(......I wonder how Kaito-kun felt? Even if it was my fault, he stayed beside me while I was asleep, right? I- I’m absolutely sure he’s not the type to do anything strange to a sleeping girl, so there’s no doubt nothing happened...... but still, I wonder if his thought headed that way, even just a little...... If he was at least conscious of me as the opposite sex...... that would make me...... a little happy.)","As she thought about such things and let her whole body soak in the blissful warmth, drowsiness began to creep up on her again.","(......I’m getting sleepy. But, well, I guess it’s fine...... Kaito-kun doesn’t look like he’s going to wake up anytime soon either, and it’s still dark outside...... it’s warm and comforting...... I’ll just fall asleep like this.)","It had been an unexpected turn of events, but the warmth and the pull of sleep were hard to resist...... And so, Kaori closed her eyes and gently sank back into slumber.","<Afterword>","Makina : [Wonderful. This makes me look forward to how their relationship will develop.]","Popcorn-senpai : [Ah, my name’s kinda back to normal. That aside, Kaori is totally a maiden in love, isn’t she!? Even if it’s all thanks to Makina’s heavy-handed assist of the script, she’s completely playing the heroine role!!!]","Makina : [No, I want you not to misunderstand. I had nothing to do with my child drinking cocoa and falling asleep, or with her hugging my beloved child around the waist. I did tweak things a little afterward, but of course, I didn’t mess with either of their thoughts in any weird way. The same goes for my beloved child hugging my child while they were sleeping, and this time too, with my child sleeping on my beloved child’s chest, I didn’t do anything there either. Oh, and just as a side note, I did make it so my beloved child would relax when being hugged by my child, but I didn’t do anything to my child’s side in particular.]","Popcorn-senpai : [So in the end, it’s Kaito’s romcom constitution that’s the real problem huh...... and on top of that, it’s basically confirmed that Kaori is way more in love with Kaito than she herself realizes......]"]},{"number":2491,"title":"Chapter 2491: Chapter 2492: Movie Watching with Kaori 28","paragraphs":["Feeling the faint light filtering through the gap in the curtains behind my eyelids, my consciousness rapidly surfaced. I’m actually pretty good at waking up, when it’s time to get up, I can usually do it in one smooth motion.","When I slowly opened my eyes, what jumped into view was Kaori-san’s face, sleeping so peacefully...... h- hmmm...... ah, r- right, that’s what happened!? So I ended up falling asleep like that after all...... I really messed up.","I was startled for a moment, but as I recalled the situation from before we went to sleep, an indescribable sense of guilt welled up inside me. I’d wanted to wait until Kaori-san woke up, if possible, but I’d just gone and fallen asleep so easily...... and what’s more, I’d slept soundly all the way till morning.","Wait, hold on. Isn’t this weird......? The smooth texture of her clothes and a soft warmth were reaching my hand. And this closeness...... aren’t I in a position where I’m hugging Kaori-san!? No, it’s more than that, we’re completely holding each other, aren’t we!?","Did we unconsciously end up like this while we were asleep? A- Anyway, if Kaori-san wakes up in this state, how am I supposed to explain it...... I need to let go right away......","[......nnn...... ahfuu.]","[ ! ? ]","But reality is cruel like that. Just as I thought that, Kaori-san shifted slightly, then opened her eyes with a sleepy little sound...... and our gazes met perfectly.","[........................]","[........................]","Awkward...... unbearably awkward. Kaori-san looked surprised for a split second when she saw me, but soon she seemed to grasp the situation and put on an awkward expression of her own.","The fact that she wasn’t panicking, did that mean she might have woken up at some point during the night......? But since we hadn’t separated...... ah, could it be that by then I was already holding her and she couldn’t pull away, or something like that!?","[......M- Morning.]","[......Good morning.]","[......E- Errr......]","[S- Sorry. I mean, I know this is kind of a strange situation, but...... errr, I just feel bad about it.]","[N- No! It’s probably like this, right? I fell asleep, and then after that I ended up bothering you unconsciously!? If anything, I’m the one who caused you trouble in all sorts of ways, sorry!]","It was like we both didn’t know how to move, so we just exchanged words for the time being. Thankfully, Kaori-san seemed to have grasped the situation pretty accurately, and it didn’t look like she was harboring any weird misunderstandings.","Of course, she was blushing from embarrassment, and I was probably red-faced too, but it was reassuring that the conversation itself seemed to be moving along smoothly.","[From my side too, it probably ended up like this while we were asleep, right?]","[I- I think so. I actually woke up once in the middle of the night, and even then we were already in this position......]","[No, I’m really sorry.]","[No, it’s more my fault, and it’s not something Kaito-kun needs to apologize for. Besides, this is probably going to turn into a never-ending loop, so let’s just stop arguing about who’s at fault for now. Let’s just say we both have things to reflect on......]","[Y- Yeah.]","What was truly fortunate was that Kaori-san was quick to switch gears. If we kept blaming each other and apologizing, the conversation wouldn’t go anywhere, so I appreciated that she shifted to the next topic.","[......M- Maybe it’s about time we let go, both of us......]","[Y- Yeah.]","After taking a breath there, I realized we were still in that embracing position and hastily pulled my body away.","[D- Did I sweat in my sleep? I didn’t smell weird or anything, did I?]","[N- No, if anything you smelled nice...... I mean, in that sense, I’m more worried about whether I made you uncomfortable......]","[Y- Yeah, no, that’s totally fine. I mean, of course it was super embarrassing, but...... i- it’s not like I hated it or anything...... a- anyway! Let’s just say there’s no problem on either side!!! Yes, this topic is over!!! F- For now, I’ll go back to my room and change. B- Breakfast is fine here, right?]","[Y- Yes, that’s fine.]","[T- Then I’ll come back here after I change. S- So, um, see you later!!!]","Overwhelmed by embarrassment, Kaori-san rattled all that off with a red face and then left the room. I was left with an indescribable sense of awkwardness myself and lightly scratched my cheek.","It wasn’t like things had turned sour, and considering Kaori-san’s personality, she’d probably be back to her usual self by the time she returned.","Still, that aside, the sensation of holding Kaori-san was lingering in my memory pretty vividly...... I feel like I’m going to be quite conscious of it from now on.","But since Kaori-san also said it wasn’t unpleasant for her...... it might just be my own conceit, but I can’t help thinking that she might be looking at me in a somewhat favorable light too.","Man, just thinking about it is pretty embarrassing...... Anyway, I should get changed too.","<Afterword>","Pop-senpai : [Guaaaah, so sweet...... K- Kaori, how terrifying...... and on top of that, she’s cleared the part that’s arguably the highest difficulty and takes the most time. She’s completed the step of making Kaito consciously see her as a romantic interest...... I- In one go, she’s become the top contender for \"next girlfriend\"......]","Makina : [With such a perfect flow, even Mama is completely satisfied. That aside though...... Your name's actually coming back that half-baked way?]","Pop-senpai : [I feel like the cause is you, if anything......]"]},{"number":2492,"title":"Chapter 2492: Chapter 2493: Movie Watching with Kaori 29","paragraphs":["As I thought, or should I say, as expected, Kaori-san seemed to have fully switched gears while she went to change, and by the time she returned, she was back to her usual self.","She was happily eating the breakfast that had been brought to my room, just like at dinner.","[Mm~~ this croissant is delicious! Freshly baked bread really is amazing, isn’t it?]","[Come to think of it, you mentioned you were thinking of adding bread-friendly items to your menu at your shop. Do you actually bake the bread yourself?]","The stew we had tasted together with Akane-san before had been a test dish for bread-friendly meals, so I figured Kaori-san had gone beyond just planning and had done at least some preparation.","But baking bread seemed like it would be complicated, so I asked if she was planning to just source it instead, to which Kaori-san made a thoughtful expression.","[Hmm...... it would be fun to bake it myself, but baking bread requires equipment. I did work at a bakery for a while when I was traveling, so I can bake, technically.]","[Yeah, with Suiren's current kitchen, I feel like you’d need to renovate if you wanted to bake bread here.]","[Well, I do have a magic tool with oven-like functions, so it’s not like I couldn’t bake if I really wanted to. Besides, the bread-friendly menu is still in the prototype stage. For now, I think I’ll just source it. If it becomes popular and I expand the menu, I’ll think about it then.]","[I see......]","[Kaito-kun, do you know any good bakeries? There aren’t really any around my shop.]","[Hmmm, bakeries huh......]","I mostly eat rice anyway...... and in the central area where I live, which caters more to nobles, you have to go to the main street to find a bakery.","The bakeries on the main street are good, no doubt, but it's more like their jam that's tasty...... bread huh......","[......Ah, now that I think about it, I remember Tir-san mentioned growing wheat and supplying it...... Tir-san’s crops are excellent, so I bet there are some good bakeries she supplies to.]","[Tir-san? Hmm...... I have a bad feeling about this. That’s a nickname, right? Her full name might be...... Tirtania-sama or something like that?]","[Yes, Tir-san of the Seven Princesses.]","[Gahh, I think I asked the wrong person! I’d rather not have the Six Kings’ Executives casually mentioned here...... Even if they’re good, there’s no way to negotiate with someone like that......]","Kaori-san looked at me with a mixture of exasperation and disbelief upon hearing Tir-san’s name, but in this case, I actually thought it was a topic Kaori-san might be able to handle.","[No, actually...... Tir-san is really close with Raz-san, so if Kaori-san asks Raz-san, she can probably introduce you easily. I could also introduce you myself, it wouldn’t be a problem......]","[Ah, right, Raz-sama is a Fairy, so they had that connection. Hmm...... I certainly am a bit interested in that......]","[Also, I know someone named Trois-san, who’s extremely knowledgeable about all kinds of shops. If you ask him, he might be able to recommend a good bakery.]","[......I see...... By the way, is this person, like, someone important?]","[He’s the special advisor for the Seditch Magical Tools Trading Company and a Count-rank High Treant.]","[............Don’t you have any commoner acquaintances?]","Trois-san is the special advisor for the sales division of the Seditch Magic Tools Trading Company and an incredible person who knows the products of all sorts of guilds and shops.","He’s kind and a good conversationalist, so it’s fairly easy to consult with him...... but if there’s one problem, it’s that whenever you ask Trois about a product, you often end up buying it before you even realize it.","He’s just that good at presenting products. Listening to him makes your desire to buy grow rapidly, and his sales talk is impressively top-tier, truly befitting someone skilled in sales.","[I can introduce you to Trois-san, but he’s extremely good at sales talk. There’s a high chance you might end up signing a contract without even noticing.]","[Facing such a super-skilled salesperson, I feel a bit hesitant...... h- hmm, I’ll think about it, but perhaps, I might just ask for an introduction to Tir-sama instead?]","[Sure, just let me know anytime. Tir-san, like Raz-san, is sociable and fun to hang out with, so you’ll probably get along right away.]","As an introduction target, Tir-san is as safe as Raz-san; her social skills are top-notch, so she’s a reliable person to be introduced to.","With that lighthearted chatter, I enjoyed breakfast with Kaori-san.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [Feels like things have settled down...... then it’s about time the scattered stomachache landmines start exploding.]","Serious-senpai : [Stop with the sugar-and-stomachache Dempsey roll......]"]},{"number":2493,"title":"Chapter 2493: Chapter 2494: Company and Exclusive Brush 1","paragraphs":["When I visited a room inside Kuro’s castle in the Demon Realm, I was greeted by a refreshing, tall man with light green, smooth mushroom-cut hair...... Trois-san.","[Hey, Kaito. You came at just the right time.]","[Hello, Trois-san. Sorry for dropping by so suddenly today.]","[Don’t worry about it. I’m glad you came to see me. It’s not much of a room, but come on in.]","[Excuse me.]","Trois-san smiled gently. Somehow, he always gives off the aura of an overwhelmingly handsome guy, no matter when I see him, he’s cool. He wears a suit-like outfit sharply, has long limbs, a tall build, and kind-looking features...... If Ozma-san is the hard-boiled, cool adult type, then Trois-san feels more like a bright and refreshing handsome older brother.","Trois-san belongs to a race called the High Treants. In terms of nature, they seem closer to Spirits, but appearance-wise, he looks no different from a normal human. Still, since he once showed me by turning his hand into wood, this current form is probably something close to Humanization Magic.","[......So, you said you had something you wanted to consult about?]","[Well, it’s less a consultation and more something I wanted to ask for reference...... Errr, someone I know runs a set-meal restaurant called Suiren. Do you know it?]","I sat down in the seat Trois-san prepared and explained the reason for my visit. Earlier, when I was talking with Kaori-san about bread procurement and such, I happened to be coming to Kuromu Lake for shopping anyway. So I figured I’d ask Trois-san whether there were shops like that within the Friendship City, regardless of whether I’d actually make an introduction.","[Yeah, the otherworld cuisine restaurant in Friendship City, right?]","[As expected, you know it well.]","[Hahaha, well, I’ve more or less memorized the stores in the major cities of the Human Realm, so I only know the name though.]","He said it so casually, like remembering most of the shops in the Human Realm was nothing...... but with Trois-san, it wouldn’t be strange if he had nearly all the shops in the Demon Realm memorized too.","And even though he said he only knew the name, I have a feeling he probably also knew their popular menu items.","[Errr, so, when I met her last time, we talked about how she’s thinking of eventually making bread-based set meals. It’s not finalized at all yet, but if that happens, she’s planning to source the bread...... Do you know any good shops, Trois-san?]","[There are a few. Friendship City Hikari has fairly high-quality bakeries, after all.]","[Is that so?]","[Kaito, you know about the Heavenly Light Worship, right? During the Heavenly Light Worship, devout believers eat white bread, like they do at New Year’s. White is generally considered a sacred color that symbolizes Shallow Vernal-sama. That’s why it has quite a bit of demand in Friendship City, where the Central Cathedral stands. That said, baking white bread beautifully actually requires quite a bit of skill, so many of the bakeries that set up shop in Friendship City have very capable craftsmen.]","I nodded in admiration at Trois-san’s clear and easy-to-understand explanation. Now that he mentioned it, it was true, there’s a custom of eating white bread during the New Year in the Human Realm, so it wouldn’t be strange for it to be eaten during the Heavenly Light Worship as well.","While I was thinking about that, Trois-san took out a memo, scribbled something down, and handed it to me. When I looked at it, several names that seemed to belong to bakeries were lined up.","[These are relatively close to Suiren and accept bread orders. They all handle high-quality bread, so if you get the chance, it might be nice to go shopping there normally too.]","[Thank you very much. I’ll use this as a reference.]","[Unn. But well, if we’re talking purely about bread quality, I think the bread handled at your place, Nifty, is overwhelmingly better...... Though I guess that’s high-end stuff meant for upscale shops, so it might be difficult to use at a set-meal restaurant?]","[Ah, right, now that you mention it, the bread we serve at the café is from Canalis-san......]","Come to think of it, asking Canalis-san might also be an option...... No, if I consult Canalis-san, I have a feeling she’d start talking about making exclusive bread just for Kaori-san’s shop.","Kaori-san herself is still in the phase of experimenting and thinking about adding bread to the menu, so I’ll wait until things are more firmly decided and she asks me to introduce her to someone like Tir-san.","[Speaking of which, speaking of Nifty, it seems like Nove and the others were taken care of there before.]","[Ah, no, I was just about to go to the café myself, so I only asked Canalis-san to arrange a seat for them......]","[Oh right, you’re acquainted with someone from the Sharon Trading Company, aren’t you? Actually, I’m planning to visit the Sharon Trading Company soon.]","[Huh? You are, Trois-san? ......Is it some kind of business deal?]","[It’s more like a proposal for partial business cooperation. You see, recently our introductions have been expanding into the Human Realm, so we figured we should strengthen our ties with the Sharon Trading Company, which is one of the major magic tool trading companies there. Tetra is quite enthusiastic about it too and even allocated a generous budget, so it’s likely to become a fairly large-scale deal.]","[Hehh, I see...... That sounds pretty big.]","I don’t really understand the ins and outs of business between trading companies, but if Trois-san is going there in person, it must be a fairly significant deal, right? If it’s also a good opportunity for the Sharon Trading Company, then as Cornelia-san’s friend, I can only be happy about it.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......I see...... the landmine that’s going to explode...... is on Cornelia's side huh......]"]},{"number":2494,"title":"Chapter 2494: Chapter 2495: Company and Exclusive Brush 2","paragraphs":["Trois-san is extremely good at talking, and also an excellent listener...... or rather, his way of expanding topics and guiding the conversation makes it easy and pleasant for the other person to talk.","When I have plenty of topics to draw from, he mainly takes the role of listener, reacting at just the right moments with surprise or admiration, skillfully drawing me out and letting me speak.","On the other hand, when I’ve talked for a while and the conversation seems about to run dry, he casually throws out a new topic to keep things flowing.","[Ah, that reminds me, I heard Kaito previously went around introducing Dual Star Trading Company’s new products, right? Thanks to that, their sales seem to be doing quite well.]","[No, I only recommended them to a few acquaintances, but I'd be glad if it helped...... Arehh? Wait, Trois-san, are you involved with Dual Star Trading Company as well?]","[No, it’s not like I’m directly involved in sales. Rather, I taught various people about sales, to put it very simply, there are a few kids who are like my disciples working there. I heard it from them.]","[Hehh. Well, both are Kuro’s trading companies, so it wouldn’t be strange for there to be some kind of connection.]","[Most of Kuromu-sama’s family members belong to one trading company or another. Of course, not every single one of them does...... but changing the subject, how do you like coffee, Kaito?]","[I like it quite a bit. Though not to the level of being super obsessed and carefully selecting beans and all that.]","Trois-san is apparently something of a legend when it comes to sales-related matters, so it wouldn’t be surprising if he had a lot of disciples.","[Ah, I get that. People who are really particular about that sort of thing have an unbelievable amount of passion, don’t they?]","[Yeah. People who truly love it have incredible standards. They can even tell subtle differences in flavor that I honestly can’t. As for me, as long as it tastes reasonably good, that’s enough...... I have a friend named Amel-san from the Winged Tribe, and she owns a magic tool that automatically brews coffee from beans, so I figured something like that would be good enough for me.]","[True, that type of magic tool exists, and since it’s easy to use, it’s quite popular. What kind of device was the one Kaito saw?]","[Errr, I think it was......]","As the topic continued to expand and I talked about the coffee-maker-like magic tool I’d seen at Amel-san’s house, Trois-san listened with gentle smiles and nods, and when I reached a pause in my story, he opened his mouth.","[What Kaito saw was the simple type of magic tool.]","[Unn? So there are more multifunctional types as well?]","[There are. In fact, the latest model was released fairly recently. Let me see, the sales sample is...... ah, here it is. This one.]","[Oh, the size isn’t that different, but...... there are multiple magic crystals?]","What Trois-san took out was about the same size as the device I had seen at Amel-san’s place, but this one had several magic crystals attached to it.","Since he said it was multifunctional, I suppose these multiple magic crystals add various features.","[The one Kaito saw was probably the type that only brews coffee from beans, but this one can also add sugar and milk by adjusting these scales here. On the back, next to where you put in the coffee beans and water, there are inlets for milk and sugar as well.]","[Hehh, so it really can do everything fully automatically. But wouldn’t milk spoil if you don’t put in the exact amount and there’s leftovers?]","[That’s what you’d think, right? That’s where its high performance comes in. This magic tool automatically comes under State Preservation Magic when it’s not in use. So if you put in coffee beans and milk all at once, you can drink whenever you like without worrying about deterioration.]","[Oh, that’s great. You wouldn’t even need to store it in a magic box every time......]","That function really does sound amazing. If it automatically preserves its contents when not in use, that’s reassuring, and it means you can just leave it in your room and have coffee whenever you want...... I want one.","[Still, it does have its drawbacks. To support all those features, grinding and brewing from coffee beans, adjusting the amount and mixing of sugar and milk, making espresso and the like, dispensing the proper amount when you place a mug under the spout, and on top of that, State Preservation Magic, you naturally need multiple magic crystals. And as the number of magic crystals and functions increases, the price inevitably goes up.]","[I see. By the way, about how much does it cost?]","[For this type, two gold coins.]","[......Ah, so it's just that much huh.]","[Hahaha. For Kaito, that’s probably not a big amount, but for ordinary citizens, if someone loves coffee enough to be willing to pay two gold coins just to drink it, they’d probably grind the beans themselves anyway...... This magic tool is more aimed at fairly wealthy customers, like nobles who find it troublesome to call a servant to make coffee first thing in the morning.]","[Ah, now that you put it that way, being able to spend two gold coins on a luxury item like that would require being quite well-off.]","Compared to magic boxes or teleportation devices, it’s much cheaper, but if you think of it as a coffee maker, converting it to Japanese yen would put it at around two million yen, which is ridiculously expensive.","Still, I honestly want one...... Waking up in the morning, brewing coffee with this magic tool, and drinking it from a mug while looking out at a garden bathed in the morning sunlight...... that sounds nice.","[......Um, Trois-san, if I go to the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company, can I buy that magic tool there?]","[Normally it’s made to order, but if Kaito wants one, I can arrange it. I have a few reserved under my authority, so I can sell you one right away.]","[Ah, then please, I’d love to buy it.]","[Of course. Since it’s you, Kaito, I’d like to give you some kind of service, but a discount probably wouldn’t be very appealing to you...... so I’ll prepare one with convenient additional functions at the same price.]","[Additional convenient functions?]","[Yeah, an automatic filter replacement and cleaning function. After use, the spent filter and the ground coffee residue are discarded into a box attached to the side, a new filter is set automatically, and at the same time, the interior is cleaned. All the waste gets collected into that box, so you only need to throw away its contents.]","[That’s incredibly convenient! Thank you very much!]","[I’m glad you’re happy. I’ll tell them to prepare it, so when you’re heading back, just stop by the main reception desk of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company.]","[Understood.]","Man, I’d been thinking about getting a coffee maker someday anyway, so I’m glad I managed to buy such a good one. Since it looks like I can take it home today, I’m already looking forward to using it.","Maybe I should buy some coffee beans on the way back too...... Either way, this was a great purchase. I’m really grateful to Trois-san.","........................Arehh? I came here to ask about a bakery, so why did I end up buying a coffee maker? W- Well, whatever. I wanted one anyway......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Come to think of it, when he was talking with Kaori about chatting with Trois, he said something like how you somehow end up buying products before you even realize it...... so this is exactly like this pattern huh......]","? ? ? : [Well, it’s not like he’s deceiving people or forcing them to buy anything. What’s impressive is how he picks up on what Kaito-san wants and subtly recommends it. Kaito-san was the one who said he wanted to buy it in the first place, and he’s happy about having made a good purchase, so there’s really no problem.]"]},{"number":2495,"title":"Chapter 2495: Chapter 2496: Company and Exclusive Brush 3","paragraphs":["Although it wasn’t my original objective, since I’d managed to get my hands on a coffee maker, I figured I might as well buy some coffee beans on the way back too.","To be honest, I don’t really know much about coffee...... well, it’s not like I know much about tea either...... Since I had no idea which beans to choose, I decided this was a case where I should ask someone who actually knows coffee.","With that in mind, I headed to Elise-san’s shop. Checking the sign on the door, it read \"Open\". At Elise-san’s place, once a group of customers enters, the front sign automatically switches to \"Closed\", so with the current state, there was no problem.","[......Hello.]","[......It’s Human-san. You really do always show up at the exact moment when the flow of customers stops. In my mind, the \"Human-san is a stalker\" suspicion has gained another level of credibility.]","[Please stop with those outrageous misunderstandings.]","[Well, don’t just stand there, come over here and sit down. I don’t think you came for a fortune-telling session, so what do you need?]","Her tone sounded slightly exasperated, but this was basically Elise-san’s default. She invited me to sit and listened normally, so it wasn’t like she was treating me coldly.","In fact, given Elise-san’s personality, if it were inconvenient, she’d probably just tell me to \"go home\" outright. If she was willing to hear me out, that meant things were fine.","[Actually, something came up, and I bought a magic tool for brewing coffee. So I was hoping Elise-san, who knows a lot about coffee, could recommend some good coffee beans or something......]","[A magic tool for brewing coffee? If you’re looking for beans, does that mean it’s the type that grinds the beans and brews them?]","[Yeah. Sorry to put this on your table for a moment. This is it.]","[......This is...... You managed to buy this? Ah, well, if it’s Human-san, you can probably buy things through all sorts of special routes.]","When she saw the magic tool I took out, Elise-san wore a slightly surprised expression, which was rare for her. If she reacted like this, did that mean it was a fairly hard-to-obtain magic tool?","[Is it that hard to buy?]","[Well, more like, this just came out five days ago, it’s the latest model. On top of that, it’s made-to-order only, and they’re limiting the number of orders, so at this stage you can’t buy it without connections. For high-quality made-to-order magic tools like this, the order restrictions usually get relaxed a few months after release, making them easier to buy.]","[Hehh, I see...... Well, I happened to buy it from a special advisor at the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company......]","[How many people in the world do you think can purchase directly from there...... You really are the same as always, Human-san. In a way, that’s reassuring.]","Muttering with a fed-up look, Elise-san still examined the coffee maker magic tool with obvious interest.","[......Actually, I was debating whether to buy this myself.]","[Eh? You, Elise-san, buying a magic tool that brews coffee automatically?]","Since Elise-san even roasts her own beans and seems particular about grinding and brewing, the idea that she’d buy a fully automatic magic tool was unexpected.","[Well, I wouldn’t use it regularly. I just wanted to try it once. This latest model is advertised as being able to brew quite authentic coffee, and since the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company is selling it as a fully made-to-order product...... I wanted to know just how good it actually tastes. But I was hesitant to buy such an expensive magic tool when I didn’t plan to use it all the time.]","[Ah, I get what you mean...... Then, since we’re here anyway, want to try brewing some coffee with this and have a taste? Though I literally just bought it, so I don’t have anything besides the magic tool......]","[Is that okay? Then I’d love to try it. I’ll prepare the coffee beans and filters.]","As a coffee lover, clearly very curious about how good the latest coffee maker could be, Elise-san immediately accepted my suggestion and promptly brought over coffee beans, filters, and coffee cups.","Seeing how interested she was, I quickly set the beans she brought into the machine and tried using it.","[I see, it can even adjust the grind size to some extent, even if it’s a bit rough. This really raises my expectations. Human-san actually does something nice once in a while. As a thank-you, I’ll prepare some cake too. You should eat some.]","[Thank you.]","She really does seem to love coffee. Elise-san, unusually high-spirited, brought over some cake and set it in front of me.","While we were doing that, the coffee finished brewing, so we poured it into cups and tried it right away. The aroma was good and the taste was nice...... but since I couldn’t really tell the finer details, I decided to watch Elise-san’s reaction instead.","Elise-san took a sip of the coffee and nodded with an impressed expression.","[......This is quite something. Even for someone as picky about coffee as me, it tastes reasonably good. Of course, when I brew it myself, I can fine-tune things more and the flavor is better...... but for a fully automatic machine to produce this level of taste is impressive. It’s better than the coffee at some mediocre cafés or coffee shops. You can really feel the progress of technology.]","[Speaking of which, it seems it can also make espresso.]","[Espresso too? I suppose it can grind extremely fine, and if it applies pressure with magic, then espresso as well...... It’s amazing that this one machine can do so many things. I’m impressed.]","Watching Elise-san sip her coffee with a faintly cheerful air, I enjoyed my own coffee as well, eating the cake she had prepared that paired perfectly with it.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [By the way, Elise doesn’t really like cake, so it's highly likely she originally prepared that cake for Kaito-san.]"]},{"number":2496,"title":"Chapter 2496: Chapter 2497: Company and Exclusive Brush 4","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I’ll be busy tomorrow and probably won’t have time to write, so the next update will be the day after tomorrow.","After having coffee with Elsie, she told me about a coffee shop in Symphonia's royal capital and recommended some beans, so I stopped by on the way home and bought some.","As I was thinking how excited I was to brew it, Nebula greeted me at the door.","[Welcome home, Master. A package has arrived.]","[I'm back, Nebula...... a package?]","[Yes, Master. It’s the exclusive brushes for the monsters that you requested from Victor Trading Company. The box is large, so I’ve placed it in the backyard warehouse.]","[Oh, it’s already here!]","That was faster than I expected. Since I had ordered every possible combination, I thought it might take months, but it arrived in less than a month...... maybe they prioritized making it for me.","Either way, they were the exclusive brushes I’d been looking forward to. Excited, I headed to the backyard warehouse with Nebula, and sure enough, there was a very large box waiting.","[Master, here’s the letter that came with it.]","[Thanks. Errr...... ahh, I see. So they didn’t send all of them at once, just the ones that were ready first......]","Looking at the letter, it seemed that not every combination of brushes had been delivered yet. For now, they sent 20 for Bell, 40 for Lynn, and 40 for Sela, a total of 100 brushes.","Still, that was more than enough. Even if all the brushes arrived at once, I couldn’t use them all immediately, so receiving them in batches makes it easier to test them.","The reason Bell’s brushes were fewer than Lynn’s and Sela’s is probably because they are larger and take longer to make.","For now, let’s check the brushes that have arrived.","[......They’re all well-made. This one, for example, seems to have the right stiffness for Bell’s fur...... I’ll try them all, but first I’ll start with the ones that feel most familiar......]","[The ones in this stiffness range are closest to what we usually use. I see...... indeed, I can slightly sense Bellfried and the others’ magical wavelengths. With these, brushing shouldn’t cause them any stress.]","[Unn. Let’s try them right away.]","[I’ll help too.]","[Thanks, I appreciate it.]","We decided to start brushing immediately, choosing the brushes that felt closest to the ones we currently use. With Nebula, we moved to where Bell and the others were waiting.","The texture feels great, but more importantly, it’s crucial to see how Bell and the others react when we actually use them. If it works well, I plan to recommend them to Frea-san and Magnawell-san, so we need to test carefully.","And so, starting with Bell...... the brushing feels amazing. The brush glides smoothly, and through Sympathy Magic, I can tell that Bell is relaxed.","[......Bell, is the new brush good?]","[Gau!]","Bell is quite sensitive to magic power, so she seems to really like the feel of a brush tuned to her magical wavelength, nodding happily at my question.","The same applies to human skin, stress has a significant impact. Whether Bell can relax affects the shine of her fur.","With this, there’s no doubt her coat will look even more magnificent than before.","[......Fumu, this is...... I see.]","[Nebula?]","[Ahh, no, this brush is already very good, but with a little adjustment, it could be even more effective.]","[Eh? How so?]","[Yes. Please wait a moment...... Canalis-san! Could you come here for a moment?]","[Yes! Sorry to keep you waiting!]","When Nebula called out, Canalis-san appeared immediately. I tilted my head, wondering what they intended to do, and then Nebula explained something to Canalis-san. Nodding, Canalis-san created a small tool.","[Kaito-sama, please attach this to the handle of the brush. It’s detachable, so you can use it with other brushes as well.]","[......What's this?]","[To put it simply, it’s a tool that converts the magic power you infuse into the brush into the brush’s own magical wavelength.]","[By permeating your magic power while they are relaxed, it enhances the quality of their fur. Master’s magic power has excellent adaptability, so by channeling it in the same wavelength, it should further improve the fur’s quality. Only a light infusion of magic power is needed. Too much could have the opposite effect......]","I see. So by infusing magic power, the brush’s effective magic power increases, which enhances relaxation and improves fur quality...... In that case, let’s try it.","[......Gau~~]","As I lightly infused magic power while brushing, Bell clearly looked incredibly comfortable...... her expression almost melting. She seemed to be enjoying it immensely.","Not only that, but the shine of the brushed fur visibly increased. I- It really changes this much huh...... Incredible. With the help of the tool Canalis-san made and the excellence of the exclusive brush itself, the results were perfect.","This really was a good purchase...... I’ll definitely recommend it to Frea-san and Magnawell-san.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Kaito...... sorry to burst your bubble, but that’s almost like a death sentence for Cornelia...... I think the visible results are probably mostly due to the tool Canalis made...... but since with him that hyped up, he might end up giving all the credit to the exclusive brush......]"]},{"number":2497,"title":"Chapter 2497: Chapter 2498: Company and Exclusive Brush 5","paragraphs":["A few days after the exclusive brush arrived, I visited Frea-san’s house in the Demon Realm and, as promised, explained how it felt to use it. I had already visited Magnawell-san beforehand and had recommended it to him as well.","[......I see. My comrade’s evaluation is favorable then.]","[Yes. I had Canalis-san make me a support tool, but when I use it on myself, there’s no need to return magic. By simply pouring magic power into the brush, according to Nebula, it allows the magic power to penetrate effectively.]","[Fumu...... Magic power permeation huh. Indeed, such beauty-related magic formulas do exist. In that sense, this exclusive brush might indeed be an ideal tool.]","[Is that so?]","For me, when using it on Bell or Lynn, I had to convert it to match their magic power, but when using it on myself for brushing, no conversion was needed.","According to Nebula, while it’s not as extreme as my special magic power, it’s effective for improving the shine of hair and scales.","[Fumu. Eingana knows more than I do, but the magic formulas for evenly permeation of magic power for beauty purposes does exist. As with myself, beings like dragons and monsters have a lot of magic power flowing through various parts of their bodies, including their blood. The amount of magic power flowing to each part is called the magic power permeation rate, and making it as uniform as possible is said to be the key to beautiful scales and hair.]","[I see. So Eingana-san practices this then.]","[Yeah, though it’s easier said than done. Magic power is generated internally, so the further it is from the body’s core, like the tips of scales or hair, the lower the permeation rate. This is entirely different from coating oneself with magic power for defense or body strengthening. To put it simply, it’s similar to improving blood circulation.]","Nebula mentioned that the extra magic formula for the exclusive brush seems to be a form of beauty care originally meant for dragons and monsters, but if even Frea-san says it’s difficult, perhaps only a few can truly do it.","[The important part here is uniformity. If you try to ensure magic power fully permeates the tips of hair or scales, you might end up overloading magic power in other parts. It’s like trying to reach a distant point with too much force. Therefore, evenly adjusting magic power permeation requires very delicate control.]","[......Ah, I see. So, if the exclusive brush allows magic power to permeate from the outside, it makes it easier to even out the permeation rate without delicate magic control.]","[Exactly. Many dragons care about the beauty of their scales...... well, honestly, I don’t really care, but Eingana and her subordinates are very particular, and many of my own subordinates care as well. It’s the same for dragon scales or the fur of Beast-type Demons...... In that sense, this exclusive brush might be in high demand.]","[I see. If it becomes popular, Cornelia-san would be pleased, so if you meet anyone interested, let them know.]","[Yeah, alright. Leave it to me...... I’ll mention it to Eingana as well.]","It seems that Humans and Demons alike are interested in beauty. In fact, the demand in this field is huge, so it would be great if it gained some popularity.","According to Akane-san, Cornelia-san’s related products would probably benefit from being popular, so I hope it spreads among the Dragon King’s subordinates, who seem likely to want it.","If it can accommodate Beast-type Demons, Anima and Caraway might want one too, so I should try talking to them. What about Amel-san though? If brushes for fur and horns can be made, I feel like a brush for wings could be made as well. The Wingeds are a closed-off species, but they seem very particular about wing care, so maybe this could even be a chance to increase their interaction with the outside world.","Amel-san has expressed wanting the Wingeds to engage more with outsiders, so it might be worth recommending it. Perhaps introducing Cornelia-san-san to them could work too? Well, the Wingeds seem to have strict rules, so I’d need to consult Amel-san properly first...... but it seems possible. No, maybe I should first talk to Cornelia-san and have Victor Trading Company check if a brush for wings can actually be made?","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [......Die! (Your stomach, that is.)]","Serious-senpai : [T- This guy...... he's a genius at increasing the damage with his goodwill...... And once again, I’m reminded that Cornelia is the type that gets hit hard with that one strike.]","? ? ? : [Well then, shall I have some wine along with this?]"]},{"number":2498,"title":"Chapter 2498: Chapter 2499: Company and Exclusive Brush 6","paragraphs":["After finishing recommending things to Frea-san and Magnawell-san, I thought I’d go home and check Amel-san-san’s schedule...... but then I remembered that the magazine I regularly read was released today, so I decided to pick it up while I was out.","Since I had registered the Nifty store in Symphonia Kingdom as a teleportation point, I teleported there first and then walked to the bookstore.","As I passed through the luxury shopping district and reached the main street, by a strange coincidence, I saw a familiar figure approaching from the front.","A petite woman with loosely waved golden hair, a bucket hat hiding her eyes, a slightly fluffy high-neck jacket, a long skirt, and a long coat embroidered beautifully in gold and silver...... it was Tetra-san.","[Hello, Tetra-san. What a coincidence to see you here.]","[......Ya, Kaito. It’s a coincidence, but I’m glad to see you.]","[Are you working?]","[......Of course, I came to see my beloved. You keep me so captivated, yet you’re still so cold.]","[You just said it was a coincidence that we met......]","[......Fufu, well, in reality, I was returning from a budget-related meeting at the capital branch.]","Though I couldn’t see her eyes, Tetra-san’s mouth curved into a somehow cheerful smile as she spoke in a clear, calm voice, making it hard to tell how serious she really was.","[......By the way, I heard about it, Kaito. You visited Trois a while ago, right? You didn’t even drop by to see me, someone who’s been longing for you...... That’s terrible...... well, I was out that day.]","[Then I wouldn’t have found you there if I had gone......]","[......If I had been there, would you have come to spend a sweet moment with me?]","[Shall we have some cake together?]","[......You’re still so cold. I love that about you.]","Tetra-san’s true intentions were hard to read; her teasing tone made it unclear how much she meant seriously.","Well, I guess she enjoyed conversations like that.","[......Then, since fate has allowed us to meet like this, if your schedule is free, let’s spend a sweet moment together at that café.]","[I didn’t have any urgent plans, so that’s fine. Shall we go?]","[......By the way, what were you doing today, Kaito?]","[Until just now, I went to see Frea-san and Magnawell-san to recommend the feel of the dedicated brushes.]","[......Ahh, the brushes you bought at Victor Trading Company? How were they? Good quality?]","[Yes, they were really good. They have additional features as well......]","Invited by Tetra-san, I ended up going to a nearby café for tea. Since I had only planned to buy a magazine, I had time to spare. We chatted lightly while walking, and once we sat down and placed our orders at the café...... Tetra-san muttered, sounding somewhat intrigued.","[......Uniform distribution of magic power permeation huh...... I see. Indeed, that seems to be in high demand. Throughout the world, beauty captivates people as much as wealth does.]","[By the way, Tetra-san, you’re also a Beast-type Demon, right?]","[......Ah, yes, technically. See, I even have horns.]","She removed her bucket hat, revealing sheep-like curled horns beside her head...... I wondered how such horns usually fit under that hat, it was strange.","[......Well, I can handle the uniform distribution of magic power permeation myself, so I make sure even the tips are beautiful...... want to check thoroughly?]","[Tetra-san’s hair really does look like gold. It’s a slightly darker shade of gold, but shiny and beautiful.]","[......Should I lament your coldness or rejoice at your praise? You always confuse my heart. That said, this feeling of being toyed with, I don't hate it. But aside from that, I’d like to hear more about it...... if possible, could you show me the thing you use to convert magic power?]","[Sure. Here, go ahead.]","Canalis-san generally creates items using technologies that can be reproduced in this world, since she has a contract with Shiro-san whenever she makes something. There are exceptions, like Isis-san’s bracelet, items that would be impossible without a god power, but even then, she obtains Shiro-san’s permission beforehand.","The item attached to the handle of this brush was something Nebula requested and had made almost immediately, so it’s probably something that can be reproduced with this world’s existing technology. I figured it would be fine to show it.","[......This is...... hehh, I see...... It can’t be made this small, but it looks like it could be replicated as a magic tool...... Come to think of it, Trois will be heading to the Sharon Count family soon...... Fufufu.]","[Tetra-san?]","[......Ahh, thank you. You’ve shown me something very interesting. You really do bring me fresh surprises and the delightful scent of money. Every time I see you, I fall for you more and more. I love you, darling.]","[Hahh...... t- thanks, I guess.]","[......Oi, oi, you could at least play along and call me \"honey\" in return.]","[If I respond like that to you, Tetra-san, I feel like you’d say I’d given you verbal confirmation of something......]","[......You’re really cold. That’s exactly what I love about you.]","Laughing cheerfully, she pushed up the brim of her bucket hat, looked at me with her silver eyes, and gave a sharp wink. The emotions conveyed through her Sympathy Magic sensed amusement as well...... as usual, I still couldn’t tell how serious she was, but she seemed to be having fun, and that was enough to put me at ease.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......To think that, even after the setup up through the previous chapter, there was still room to expand the damage further, I’m trembling at the unfathomable depths of the Stomachache Devil.]"]},{"number":2499,"title":"Chapter 2499: Chapter 2500: Company and Exclusive Brush 7","paragraphs":["Chatting with Tetra-san over tea somehow made the time pass pleasantly. She had a way of teasing me with her words, but it was obviously teasing, and it felt like she enjoyed it along with my retorts. Her voice and demeanor were calm and gentle, but I thought she had a surprisingly lively side.","[......Kaito, is it alright if we talk a little about work?]","[Eh? Ah, sure, that’s fine......]","[......It’s about the thing you attach to the handle of that exclusive brush. Would it be okay if our trading company made something similar?]","[Um, you mean like recreating it as a magic tool, right?]","[......Yeah, the effect itself is simple, so reproducing it as a magic tool wouldn’t take much effort. On top of that, here’s the thing: for Dragons or Beastmen Demons using it themselves, no conversion is needed. But for someone like you using it on pets, conversion is necessary. Since it’s such a high-quality brush that even you like, anyone who values their pet enough to want an exclusive brush would probably want one.]","[That’s true, it visibly makes the fur shinier, so I can imagine many people would want it...... but the exclusive brush is, after all, a product of the Victor Trading Company. Is it really okay to make the attachments on our own?]","Regarding the creator’s rights, as long as confirmation is obtained, Nebula and Canalis-san would likely be fine with whatever is done, so that part isn’t an issue.","However, the exclusive brush is still the Victor Trading Company’s product. I couldn’t unilaterally approve development of an item that’s essentially an attachment, except for personal use.","[......Ah, of course. We’ll get permission from the Victor Trading Company and the Sharon County before making it. Formally, it would probably be a joint development and sale by the Victor Trading Company, Sharon Trading Company, and ours. The Victor Trading Company isn’t strong in magic tools, and Sharon Trading Company is a good trading company, but they still have technical challenges in magic tool development. Making a conversion tool on their own would take considerable time and money. So I want our trading company to support that part.]","[Ah, I see...... If you can get permission from them, I’m fine with it. I’ll check with Canalis-san and Nebula just in case.]","[......Thank you. Sorry for making you wait suddenly. But seeing you move so quickly like that, it’s really impressive.]","If permission can be obtained from the Victor Trading Company and the Sharon County, it’s completely fine on my end. Just to be sure, I immediately sent a hummingbird to Nebula and Canalis-san to confirm, and as expected, both said we could do as we like, including regarding the rights.","[I also want people who value their pets to have high-quality items, so I don’t need any stakes myself. Please just coordinate with the Victor Trading Company and the Sharon County on that.]","[......Got it. Trois is visiting Count Sharon’s estate soon, so I’ll make sure to bring it up with him as a proposal then.]","Somehow, I had the feeling that if the skilled salesman Trois-san took the matter, it could be contracted by the end of the day.","Well, it would probably be profitable for someone like Cornelia-san as well, so there shouldn’t be a problem.","After that, we went back to lighthearted chatter, enjoying tea and cake...... and the time came when it felt like we should leave the café. That meant paying the bill, so I decided I’d cover it and reached for the receipt...... arehh? It’s not here?","[......You’re a naughty one. Looking around like that...... what are you planning to mischief with?]","[......Ah.]","When I turned to Tetra-san, she was holding the receipt delicately between her index and middle fingers, a defiant smile on her face. T- This defiant smile...... c- could it be that Tetra-san is...... one fighting for the bill too?","The timing of this preemptive move, snatching the receipt with such precision, made it seem like I was about to engage in a payment battle for the first time with someone other than Dr, Vier.","Having the first strike taken by her grabbing the receipt was bad enough, but Tetra-san hadn’t said anything yet, so it was still a weak preemptive attack. If I brought up the suggestion to pay here......","[......Oh, I don’t suppose...... Kaito, are you planning to embarrass me?]","[Eh? E- Embarrass?]","[......Think about it. I’m the one who invited you to this café today. On top of that, you even listened to my consultation. If I had you pay even a single R with that, it would be a huge embarrassment for me.]","[Kuh......]","My opening move had been crushed!? And she casually played a simple but strong card: \"the inviter pays\".","Indeed, there was no prior arrangement, no discussion about the café, it was Tetra-san who invited me, and I merely went along...... The situation was already disadvantageous.","And worse, I didn’t have a counter for this attack. If I tried to force a response, the strongest card I could play would be \"thanks for celebrating my birthday\", but...... no, that would definitely be countered.","After all, Tetra-san also has that card representing thanks for when I secured the seats at Nifty Café, even though it was something Torre-san suggested.","If I played a \"thanks\" card, she would immediately counter with the same \"thanks\" card.","[......Even if you have a sinful preference for embarrassing women, if you want to embarrass me, I’d prefer it in bed.]","She’s summarizing the argument while I’m still thinking!? T- This is bad, even knowing it would be countered, I have to play a card or she’ll steamroll me.","[N- No——–]","[......Whoa there, wait a moment. Aren’t we close, Kaito? I know how you feel without you saying it. You’re kind, so you’d feel uncomfortable being treated one-sidedly, right?]","[———-Ah, y- yes.]","[......Then by all means, next time I want you to invite me and treat me. I’ll be looking forward to it, darling.]","With that, she pushed up the brim of her hat and winked...... no, she completely shut me down. From the start and even now, she perfectly crushed my timing the moment I tried to act, leaving me no room to argue.","Looking back, even when she initially held the receipt without me noticing, she had likely calculated my reactions and planned the conversation accordingly.","Not saying she would pay at that moment was to set me up, so that when I suggested paying, she could crush my opening move and take complete control of the flow.","Too brilliant...... could she be a high-class bill-swiping battle strategist......? Ugh. I lost completely this time, but next time, I’ll make sure to prepare a countermeasure so this doesn’t happen again.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [As always, he's up to fight people when it comes to deciding who pays the bill...... hides the fact that an even bigger strike against Sharon Trading Company is already guaranteed. Pitiful, they're really pitiful......]"]},{"number":2500,"title":"Chapter 2500: Chapter 2501: Company and Exclusive Brush 8","paragraphs":["Tetra, having returned to Kuromueina's stronghold in Demon Realm, spread her magical sensing with a somewhat cheerful demeanor.","[......Oh, there you are. Well then, I might as well pay you a visit while I’m at it.]","Confirming via magical sensing that her target was indeed inside the castle, Tetra began walking in that direction. After a short while, she saw her target...... Sechs up ahead.","[......Ya, Sechs.]","[Ah, Tetra-dono...... you seem to be in quite a good mood.]","[......I was just having the best time until now, after all. Of course, my spirits are high. Though, sadly...... time spent with him passes far too quickly. It feels like it ended in the blink of an eye.]","[I see...... so you were with Miyama-dono...... Now then, does this relate to the reason you came to see me?]","Sechs, being a Peak Count-rank himself, understood that Tetra had tracked him with magical sensing before visiting.","Therefore, when he assumed she must have some business with him and asked, Tetra opened her mouth while presenting a folded piece of paper.","[......First, I want you to look at this. It’s a provisional arrangement of a magic formula. I can construct a magic formula to a certain extent, but when it comes to creating magic tools, I’m far from your level, Sechs, so please forgive any clumsiness in the formula’s construction.]","[Fumu, let’s see...... wha!? T- This is......]","[......Now, having looked at that, I’ll explain the sequence of events. It started with a matter regarding exclusive brushes that Kaito purchased......]","Seeing Sechs' astonished expression, Tetra seemed almost pleased, as if to say he had reacted just as she expected. She then explained her interactions with Kaito: the tool that converts magic power when attached to the exclusive brush, how she used it to provisionally construct the magic formula, and the subsequent events...... After that, she spoke in a serious tone:","[......The item Kaito had didn’t have a magic crystal, but it seemed to generate magic power internally. It’s probably similar in nature to the white magic crystal Kaito possesses, so it would be impossible for us to obtain it. However, that tool was constructed making use of a magic formula just like a magic tool. Presumably, it was adapted to the technological system of that world.]","[And then, Tetra-dono saw it and provisionally constructed its magic formula for creating a magic tool...... in other words, a magic formula suited for making it with a magic crystal...... but this is......]","[......Quite stimulating, isn’t it? After all, changing the wavelength of one’s own magic power into something else is an advanced technique. Apparently, Phantasmal King-sama uses it often, but that’s only because of her skill. I might be able to manage it a little too, but I can’t guarantee changing the wavelength exactly as I intend.]","[Indeed. The magic formula would become far too complex, and even attempting to adapt it into a magic tool would be impossible...... or so I thought...... but now there’s this method......]","[......The originator seems to be the Spirit of Kaito's World Tree, but the idea is astonishingly genius. She broke down the magical wavelength conversion into ten simple magic formulas per step, then linked them together to make it work.]","[This is remarkable...... I can understand the logic. Normally, wavelength conversion involves simultaneously decomposing magic power, eliminating the existing wavelength, preparing a foundation for the new wavelength, applying it, and recombining the decomposed power, hence its extreme complexity. But by separating these into individual simple magic formulas, and then linking and synchronizing them step by step, it’s simplified...... though deciding exactly where to split and how to link and synchronize...... in reality, one would have to go through mind-numbing trial and error to finally reach the correct solution.]","Yes, the structure of that magic formula was exquisitely refined. Technically, it could be reproduced with existing techniques. Yet, under normal circumstances, reaching this particular form of such a special magic formula would require countless rounds of trial and error over an immense span of time, arriving at an almost perfect solution.","The way multiple steps were divided, the order in which they were combined to link together, it was so beautiful it could draw sighs.","[......If I recall correctly, wasn’t it the Spirit girl who devised the method to make the magic formula work even after splitting it?]","[Yes. Presumably, Nebula-dono came up with the idea, and Canalis-dono used Omniscience to deduce the correct arrangement, arriving at this form. But the original concept itself is remarkable. Seeing it presented like this, fully realized, you can’t help but nod in understanding. The real question is, could anyone arrive at this idea on their own...... Perhaps because they first conceived of the split formulas, they were able to think of linking multiple formulas to achieve a greater effect. In any case, I take my hat off to them.]","Tetra nodded in agreement with Sechs, who muttered with genuine admiration, and then continued in a serious tone:","[......And now, to the main point. Sechs, I want an expert opinion. After seeing this, I judged that it should be possible to imbue a magic tool with a magic formula capable of converting the infused magic power into any desired type of magic power. What do you think?]","[That’s possible. Of course, to make it function as a magic tool, you’d need some trial and error and likely modify the magic formula to some extent. But since the hardest part has already been solved, I think a magic tool capable of performing magic power conversion could be created without too much difficulty.]","[......On that premise, I want to ask, if we incorporate this mechanism, could we achieve things like: \"allowing the user to activate magic formulas with low-purity magic crystals by infusing their own magic power\", \"replenishing magic power in consumed crystals without waiting for natural recovery\", or \"activating magic formulas that were impossible even with black magic crystals\"...... these are just the ideas that came to me immediately. Do you think these are possible?]","[......They should be possible.]","At this very moment, quietly but decisively...... a major revolution in magic tools was on the verge of happening.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Have you noticed?]","~~~~~~~~~","Kaito : [If you’re turning that item into a magic tool, get permission from the Sharon County.]","Tetra : [Understood. I’ll frame it as a joint development.]","Kaito : [Alright then, let’s go with that.]","Tetra : [Sharon County-san, let’s bring a revolution to magic tools together♪]","~~~~~~~~~","Serious-senpai : [......Oi, oi, you're killing Cornelia’s stomach.]"]}]);
